// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — LiveABC Level 3–5 Basic
window.LB_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"global – fatal","cards":[{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the whole world; worldwide.","c":"全球的","s":"The global company has offices in 28 countries worldwide, and it plans to expand its business into new markets soon.","t":"這家全球的公司在世界各地28個國家設有辦事處，並計劃很快將業務擴展到新市場。"},{"w":"globe","p":"n.","d":"The earth, or a spherical representation of it.","c":"地球；地球儀","s":"Our teacher brought a large globe into the classroom so we could easily locate different countries and continents during the geography lesson.","t":"老師帶了一個大地球儀進教室，這樣我們在地理課時就能輕鬆找到不同的國家和大陸。"},{"w":"globalization","p":"n.","d":"The process by which businesses develop international influence.","c":"全球化","s":"Due to the rapid pace of globalization, local businesses must find new ways to compete with international corporations to survive.","t":"由於全球化的步伐快速，本土企業必須尋找新方法來與國際公司競爭以求生存。"},{"w":"global warming","p":"phr.","d":"A gradual increase in the overall temperature of the earth's atmosphere.","c":"全球暖化","s":"Many scientists believe that global warming is causing the polar ice caps to melt at a dangerously accelerated rate.","t":"許多科學家相信全球暖化正導致極地冰帽以危險的加速速率融化。"},{"w":"globally","p":"adv.","d":"In a way that relates to the whole world.","c":"全球地","s":"The brand is recognized globally, which gives it a significant advantage over its smaller, more regional competitors.","t":"這個品牌在全球地受到認可，讓它比那些規模較小、較具區域性的競爭對手擁有顯著優勢。"},{"w":"global village","p":"phr.","d":"The world considered as a single community linked by telecommunications.","c":"地球村","s":"With the invention of the internet, the world has truly become a global village, allowing instant communication across national borders.","t":"隨著網際網路的發明，世界已真正成為一個地球村，允許跨越國界的即時通訊。"},{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"To strengthen or support physically or mentally.","c":"維持；支撐","s":"The roof is not strong enough to sustain the heavy weight of the snow, and it might collapse if we don't clear it.","t":"這個屋頂不夠堅固，無法支撐積雪的沉重重量，如果不清理可能會倒塌。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"Able to be maintained at a certain rate or level.","c":"永續的；可持續的","s":"The company is looking for sustainable methods of producing electricity to reduce its negative impact on the fragile natural environment.","t":"這間公司正在尋找永續的發電方法，以減少其對脆弱自然環境的負面影響。"},{"w":"unsustainable","p":"adj.","d":"Not able to be maintained at the current rate or level.","c":"無法永續的","s":"Using oil is considered an unsustainable type of energy, so governments must find alternative sources before it completely runs out.","t":"使用石油被認為是一種無法永續的能源，因此政府必須在它完全耗盡之前尋找替代來源。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"The ability to be maintained at a certain rate or level.","c":"永續性","s":"Environmental sustainability is one of the most important goals for modern businesses that care deeply about the future of our planet.","t":"對於深切關心地球未來的現代企業來說，環境的永續性是最重要的目標之一。"},{"w":"sustainable development","p":"phr.","d":"Economic development conducted without depletion of natural resources.","c":"永續發展","s":"The city council passed a new law to promote sustainable development, ensuring that future generations will have enough natural resources.","t":"市議會通過了一項新法律來促進永續發展，確保後代將有足夠的自然資源。"},{"w":"vanish","p":"v.","d":"To disappear suddenly and completely.","c":"消失","s":"Many endangered animals could vanish as a result of climate change, which would severely damage the delicate balance of our ecosystem.","t":"由於氣候變遷，許多瀕危動物可能會消失，這將嚴重破壞我們生態系統的微妙平衡。"},{"w":"vanish into thin air","p":"phr.","d":"To disappear suddenly and completely without leaving a trace.","c":"憑空消失","s":"I don't know what happened to my car keys, but they seem to have vanished into thin air, and I can't find them anywhere.","t":"我不知道我的車鑰匙怎麼了，但它們似乎憑空消失了，我到處都找不到。"},{"w":"vanishing","p":"adj.","d":"Disappearing from sight or existence.","c":"正在消失的","s":"The vanishing forests are a major concern for environmentalists who are fighting hard to protect the habitats of wild animals.","t":"正在消失的森林是環保人士的主要擔憂，他們正努力保護野生動物的棲息地。"},{"w":"vanished","p":"adj.","d":"Having disappeared completely.","c":"消失的；絕跡的","s":"The archaeologists discovered the ancient ruins of a vanished civilization that existed thousands of years ago in the dense jungle.","t":"考古學家在茂密的叢林中發現了一個數千年前存在的消失的文明的古老遺跡。"},{"w":"disappear","p":"v.","d":"To cease to be visible.","c":"消失","s":"The talented magician waved his wand, and the white rabbit seemed to disappear from the stage, leaving the audience in absolute shock.","t":"才華洋溢的魔術師揮舞著他的魔杖，白兔似乎從舞台上消失了，讓觀眾感到絕對震驚。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v.","d":"To roughly calculate or judge the value or quantity of something.","c":"估計；估算","s":"A recent study estimates that there are over three trillion trees in the world, which is much higher than previous counts.","t":"一項最近的研究估計世界上有超過三兆棵樹，這比之前的統計高出許多。"},{"w":"estimated","p":"adj.","d":"Roughly calculated or approximate.","c":"估計的","s":"An estimated 1,000 people were injured in the disaster, and emergency rescue teams are still working hard to find survivors.","t":"災難中約有估計的1,000人受傷，緊急救援隊仍在努力尋找倖存者。"},{"w":"it is estimated that","p":"phr.","d":"Used to show that a number or amount is an approximation.","c":"據估計","s":"In a recent study, It is estimated that there are over three trillion trees in the world, highlighting the vastness of our global forests.","t":"在最近的一項研究中，據估計世界上有超過三兆棵樹，凸顯了我們全球森林的浩瀚。"},{"w":"estimation","p":"n.","d":"A rough calculation of the value, number, or extent of something.","c":"估計；判斷","s":"In my estimation, the project will take at least three months to complete if everyone works overtime to meet the strict deadline.","t":"依我的判斷，如果每個人都加班以趕上嚴格的截止日期，這個專案至少需要三個月才能完成。"},{"w":"underestimate","p":"v.","d":"To estimate something to be smaller or less important than it actually is.","c":"低估","s":"You should never underestimate the power of nature, because severe storms can cause massive destruction in just a few short hours.","t":"你永遠不該低估大自然的力量，因為強烈的風暴能在短短幾個小時內造成巨大的破壞。"},{"w":"overestimate","p":"v.","d":"To estimate to be better, larger, or more important than it really is.","c":"高估","s":"The manager tended to overestimate his own abilities, which eventually led to the failure of the company's most important marketing campaign.","t":"經理傾向於高估自己的能力，這最終導致了公司最重要的行銷活動的失敗。"},{"w":"trillion","p":"n.","d":"The number equivalent to the product of a million and a million.","c":"兆","s":"A recent study estimates that there are over three trillion trees in the world, highlighting the vastness of our global forests.","t":"一項最近的研究估計世界上有超過三兆棵樹，凸顯了我們全球森林的浩瀚。"},{"w":"billion","p":"n.","d":"The number equivalent to the product of a thousand and a million.","c":"十億","s":"The new government policy will cost several billion dollars to implement, but it is expected to greatly improve public transportation.","t":"新的政府政策將耗資數十億美元來實施，但預計將大大改善公共交通。"},{"w":"million","p":"n.","d":"The number equivalent to the product of a thousand and a thousand.","c":"百萬","s":"The popular music video quickly reached over a million views on the internet, making the creator famous overnight.","t":"這部受歡迎的音樂影片在網路上很快就達到了超過一百萬次的觀看，讓創作者一夜成名。"},{"w":"millions of","p":"phr.","d":"A very large but unspecified number of people or things.","c":"數以百萬計的","s":"The ambitious investors are injecting millions of dollars into the new wearable device, hoping it will become the next big trend.","t":"雄心勃勃的投資者正向這款新的穿戴式裝置注資數以百萬計的美元，希望它能成為全球市場的下一個大趨勢。"},{"w":"profound","p":"adj.","d":"Very great or intense; showing great knowledge.","c":"深刻的；深奧的","s":"The professor has a profound knowledge of mathematics, and he is always willing to help his students understand complex theories.","t":"這位教授擁有深奧的數學知識，而且他總是樂於幫助學生理解複雜的理論。"},{"w":"profoundly","p":"adv.","d":"Deeply or extremely.","c":"深刻地","s":"The writer is known for his profoundly insightful observations on human nature, which have influenced many modern philosophers.","t":"這位作家以他對人性的深刻地具洞察力的觀察而聞名，這些觀察影響了許多現代哲學家和讀者。"},{"w":"profound impact","p":"phr.","d":"A very strong and deep effect on someone or something.","c":"深遠的影響","s":"The invention of the smartphone has had a profound impact on the way we communicate and share information with each other.","t":"智慧型手機的發明對我們溝通和彼此分享資訊的方式產生了深遠的影響。"},{"w":"profound effect","p":"phr.","d":"A significant and deep consequence or outcome.","c":"深刻的效果","s":"Listening to classical music can have a profound effect on your ability to concentrate and reduce stress during long study sessions.","t":"聽古典音樂可以對你集中注意力的能力產生深刻的效果，並在長時間學習中減輕壓力。"},{"w":"profound knowledge","p":"phr.","d":"A deep, comprehensive understanding of a subject.","c":"淵博的知識","s":"It takes years of dedicated research and continuous study to acquire such profound knowledge about ancient Egyptian culture.","t":"獲得如此關於古埃及文化及其傳統的淵博的知識需要多年專注的研究和持續的學習。"},{"w":"annually","p":"adv.","d":"Once a year; every year.","c":"每年地","s":"Most doctors advise getting a physical checkup annually to ensure that any potential health problems are caught early.","t":"大多數醫生建議每年地進行一次健康檢查，以確保任何潛在的健康問題都能及早被發現和有效治療。"},{"w":"annual","p":"adj.","d":"Occurring once a year.","c":"每年的","s":"The company's annual meeting will be held next month, and all employees are expected to attend to discuss future business goals.","t":"公司的每年的會議將於下個月舉行，所有員工都被期望出席以討論未來的商業目標。"},{"w":"annual report","p":"phr.","d":"A comprehensive report on a company's activities throughout the preceding year.","c":"年度報告","s":"The cautious investors carefully reviewed the annual report to see if the company had made a reasonable profit over the past year.","t":"謹慎的投資者仔細審閱了年度報告，以查看該公司在過去一年中是否獲得了合理的利潤。"},{"w":"bi-annually","p":"adv.","d":"Occurring twice a year.","c":"一年兩次地","s":"The fashion magazine is published bi-annually, meaning loyal subscribers will receive a new and exciting issue every six months.","t":"這本時尚雜誌一年兩次地出版，這意味著忠實訂閱者每六個月一定會收到一期全新且精彩的期刊。"},{"w":"annual leave","p":"phr.","d":"Paid time off work granted by employers to employees.","c":"特休；年假","s":"After working incredibly hard for twelve months, John finally took his annual leave to travel across Europe with his beloved family.","t":"辛苦工作十二個月後，約翰終於休了年假，和他深愛的家人一起去歐洲旅行。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"To be greater than a number or amount, or to go beyond what is allowed.","c":"超過；超出","s":"When you are driving on the highway, please be very careful and do not exceed the speed limit, otherwise you will have to pay a steep penalty.","t":"在高速公路上行駛時，請不要超過速限，否則你將必須支付高昂的罰款。"},{"w":"excess","p":"n.","d":"An amount of something that is more than necessary, permitted, or desirable.","c":"過量；過多","s":"If you consume alcohol to excess, it will severely damage your liver and negatively impact your overall physical well-being.","t":"如果你飲酒過量，它將嚴重損害你的肝臟並對你的整體身體健康產生負面影響。"},{"w":"excessive","p":"adj.","d":"More than is necessary, normal, or desirable.","c":"過度的","s":"Excessive use of social media is not good for your mental health, as it can easily lead to feelings of intense anxiety and loneliness.","t":"過度的使用社群媒體對你的心理健康不利，因為它很容易導致強烈焦慮和孤獨的感覺。"},{"w":"excessive use of","p":"phr.","d":"The action of using something too much or more than is considered normal.","c":"過度使用","s":"Many experts strongly warn that Excessive use of social media is not good for your mental health and can lead to feelings of intense anxiety.","t":"許多專家強烈警告，過度使用社群媒體對你的心理健康不利，並且很容易導致強烈的焦慮感。"},{"w":"excessive amount","p":"phr.","d":"A quantity that is much larger than what is considered normal or acceptable.","c":"過量","s":"Eating an excessive amount of artificial sugar can lead to serious health problems like diabetes and heart disease in the long run.","t":"從長遠來看，吃下過量的人造糖可能會導致嚴重的健康問題，如糖尿病和心臟病。"},{"w":"excessively","p":"adv.","d":"To a greater degree than is necessary or desirable.","c":"過度地","s":"The angry boss complained that the team was spending excessively on business trips, so he immediately cut the travel budget by half.","t":"生氣的老闆抱怨團隊在出差上花費過度地多，所以他立刻將差旅預算削減了一半。"},{"w":"emerge","p":"v.","d":"To move out of or away from something and come into view.","c":"出現；浮現","s":"After several days of waiting, the beautiful butterfly finally emerged from the cocoon and prepared to fly for the very first time.","t":"經過幾天的等待，這隻美麗的蝴蝶終於從繭中出現，並準備進行第一次的飛行。"},{"w":"emergence","p":"n.","d":"The process of coming into view or becoming exposed after being concealed.","c":"出現；崛起","s":"The sudden emergence of new internet technologies has drastically changed the way traditional businesses operate in the modern global economy.","t":"新網際網路科技的突然出現已徹底改變了傳統企業在現代全球經濟中的運作方式。"},{"w":"emerging","p":"adj.","d":"Becoming apparent, important, or prominent.","c":"新興的","s":"Investors are increasingly interested in emerging markets because they offer significant opportunities for rapid growth and high returns.","t":"投資者對新興的市場越來越感興趣，因為它們為快速增長和高財務回報提供了重大的機會。"},{"w":"emerge from","p":"phr.","d":"To come out of a place or situation.","c":"從...出現/擺脫","s":"The country managed to emerge from the severe economic crisis much stronger than before, thanks to a series of brilliant government policies.","t":"該國成功地從嚴重的經濟危機中擺脫出來，變得比以前更強大，這要歸功於一系列出色的政府政策。"},{"w":"newly emerged","p":"phr.","d":"Recently come into view or existence.","c":"新出現的","s":"The newly emerged evidence strongly proved that the suspect was completely innocent, forcing the police to restart their criminal investigation immediately.","t":"新出現的證據強烈證明了嫌疑犯是完全無辜的，迫使警方立刻重新開始他們的刑事調查。"},{"w":"manifest","p":"v.","d":"To display or show a quality or feeling by one's acts or appearance.","c":"展現；顯露","s":"This captivating novel clearly manifests the excellent writing skills of the author, proving that she is a true master of storytelling.","t":"這本迷人的小說清楚地展現了作者出色的寫作技巧，證明了她是一位真正的說故事大師。"},{"w":"manifestation","p":"n.","d":"An event, action, or object that clearly shows or embodies something.","c":"表現；顯現","s":"His constant and loud complaining is just a manifestation of his deep dissatisfaction with his current job and his lack of career progress.","t":"他不斷且大聲的抱怨只是他對目前工作深感不滿以及缺乏職涯進展的一種表現。"},{"w":"manifest itself","p":"phr.","d":"To appear or become easy to see.","c":"顯現出來","s":"Tyson's deep depression began to manifest itself in increased bouts of sudden anger that frightened his family and his closest friends.","t":"泰森的重度憂鬱開始在越來越多突發的憤怒中顯現出來，這嚇壞了他的家人和最親密的朋友。"},{"w":"manifestly","p":"adv.","d":"In a way that is clear or obvious to the eye or mind.","c":"顯然地","s":"The recently proposed solution is manifestly unfair to the hardworking factory employees, and the labor union has declared they will strictly oppose it.","t":"最近提議的解決方案對辛勤工作的工廠員工來說顯然地是不公平的，而工會已宣布他們將嚴格反對它。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"To make previously unknown or secret information known to others.","c":"揭露","s":"The critical software bugs didn't reveal themselves until the device had already been released to the public, causing massive customer complaints.","t":"直到該設備已經向公眾發布後，關鍵的軟體錯誤才揭露出來，引起了大量的顧客抱怨。"},{"w":"reveal the truth","p":"phr.","d":"To make a secret or hidden fact known to others.","c":"揭露真相","s":"The courageous journalist worked tirelessly for several months to reveal the truth, proving that the woman was completely innocent of the terrible crime.","t":"這位勇敢的記者不知疲倦地工作了幾個月以揭露真相，證明該名婦女對那起可怕的罪行是完全無辜的。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"To make something hidden able to be seen, or reveal something bad or dishonest.","c":"暴露；揭發","s":"The investigative reporter published a comprehensive article to expose the corrupt practices within the local government, causing a massive uproar.","t":"那位調查記者發表了一篇全面的文章來揭發當地政府內部的腐敗行為，在憤怒的公民中引起了巨大的騷動。"},{"w":"expose a scandal","p":"phr.","d":"To reveal a situation that causes public outrage due to immoral behavior.","c":"揭發醜聞","s":"The newspaper editor ultimately decided to expose a scandal, which was fueled by shocking rumors about the popular politician's private life and illegal financial activities.","t":"報社編輯最終決定揭發一樁醜聞，這樁醜聞是由關於那位受歡迎政治人物的私生活和非法財務活動的令人震驚的謠言所引起的。"},{"w":"be exposed to","p":"phr.","d":"To be put in a situation where one is not protected from something dangerous.","c":"暴露於...；接觸到...","s":"If children are constantly exposed to violent video games and movies, they might develop aggressive behaviors and lack empathy for other people's suffering.","t":"如果孩子們不斷地暴露於暴力的電玩遊戲和電影中，他們可能會發展出具攻擊性的行為，並且對他人的痛苦缺乏同理心。"},{"w":"exposure","p":"n.","d":"The state of being placed in an unprotected condition, or public attention.","c":"暴露；曝光","s":"The company's new marketing campaign gained a lot of media exposure on the internet, which helped boost their overall sales significantly.","t":"該公司的新行銷活動在網路上獲得了大量的媒體曝光，這有助於在繁忙的假期期間顯著提升他們的整體銷售額。"},{"w":"exposure to","p":"phr.","d":"The condition of experiencing or being affected by something.","c":"暴露於...；接觸...","s":"Prolonged exposure to the harsh summer sunlight without wearing proper protection can severely damage your delicate skin.","t":"在沒有採取適當保護的情況下，長時間暴露於強烈的夏日陽光下會嚴重損害你嬌嫩的皮膚。"},{"w":"ecological","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the relation of living organisms to their surroundings.","c":"生態的","s":"The government often has to address serious ecological issues that are ignored by big businesses in their relentless pursuit of profit.","t":"政府經常必須解決大企業在無情追求利潤時所忽視的嚴重生態的問題。"},{"w":"ecologically","p":"adv.","d":"In a way that relates to the physical environments of plants and animals.","c":"生態上地","s":"The new farming practices are ecologically sustainable and will not harm the local wildlife that depends heavily on this specific habitat.","t":"新的農作實踐在生態上地是永續的，且不會傷害嚴重依賴這個特定棲息地的當地野生動物。"},{"w":"ecologist","p":"n.","d":"An expert in or student of ecology.","c":"生態學家","s":"The famous ecologist warned that destroying the wetlands would have a disastrous effect on the populations of migratory birds in the region.","t":"那位著名的生態學家警告說，破壞濕地將對該地區的候鳥數量產生災難性的影響。"},{"w":"ecology","p":"n.","d":"The branch of biology dealing with relations of organisms to their surroundings.","c":"生態學","s":"Students taking the university's ecology course will spend a week in the forest to directly observe the complex interactions between different species.","t":"選修大學生態學課程的學生將在森林裡待上一個星期，以直接觀察不同物種之間複雜的互動。"},{"w":"eco-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"Not harmful to the environment.","c":"環保的","s":"Many conscious consumers now prefer to buy eco-friendly products to reduce their carbon footprint and help protect the earth for future generations.","t":"許多有意識的消費者現在更喜歡購買環保的產品，以減少他們的碳足跡並幫助為後代保護地球。"},{"w":"environmentally-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"Designed to have little or no damaging effect on the environment.","c":"環保的；對環境友善的","s":"As more consumers become conscious of the planet, they prefer to purchase environmentally-friendly products that reduce their carbon footprint.","t":"隨著越來越多的消費者對地球產生意識，他們更喜歡購買能減少碳足跡並幫助防止全球暖化的環保的產品。"},{"w":"environmental protection","p":"phr.","d":"The practice of protecting the natural environment.","c":"環境保護","s":"The government committee will be conducting a comprehensive study on environmental protection to ensure that future generations can live in a safe, healthy, and sustainable world.","t":"政府委員會將針對環境保護進行一項全面的研究，以確保後代能生活在一個安全、健康且永續的世界中。"},{"w":"disaster","p":"n.","d":"A sudden event that causes great damage or loss of life.","c":"災難","s":"Last month's devastating earthquake was the worst disaster I have ever experienced, and many people were unfortunately left homeless in its wake.","t":"上個月的毀滅性地震是我經歷過最糟糕的災難，許多人不幸地因此無家可歸。"},{"w":"disastrous","p":"adj.","d":"Causing great damage.","c":"災難性的","s":"Ian's first attempt at making dinner was a completely disastrous event, as he accidentally burned the chicken and broke an expensive plate.","t":"伊恩第一次嘗試做晚餐是一件完全災難性的事件，因為他不小心把雞肉燒焦還打破了一個昂貴的盤子。"},{"w":"spell disaster","p":"phr.","d":"To cause serious problems or ruin.","c":"帶來災難","s":"The rapidly rising river could spell disaster for those who fish on its banks or live in the nearby low-lying coastal areas.","t":"迅速上漲的河水可能會為那些在河岸捕魚或住在附近低窪沿海地區的人帶來災難。"},{"w":"natural disaster","p":"phr.","d":"A natural event such as a flood or earthquake that causes great damage.","c":"自然災害","s":"The government has established a special emergency fund to help citizens rebuild their homes quickly after a natural disaster unexpectedly occurs.","t":"政府建立了一個特別緊急基金，以幫助公民在自然災害意外發生後迅速重建家園。"},{"w":"disaster relief","p":"phr.","d":"The provision of help to people who have experienced a disaster.","c":"救災","s":"Several international organizations sent disaster relief teams to the flooded region to distribute clean water and medical supplies to the desperate victims.","t":"幾個國際組織派遣了救災隊伍前往水患地區，向絕望的災民分發乾淨的水和醫療物資。"},{"w":"humanitarian aid","p":"phr.","d":"Material and logistic assistance to people in times of crisis.","c":"人道救援","s":"After the devastating earthquake destroyed the entire coastal city, several international organizations quickly sent humanitarian aid to provide clean water, food, and urgent medical supplies.","t":"在毀滅性的地震摧毀了整座沿海城市之後，幾個國際組織迅速送來人道救援以提供乾淨的水、食物和緊急的醫療物資。"},{"w":"surge","p":"","d":"","c":"","s":"Lately, there has been a massive surge of interest in taking action against climate change among the younger generations across the globe.","t":"最近，在全球年輕世代中，採取行動對抗氣候變遷的興趣出現了大規模的激增。"},{"w":"surging","p":"adj.","d":"Moving suddenly and powerfully forward or upward.","c":"洶湧的；猛增的","s":"The surging waves from the powerful typhoon crashed forcefully onto the shore, causing significant structural damage to the coastal buildings.","t":"強烈颱風帶來洶湧的海浪猛烈地拍打著海岸，對沿海建築造成了重大的結構性破壞。"},{"w":"a surge of","p":"phr.","d":"A sudden large increase in a feeling or in an amount of something.","c":"一陣（情緒）；大量的","s":"The marathon runner felt a sudden a surge of energy as she heard the massive crowd cheering for her near the finish line.","t":"當馬拉松選手在終點線附近聽到大批人群為她歡呼時，她感到一陣突如其來的能量。"},{"w":"surge ahead","p":"phr.","d":"To move forwards quickly and forcefully.","c":"猛衝向前；遙遙領先","s":"Despite a slow start in the race, the determined athlete managed to surge ahead of her competitors in the final lap.","t":"儘管在比賽一開始進展緩慢，這位意志堅定的運動員在最後一圈成功地遙遙領先。"},{"w":"threaten","p":"v.","d":"To state one's intention to take hostile action against someone.","c":"威脅","s":"Kelly angrily threatened to tell her mother if Peter said those incredibly mean and hurtful things to her ever again.","t":"凱莉生氣地威脅說，如果彼得再對她說那些極其刻薄傷人的話，她就要告訴她媽媽。"},{"w":"threat","p":"n.","d":"A statement of an intention to inflict pain, injury, or damage.","c":"威脅","s":"The environmental group warned that the massive building of the new freeway posed a serious threat to the rare bird's natural home.","t":"環保團體警告說，大規模建造新高速公路對這種稀有鳥類的自然家園構成了嚴重的威脅。"},{"w":"threatening","p":"adj.","d":"Having a hostile or deliberately frightening quality.","c":"具威脅性的","s":"The dark, heavy clouds looking incredibly threatening in the sky forced the organizers to cancel the outdoor music festival entirely.","t":"天空中看起來極其具威脅性的烏雲迫使主辦單位完全取消了戶外音樂節。"},{"w":"threaten to V","p":"phr.","d":"To seem likely to produce an unpleasant or unwelcome result.","c":"威脅將要；有...的危險","s":"The ongoing bad weather threatens to ruin the weekend camping trip that we had been eagerly planning for several long months.","t":"持續的惡劣天氣有毀掉我們已經熱切計畫了好幾個月的週末露營之旅的危險。"},{"w":"life-threatening","p":"adj.","d":"Potentially fatal; carrying a risk of death.","c":"致命的；危及生命的","s":"The brave firefighter was rushed to the hospital with life-threatening injuries after he bravely rescued the trapped family from the burning house.","t":"這位勇敢的消防員在英勇地將受困家庭從燃燒的房子中救出後，帶著危及生命的傷勢被緊急送往醫院。"},{"w":"pose a threat to","p":"phr.","d":"To present a danger or risk to someone or something.","c":"對...構成威脅","s":"Having a new house built so close to the river poses a threat to your family's safety because the water floods the area every few years.","t":"把新房子建在離河這麼近的地方對你家人的安全構成嚴重的威脅，因為河水每隔幾年就會淹沒該地區。"},{"w":"pose a risk to","p":"phr.","d":"To create a possible danger or harm to someone or something.","c":"對...構成風險","s":"Eating an excessive amount of processed foods can pose a risk to your overall health and eventually lead to severe chronic diseases.","t":"吃過量的加工食品可能會對你的整體健康構成顯著的風險，並最終導致嚴重的慢性疾病。"},{"w":"at risk","p":"phr.","d":"In a situation where something bad or harmful might happen.","c":"處於危險中；有風險","s":"The famous politician's outstanding reputation will undoubtedly be at risk if he fails to win his difficult court case.","t":"如果這位著名的政治人物未能在艱難的官司中勝訴並被判有罪，他傑出的名聲無疑將處於危險中。"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"To frighten or threaten someone to persuade them to do something.","c":"威嚇；脅迫","s":"The aggressive lawyer tried to intimidate the shy witness during the intense trial, hoping she would become too scared to tell the truth.","t":"這位咄咄逼人的律師試圖在激烈的審判中威嚇害羞的證人，希望她會因為太害怕而不敢對嚴格的法官說出真相。"},{"w":"intimidating","p":"adj.","d":"Making you feel frightened or nervous.","c":"令人敬畏的；嚇人的","s":"Starting a new job in a large and busy corporation can be an incredibly intimidating experience, especially if you are not yet acquainted with your new colleagues.","t":"在一家龐大且繁忙的公司開始一份新工作可能是一次極其嚇人的經歷。"},{"w":"destiny","p":"n.","d":"The events that will necessarily happen to a particular person in the future.","c":"命運","s":"He always strongly believed that it was his destiny to become a great leader and positively change his country for the better.","t":"他總是強烈地相信，成為一位偉大的領導人並積極地讓他的國家變得更好是他的命運。"},{"w":"destined","p":"adj.","d":"Intended for a particular purpose or bound for a destination.","c":"注定的；前往...的","s":"These large wooden boxes full of donated clothes and essential medical supplies are destined for South Africa to help people in urgent need.","t":"這些裝滿捐贈衣物和基本醫療物資的大木箱是前往南非去幫助急需援助的人的。"},{"w":"be destined to","p":"phr.","d":"To be certain to do something or to happen in the future.","c":"注定要","s":"Everyone agrees that Alex is destined to become an incredibly famous singer because he has so much natural talent and charisma.","t":"每個人都同意亞歷克斯注定要成為一位極其著名的歌手，因為他擁有如此多的天賦和魅力。"},{"w":"be destined for","p":"phr.","d":"Bound for a certain destination or outcome.","c":"目的地是...；注定會得到...","s":"She worked incredibly hard during her university years because she knew she was destined for great success in the competitive corporate world.","t":"她在大學期間非常努力工作，因為她知道她注定會得到競爭激烈的企業界中的巨大成功。"},{"w":"manifest destiny","p":"phr.","d":"The 19th-century doctrine that the expansion of the US throughout the Americas was both justified and inevitable.","c":"天命論","s":"The historical concept of manifest destiny was frequently used to justify the rapid and controversial westward expansion of the United States in the 1800s.","t":"天命論的歷史概念經常被用來為1800年代美國快速且具爭議的向西擴張辯護。"},{"w":"fate","p":"n.","d":"The development of events beyond a person's control.","c":"命運","s":"After the large company suffered massive financial losses for three consecutive years, its fate was sealed and the owner had no choice but to declare bankruptcy.","t":"在這家大公司連續三年遭受巨額財務損失之後，它的命運就已注定，老闆除了宣佈破產別無選擇。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"Causing death or leading to failure or disaster.","c":"致命的；災難性的","s":"Thankfully, his sudden illness was not fatal, and the experienced doctor assured his anxious family that he would make a full recovery in just a few weeks.","t":"幸好，他的突發疾病不是致命的，且經驗豐富的醫生向他焦急的家人保證他會在短短幾週內完全康復。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"mutual – airtight alibi","cards":[{"w":"mutual","p":"adj.","d":"Shared, felt, or shown equally by two or more people.","c":"互相的；共同的","s":"Even though they have very different personalities, John and Carrie share a mutual appreciation for classic jazz music.","t":"儘管他們有著非常不同的個性，約翰和凱莉對經典爵士樂有著共同的欣賞。"},{"w":"solid","p":"adj.","d":"Firm and stable in shape; not liquid or fluid.","c":"堅固的；紮實的","s":"You need a solid understanding of basic mathematical principles before you can attempt to solve these advanced physics equations.","t":"在你嘗試解開這些進階物理方程式之前，你需要對基本數學原理有紮實的理解。"},{"w":"sociable","p":"adj.","d":"Willing to talk and engage in activities with others; friendly.","c":"好交際的；合群的","s":"The Millers are incredibly sociable people who frequently enjoy having loud and exciting dinner parties with their neighbors.","t":"米勒一家是極其好交際的人，他們經常喜歡和鄰居舉辦熱鬧又刺激的晚宴。"},{"w":"unsociable","p":"adj.","d":"Not enjoying the company of others; not friendly.","c":"不愛交際的","s":"Ever since he lost his job, he has become quite unsociable, refusing to leave his room or speak to anyone.","t":"自從他失業後，他變得相當不愛交際的，拒絕離開他的房間或和任何人說話。"},{"w":"antisocial","p":"adj.","d":"Contrary to the laws and customs of society; not sociable.","c":"反社會的；不擅社交的","s":"His habit of ignoring people when they speak to him is considered completely antisocial and rude by his colleagues.","t":"當別人跟他說話時他總是不理睬的習慣，被他的同事認為是完全反社會的且粗魯的。"},{"w":"wild","p":"adj.","d":"Living or growing in the natural environment; not domesticated.","c":"野生的","s":"We went on an exciting safari in Africa and took incredible photographs of wild lions, elephants, and giraffes.","t":"我們去非洲參加了一場刺激的野生動物園之旅，並拍下了野生的獅子、大象和長頸鹿的驚人照片。"},{"w":"enhanced","p":"adj.","d":"Intensified or further improved in quality or value.","c":"增強的；提升的","s":"The newest version of the sports car comes with several enhanced safety features to better protect the driver during an accident.","t":"最新版本的跑車配備了幾項增強的安全功能，以在事故中更好地保護駕駛。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"Aware of and responding to one's surroundings; awake.","c":"有意識的；意識到的","s":"Bobby bites his fingernails all the time when he's nervous, but he doesn't usually do it in a conscious manner.","t":"波比緊張時總是在咬指甲，但他通常不是以有意識的方式在做這件事。"},{"w":"tolerant","p":"adj.","d":"Showing willingness to allow the existence of different opinions.","c":"寬容的；容忍的","s":"In a diverse and modern society, it is essential that citizens be more tolerant of cultures and beliefs that are different from their own.","t":"在一個多元且現代的社會中，公民必須對與自己不同的文化和信仰更加寬容的。"},{"w":"airtight","p":"adj.","d":"Not allowing air to escape; having no weaknesses.","c":"密不透風的；無懈可擊的","s":"The careful engineer made absolutely sure to have airtight knowledge of the challenging landscape before he started building the suspension bridge.","t":"這位謹慎的工程師在開始建造吊橋之前，絕對確保自己對這個具挑戰性的地形擁有無懈可擊的知識。"},{"w":"indisputable","p":"adj.","d":"Unable to be challenged or denied.","c":"不容置疑的","s":"The surveillance video provided clear and indisputable evidence that the suspect was nowhere near the bank when the robbery actually occurred.","t":"監視器影片提供了清晰且不容置疑的證據，證明當搶劫實際發生時，嫌疑犯根本不在銀行附近。"},{"w":"sealed","p":"adj.","d":"Closed securely so that nothing can get in or out.","c":"密封的","s":"The ancient Egyptian tomb had remained completely sealed for thousands of years until modern archaeologists finally discovered its hidden entrance.","t":"這個古埃及陵墓已經完全密封的數千年，直到現代考古學家終於發現了它隱藏的入口。"},{"w":"visible","p":"adj.","d":"Able to be seen.","c":"可見的","s":"The bright stars were clearly visible in the night sky because we were camping far away from the city's light pollution.","t":"明亮的星星在夜空中清晰可見的，因為我們在遠離城市光害的地方露營。"},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"Used or intended to defend; oversensitive to criticism.","c":"防禦的；防備的","s":"Whenever I gently suggest that he could improve his writing skills, he immediately gets incredibly defensive and starts arguing with me.","t":"每當我溫和地建議他可以改善寫作技巧時，他立刻變得極具防備的並開始和我爭論。"},{"w":"predatory","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to an animal or person that preys on others.","c":"掠食的；剝削的","s":"The government is trying to pass new laws to protect vulnerable citizens from the predatory lending practices of some banks.","t":"政府正試圖通過新法律，以保護弱勢公民免受某些銀行剝削的放貸行為所害。"},{"w":"mutually","p":"adv.","d":"In a shared manner or to an equal degree.","c":"互相地","s":"The two rival companies eventually reached a mutually beneficial agreement that allowed both of them to increase their profits.","t":"兩家競爭公司最終達成了一項互相地有益的協議，讓雙方都能增加利潤。"},{"w":"consciously","p":"adv.","d":"In a deliberate and intentional way.","c":"有意識地；蓄意地","s":"You must consciously force yourself to sit up straight at your desk, otherwise you will eventually develop terrible back pain.","t":"你必須有意識地強迫自己坐在辦公桌前挺直腰板，否則你最終會發展出可怕的背痛。"},{"w":"unconsciously","p":"adv.","d":"Without realizing or being aware of one's actions.","c":"無意識地","s":"As the suspenseful movie reached its climax, I was unconsciously holding my breath the entire time until the scene ended.","t":"當這部懸疑電影達到高潮時，我無意識地一直屏住呼吸，直到該場景結束。"},{"w":"subconsciously","p":"adv.","d":"In a way influenced by the part of the mind one is not fully aware of.","c":"潛意識地","s":"Even though he smiled and said he was fine, he was subconsciously rubbing his sore shoulder throughout the entire meeting.","t":"即使他笑著說他沒事，在整個會議中他卻潛意識地在揉他痠痛的肩膀。"},{"w":"solidarity","p":"n.","d":"Unity or agreement of feeling or action among people with a common interest.","c":"團結","s":"The factory workers showed incredible solidarity during the strike, refusing to return to work until their demands were met.","t":"工廠工人在罷工期間展現了令人難以置信的團結，拒絕重返工作崗位直到他們的要求得到滿足。"},{"w":"motto","p":"n.","d":"A short sentence chosen as encapsulating the beliefs guiding an individual or group.","c":"座右銘；格言","s":"Many successful professional athletes apply the motto 'no pain, no gain' to their strict daily training routines.","t":"許多成功的職業運動員將「沒有痛苦就沒有收穫」的座右銘應用在他們嚴格的日常訓練中。"},{"w":"longevity","p":"n.","d":"Long life; long existence or service.","c":"長壽；持久","s":"Extreme longevity is quite normal in my family, as both of my grandparents lived to be over 100 years old.","t":"極端的長壽在我家是很正常的，因為我的祖父母都活到了100歲以上。"},{"w":"wildlife","p":"n.","d":"Wild animals collectively; the native fauna of a region.","c":"野生動植物","s":"Taiwan's central mountain ranges are home to a diverse and beautiful range of wildlife, including monkeys, birds, and bears.","t":"台灣的中央山脈是各種美麗野生動植物的家園，包含猴子、鳥類和熊。"},{"w":"prey","p":"n./v.","d":"An animal that is hunted and killed by another for food.","c":"獵物；捕食","s":"Many small mammals and insects on this remote island are easy prey for the large, venomous snakes that live here.","t":"這座偏遠島嶼上的許多小型哺乳動物和昆蟲，都是生活在這裡的大型毒蛇的容易到手的獵物。"},{"w":"predator","p":"n.","d":"An animal that naturally preys on others.","c":"掠食者","s":"Nesting high on the steep cliff wall, the young birds were completely safe from dangerous predators that roamed below.","t":"在陡峭的懸崖壁高處築巢，幼鳥們完全免於在下方漫遊的危險掠食者的威脅。"},{"w":"enhancement","p":"n.","d":"An increase or improvement in quality, value, or extent.","c":"提升；改進","s":"The software update provides a significant enhancement to the system's security, making it much harder for hackers to steal information.","t":"這次軟體更新為系統的安全性提供了顯著的提升，讓駭客更難竊取資訊。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"The faculty of being able to see; the ability to plan the future with imagination.","c":"視力；願景","s":"Marcus has a great and ambitious vision for his startup company, but it will be quite difficult to make it happen.","t":"馬庫斯對他的新創公司有一個偉大且雄心勃勃的願景，但要實現它將會相當困難。"},{"w":"mammal","p":"n.","d":"A warm-blooded vertebrate animal with hair or fur.","c":"哺乳動物","s":"It is a fascinating scientific fact that the largest mammal in the entire world is the massive blue whale.","t":"整個世界上最大的哺乳動物是巨大的藍鯨，這是一個迷人的科學事實。"},{"w":"consciousness","p":"n.","d":"The state of being awake and aware of one's surroundings.","c":"意識；知覺","s":"After being struck heavily on the head by a falling rock, the injured hiker briefly lost consciousness before the rescue team arrived.","t":"在頭部被落石重擊後，受傷的登山客在救援隊抵達前短暫失去了意識。"},{"w":"shortcoming","p":"n.","d":"A fault or failure to meet a certain standard.","c":"缺點；短處","s":"Jesse is a brilliant engineer, but her only major shortcoming is that she completely refuses to learn how to speak Chinese.","t":"潔西是位才華洋溢的工程師，但她唯一主要的缺點是她完全拒絕學習如何說中文。"},{"w":"weakness","p":"n.","d":"A disadvantage or fault; lack of strength.","c":"弱點","s":"During the demanding job interview, the manager asked me to truthfully describe my greatest professional strength and my greatest weakness.","t":"在要求嚴格的工作面試中，經理要求我如實描述我最大的專業優勢和我最大的弱點。"},{"w":"tolerance","p":"n.","d":"The ability or willingness to tolerate something.","c":"寬容；忍耐力","s":"The wise leader preached a message of peace and religious tolerance to help unite the deeply divided country during the crisis.","t":"明智的領袖傳達了和平與宗教寬容的訊息，以幫助在危機期間團結嚴重分裂的國家。"},{"w":"circumstance","p":"n.","d":"A fact or condition connected with or relevant to an event or action.","c":"情況；環境","s":"The two men didn't get along well, but under entirely different circumstances, they could have actually been great friends.","t":"這兩個男人相處得不好，但在完全不同的情況下，他們實際上可能成為很好的朋友。"},{"w":"condition","p":"n.","d":"The state of something, especially with regard to its appearance or working order.","c":"狀況；條件","s":"The used car was highly affordable, but it was unfortunately in terrible condition and needed expensive repairs to its engine.","t":"這輛二手車非常負擔得起，但不幸的是它的狀況很糟，且需要對其引擎進行昂貴的維修。"},{"w":"defense","p":"n.","d":"The action of defending from or resisting attack.","c":"防禦；防衛","s":"Sadly, the ancient city's strong stone defense did not stop the invading enemy soldiers from climbing the walls and getting inside.","t":"令人遺憾地，這座古城堅固的石頭防禦並沒有阻止入侵的敵方士兵爬上城牆並進入內部。"},{"w":"self-defense","p":"phr.","d":"The defense of one's person using physical force.","c":"自衛","s":"The lawyer argued that his frightened client only attacked the aggressive man in an act of pure self-defense to save her own life.","t":"律師辯稱，他受驚的委託人只是出於純粹的自衛行為才攻擊那名具攻擊性的男子以保住自己的性命。"},{"w":"solidify","p":"v.","d":"To make or become hard or solid; to make stronger.","c":"鞏固；凝固","s":"The recent successful project helped to solidify her position as the most capable manager in the entire marketing department.","t":"最近成功的專案有助於鞏固她作為整個行銷部門中最有能力經理的地位。"},{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"To mix socially with others.","c":"交際；參與社交","s":"The weekend conference is a perfect opportunity for young professionals to socialize and build valuable connections within the industry.","t":"這個週末會議是年輕專業人士參與社交並在業界建立寶貴人脈的完美機會。"},{"w":"roam","p":"v.","d":"To move about or travel aimlessly over a wide area.","c":"漫遊；遊蕩","s":"Thousands of years ago, massive herds of wild bison once roamed freely across the vast and empty American plains.","t":"數千年前，大量的野生野牛群曾經在廣闊空曠的美洲平原上自由漫遊。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"To walk or move in a leisurely, casual, or aimless way.","c":"徘徊；閒逛","s":"On Sunday afternoons, I love to just wander through the city's botanical gardens and admire the beautiful blooming flowers.","t":"在星期天下午，我喜歡只是在城市的植物園裡閒逛，並欣賞美麗盛開的花朵。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"To intensify or further improve the quality, value, or extent of.","c":"提高；增加","s":"The chef added a variety of fresh local herbs and spices to enhance the natural flavor of the expensive steak.","t":"廚師加入各種新鮮的當地香草和香料，以提升這塊昂貴牛排的天然風味。"},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"To allow the existence of something one does not necessarily like or agree with.","c":"容忍；忍受","s":"The strict teacher clearly stated on the first day of class that she is not going to tolerate your rudeness any longer.","t":"嚴格的老師在開學第一天就清楚聲明她不打算再容忍你的粗魯了。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"To resist an attack; to protect from harm or danger.","c":"保衛；防守","s":"The brave soldiers were ordered to fiercely defend the strategic bridge against the advancing enemy troops at all costs.","t":"勇敢的士兵們被命令要不惜一切代價猛烈地保衛這座具戰略意義的橋樑，抵禦推進的敵軍。"},{"w":"lengthen","p":"v.","d":"To make or become longer.","c":"加長；延長","s":"Doing regular stretching exercises can help to lengthen your muscles and significantly reduce the risk of sports injuries.","t":"規律地做伸展運動可以幫助延長你的肌肉並顯著降低運動傷害的風險。"},{"w":"long for","p":"v.","d":"To want or desire something very much; to yearn for.","c":"期盼；渴望","s":"The job seeker longed for a chance to get a full-time job with a decent salary.","t":"這位求職者期盼渴望得到全職工作且有不錯的薪資。"},{"w":"mutual trust","p":"phr.","d":"A shared belief in the reliability, truth, or ability of each other.","c":"互信","s":"Building strong mutual trust is essential for any successful partnership, especially when starting a new business together.","t":"建立堅強的互信對於任何成功的合夥關係都是不可或缺的，尤其是在一起開創新事業時。"},{"w":"mutual respect","p":"phr.","d":"A shared feeling of admiration and consideration for each other.","c":"互相尊重","s":"A healthy and long-lasting marriage must be built on a foundation of honesty, excellent communication, and deep mutual respect.","t":"一段健康且長久的婚姻必須建立在誠實、良好的溝通和深深的互相尊重的基礎上。"},{"w":"show solidarity with","p":"phr.","d":"To demonstrate support for a group or cause.","c":"展現對...的團結/支持","s":"Hundreds of university teachers joined the massive street march to show solidarity with their protesting students.","t":"數百名大學教師加入了大規模的街頭遊行，以展現對抗議學生的團結。"},{"w":"express solidarity","p":"phr.","d":"To state or communicate one's support for a group.","c":"表達支持/團結","s":"Several international leaders released statements to express solidarity the nation after it was struck by the terrible earthquake.","t":"在該國遭受可怕的地震襲擊後，幾位國際領袖發表聲明以表達支持。"},{"w":"live by the motto","p":"phr.","d":"To base one's life choices on a specific phrase or belief.","c":"秉持...的座右銘生活","s":"I always try to live by the motto that honesty is the best policy, even when telling the truth is difficult.","t":"我總是試著秉持「誠實為上策」的座右銘生活，即使說出真相很困難。"},{"w":"school motto","p":"phr.","d":"A phrase representing the educational beliefs or values of a school.","c":"校訓","s":"The principal proudly reminded the graduating students of the school motto, encouraging them to always strive for excellence.","t":"校長自豪地提醒畢業生們校訓，鼓勵他們永遠追求卓越。"},{"w":"company motto","p":"phr.","d":"A short phrase expressing the guiding principles of a business.","c":"公司宗旨","s":"The newly established tech firm chose 'Innovation through Collaboration' as its official company motto to inspire all its employees.","t":"這家新成立的科技公司選擇「透過合作創新」作為其官方的公司宗旨以激勵所有員工。"},{"w":"secret to longevity","p":"phr.","d":"The reason or method for living a very long time.","c":"長壽的秘訣","s":"Many researchers believe that the secret to longevity involves a combination of a healthy diet, daily exercise, and low stress.","t":"許多研究人員相信，長壽的秘訣包含了健康飲食、日常運動和低壓力的結合。"},{"w":"promote longevity","p":"phr.","d":"To encourage or contribute to a longer lifespan.","c":"促進長壽","s":"Eating plenty of fresh vegetables and avoiding processed foods are proven lifestyle habits that actively promote longevity in human beings.","t":"多吃新鮮蔬菜並避免加工食品是被證實能積極促進人類長壽的生活習慣。"},{"w":"wildlife conservation","p":"phr.","d":"The practice of protecting wild plant and animal species and their habitats.","c":"野生動物保育","s":"The government has heavily invested in wildlife conservation programs to ensure that endangered species are protected from illegal hunting.","t":"政府已大量投資於野生動物保育計畫，以確保瀕危物種免受非法狩獵的威脅。"},{"w":"wildlife habitat","p":"phr.","d":"The natural environment in which a particular species of wild animal lives.","c":"野生動物棲息地","s":"Cutting down ancient forests destroys the essential wildlife habitat that thousands of rare animals depend on for their survival.","t":"砍伐古老森林摧毀了數千種珍稀動物賴以生存的必要野生動物棲息地。"},{"w":"in the wild","p":"phr.","d":"In a natural state or environment, unconfined by humans.","c":"在野外","s":"It is absolutely thrilling to see a powerful tiger running freely in the wild rather than locked inside a small cage.","t":"看到一隻強壯的老虎在野外自由奔跑，而不是被關在小籠子裡，絕對是令人興奮的。"},{"w":"social animal","p":"phr.","d":"An animal (including humans) that is highly interactive with other members of its species.","c":"群居動物；喜歡社交的人","s":"Humans are naturally a social animal, meaning that we desperately need communication and connection with others to maintain good mental health.","t":"人類天生就是一種群居動物，這意味著我們極度需要與他人溝通和連結以維持良好的心理健康。"},{"w":"fall prey to","p":"phr.","d":"To be vulnerable to or overcome by something.","c":"成為...的犧牲品；受...所害","s":"Unfortunately, the elderly woman fell prey to a sophisticated online scam and lost almost all of her life savings.","t":"不幸地，這位老婦人成為一場複雜網路詐騙的犧牲品，失去了幾乎所有的畢生積蓄。"},{"w":"prey on","p":"phr.","d":"To hunt and kill for food; to take advantage of someone.","c":"捕食；利用","s":"It is a known fact that domestic cats will often prey on wild birds and rats if they are allowed outside.","t":"眾所周知，如果允許家貓外出，牠們經常會捕食野鳥和老鼠。"},{"w":"bird of prey","p":"phr.","d":"A bird that feeds on animal flesh, with a strong hooked bill and sharp talons.","c":"猛禽","s":"The eagle is a magnificent bird of prey that can easily spot small animals from hundreds of feet in the air.","t":"老鷹是一種壯麗的猛禽，能從數百英尺的高空輕鬆發現小動物。"},{"w":"easy prey","p":"phr.","d":"Someone or something that is easily attacked or deceived.","c":"容易下手的目標","s":"Tourists who carry expensive cameras and leave their bags unzipped are often easy prey for clever pickpockets in crowded areas.","t":"帶著昂貴相機且包包沒拉上拉鍊的遊客，在擁擠的地區通常是聰明扒手容易下手的目標。"},{"w":"apex predator","p":"phr.","d":"A predator at the top of a food chain, without natural predators of its own.","c":"頂級掠食者","s":"The great white shark is an apex predator in the ocean, playing a crucial role in maintaining the balance of marine life.","t":"大白鯊是海洋中的頂級掠食者，在維持海洋生物平衡中扮演著關鍵的角色。"},{"w":"natural predator","p":"phr.","d":"An animal that hunts and eats a particular species in nature.","c":"天敵","s":"Because the invasive insect has no natural predator in this new environment, its population has multiplied out of control rapidly.","t":"因為這種入侵昆蟲在這個新環境中沒有天敵，牠的數量已迅速繁殖到失控的地步。"},{"w":"performance enhancement","p":"phr.","d":"The act of improving the efficiency or output of something.","c":"效能提升；表現增強","s":"The athlete was banned from the upcoming Olympic games after testing positive for illegal performance enhancement drugs during a random check.","t":"這名運動員在隨機檢查中對非法的表現增強藥物呈陽性反應後，被禁止參加即將到來的奧運會。"},{"w":"night vision","p":"phr.","d":"The ability to see in low light conditions.","c":"夜視能力","s":"Gail says that her night vision is very bad, so she strongly prefers to never drive a car after the sun goes down.","t":"蓋兒說她的夜視能力非常差，所以她強烈傾向在太陽下山後絕不開車。"},{"w":"field of vision","p":"phr.","d":"The entire area a person or animal is able to see when their eyes are fixed in one position.","c":"視野","s":"When driving on the highway, a sudden movement in my field of vision warned me that a deer was jumping onto the road.","t":"在高速公路上開車時，我視野中突然的移動警告我有一隻鹿正跳到路上。"},{"w":"visionary","p":"","d":"","c":"","s":"Steve Jobs was widely recognized as a brilliant visionary who completely revolutionized the personal computer and mobile phone industries.","t":"史蒂夫·賈伯斯被廣泛認可為一位才華洋溢的有遠見的人，他徹底顛覆了個人電腦和行動電話產業。"},{"w":"marine mammal","p":"phr.","d":"A mammal that lives in the ocean or depends on the ocean for its food.","c":"海洋哺乳動物","s":"Dolphins and seals are highly intelligent marine mammals that rely heavily on sound to communicate underwater.","t":"海豚和海豹是高度聰明的海洋哺乳動物，牠們嚴重依賴聲音在水下溝通。"},{"w":"land mammal","p":"phr.","d":"A mammal that primarily lives on land.","c":"陸地哺乳動物","s":"The cheetah is widely known for being the fastest land mammal on the planet, capable of reaching incredible speeds during a hunt.","t":"獵豹以地球上跑得最快的陸地哺乳動物而廣為人知，能夠在狩獵期間達到驚人的速度。"},{"w":"roam around","p":"phr.","d":"To walk or travel without a specific destination in a particular area.","c":"在...四處走動/遊蕩","s":"During our vacation in Rome, we spent the entire morning roaming around the ancient ruins and taking beautiful photos.","t":"在羅馬度假期間，我們花了整個早上在古老遺跡中四處走動並拍下美麗的照片。"},{"w":"roam freely","p":"phr.","d":"To move about without restrictions or boundaries.","c":"自由漫遊","s":"The national park was established so that endangered elephants and rhinos could roam freely without the threat of being hunted.","t":"建立國家公園是為了讓瀕危的大象和犀牛可以自由漫遊，而不受被狩獵的威脅。"},{"w":"overcome a shortcoming","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully deal with a personal fault or flaw.","c":"克服缺點","s":"Through months of dedicated practice and public speaking classes, Daniel finally managed to overcome a shortcoming of being extremely shy.","t":"透過幾個月的專心練習和公開演講課程，丹尼爾終於成功克服了他極度害羞的缺點。"},{"w":"major shortcoming","p":"phr.","d":"A significant or prominent fault or weakness.","c":"主要缺點","s":"The major shortcoming of this new software is that it frequently crashes when too many people try to use it at the same time.","t":"這款新軟體的主要缺點是當太多人試圖同時使用它時，它經常會崩潰。"},{"w":"zero tolerance","p":"phr.","d":"A strict policy of not allowing a particular type of behavior.","c":"零容忍","s":"The school board recently adopted a strict zero tolerance policy towards bullying, meaning any offender will be suspended immediately.","t":"學校董事會最近對霸凌採取了嚴格的零容忍政策，這意味著任何違規者將在沒有警告的情況下被立即停學。"},{"w":"put up with","p":"phr.","d":"To endure or tolerate someone or something.","c":"忍受","s":"We'll just have to patiently put up with the terrible noise from the construction site next door until the building work is completed.","t":"我們只好耐心地忍受隔壁建築工地的可怕噪音，直到建築工程完成。"},{"w":"on condition that","p":"phr.","d":"Only if a specific thing happens; provided that.","c":"條件是…；在…的條件下","s":"The school allowed Marcus to take the elective course on condition that he attended every single class.","t":"學校允許馬庫斯選修這門選修課，條件是他每堂課都必須出席。"},{"w":"in critical condition","p":"phr.","d":"Extremely ill or injured, and likely to die or face serious danger.","c":"情況危急；病危","s":"Following the severe traffic accident, the truck driver was rushed to the hospital and remains in critical condition.","t":"在那場嚴重的交通意外之後，卡車司機被緊急送往醫院，目前仍情況危急。"},{"w":"in good condition","p":"phr.","d":"Healthy, working well, or looking clean and undamaged.","c":"狀態良好；完好無缺","s":"Although this smartphone is a used model, it is still in good condition and looks completely new.","t":"雖然這款智慧型手機是二手型號，但它依然狀態良好，而且看起來像全新的一樣。"},{"w":"in bad condition","p":"phr.","d":"Sick, not working properly, or heavily damaged.","c":"狀態不佳；破舊不堪","s":"The historic mountain cabin was in bad condition after being abandoned and neglected for over twenty years.","t":"這座歷史悠久的山區小屋在被遺棄並疏於照顧二十多年後，已經破舊不堪（狀態不佳）。"},{"w":"under no circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"Never; absolutely not.","c":"無論在任何情況下都不","s":"The doctor emphasized that Under no circumstances are you officially allowed to look at another patient's private and confidential medical records.","t":"醫生強調，無論在任何情況下都不正式允許你查看另一位病人的私人且機密的醫療記錄。"},{"w":"under normal circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"Usually; in a typical situation.","c":"在正常情況下","s":"Under normal circumstances, the flight from New York to London only takes about seven hours, but a massive storm caused severe delays today.","t":"在正常情況下，從紐約飛往倫敦只需大約七個小時，但今天一場巨大的風暴造成了嚴重的延誤。"},{"w":"unforeseen circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"Unexpected events or situations that could not be predicted.","c":"不可預見的情況","s":"Due to completely unforeseen circumstances, the popular outdoor music festival had to be suddenly canceled just hours before it was supposed to begin.","t":"由於完全不可預見的情況，這個受歡迎的戶外音樂節不得不在原定開始前幾個小時突然被取消。"},{"w":"airtight container","p":"phr.","d":"A box or jar designed to keep air out.","c":"密封容器","s":"If you keep your leftover meals stored in an airtight container inside the refrigerator, the food will stay fresh for much longer.","t":"如果你把吃剩的飯菜存放在冰箱裡的密封容器中，食物會保鮮更久。"},{"w":"airtight alibi","p":"phr.","d":"A claim of being elsewhere when a crime was committed that is impossible to disprove.","c":"完美的不在場證明","s":"The detective was extremely frustrated because the primary suspect had an airtight alibi verified by dozens of reliable witnesses at the party.","t":"偵探感到極度挫折，因為主要嫌疑犯擁有數十名在派對上的可靠證人所證實的完美的不在場證明。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"equivalent – domain name","cards":[{"w":"equivalent","p":"adj.","d":"Equal in value, amount, function, or meaning.","c":"相等的；等值的","s":"The doctor said that drinking one large glass of this special juice is exactly equivalent to eating three servings of raw vegetables.","t":"醫生說喝一大杯這種特別的果汁完全相當於吃三份生菜。"},{"w":"negotiable","p":"adj.","d":"Open to discussion or modification.","c":"可協商的","s":"The starting salary for this position is fixed, but the number of vacation days is entirely negotiable depending on your experience.","t":"這個職位的起薪是固定的，但休假天數完全是可協商的，這取決於你的經驗。"},{"w":"transactional","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the conducting of business or exchange.","c":"交易的","s":"Some people view modern relationships in a purely transactional way, measuring exactly what they give and what they get in return.","t":"有些人以純粹交易的方式看待現代人際關係，精確地衡量他們付出了什麼以及得到了什麼回報。"},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"Restricted or limited to the person, group, or area concerned.","c":"獨家的；專屬的","s":"Residents of this luxury community enjoy the exclusive use of the large outdoor swimming pool and the fully equipped modern gym.","t":"這個豪華社區的居民享有大型戶外游泳池和設備齊全的現代化健身房的專屬的使用權。"},{"w":"cyber","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the culture of computers, information technology, and virtual reality.","c":"網路的；電腦的","s":"The national government has hired a team of experts to protect the country's essential infrastructure from potential cyber attacks by hackers.","t":"國家政府聘請了一個專家團隊來保護國家重要的基礎設施，免受駭客潛在的網路的攻擊。"},{"w":"roughly equivalent","p":"phr.","d":"Approximately equal in value or amount.","c":"大約相等的","s":"The amount of energy consumed by this small town is roughly equivalent to the energy used by a single large factory.","t":"這個小鎮消耗的能源數量與一家大型工廠使用的能源大約相等的。"},{"w":"exclusively","p":"adv.","d":"To the exclusion of others; only.","c":"專門地；獨家地","s":"The expensive new restaurant caters exclusively to wealthy celebrities and powerful politicians who want a quiet place to eat in peace.","t":"這家昂貴的新餐廳專門地迎合想要一個安靜的地方和平用餐的富有的名人和有權勢的政治人物。"},{"w":"asset","p":"n.","d":"A useful or valuable thing, person, or quality.","c":"資產；有用的人或物","s":"The manager believes that Jason is a hard-working, intelligent employee who would undoubtedly be an asset to any company.","t":"經理相信傑森是一位努力工作且聰明的員工，他無疑會是任何公司的寶貴資產。"},{"w":"token","p":"n.","d":"A thing serving as a visible or tangible representation of a fact, quality, or feeling.","c":"代幣；象徵","s":"If you don't have a modern electronic travel card, you can simply buy a plastic token from the vending machine.","t":"如果你沒有現代的電子交通卡，你可以直接從自動售票機買一枚塑膠代幣。"},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"The action or process of investing money for profit or material result.","c":"投資","s":"Buying a house in this rapidly growing neighborhood is generally considered a very safe and profitable investment for the future.","t":"在這個快速發展的社區買房子，通常被認為是對未來非常安全且有利可圖的投資。"},{"w":"investor","p":"n.","d":"A person or organization that puts money into financial schemes.","c":"投資者","s":"The young entrepreneur is actively searching for a wealthy investor who can provide enough funding to start his new tech business.","t":"這位年輕的企業家正在積極尋找一位富有的投資者，以提供足夠的資金來啟動他的新科技事業。"},{"w":"equivalence","p":"n.","d":"The condition of being equal or equivalent in value, worth, or function.","c":"相等；等值","s":"The mathematics teacher spent the entire lesson explaining the logical equivalence between the two complex formulas written on the board.","t":"數學老師花了整節課解釋寫在黑板上的兩個複雜公式之間的邏輯相等關係。"},{"w":"property","p":"n.","d":"A thing or things belonging to someone; a characteristic.","c":"財產；特性","s":"Owen had always wanted to build a large wooden house on his own property, far away from the noisy city streets.","t":"歐文一直想在自己的財產（土地）上建一棟大木屋，遠離喧囂的城市街道。"},{"w":"possession","p":"n.","d":"The state of having, owning, or controlling something.","c":"擁有；所有物","s":"The tragic family lost all their valuable possessions when their wooden house suddenly burned down during the terrible summer wildfire.","t":"這個悲慘的家庭失去了所有寶貴的所有物，當他們木造的房子在可怕的夏季野火中突然燒毀時。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"Discussion aimed at reaching an agreement.","c":"談判","s":"After three days of intense negotiation, the labor union and the factory managers finally agreed on a fair salary increase for workers.","t":"經過三天的激烈談判，工會和工廠經理們終於同意為工人提供公平的加薪。"},{"w":"negotiator","p":"n.","d":"A person who conducts negotiations.","c":"談判者","s":"The police department sent in their best and most experienced negotiator to convince the armed bank robbers to release the terrified hostages.","t":"警察局派出了他們最優秀且經驗最豐富的談判者，以說服武裝的銀行搶匪釋放受驚的人質。"},{"w":"transaction","p":"n.","d":"An instance of buying or selling something; a business deal.","c":"交易","s":"John carefully checked his printed receipt after making a large transaction at the local bank to ensure no mistakes were made.","t":"在當地銀行進行了一筆大額交易後，約翰仔細檢查了他列印出來的收據，以確保沒有發生錯誤。"},{"w":"trail","p":"n./v.","d":"A mark or series of signs left behind; a path in the countryside.","c":"痕跡；小徑","s":"The experienced hunters quietly followed the trail of fresh footprints in the deep snow to eventually find the large bear.","t":"經驗豐富的獵人安靜地沿著深雪中新鮮腳印的痕跡，最終找到了那隻大熊。"},{"w":"owner","p":"n.","d":"A person who owns something.","c":"擁有者；主人","s":"The proud owner of the newly opened bakery stood outside his shop, offering free samples of bread to passing customers.","t":"新開的麵包店自豪的老闆站在他的店外，向路過的顧客提供免費的麵包試吃。"},{"w":"ownership","p":"n.","d":"The act, state, or right of possessing something.","c":"所有權","s":"John now has the legal documents required to formally show his ownership of the beautiful beach house that he just purchased.","t":"約翰現在擁有了正式顯示他對剛買的美麗海灘別墅的所有權所需的法律文件。"},{"w":"domain","p":"n.","d":"An area of territory owned or controlled; a specified sphere of activity or knowledge.","c":"領土；領域","s":"In historical times, the powerful king's domain spread from the western snowy mountains all the way to the hot eastern desert.","t":"在歷史時期，這位強大國王的領土從西邊的雪山一直延伸到東邊炎熱的沙漠。"},{"w":"inclusiveness","p":"n.","d":"The quality of including all sections of society.","c":"包容性","s":"The progressive school prides itself on its high level of inclusiveness, ensuring that students from all different backgrounds feel totally welcome.","t":"這所進步的學校為其高度的包容性感到自豪，確保來自所有不同背景的學生都感到完全受歡迎。"},{"w":"cryptocurrency","p":"n.","d":"A digital currency in which transactions are verified by a decentralized system.","c":"加密貨幣","s":"Many young investors believe that cryptocurrency will eventually replace traditional banks and completely change the way we buy and sell goods.","t":"許多年輕投資者相信加密貨幣最終將取代傳統銀行，並徹底改變我們買賣商品的方式。"},{"w":"format","p":"v./n.","d":"To arrange or set out something in a particular way.","c":"格式；編排","s":"Katherine carefully formatted the final financial report in an easy-to-read way so that the clients could understand it quickly.","t":"凱薩琳小心地將最終的財務報告編排成易於閱讀的方式，以便客戶能迅速理解。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"v./n.","d":"To accept or support a belief or change willingly and enthusiastically; a hug.","c":"欣然接受；擁抱","s":"The citizens happily embraced the new safety law because they believed it would make the crowded city much safer for their children.","t":"公民們快樂地欣然接受了新的安全法律，因為他們相信這將使擁擠的城市對他們的孩子來說安全許多。"},{"w":"invest in","p":"v.","d":"To put money into financial schemes, shares, property, or a commercial venture.","c":"投資","s":"If you choose to invest your savings wisely in the stock market, you could potentially double your money in just a few years.","t":"如果你選擇明智地將積蓄投資於股票市場，你可能會在短短幾年內讓你的錢翻倍。"},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"To have or own something.","c":"擁有","s":"In order to become a successful detective, you must possess a highly logical mind and excellent problem-solving skills.","t":"為了成為一名成功的偵探，你必須擁有高度邏輯的頭腦和出色的解決問題技巧。"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"To try to reach an agreement or compromise by discussion with others.","c":"談判；協商","s":"The government firmly refuses to negotiate with terrorists because it would encourage them to commit even more violent crimes in the future.","t":"政府堅決拒絕與恐怖份子談判，因為這會鼓勵他們在未來犯下更暴力的罪行。"},{"w":"ensure","p":"v.","d":"To make certain that something shall occur or be the case.","c":"確保（+事情）","s":"Exercising every day will effectively ensure that you fall into a deep and restful sleep when you go to bed at night.","t":"每天運動將有效地確保你在晚上上床睡覺時能進入深層且平靜的睡眠。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"To tell someone something positively or confidently to dispel any doubts.","c":"向某人保證","s":"The experienced mechanic assured me that the car would be perfectly safe to drive after he completely repaired the damaged brakes.","t":"經驗豐富的技師向我保證，在他完全修好損壞的煞車後，這輛車開起來會非常安全。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v./n.","d":"To promise; a formal promise or assurance.","c":"保證；擔保","s":"I can confidently guarantee that you will be incredibly successful in your new career if you just continue to work hard.","t":"我可以自信地保證，如果你只是繼續努力工作，你在你的新職涯中將會難以置信地成功。"},{"w":"fully embrace","p":"v.","d":"To accept something completely and enthusiastically.","c":"完全接受","s":"To succeed in this fast-paced technology industry, you must fully embrace new ideas and never stop learning from your mistakes.","t":"要在這個快節奏的科技產業中取得成功，你必須完全接受新想法，並且永遠不要停止從錯誤中學習。"},{"w":"physical asset","p":"phr.","d":"An item of economic value that has a tangible existence.","c":"實體資產","s":"The struggling business was forced to sell off a major physical asset to quickly pay its mounting debts to the bank.","t":"這家陷入困境的企業被迫賣掉一項主要的實體資產，以迅速償還其對銀行不斷增加的債務。"},{"w":"valuable asset","p":"phr.","d":"Something that is very useful or worth a lot of money.","c":"寶貴的資產","s":"Your ability to speak three different languages fluently is a valuable asset in today's highly competitive global job market.","t":"你能流利地說三種不同語言的能力，在當今競爭激烈的全球就業市場中是一項寶貴的資產。"},{"w":"liquid asset","p":"phr.","d":"Cash or an asset that can be readily converted to cash.","c":"流動資產","s":"During the severe economic crisis, the investors wanted to ensure they had enough liquid assets available to survive the year.","t":"在嚴重的經濟危機期間，投資者希望確保他們有足夠的流動資產來度過這一年。"},{"w":"single journey token","p":"phr.","d":"A coin-like object used to pay for one trip on public transport.","c":"單程代幣","s":"The tourist who was visiting Taipei for the first time bought a single journey token to take the MRT to the famous night market.","t":"第一次來台北旅遊的遊客買了一枚單程代幣，搭乘捷運去著名的夜市。"},{"w":"as a token of","p":"phr.","d":"As a sign or symbol of something.","c":"作為...的象徵/表示","s":"Edward gave his lovely girlfriend some expensive gold jewelry as a token of his deep and eternal love for her.","t":"愛德華給了他可愛的女朋友一些昂貴的金飾，作為他對她深切且永恆之愛的象徵。"},{"w":"by the same token","p":"phr.","d":"In the same way or for the same reason.","c":"同理；同樣地","s":"There isn't enough hard evidence to prove your claim, but by the same token, I cannot prove that you are entirely wrong either.","t":"沒有足夠的確鑿證據來證明你的主張，但同理，我也無法證明你完全錯了。"},{"w":"token of appreciation","p":"phr.","d":"A small gift or gesture to express gratitude.","c":"感謝的表示","s":"The boss gave everyone a small bonus at the end of the busy week as a token of appreciation for their hard work.","t":"在忙碌的一週結束時，老闆給了每個人一筆小獎金，作為對他們辛勤工作的感謝的表示。"},{"w":"format a document","p":"phr.","d":"To arrange the text and layout of a computer file.","c":"將文件格式化/編排文件","s":"It usually takes me about twenty minutes to format a document properly before I send it to my university professor.","t":"在我將文件發送給大學教授之前，通常需要花大約二十分鐘來正確地編排文件。"},{"w":"electronic format","p":"phr.","d":"The arrangement of data for computer processing or display.","c":"電子格式","s":"In the modern age, most of these classic books are now widely available in electronic format for digital readers.","t":"在現代，大多數這些經典書籍現在都廣泛地以電子格式提供給數位閱讀器。"},{"w":"digital format","p":"phr.","d":"Data that is stored in a binary form for computers.","c":"數位格式","s":"We need to save all the old family photographs in a digital format so they won't be ruined by moisture over time.","t":"我們需要將所有舊的家庭照片以數位格式保存，這樣它們才不會隨著時間的推移而被濕氣破壞。"},{"w":"standard format","p":"phr.","d":"A usual or accepted way of arranging something.","c":"標準格式","s":"When you write a formal business email, you should always follow the standard format to maintain a professional appearance.","t":"當你寫正式的商業電子郵件時，你應該總是遵循標準格式以維持專業的形象。"},{"w":"warm embrace","p":"phr.","d":"A friendly and affectionate hug.","c":"溫暖的擁抱","s":"After being away for a whole year, she greeted her beloved mother at the airport with a very warm embrace.","t":"離開整整一年後，她在機場用一個非常溫暖的擁抱迎接了她深愛的母親。"},{"w":"embrace change","p":"phr.","d":"To accept new situations and adapt to them willingly.","c":"欣然接受改變","s":"Some older employees find it difficult to embrace change, but it is absolutely necessary for the company to grow and evolve.","t":"一些較年長的員工覺得很難欣然接受改變，但這對於公司的成長和發展是絕對必要的。"},{"w":"overseas investment","p":"phr.","d":"Money put into businesses or property in foreign countries.","c":"海外投資","s":"The local government is currently trying to encourage overseas investment to boost the economy and create more job opportunities for citizens.","t":"當地政府目前正試圖鼓勵海外投資，以刺激經濟並為公民創造更多就業機會。"},{"w":"return on investment","p":"phr.","d":"The profit from an activity compared to its cost.","c":"投資回報率","s":"Before buying the expensive new machinery, the factory manager carefully calculated the expected return on investment to ensure it was worthwhile.","t":"在購買昂貴的新機器之前，工廠經理仔細計算了預期的投資回報率，以確保這是值得的。"},{"w":"the equivalent of","p":"phr.","d":"Something that has the same value or meaning as another thing.","c":"...的等值物/等同於","s":"For young Alex, paying his monthly taxes was basically the equivalent of having a healthy tooth slowly pulled out by a dentist.","t":"對年輕的亞歷克斯來說，繳納每月的稅金基本上就等同於讓牙醫慢慢拔掉一顆健康的牙齒。"},{"w":"equivalent amount","p":"phr.","d":"An equal quantity of something.","c":"等量","s":"If you substitute honey for sugar in this recipe, you should use an equivalent amount to ensure the cake tastes sweet enough.","t":"如果你在這個食譜中用蜂蜜代替糖，你應該使用等量以確保蛋糕嚐起來夠甜。"},{"w":"personal property","p":"phr.","d":"Movable belongings owned by an individual.","c":"個人財產","s":"Please remember to take all your personal property with you when leaving the train, including your bags, phones, and umbrellas.","t":"離開火車時，請記得帶走你所有的個人財產，包含你的包包、手機和雨傘。"},{"w":"public property","p":"phr.","d":"Land, buildings, or equipment owned by the government.","c":"公共財產","s":"The city's beautiful parks and outdoor sports facilities are considered public property, and they are strictly for the enjoyment of everyone.","t":"城市裡美麗的公園和戶外運動設施被認為是公共財產，且嚴格來說是為了讓大家享受的。"},{"w":"intellectual property","p":"phr.","d":"Intangible property that is the result of creativity, such as patents or copyrights.","c":"智慧財產","s":"The tech company takes intellectual property theft very seriously, and they will immediately sue anyone who steals their software designs.","t":"這家科技公司非常重視智慧財產的竊盜，他們會立刻起訴任何竊取他們軟體設計的人。"},{"w":"healing property","p":"phr.","d":"The characteristic of a substance that helps cure illness.","c":"療效；治療特性","s":"I read in an ancient medical book that pure honey may actually have some remarkable healing property for curing sore throats.","t":"我在一本古老的醫學書上讀到，純蜂蜜實際上可能對治癒喉嚨痛有一些顯著的療效。"},{"w":"take possession of","p":"phr.","d":"To begin to own or control something.","c":"取得...的所有權","s":"Valerie excitedly took possession of her shiny new sports car exactly two weeks after she paid the dealership in full.","t":"瓦萊麗在全額付給經銷商整整兩週後，興奮地取得了她閃亮新跑車的所有權。"},{"w":"in possession of","p":"phr.","d":"Holding or owning something.","c":"擁有...","s":"The police officer quickly discovered that Harold was in possession of the secret code needed to open the bank's main safe.","t":"警察很快就發現哈羅德擁有打開銀行主保險箱所需的密碼。"},{"w":"have something in one's possession","p":"phr.","d":"To physically hold or control an item.","c":"擁有某物；持有某物","s":"A kind man called me this morning to say he found my lost wallet and currently has it in his possession.","t":"一位好心的男士今早打電話給我說他找到了我遺失的錢包，並且目前持有它。"},{"w":"refuse to negotiate","p":"phr.","d":"To decline to discuss an agreement.","c":"拒絕談判","s":"If the buyers stubbornly refuse to negotiate the high price of the house, we will just have to look for another buyer.","t":"如果買家固執地拒絕協商這棟房子的高昂價格，我們就只好尋找另一個買家了。"},{"w":"make a transaction","p":"phr.","d":"To complete a business deal or payment.","c":"進行交易","s":"Whenever you make a transaction online, you should always double-check that the website is completely secure and highly trustworthy.","t":"每當你在線上進行交易時，你應該總是再次確認該網站是完全安全且高度值得信賴的。"},{"w":"business transaction","p":"phr.","d":"An interaction between a buyer and a seller.","c":"商業交易","s":"The two massive international companies finalized their complex business transaction after months of planning and consulting with expensive corporate lawyers.","t":"經過幾個月的計畫並諮詢了昂貴的企業律師後，這兩家龐大的國際公司最終完成了他們複雜的商業交易。"},{"w":"financial transaction","p":"phr.","d":"An agreement or movement carried out between a buyer and a seller to exchange an asset for payment.","c":"財務交易","s":"Modern banking apps allow users to track every single financial transaction they make directly from their smartphones with incredible ease.","t":"現代銀行應用程式讓使用者能極其輕鬆地直接從他們的智慧型手機追蹤他們進行的每一筆財務交易。"},{"w":"follow the trail","p":"phr.","d":"To walk along a path or track.","c":"沿著小徑/蹤跡走","s":"If we just follow the trail carefully through the thick forest, we will eventually reach the beautiful waterfall at the end.","t":"如果我們只是小心地沿著小徑走穿過茂密的森林，我們最終會到達盡頭美麗的瀑布。"},{"w":"off the trail","p":"phr.","d":"Away from the designated path.","c":"偏離小徑","s":"Jessica wandered off the trail to take some photos of the wild flowers and unfortunately got completely lost in the forest.","t":"潔西卡偏離小徑去拍一些野花的照片，不幸地完全在森林中迷路了。"},{"w":"leave a trail","p":"phr.","d":"To create a series of marks or signs behind you.","c":"留下痕跡","s":"The leaky pipe managed to leave a trail of dirty water all the way from the kitchen to the front door.","t":"漏水的水管一路從廚房到前門留下了一道髒水的痕跡。"},{"w":"hiking trail","p":"phr.","d":"A path created for people to walk through nature.","c":"登山步道","s":"The national park boasts a famously difficult hiking trail that attracts thousands of adventurous climbers from all over the world.","t":"這個國家公園擁有一條著名的困難登山步道，吸引了來自世界各地數千名熱愛冒險的攀岩者。"},{"w":"ensure safety","p":"phr.","d":"To make certain that people are protected from harm.","c":"確保安全","s":"The airline has introduced several new and strict regulations to ensure safety for all passengers traveling during the harsh winter storm.","t":"該航空公司引入了幾項新的嚴格規定，以確保在惡劣冬季風暴期間旅行的所有乘客的安全。"},{"w":"I assure you","p":"phr.","d":"A phrase used to confidently tell someone that something is true.","c":"我向你保證","s":"I assure you, your pet pig will be well cared for and given plenty of delicious food while you are on vacation.","t":"我向你保證，在你度假期間，你的寵物豬會得到很好的照顧並獲得大量美味的食物。"},{"w":"make sure","p":"phr.","d":"To confirm or ensure that something happens.","c":"確保；確定","s":"You need to make sure that all of your construction materials arrive at the building site in a timely and organized manner.","t":"你需要確保你所有的建築材料都能及時且有條理地抵達建築工地。"},{"w":"exclusive of","p":"phr.","d":"Not including something.","c":"不包括","s":"The beautiful silver watch costs exactly $200, exclusive of the local sales tax that will be added at the cash register.","t":"這隻美麗的銀色手錶剛好要價200美元，不包括將在收銀台附加的當地營業稅。"},{"w":"exclusive right","p":"phr.","d":"The power to do something that is granted to only one person or group.","c":"獨家權利/專屬權利","s":"The author gave the publishing company the exclusive right to print and distribute her brand new fantasy novel across North America.","t":"作者給予這家出版公司在整個北美印製和發行她全新奇幻小說的獨家權利。"},{"w":"joint ownership","p":"phr.","d":"The state of a property being owned by two or more people.","c":"共同擁有","s":"The two brothers have joint ownership of the family farm, which unfortunately means they often argue over how to run it.","t":"這兩兄弟對家庭農場擁有共同擁有權，不幸的是這意味著他們經常為了如何經營它而爭吵。"},{"w":"money back guarantee","p":"phr.","d":"A promise to return a buyer's money if they are not satisfied.","c":"退款保證","s":"All of our company's high-quality electronic products come with a 30-day money back guarantee to ensure complete customer satisfaction and trust.","t":"我們公司所有高品質的電子產品都附有30天的退款保證，以確保顧客完全的滿意和信任。"},{"w":"lifetime guarantee","p":"phr.","d":"A promise to repair or replace a product for the duration of its life.","c":"終身保固","s":"The durable backpack comes with a lifetime guarantee, meaning the manufacturer will repair any ripped seams for free, forever.","t":"這個耐用的背包附有終身保固，這意味著製造商將永遠免費修理任何撕裂的縫線。"},{"w":"under guarantee","p":"phr.","d":"Covered by a warranty.","c":"在保固期內","s":"Luckily, my broken laptop is still under guarantee, so the technology company will definitely fix the shattered screen without charging me.","t":"幸運的是，我壞掉的筆記型電腦仍在保固期內，所以科技公司絕對會免費修理碎裂的螢幕。"},{"w":"absolute guarantee","p":"phr.","d":"A promise made with complete certainty.","c":"絕對保證","s":"There is no absolute guarantee that the stock market will go up tomorrow, so you must invest your money very carefully.","t":"沒有絕對保證股市明天會上漲，所以你必須非常謹慎地投資你的錢。"},{"w":"domain name","p":"phr.","d":"The part of a network address that identifies it as belonging to a particular domain.","c":"網域名稱","s":"Every modern business should have its own memorable domain name for the internet so that customers can easily find their website.","t":"每個現代企業都應該擁有自己好記的網路網域名稱，這樣顧客才能輕鬆找到他們的網站。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"abundant – heavenly body","cards":[{"w":"abundant","p":"adj.","d":"Existing or available in large quantities; plentiful.","c":"豐富的；大量的","s":"The region is famous for its abundant sunshine, which makes it the absolute perfect place for growing high-quality wine grapes.","t":"該地區以其豐富的陽光而聞名，這使得它成為種植高品質釀酒葡萄絕對完美的地方。"},{"w":"resourceful","p":"adj.","d":"Having the ability to find quick and clever ways to overcome difficulties.","c":"足智多謀的","s":"The resourceful survivor managed to build a safe shelter out of broken tree branches and large green leaves in the jungle.","t":"這位足智多謀的倖存者設法在叢林裡用斷裂的樹枝和巨大的綠葉建了一個安全的庇護所。"},{"w":"extreme","p":"adj.","d":"Reaching a high or the highest degree; very great.","c":"極端的","s":"People who participate in extreme sports must be fully aware of the serious physical risks before they start their dangerous activities.","t":"參與極端的運動的人在開始他們危險的活動之前，必須充分了解嚴重的身體風險。"},{"w":"broad","p":"adj.","d":"Having an ample distance from side to side; wide.","c":"寬闊的；廣泛的","s":"The experienced politician gave a broad overview of his new economic plan, touching on taxes, healthcare, and educational reforms.","t":"這位經驗豐富的政治人物對他的新經濟計畫做了一個廣泛的概述，涉及稅收、醫療和教育改革。"},{"w":"steep","p":"v.","d":"To soak food or tea in water or other liquid to extract its flavor.","c":"浸泡","s":"Climbing up the extremely steep hill completely tired us out, but the breathtaking view at the top was entirely worth the effort.","t":"爬上極度陡峭的山丘讓我們完全累壞了，但山頂上令人驚嘆的景色完全值得這番努力。"},{"w":"awe-inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"Arousing awe through being impressive or magnificent.","c":"令人驚嘆的；令人敬畏的","s":"The view from the top of the snow-covered mountain was so awe-inspiring that we stood there in complete silence for several minutes.","t":"從白雪覆蓋的山頂看下去的景色是如此令人驚嘆的，以至於我們完全安靜地在那裡站了好幾分鐘。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely impressive or daunting; inspiring great admiration.","c":"令人驚嘆的；極好的","s":"The outdoor rock concert last night was absolutely awesome, featuring incredible special effects and breathtaking performances by all the famous musicians.","t":"昨晚的戶外搖滾演唱會絕對是極好的，特色是令人難以置信的特效以及所有著名音樂家激動人心的表演。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"In, relating to, or characteristic of the countryside rather than the town.","c":"鄉村的","s":"The quiet rural area did not have many big grocery stores, but the air was perfectly clean and the local people were remarkably friendly.","t":"這個安靜的鄉村的地區沒有許多大型雜貨店，但空氣非常乾淨，當地人也異常地友善。"},{"w":"cosmopolitan","p":"adj.","d":"Containing people from many different countries, cultures, and diverse backgrounds.","c":"世界主義的；國際化的","s":"Taipei is a vibrant, cosmopolitan city where modern technology frameworks seamlessly blend with various traditional cultures.","t":"台北是一個充滿活力的國際化城市，在這裡現代科技架構與各種傳統文化完美融合。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"In, relating to, or characteristic of a town or city.","c":"城市的","s":"The rapid growth of the urban population has forced the city government to eagerly build more high-rise apartment buildings.","t":"城市的人口快速成長，迫使市政府急切地建造更多高層公寓和高效率的公共交通系統。"},{"w":"civilized","p":"adj.","d":"Polite and well-mannered; culturally, socially, and technologically advanced.","c":"文明的；有教養的","s":"Instead of yelling angrily at each other, the two colleagues decided to sit down and have a perfectly civilized discussion about their fundamental disagreement.","t":"這兩位同事決定不向對方生氣地大吼大叫，而是坐下來對他們根本的分歧進行一場完全有教養的討論。"},{"w":"isolated","p":"adj.","d":"Far away from other places, buildings, or people; remote.","c":"孤立的；偏僻的","s":"Because Vince didn't understand the local language at all, he often felt terribly isolated and depressed when he first moved to the foreign country.","t":"因為文斯完全不懂當地語言，當他剛搬到這個外國國家時，他經常感到非常孤立的且沮喪。"},{"w":"alienated","p":"adj.","d":"Experiencing strong feelings of isolation, social detachment, or exclusion from others.","c":"感到疏離的；孤立的","s":"The tech intern felt completely alienated during his first week because the team was occupied with a critical database crisis.","t":"這位科技實習生在第一週感到完全被孤立，因為團隊正忙於一場關鍵的資料庫危機。"},{"w":"heavenly","p":"adj.","d":"Of heaven, divine; very pleasing, wonderful.","c":"天堂般的；美好的","s":"Spending two relaxing weeks in a luxurious oceanfront resort in Tahiti sounds absolutely heavenly, especially after surviving such a stressful year at work.","t":"在大溪地的豪華海濱度假村度過兩個輕鬆的星期聽起來絕對是天堂般的，尤其是在熬過了工作壓力如此大且疲憊的一年之後。"},{"w":"extremely","p":"adv.","d":"To a very great degree; very.","c":"極端地；非常","s":"Although the highly anticipated science fiction movie was extremely long, it was still incredibly fun to watch with my friends.","t":"儘管這部備受期待的科幻電影非常長，但和我的朋友們一起看仍然覺得難以置信地有趣。"},{"w":"extraordinarily","p":"adv.","d":"In a very unusual or remarkable way.","c":"異常地；非凡地","s":"The young gymnast performed an extraordinarily difficult routine that impressed all the strict judges and won her the gold medal.","t":"這位年輕的體操運動員表演了一套異常地困難的動作，讓所有嚴格的裁判印象深刻並為她贏得了金牌。"},{"w":"severely","p":"adv.","d":"To an undesirably great or intense degree.","c":"嚴重地；嚴厲地","s":"The old wooden bridge was severely damaged by the powerful storm, and it will take several months to fully repair it.","t":"這座古老的木橋被強烈的風暴嚴重地損壞，這將需要好幾個月才能完全修復它。"},{"w":"inland","p":"adv.","d":"Into or towards the interior of a country.","c":"往內陸地","s":"After spending a relaxing week at the coast, the tour traveled inland to explore the magnificent and remote mountain ranges.","t":"在海邊度過輕鬆的一週後，旅行團往內陸地行駛去探索壯麗且偏遠的山脈。"},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"The angular distance of a place north or south of the earth's equator.","c":"緯度","s":"Paris and Vancouver share the exact same latitude, which partly explains why they might have some similar seasonal weather patterns.","t":"巴黎和溫哥華擁有完全相同的緯度，這部分解釋了為什麼它們的季節性天氣模式有些相似。"},{"w":"longitude","p":"n.","d":"The angular distance of a place east or west of the meridian at Greenwich.","c":"經度","s":"In geography class, the teacher explained how to use both latitude and longitude to find a specific location on a map.","t":"在地理課上，老師解釋了如何使用緯度和經度來在地圖上找到特定位置。"},{"w":"altitude","p":"n.","d":"The height of an object or point in relation to sea level or ground level.","c":"海拔；高度","s":"The mountain climbers struggled to breathe easily because the altitude was extremely high and the oxygen was incredibly thin.","t":"登山者呼吸困難，因為海拔極高且氧氣極其稀薄。"},{"w":"aptitude","p":"n.","d":"A natural ability to do something.","c":"天資；才能","s":"Even as a young child, Mozart showed an extraordinary aptitude for music and could play the piano perfectly without lessons.","t":"即使在小時候，莫札特就展現了非凡的音樂天資，不用上課就能完美地彈奏鋼琴。"},{"w":"attitude","p":"n.","d":"A settled way of thinking or feeling about someone or something.","c":"態度","s":"If you want to succeed in this difficult project, you must maintain a positive attitude and never give up easily.","t":"如果你想在這個艱難的專案中取得成功，你必須保持積極的態度並且永不輕易放棄。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"The quality of being thankful; readiness to show appreciation.","c":"感激","s":"The rescued hikers expressed their deep gratitude to the brave emergency workers who had risked their lives to save them.","t":"獲救的登山客對冒著生命危險拯救他們的勇敢急救人員表達了深深的感激。"},{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"A very large quantity of something.","c":"豐富；充足","s":"Because of the unusually good weather this year, the local farmers were able to produce an abundance of fresh vegetables.","t":"由於今年異常良好的天氣，當地農民得以生產出豐富的新鮮蔬菜。"},{"w":"resource","p":"n.","d":"A stock or supply of money, materials, staff, and other assets.","c":"資源","s":"The CEO strongly believes that the intelligent and hardworking employees in the company are undoubtedly its most valuable resource.","t":"執行長堅信公司裡聰明且努力工作的員工無疑是其最寶貴的資源。"},{"w":"folklore","p":"n.","d":"The traditional beliefs, customs, and stories of a community passed through generations.","c":"民間傳說","s":"Many of the fascinating stories collected in this thick historical book come directly from the country's rich and ancient folklore.","t":"收集在這本厚重歷史書中的許多迷人故事直接來自該國豐富且古老的民間傳說。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"The traditional stories and customs specific to a particular area.","c":"傳奇故事","s":"According to the legend passed down for generations, a mysterious ghost wanders the halls of the abandoned castle on the night of a full moon.","t":"根據流傳世代的傳奇故事，在滿月之夜，一個神祕的鬼魂會在廢棄城堡的走廊上遊蕩。"},{"w":"boarding pass","p":"n.","d":"An official document given to a passenger that authorizes them to enter an aircraft or ship.","c":"登機證；船票","s":"The corporate representative accidentally dropped her digital boarding pass while looking for her automated platform credentials.","t":"這位公司代表在尋找她的自動化平台憑證時，不小心弄丟了她的數位登機證。"},{"w":"boarding school","p":"n.","d":"A private school where pupils receive formal education while living on campus.","c":"寄宿學校","s":"The wealthy businessman decided to send his adolescent son to a prestigious boarding school in England.","t":"這位富有的商人決定將他正值青少年的兒子送到英國一所聲譽卓著的寄宿學校。"},{"w":"ferry","p":"n.","d":"A boat or ship for conveying passengers and goods.","c":"渡輪","s":"Passenger ferries usually run every 15 minutes to take people across the busy harbor during the peak summer tourist season.","t":"客運渡輪通常在夏季旅遊旺季每15分鐘開一次，載著人們穿過繁忙的港口。"},{"w":"steep slope","p":"n.","d":"A hillside with a large angle.","c":"陡坡","s":"The steep slope near the edge of the mountain is so challenging that inexperienced hikers are strongly advised not to walk there.","t":"靠近山邊的陡坡是這麼陡峭以至於強烈建議缺乏經驗的登山客不要走在那裡。"},{"w":"gentle slope","p":"n.","d":"A piece of ground that inclines or rises gradually rather than steeply.","c":"緩坡","s":"The active tourists enjoyed walking along the gentle slope of the hill to observe rare local plants.","t":"活潑的遊客們喜歡沿著小山丘的緩坡散步，以觀察罕見的當地植物。"},{"w":"valley","p":"n.","d":"A low area of land situated between mountains or hills, typically with a river flowing through.","c":"山谷","s":"The historical community built an automated agricultural drone framework to monitor fields inside the deep valley.","t":"這個歷史悠久的社區建立了一個自動化農業無人機架構，以監控深谷內的農田。"},{"w":"plain","p":"n.","d":"A large, extensive area of flat land with very few trees.","c":"平原","s":"Thousands of sheep bred by the wealthy ranch owner are currently grazing across the open plain.","t":"這位富有農場主人所飼養的數千隻綿羊，目前正在開闊的平原上吃草。"},{"w":"basin","p":"n.","d":"A large bowl-shaped depression in the earth's surface surrounded by higher land.","c":"盆地","s":"The engineering team deployed high-tech weather sensors throughout the geographic basin to track heavy rainfall routines.","t":"工程團隊在整個地理盆地部署了高科技天氣感測器，以追蹤豪雨的常規習性。"},{"w":"tundra","p":"n.","d":"A vast, flat, and treeless Arctic region where the subsoil is permanently frozen.","c":"苔原；凍原","s":"The scientific research staff had to adapt to the extremely freezing climate of the northern tundra.","t":"科學研究人員必須適應北部苔原極度寒冷的氣候。"},{"w":"cliff","p":"n.","d":"A steep rock face, especially at the edge of the sea.","c":"懸崖","s":"We cautiously stood on the edge of the mountain cliff and looked down at the dark blue sea violently crashing against the sharp rocks.","t":"我們小心翼翼地站在山懸崖的邊緣，看著深藍色的海水猛烈地拍打著尖銳的岩石。"},{"w":"cliffhanger","p":"n.","d":"A dramatic and exciting ending to an episode of a serial, leaving the audience in suspense.","c":"扣人心弦的結局；懸念","s":"The exciting television show ended on a massive cliffhanger, leaving millions of loyal fans eagerly waiting for the next season to air.","t":"這部刺激的電視節目以一個巨大的扣人心弦的結局收尾，讓數百萬忠實粉絲熱切期待下一季的播出。"},{"w":"glacier","p":"n.","d":"A slowly moving mass or river of ice formed by the accumulation and compaction of snow on mountains.","c":"冰川","s":"Thousands of years ago, the northern parts of Canada were entirely covered by massive glaciers that slowly shaped the geographical landscape.","t":"數千年前，加拿大北部完全被巨大的冰川覆蓋，這些冰川隨著時間緩慢地塑造了地理景觀。"},{"w":"awe","p":"n.","d":"A feeling of reverential respect mixed with fear or wonder.","c":"敬畏","s":"The young students stared in complete awe at the massive dinosaur skeleton prominently displayed in the center of the natural history museum.","t":"年輕的學生滿懷完全的敬畏凝視著自然史博物館中央醒目展示的巨大恐龍骨架。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"An outlying district of a city, especially a residential one.","c":"郊區","s":"Many families choose to move from the noisy city center to a peaceful suburb for additional living space.","t":"許多家庭選擇從嘈雜的市中心搬到寧靜的郊區，以獲得額外的居住空間。"},{"w":"civilization","p":"n.","d":"The stage of human social and cultural development considered most advanced.","c":"文明","s":"Jacob eagerly read a fascinating history book about the ancient Egyptian civilization and how they managed to build the giant pyramids so long ago.","t":"雅各熱切地讀了一本引人入勝的歷史書，關於古埃及文明以及他們是如何奇蹟般地建造巨大金字塔的。"},{"w":"civilian","p":"n.","d":"A person not in the armed services or the police force.","c":"平民","s":"The brave soldiers constantly risked their own lives to protect innocent civilians from the dangerous crossfire during the exceptionally fierce battle.","t":"在這座廢墟城市異常激烈的戰鬥中，勇敢的士兵不斷冒著生命危險保護無辜的平民免受危險的交火波及。"},{"w":"isolation","p":"n.","d":"The process or fact of isolating or being isolated.","c":"隔離；孤立無援","s":"After living in complete isolation in a remote wooden cabin for six months, the writer seriously struggled to interact with people when he returned.","t":"在偏遠的木屋裡完全隔離生活了六個月後，這位作家回到城市時，嚴重地難以與人們互動。"},{"w":"social distancing","p":"n.","d":"The practice of maintaining a certain physical space between individuals to prevent transmitting illness.","c":"社交距離","s":"Implementing proper social distancing in public transport vehicles successfully minimized the risk of seasonal chronic infections.","t":"在大眾運輸工具中保持適當的社交距離，成功降低了季節性慢性感染的風險。"},{"w":"heaven","p":"n.","d":"A place regarded as the abode of God; a place or state of supreme bliss.","c":"天堂","s":"The deeply religious woman firmly believed that she would eventually be joyfully reunited with all her deceased loved ones in heaven after her passing.","t":"這位非常虔誠的婦女堅信，她去世後最終將在天堂與所有已故的摯愛歡樂地重逢。"},{"w":"broaden","p":"v.","d":"To become larger; to expand to encompass more people, ideas, or things.","c":"擴展；拓寬","s":"The successful international company quickly broadened its search to find highly qualified software engineers from all around the world.","t":"這家成功的跨國公司迅速擴展了其搜尋範圍，以從世界各地尋找高度合格的軟體工程師。"},{"w":"board","p":"v.","d":"To officially get on or enter a ship, aircraft, train, or other public vehicle.","c":"登上（大眾運輸工具）","s":"Passengers are requested to board the international flight immediately after completing the security check.","t":"旅客們被要求在完成安全檢查後，立刻登上這班國際航班。"},{"w":"steep","p":"v.","d":"To soak food or tea in water or other liquid to extract its flavor.","c":"浸泡","s":"You must steep your special herbal tea well for at least five minutes before drinking it to get the best possible flavor.","t":"你必須將你的特製花草茶好好浸泡至少五分鐘再喝，才能獲得最佳的風味。"},{"w":"civilize","p":"v.","d":"To bring a place or people to a stage of social, cultural, and moral development considered more advanced.","c":"使文明；教化","s":"The ambitious empire foolishly believed it was its grand destiny to completely conquer and civilize the supposedly wild tribes living across the vast ocean.","t":"這個雄心勃勃的帝國愚蠢地相信，徹底征服並教化據稱生活在浩瀚海洋彼岸的野蠻部落是其偉大的命運。"},{"w":"isolate","p":"v.","d":"To remain alone or apart from others; to keep separate.","c":"隔離；孤立","s":"The doctors immediately commanded that people who've shown signs of having the highly infectious virus must be successfully isolated in a special hospital room.","t":"醫生立刻下令，出現感染高度傳染性病毒的令人擔憂跡象的人，必須成功地在特殊的醫院病房被隔離。"},{"w":"alienate","p":"v.","d":"To cause someone to feel isolated, estranged, or excluded from a specific group or community.","c":"使疏離；使孤立；排斥","s":"The manager's arrogant decision to flaunt corporate revenue served to alienate the hardworking engineering staff.","t":"經理張揚公司營收的傲慢決定，反而使辛勤工作的工程人員感到被疏離。"},{"w":"be grateful for","p":"phr.","d":"To be thankful for something.","c":"感謝的","s":"We write the card for our parents to show that we are grateful for their devotion to raising kids.","t":"我們寫卡片感謝父母養育我們。"},{"w":"an abundance of","p":"phr.","d":"A very large quantity of something.","c":"大量的","s":"The luxurious five-star hotel buffet offered an abundance of delicious seafood, including fresh crabs, oysters, and perfectly grilled salmon.","t":"豪華的五星級飯店自助餐提供了大量的美味海鮮，包含新鮮螃蟹、生蠔和完美燒烤的鮭魚。"},{"w":"human resources","p":"phr.","d":"The personnel of a business or organization.","c":"人力資源","s":"If you have any serious complaints about your current salary or working conditions, you should contact the human resources department immediately.","t":"如果你對目前的薪水或工作條件有任何嚴重的抱怨，你應該立刻聯絡人力資源部門。"},{"w":"natural resources","p":"phr.","d":"Materials or substances such as minerals, forests, water, and fertile land that occur in nature.","c":"自然資源","s":"The country is heavily reliant on exporting its natural resources, such as coal and oil, to sustain its growing economy.","t":"該國嚴重依賴出口其自然資源（如煤炭和石油）來維持其不斷增長的經濟。"},{"w":"renewable energy resources","p":"phr.","d":"Sources of energy that are not depleted by use, such as water, wind, or solar power.","c":"再生能源資源","s":"To combat the severe effects of climate change, the government must invest heavily in renewable energy resources instead of burning fossil fuels.","t":"為了對抗氣候變遷的嚴重影響，政府必須大量投資於再生能源資源，而不是燃燒化石燃料。"},{"w":"go to extremes","p":"phr.","d":"To do something much more than is usual or reasonable.","c":"走極端","s":"You don't need to go to extremes to lose weight; just eat a balanced diet and exercise regularly every week.","t":"你不需要走極端來減肥；只要每週吃均衡的飲食並規律地運動即可。"},{"w":"budget","p":"n./v.","d":"An estimate of income and expenditure; to allow or provide a particular amount of money.","c":"預算；編列預算","s":"Fiona plans to budget her money very carefully this year so she can finally take a long trip through Europe next summer.","t":"費歐娜計畫今年非常謹慎地為她的錢編列預算，這樣她明年夏天終於能去歐洲進行一趟長途旅行。"},{"w":"on a tight budget","p":"phr.","d":"Having a limited amount of money to spend.","c":"預算拮据","s":"Because Henry is trying to save up enough money to buy his first house, he is currently living on a tight budget.","t":"因為亨利正試圖存夠錢買他的第一棟房子，他目前過著預算拮据的生活。"},{"w":"stay on budget","p":"phr.","d":"To not spend more money than had been planned for.","c":"保持在預算內","s":"To stay on budget this month, we are going to have to significantly cut down on the amount of money we spend on expensive dinners.","t":"為了這個月保持在預算內，我們將不得不大幅削減我們在昂貴晚餐上花費的金額。"},{"w":"under budget","p":"phr.","d":"Costing less than the amount of money that was estimated or planned.","c":"低於預算","s":"Mr. Edwards happily thanked his dedicated team for successfully finishing the complicated construction project completely under budget.","t":"愛德華先生快樂地感謝他專注的團隊成功地完全低於預算完成了複雜的建設專案。"},{"w":"out of one's budget","p":"phr.","d":"Costing more money than someone can afford to spend.","c":"超出某人的預算","s":"That beautiful designer dress is absolutely stunning, but unfortunately, it is a little out of my budget right now.","t":"那件美麗的設計師洋裝絕對令人驚豔，但不幸的是，它現在有點超出我的預算。"},{"w":"folk tale","p":"phr.","d":"A story originating in popular culture, typically passed on by word of mouth.","c":"民間故事","s":"The grandmother sat by the warm fire and told a fascinating folk tale about a clever fox and a foolish bear.","t":"祖母坐在溫暖的爐火旁，講了一個關於聰明狐狸和愚蠢熊的迷人民間故事。"},{"w":"folk music","p":"phr.","d":"Music that originates in traditional popular culture or that is written in such a style.","c":"民俗音樂","s":"We spent the entire evening at the local pub listening to lively folk music played on acoustic guitars and violins.","t":"我們整個晚上都在當地的酒館裡聽著用原聲吉他和小提琴演奏的輕快民俗音樂。"},{"w":"broaden one's horizons","p":"phr.","d":"To expand one's range of interests, activities, and knowledge.","c":"拓展某人的視野","s":"Working in a foreign country for a year will definitely give you an incredible chance to broaden your horizons in the international business world.","t":"在外國工作一年絕對會給你一個難以置信的機會，在國際商業世界中拓展你的視野。"},{"w":"broaden one's knowledge","p":"phr.","d":"To increase what one knows about a subject.","c":"增廣見聞；擴充知識","s":"Jill frequently read books and watched historical documentaries to broaden her knowledge of ancient Chinese culture while she was in college.","t":"潔兒在大學期間經常閱讀書籍和觀看歷史紀錄片，以擴充她對中國古代文化的知識。"},{"w":"aboard","p":"adv./prep.","d":"On or into a ship, aircraft, train, or other transport vehicle.","c":"在（車、船、飛機）上","s":"The experienced captain welcomed all the excited tourists aboard the luxury cruise ship this morning.","t":"這位經驗豐富的船長今天上午歡迎所有興奮的遊客登上這艘豪華郵輪。"},{"w":"go sightseeing","p":"phr.","d":"To visit interesting places, especially as a tourist.","c":"去觀光","s":"I am so incredibly excited about our trip, and I absolutely can't wait to go sightseeing once we arrive in London.","t":"我對我們的旅行感到極度興奮，一旦我們抵達倫敦，我絕對等不及要去觀光了。"},{"w":"sightseeing tour","p":"phr.","d":"An organized journey to look at the sights of a place.","c":"觀光行程","s":"We booked a comprehensive sightseeing tour that took us to all the major monuments and historical museums in the capital city.","t":"我們預訂了一個全面的觀光行程，帶我們參觀了首都所有主要的紀念碑和歷史博物館。"},{"w":"take in","p":"phr. v.","d":"To fully understand or absorb something heard or seen; to deceive.","c":"吸收；領會；欺騙","s":"The university professor's lecture was so complex and detailed that Kevin could not simply take it all in during the one-hour class.","t":"大學教授的演講是如此複雜和詳細，以至於凱文無法在短短一小時的課堂上將其全部吸收。"},{"w":"take in the view","p":"phr.","d":"To spend time looking at a beautiful landscape.","c":"欣賞風景","s":"We slowly drove our rented car along the beautiful coast and stopped frequently to take in the view of the sparkling ocean.","t":"我們慢慢地沿著美麗的海岸開著我們租來的車，並經常停下來欣賞波光粼粼海洋的風景。"},{"w":"ferry terminal","p":"phr.","d":"The building and area where ferries arrive and depart.","c":"渡輪站","s":"We arrived at the newly built ferry terminal almost an hour early to ensure we wouldn't miss our scheduled boat to the island.","t":"我們提早了將近一個小時抵達新建的渡輪站，以確保我們不會錯過預定前往島嶼的船。"},{"w":"inland city","p":"phr.","d":"A city located far from the sea or ocean.","c":"內陸城市","s":"Moving from a breezy coastal town to a busy, hot inland city was a massive adjustment for the fisherman who loved the ocean.","t":"從微風徐徐的沿海城鎮搬到繁忙炎熱的內陸城市，對那位熱愛海洋的漁夫來說是個巨大的適應過程。"},{"w":"travel inland","p":"phr.","d":"To journey away from the coast toward the center of a country.","c":"往內陸旅行","s":"The courageous explorers decided to travel inland to discover the ancient ruins hidden deep within the dense, tropical jungle.","t":"勇敢的探險家決定往內陸旅行，以發現在茂密熱帶叢林深處隱藏的古老遺跡。"},{"w":"be steeped in","p":"phr.","d":"To have a lot of a particular quality or be heavily influenced by something.","c":"充滿著...；沉浸於...","s":"The ancient stone ruins that were recently found deep in the jungle are entirely steeped in mystery and historical legends.","t":"最近在叢林深處發現的古老石頭遺跡完全充滿著神秘與歷史傳說。"},{"w":"steep price","p":"phr.","d":"An unreasonably high cost.","c":"高昂的價格","s":"The famous marketing company always charges a very steep price for its professional consulting services and highly successful advertising campaigns.","t":"這家著名的行銷公司總是為其專業的諮詢服務和高度成功的廣告活動收取非常高昂的價格。"},{"w":"steep cliff","p":"phr.","d":"A cliff with a very sharp drop.","c":"陡峭的懸崖","s":"The beautiful white lighthouse was built dangerously close to a steep cliff to warn passing cargo ships about the hidden rocks below.","t":"美麗的白色燈塔建在危險地靠近陡峭的懸崖的地方，以警告路過的貨輪下方有暗礁。"},{"w":"edge of a cliff","p":"phr.","d":"The very brink or border of a steep rock face.","c":"懸崖邊緣","s":"The frightened tourist mistakenly walked too close to the edge of a cliff and almost dropped his expensive digital camera into the stormy ocean.","t":"受驚的遊客不小心走得太靠近懸崖邊緣，差點把昂貴的數位相機掉進暴風雨的海裡。"},{"w":"in awe of","p":"phr.","d":"Having a great amount of respect or admiration for someone or something.","c":"對...感到敬畏/驚嘆","s":"Even after working together for five years, I am still consistently in awe of her brilliant ability to solve complex mathematical problems.","t":"即使一起工作了五年，我仍然一直對她解決複雜數學問題的卓越能力感到驚嘆。"},{"w":"rural development","p":"phr.","d":"The process of improving the quality of life and economic well-being of people living in rural areas.","c":"鄉村發展","s":"The national government has proudly allocated billions of dollars specifically for rural development to provide significantly better schools and hospitals for struggling farmers.","t":"國家政府已自豪地撥款數十億美元專門用於鄉村發展，為苦苦掙扎的農民提供好很多的學校和醫院。"},{"w":"rural landscape","p":"phr.","d":"The visible features of an area of countryside.","c":"鄉村風景","s":"The famous painter spent several years perfectly capturing the pure beauty of the traditional English rural landscape with its green rolling hills and small farms.","t":"這位著名的畫家花了數年時間完美捕捉傳統英國鄉村風景的純粹之美，那裡有著綠意盎然的連綿山丘和小型農場。"},{"w":"ancient civilization","p":"phr.","d":"The earliest stage of human social development.","c":"古文明","s":"Exploring the majestic ruins of the Mayan ancient civilization hidden deep in the humid rainforest was an absolutely unforgettable experience for the young archaeology students.","t":"對年輕的考古學學生來說，探索隱藏在潮濕雨林深處雄偉的馬雅古文明遺跡是一次絕對難忘的經歷。"},{"w":"isolated incident","p":"phr.","d":"An event that is not part of a wider pattern or trend.","c":"偶發事件","s":"The police chief confidently assured the worried public that the recent bank robbery was merely an isolated incident and not the frightening beginning of a crime wave.","t":"警察局長自信地向擔憂的民眾保證，最近的銀行搶劫案只是一起偶發事件，而不是犯罪浪潮的可怕開端。"},{"w":"quarantine","p":"n./v.","d":"A period or state of isolation imposed to prevent the spread of disease.","c":"隔離；檢疫","s":"Medical authorities placed the infected tourists in strict quarantine to avoid a widespread outbreak within the suburb.","t":"醫療當局將受感染的遊客進行嚴格隔離，以避免在郊區內爆發大規模疫情。"},{"w":"heavenly body","p":"phr.","d":"A planet, star, or other celestial body.","c":"天體","s":"Through the incredibly powerful telescope, the eager astronomy students observed the glowing heavenly body moving slowly and gracefully across the dark, star-filled night sky.","t":"透過極高倍數的望遠鏡，熱切的天文學學生觀察到發光的天體緩慢且優雅地劃過黑暗、繁星點點的夜空。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"tribal – be subject to change","cards":[{"w":"tribal","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to a tribe or tribes.","c":"部落的","s":"The experienced guide was dressed in traditional tribal clothing as he led the tourists through the dense jungle.","t":"經驗豐富的嚮導穿著傳統的部落的服裝，帶領遊客穿過茂密的叢林。"},{"w":"aboriginal","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the people or organisms that have been in a region from the earliest time.","c":"土著的；原住民的","s":"The cultural museum features an extensive collection of aboriginal arts that showcase the traditional heritage of the island's early inhabitants.","t":"這間文化博物館展示了大量的原住民藝術收藏，展現了這座島嶼早期居民的傳統遺產。"},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adj.","d":"Originating or occurring naturally in a particular place; native to a specific region.","c":"土生土長的；當地的","s":"The scientific research team spent months analyzing how the indigenous organisms adapt to the harsh climate of the high mountains.","t":"科學研究團隊花了數個月的時間，分析當地的土生土長生物如何適應高山的惡劣氣候。"},{"w":"native","p":"adj.","d":"Associated with the place of a person's birth, or naturally belonging to a particular region.","c":"本土的；原生的","s":"The experienced botanist spent several years cataloging all the native tree species growing in the remote mountain valley.","t":"這位經驗豐富的植物學家花了幾年時間，將生長在偏遠山谷中的所有本土樹種編製成冊。"},{"w":"domestic","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the running of a home, or relating to the internal affairs of a country.","c":"國內的；家庭的","s":"The newly elected president promised to focus more on critical domestic issues rather than complex international conflicts.","t":"新當選的總統承諾將更多精力集中在關鍵的國內問題上，而不是複雜的國際衝突。"},{"w":"violent","p":"adj.","d":"Using or involving physical force intended to hurt or damage.","c":"暴力的","s":"Tina strictly wouldn't let her young children play the violent video game because she felt it was completely inappropriate.","t":"蒂娜嚴格不讓她年幼的孩子玩那款暴力的電玩遊戲，因為她覺得那完全不合適。"},{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"Designed for people to live in.","c":"住宅的","s":"We decided to move away from the noisy city center and find a quiet house in a peaceful residential neighborhood.","t":"我們決定搬離嘈雜的市中心，在一個寧靜的住宅的社區找一棟安靜的房子。"},{"w":"invasive","p":"adj.","d":"Tending to spread prolifically and undesirably.","c":"侵入性的","s":"Environmentalists are working hard to remove the highly invasive plant species that is currently destroying the local forest ecosystem.","t":"環保人士正努力移除目前正在破壞當地森林生態系統的高度侵入性的植物物種。"},{"w":"expansive","p":"adj.","d":"Covering a wide area in terms of space or scope.","c":"廣闊的；開闊的","s":"From the top of the towering skyscraper, you can easily see the incredibly expansive city skyline stretching out for miles.","t":"從高聳的摩天大樓頂端，你可以輕鬆地看到極其廣闊的城市天際線綿延數英里。"},{"w":"vast","p":"adj.","d":"Of very great extent or quantity; immense.","c":"廣大的；巨大的","s":"The exciting rock concert took place in a vast underground hall that could easily hold more than 10,000 screaming people.","t":"這場刺激的搖滾演唱會是在一個可以輕鬆容納超過10,000名尖叫人群的廣大的地下大廳舉行的。"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely large or great, especially in scale or degree.","c":"極大的","s":"After weeks of studying night and day, the student felt an immense sense of relief when he finally passed the difficult exam.","t":"經過幾週日以繼夜的學習，當這名學生終於通過了困難的考試時，他感到了一種極大的如釋重負的感覺。"},{"w":"crushed","p":"adj.","d":"Greatly disappointed or deeply saddened.","c":"極度傷心的","s":"The excited children were completely crushed when they sadly found out their highly anticipated weekend trip to Disneyland was suddenly cancelled.","t":"當興奮的孩子們悲傷地發現他們備受期待的週末迪士尼樂園之旅突然被取消時，他們感到完全極度傷心的。"},{"w":"submissive","p":"adj.","d":"Ready to conform to the authority or will of others.","c":"順從的","s":"The cruel dictator always expected his terrified citizens to be completely submissive and never question any of his harsh rules.","t":"殘酷的獨裁者總是期望他受驚的公民是完全順從的，並且從不質疑他的任何嚴苛規定。"},{"w":"enduring","p":"adj.","d":"Continuing or long-lasting.","c":"持久的","s":"The brilliant classic novel has an enduring appeal that mysteriously continues to attract thousands of new young readers every single year.","t":"這部才華洋溢的經典小說具有一種持久的吸引力，神祕地每年持續吸引數千名新的年輕讀者。"},{"w":"cosmopolitan","p":"adj.","d":"Containing people, cultures, and diverse backgrounds from many different countries.","c":"世界主義的；國際化的","s":"Taipei is a vibrant, cosmopolitan city where modern technology frameworks seamlessly blend with various traditional cultures.","t":"台北是一個充滿活力的國際化城市，在這裡現代科技架構與各種傳統文化完美融合。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to, or characteristic of a city or highly populated town.","c":"城市的；都市的","s":"Rapid urban development often leads to significant environmental challenges, such as heavy traffic and air pollution.","t":"快速的城市發展往往會帶來顯著的環境挑戰，例如嚴重的交通堵塞和空氣污染。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to, or characteristic of the countryside rather than the city.","c":"鄉村的；田園的","s":"The retired teacher decided to buy a peaceful farmhouse in a rural community to enjoy a quiet lifestyle.","t":"這位退休教師決定在一個鄉村社區買下一棟寧靜的農舍，以享受清靜的生活方式。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"Situated far away from the main centers of population; distant and isolated.","c":"偏遠的；偏僻的","s":"The medical humanitarian group traveled to a remote mountain village to provide free healthcare to the poor families.","t":"醫療人道團體前往一個偏遠的山村，為貧困家庭提供免費的醫療保健服務。"},{"w":"violently","p":"adv.","d":"In a forceful, passionate, or destructive manner.","c":"猛烈地；暴力地","s":"The angry protesters reacted violently to the new government policies, throwing rocks and breaking windows in the city center.","t":"憤怒的抗議者對新政府政策做出了猛烈地反應，在市中心扔石頭並打破窗戶。"},{"w":"tribe","p":"n.","d":"A social division in a traditional society consisting of linked families.","c":"部落","s":"The indigenous tribe has lived perfectly in harmony with the surrounding natural environment for several thousands of years.","t":"這個原住民部落幾千年來一直與周圍的自然環境完美和諧地生活著。"},{"w":"violence","p":"n.","d":"Behavior involving physical force intended to hurt or kill.","c":"暴力","s":"The police chief promised to significantly reduce the level of street violence that has been frightening the local community.","t":"警察局長承諾將顯著降低一直讓當地社區感到害怕的街頭暴力程度。"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"A person's home; the place where someone lives.","c":"住所","s":"After making a massive fortune in the technology industry, the CEO purchased a luxurious residence near the sunny beach.","t":"在科技產業賺了一大筆錢後，這位執行長在陽光明媚的海灘附近買了一棟豪華的住所。"},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"A person who lives somewhere permanently.","c":"居民","s":"Every single resident of the apartment building was forced to evacuate quickly when the loud fire alarm suddenly rang.","t":"當大聲的火災警報突然響起時，這棟公寓的每一位居民都被迫迅速撤離。"},{"w":"invader","p":"n.","d":"A person or group that invades a country or region.","c":"入侵者","s":"The brave and loyal soldiers fought tirelessly for months to protect their beloved homeland from the ruthless foreign invader.","t":"勇敢且忠誠的士兵不知疲倦地戰鬥了幾個月，以保護他們深愛的家園免受無情的外國入侵者的侵害。"},{"w":"invasion","p":"n.","d":"An instance of invading a country with an armed force.","c":"侵略；入侵","s":"The sudden and unexpected military invasion caused thousands of terrified civilians to flee across the border to seek safety.","t":"突然且出乎意料的軍事侵略導致數千名驚恐的平民逃越國境尋求安全。"},{"w":"conqueror","p":"n.","d":"A person who conquers a place or people.","c":"征服者","s":"The ambitious historical conqueror traveled across the continent, defeating massive armies and claiming all the valuable land for himself.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的歷史征服者橫跨大陸，擊敗了龐大的軍隊並將所有寶貴的土地據為己有。"},{"w":"clan","p":"n.","d":"A group of close-knit and interrelated families.","c":"氏族；家族","s":"The people living peacefully in this remote mountain village are actually all from the exact same ancient family clan.","t":"和平地生活在這個偏遠山村的人們，實際上都是來自完全相同的一個古老家族氏族。"},{"w":"warrior","p":"n.","d":"A brave or experienced soldier or fighter.","c":"戰士","s":"The highly trained warrior bravely fought a long and bloody battle against their dangerous enemy to protect the castle.","t":"訓練有素的戰士勇敢地與危險的敵人進行了一場漫長且血腥的戰鬥以保護城堡。"},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"The action of becoming larger or more extensive.","c":"擴張；擴展","s":"The rapid expansion of the international technology company naturally led to the immediate hiring of many new software employees.","t":"這家國際科技公司的快速擴張自然導致了立刻僱用許多新的軟體員工。"},{"w":"empire","p":"n.","d":"An extensive group of states or countries under a single supreme authority.","c":"帝國","s":"At the peak of its historical height, the British empire impressively included more than 20 percent of the world's total land area.","t":"在其歷史的最高峰時期，大英帝國令人印象深刻地包含了世界上超過百分之二十的總土地面積。"},{"w":"emperor","p":"n.","d":"A sovereign ruler of great power and rank.","c":"皇帝","s":"The powerful Roman emperor completely controlled the vast army and could single-handedly make laws that everyone had to follow blindly.","t":"強大的羅馬皇帝完全控制著龐大的軍隊，並且可以單槍匹馬地制定每個人都必須盲目遵守的法律。"},{"w":"crush","p":"n./v.","d":"A brief but intense infatuation; a dense crowd; or to compress forcefully.","c":"迷戀；擁擠的人群；壓碎","s":"The dangerous crush of people at the train station is naturally at its absolute worst during the busy morning rush hour.","t":"火車站危險的擁擠人群在繁忙的早晨尖峰時段自然處於絕對最糟糕的狀態。"},{"w":"opposition","p":"n.","d":"Resistance or dissent, expressed in action or argument.","c":"反對","s":"Despite facing fierce opposition from the conservative politicians, the progressive new healthcare law was finally passed successfully last night.","t":"儘管面臨保守派政治人物激烈的反對，這項進步的新醫療保健法案昨晚終於成功通過了。"},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"The fact or power of enduring an unpleasant process.","c":"忍耐力","s":"Running a grueling marathon in the extreme summer heat requires not only physical strength but also incredible mental endurance.","t":"在極端的夏日酷暑中跑一場艱苦的馬拉松不僅需要體力，還需要令人難以置信的心理忍耐力。"},{"w":"resemblance","p":"n.","d":"The state of resembling or being alike.","c":"相似之處","s":"The strange physical resemblance between the two unrelated men is so incredibly strong that everyone mistakenly thinks they are twin brothers.","t":"這兩個沒有血緣關係的男人之間奇怪的身體相似之處是如此令人難以置信地強烈，以至於每個人都誤以為他們是雙胞胎兄弟。"},{"w":"slave","p":"n.","d":"A person who is the legal property of another.","c":"奴隸","s":"The desperate slave courageously planned a dangerous escape in the middle of the dark night to finally gain his precious freedom.","t":"絕望的奴隸勇敢地在漆黑的午夜計畫了一次危險的逃跑，以最終獲得他寶貴的自由。"},{"w":"slavery","p":"n.","d":"The state or condition of being a slave.","c":"奴隸制度","s":"In the historical United States, the cruel practice of slavery was finally made entirely illegal during the bloody and divisive Civil War.","t":"在歷史上的美國，奴隸制度的殘酷行為最終在血腥且分裂的內戰期間被定為完全非法。"},{"w":"hemisphere","p":"n.","d":"A half of the earth.","c":"半球","s":"If you happen to live comfortably in the southern hemisphere, the freezing winter season surprisingly takes place from June through August.","t":"如果你碰巧舒適地住在南半球，令人驚訝地，寒冷的冬季是發生在六月到八月。"},{"w":"subject","p":"n.","d":"A member of a state other than its ruler; a person chosen to be studied in an experiment.","c":"臣民；受試者","s":"The loyal subject respectfully bowed their heads in complete silence whenever the royal king proudly walked through the grand palace hall.","t":"每當皇家國王自豪地走過宏偉的宮殿大廳時，忠誠的臣民都恭敬地在完全的沉默中低下頭。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"An outlying residential district of a city that offers a quieter lifestyle away from the core center.","c":"郊區","s":"Many families choose to move from the noisy city center to a peaceful suburb for additional living space.","t":"許多家庭選擇從嘈雜的市中心搬到寧靜的郊區，以獲得額外的居住空間。"},{"w":"downtown","p":"n./adv.","d":"The central area or primary commercial heart of a city, typically busy and crowded.","c":"市中心；鬧區","s":"Finding a convenient parking space in the downtown area during the Friday evening rush hour is almost impossible.","t":"在星期五傍晚的尖峰時段，要在市中心區域找到一個方便的停車位幾乎是不可能的。"},{"w":"invasive species","p":"n.","d":"A type of plant or animal introduced to a new environment that causes harm to native wildlife.","c":"外來侵入種；侵入性物種","s":"Environmentalists are working tirelessly to remove the invasive species that is currently destroying the local forest ecosystem.","t":"環保人士正努力移除目前正在破壞當地森林生態系統的外來侵入種。"},{"w":"endangered species","p":"n.","d":"A type of animal or plant seriously at risk of extinction.","c":"瀕危物種","s":"The wildlife organization established a secure sanctuary in the valley to protect the highly endangered species.","t":"野生動物組織在山谷中建立了一個安全的庇護所，以保護這個高度瀕危的物種。"},{"w":"living fossil","p":"n.","d":"An organism that has remained essentially unchanged from earlier geologic times.","c":"活化石","s":"The coelacanth is famously recognized as a living fossil because its physical characteristics have remained unchanged for millions of years.","t":"腔棘魚被廣泛公認為是一種活化石，因為其身體特徵數百萬年來都保持未變。"},{"w":"commercial area","p":"n.","d":"A designated district in a city intended primarily for businesses, retail stores, and offices.","c":"商業區","s":"The city council decided to develop a new commercial area filled with modern office towers and luxury shopping malls.","t":"市議會決定開發一個充滿現代辦公大樓和豪華購物中心的新商業區。"},{"w":"military zone","p":"n.","d":"A strictly protected geographic area controlled by the armed forces where civilian access is limited.","c":"軍事管制區","s":"Because that coastal region is classified as a strict military zone, civilians are completely forbidden from taking any photographs.","t":"因為該沿海地區被歸類為嚴格的軍事管制區，所以完全禁止平民拍攝任何照片。"},{"w":"zip code","p":"n.","d":"A group of letters or numbers used as part of a postal address to assist in sorting mail.","c":"郵遞區號","s":"Please remember to write down the correct zip code on the envelope to ensure your package arrives on time.","t":"請記得在信封上寫下正確的郵遞區號，以確保您的包裹能準時送達。"},{"w":"invade","p":"v.","d":"To enter a place in large numbers, especially with intrusive effect.","c":"入侵","s":"The exciting science fiction movie is about little blue men from Jupiter who ruthlessly invade our beautiful planet.","t":"這部刺激的科幻電影是關於來自木星的小藍人無情地入侵我們美麗星球的故事。"},{"w":"conquer","p":"v.","d":"To overcome and take control of a place by military force.","c":"征服；克服","s":"I desperately wanted to stop running, but I successfully conquered my terrible tiredness and kept going to the finish line.","t":"我極度想要停止跑步，但我成功地克服了我可怕的疲勞並堅持到了終點線。"},{"w":"scatter","p":"v.","d":"To throw in various random directions.","c":"散開；撒","s":"The frightened criminals immediately scattered in completely different directions when the noisy police car suddenly drove up to the house.","t":"當吵雜的警車突然開到房子前時，受驚的罪犯立刻朝著完全不同的方向散開。"},{"w":"expand","p":"v.","d":"To become or make larger or more extensive.","c":"擴大；膨脹","s":"Due to the massive increase in customer demand, the bakery plans to expand its store and add a seating area next year.","t":"由於顧客需求的大幅增加，這家麵包店計畫在明年擴大店面並增加一個座位區。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"To disapprove of and attempt to prevent.","c":"反對","s":"Some angry citizens strongly opposed the chairperson's surprising decision, while others fully agreed that it was the best choice available.","t":"一些憤怒的公民強烈反對主席令人驚訝的決定，而其他人則完全同意這是現有最好的選擇。"},{"w":"submit","p":"v.","d":"To accept or yield to a superior force; to present for consideration.","c":"屈服；提交","s":"The exhausted CEO stubbornly did not submit to the aggressive investors' demands to immediately step down from his leadership position.","t":"疲憊的執行長固執地沒有向具攻擊性的投資者要求他立即辭去領導職位的要求屈服。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"To suffer something painful or difficult patiently.","c":"忍受","s":"The dedicated soldier bravely endured terribly long hours in the hot desert completely without water during the intense war.","t":"這位盡責的士兵在激烈的戰爭中，勇敢地在炎熱的沙漠中在完全沒有水的情況下忍受了極其漫長的時間。"},{"w":"bear-bore-born","p":"v.","d":"To endure an ordeal or difficulty.","c":"忍受","s":"Michelle didn't really mind the hot temperature, but she simply couldn't bear the suffocating humidity of the tropical island.","t":"蜜雪兒其實不介意炎熱的溫度，但她就是無法忍受這座熱帶島嶼令人窒息的濕度。"},{"w":"stand","p":"v.","d":"To be able to endure or tolerate.","c":"忍受","s":"I really can't stand lazy employees who are always late for important morning meetings and never apologize for their bad behavior.","t":"我真的無法忍受那些在重要的早會總是遲到且從不為自己的不良行為道歉的懶惰員工。"},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"To allow the existence or occurrence of something.","c":"容忍","s":"The strict boss firmly stated that he will not tolerate you being late so often, so try your best to get here on time.","t":"嚴格的老闆堅定地表示他不會容忍你這麼常遲到，所以盡你所能準時到這裡。"},{"w":"resemble","p":"v.","d":"To have qualities or features in common with.","c":"像；與...相似","s":"Many people frequently say that I closely resemble my beautiful mother, especially when I smile broadly for a photograph.","t":"許多人經常說我非常像我美麗的母親，尤其是當我為了拍照而燦爛地微笑時。"},{"w":"enslave","p":"v.","d":"To make someone a slave.","c":"奴役","s":"The aggressive invading army managed to capture and brutally enslave hundreds of innocent villagers during the violent and chaotic attack.","t":"具攻擊性的入侵軍隊不幸地在暴力且混亂的攻擊中，成功俘虜並殘忍地奴役了數百名無辜的村民。"},{"w":"reside in","p":"v.","d":"To have one's permanent home in a particular place.","c":"居住","s":"Peter used to live in Taiwan, but he now resides in a small, quiet town in southern France.","t":"彼得以前住在台灣，但他現在居住在法國南部一個安靜的小鎮。"},{"w":"tribal chief","p":"phr.","d":"The head or leader of a tribe.","c":"部落首領","s":"The wise tribal chief gathered all the families together to discuss how to prepare for the approaching harsh winter.","t":"聰明的部落首領把所有家庭聚集在一起，討論如何為即將到來的嚴冬做準備。"},{"w":"tribal warfare","p":"phr.","d":"Violent conflict between two or more tribes.","c":"部落戰爭","s":"The ancient region was completely destroyed by decades of bitter tribal warfare, leaving many people without homes or food.","t":"這個古老的地區被數十年的激烈部落戰爭徹底摧毀，導致許多人沒有家或食物。"},{"w":"domestic violence","p":"phr.","d":"Violent or aggressive behavior within the home.","c":"家庭暴力","s":"The new social organization was established specifically to help victims of domestic violence escape their dangerous living situations safely.","t":"這個新社會組織的建立專門是為了幫助家庭暴力的受害者安全逃離他們危險的生活環境。"},{"w":"residential area","p":"phr.","d":"Land used in which housing predominates.","c":"住宅區","s":"Because this is a strictly residential area, heavy trucks and loud construction are completely forbidden during the night hours.","t":"因為這是一個嚴格的住宅區，所以夜間完全禁止重型卡車和嘈雜的施工。"},{"w":"conquer one's fear","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully overcome a feeling of being afraid.","c":"克服恐懼","s":"It took several months of therapy, but she finally managed to conquer her fear of flying in an airplane.","t":"這花了幾個月的治療，但她終於成功地克服了她對搭飛機的恐懼。"},{"w":"conquered territory","p":"phr.","d":"Land that has been taken over by military force.","c":"被征服的領土","s":"The powerful king imposed strict new laws and high taxes on the conquered territory to maintain complete control over the people.","t":"強大的國王對被征服的領土實施嚴格的新法律和高稅收，以維持對人民的完全控制。"},{"w":"rival clan","p":"phr.","d":"A competing or opposing family group.","c":"敵對家族","s":"The two powerful groups used to be a rival clan that fought constantly, but they eventually signed a peace treaty.","t":"這兩個強大的團體過去是經常戰鬥的敵對家族，但他們最終簽署了一項和平條約。"},{"w":"brave warrior","p":"phr.","d":"A fighter who shows courage.","c":"勇敢的戰士","s":"The brave warrior refused to run away, choosing instead to stand firmly and fiercely protect the helpless villagers from the attack.","t":"這位勇敢的戰士拒絕逃跑，反而選擇堅定地站著並猛烈地保護無助的村民免受攻擊。"},{"w":"fierce warrior","p":"phr.","d":"An aggressive and powerful fighter.","c":"勇猛的戰士","s":"Historically, the Vikings were known across Europe as fierce warriors who attacked coastal towns from their incredibly fast wooden ships.","t":"在歷史上，維京人以勇猛的戰士聞名於歐洲，他們從極快的木船上攻擊沿海城鎮。"},{"w":"warrior spirit","p":"phr.","d":"A mindset of courage, determination, and resilience.","c":"戰士精神","s":"Despite his severe injuries, the athlete showed a true warrior spirit and returned to the field to finish the game.","t":"儘管受了重傷，這位運動員展現了真正的戰士精神，並回到場上完成了比賽。"},{"w":"be scattered with","p":"phr.","d":"To be covered with things thrown randomly.","c":"散佈著...","s":"When I came home, I noticed that the entire living room floor was scattered with toys that the child had forgotten to put away.","t":"當我回家時，我注意到整個客廳地板都散佈著孩子忘記收好的玩具。"},{"w":"scatter around","p":"phr.","d":"To place or leave things in different places.","c":"散落一地","s":"His dirty clothes were lazily scattered around the bedroom, making the whole place look incredibly messy and completely unorganized.","t":"他的髒衣服懶散地散落一地在臥室裡，讓整個地方看起來極其凌亂且完全沒有條理。"},{"w":"widely scattered","p":"phr.","d":"Spread over a large area.","c":"廣泛散佈的","s":"The ancient ruins are widely scattered across the vast desert, making it extremely difficult for scientists to study them properly.","t":"古老的遺跡廣泛散佈的在浩瀚的沙漠中，使得科學家極難適當地研究它們。"},{"w":"business expansion","p":"phr.","d":"The growth of a company's operations.","c":"業務擴展","s":"The CEO requested a detailed financial report to see if they had enough money to fund the highly anticipated business expansion.","t":"執行長要求一份詳細的財務報告，以查看他們是否有足夠的資金來資助備受期待的業務擴展。"},{"w":"the vast majority","p":"phr.","d":"Almost all of a group.","c":"絕大多數","s":"The vast majority of the factory workers strongly agreed that they deserved a fair salary increase for their dedicated hard work.","t":"絕大多數的工廠工人強烈同意他們理應因為專注的辛勤工作而獲得公平的加薪。"},{"w":"vast area","p":"phr.","d":"A very large expanse of space or land.","c":"廣闊的地區","s":"The terrible summer wildfire quickly spread across a vast area of the national park, destroying thousands of ancient trees.","t":"可怕的夏季野火迅速蔓延過國家公園的一大片廣闊的地區，摧毀了數千棵古樹。"},{"w":"roman empire","p":"phr.","d":"The post-Republican period of ancient Rome.","c":"羅馬帝國","s":"The fall of the deeply influential Roman Empire drastically changed the political and cultural landscape of ancient Europe forever.","t":"影響深遠的羅馬帝國的衰亡徹底永遠改變了古代歐洲的政治和文化景觀。"},{"w":"the pacific ocean","p":"phr.","d":"The largest and deepest of Earth's oceanic divisions.","c":"太平洋","s":"The Pacific Ocean is universally recognized as the world's largest ocean, covering more area than all the landmasses combined.","t":"太平洋被普遍認為是世界上最大的海洋，覆蓋的面積比所有陸地面積的總和還要大。"},{"w":"pacific coast","p":"phr.","d":"The coastline along the Pacific Ocean.","c":"太平洋海岸","s":"Taking a long drive along the breathtaking Pacific coast provides tourists with some of the most stunning ocean views in the country.","t":"沿著令人驚嘆的太平洋海岸長途開車，為遊客提供了該國一些最令人驚豔的海景。"},{"w":"have a crush on somebody","p":"phr.","d":"To have a feeling of romantic love for someone.","c":"迷戀某人","s":"Sammy nervously passed a handwritten note to Jenny that secretly said he had had a crush on her since the semester began.","t":"薩米緊張地傳了一張手寫紙條給珍妮，秘密地說自從學期開始他就非常迷戀她。"},{"w":"be opposed to","p":"phr.","d":"To be against or disagree with something.","c":"反對...","s":"Peter is opposed to the new tax law, and he has angrily written several complaint letters to the local newspaper about it.","t":"彼得強烈反對新的稅法，並且他已經生氣地寫了幾封投訴信給當地報紙談論此事。"},{"w":"submit a report","p":"phr.","d":"To hand in a document for review or grading.","c":"提交報告","s":"Every student is required to properly submit a report detailing their scientific findings before the strict deadline strictly passes on Friday.","t":"每個學生都必須在星期五嚴格的截止日期過去之前，適當地提交一份報告，詳細說明他們的科學發現。"},{"w":"submit an assignment","p":"phr.","d":"To hand in a piece of schoolwork to a teacher.","c":"繳交作業","s":"The teacher reminded the students that they must submit an assignment through the online portal before midnight, or they would lose ten percent of their final grade.","t":"老師提醒學生們，他們必須在午夜前透過線上平台繳交作業，否則他們的期末成績將會被扣百分之十。"},{"w":"submit to","p":"phr.","d":"To yield or give in to someone or something.","c":"屈服於...","s":"The brave rebel leader vowed that his people would never submit to the oppressive enemy forces, no matter how hard the fight was.","t":"這位勇敢的叛軍領袖發誓，無論戰鬥多麼艱難，他的人民永遠不會屈服於壓迫的敵軍。"},{"w":"bear a resemblance to","p":"phr.","d":"To look like or be similar to someone or something.","c":"與...有相似之處","s":"I personally know a funny person at work who actually bears a resemblance to the famous Hollywood actor, Hugh Jackman.","t":"我私下認識一個工作上很有趣的人，他實際上與著名的好萊塢演員休·傑克曼有極為密切的相似之處。"},{"w":"closely resemble","p":"phr.","d":"To be very similar in appearance or nature.","c":"非常相似","s":"The newly discovered insect species seems to closely resemble a common leaf, which perfectly helps it cleverly hide from dangerous predators.","t":"新發現的昆蟲物種似乎非常相似於一片普通的葉子，這完美地幫助牠聰明地躲避危險的掠食者。"},{"w":"iron fist","p":"phr.","d":"Rigorous or severe control.","c":"鐵腕（統治）","s":"The unyielding dictator harshly ruled the poor country with an iron fist for three decades, fiercely crushing any signs of rebellion.","t":"這位不屈服的獨裁者用鐵腕嚴厲統治這個貧窮國家三十年，猛烈地鎮壓任何叛亂的跡象。"},{"w":"be subject to","p":"phr.","d":"To be likely to be affected by something, or dependent on a condition.","c":"易受...影響；取決於","s":"International flights departing from the cosmopolitan city often are subject to unexpected delays due to severe regional winter weather.","t":"從這個國際化城市出發的國際航班，常常容易受到區域性嚴寒天氣的影響而無預警延誤。"},{"w":"be subject to change","p":"phr.","d":"Describing a situation, rule, or price that can be modified without prior notice.","c":"隨時可能更改；可能有變動","s":"The detailed schedule for the upcoming programming tournament is subject to change without any prior announcement from the committee.","t":"即將舉行的程式設計錦標賽的詳細日程安排可能會隨時變動，委員會不會事先發布任何通知。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"physician – overcome an adversity","cards":[{"w":"physician","p":"n.","d":"a medical doctor, especially one who has general skill.","c":"內科醫生","s":"Old people should always ask their physician before starting any kind of new and strenuous exercise routine.","t":"老年人在開始任何新的且劇烈的運動計畫之前，總是應該先詢問他們的內科醫生。"},{"w":"surgeon","p":"n.","d":"a medical practitioner qualified to practice surgery.","c":"外科醫生","s":"The highly skilled surgeon successfully completed the complex heart operation after standing in the operating room for ten hours.","t":"這位技術高超的外科醫生在手術室站了十個小時後，成功完成了複雜的心臟手術。"},{"w":"dentist","p":"n.","d":"a person qualified to treat the diseases and conditions that affect the teeth and gums.","c":"牙醫","s":"You really need to visit the dentist every six months to ensure that your teeth and gums remain perfectly healthy.","t":"你真的需要每六個月去看一次牙醫，以確保你的牙齒和牙齦保持完全健康。"},{"w":"surgery","p":"n.","d":"medical treatment in which a doctor cuts open a person's body to repair or remove damaged parts","c":"外科手術","s":"The head doctor told the patient that undergoing major surgery was the only way to treat the illness safely.","t":"主治醫生告訴患者，接受重大外科手術是安全治療該疾病的唯一方法。"},{"w":"perform an operation","p":"v.","d":"do a specific procedure of cutting open a patient's body by a doctor to treat a medical condition","c":"動手術","s":"The professional medical team successfully perform an operation for 3 hours on the patient's heart this morning.","t":"專業醫療團隊今天上午成功為患者的心臟進行了三個小時的手術。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"an organized activity, mission, or campaign involving a number of people, especially soldiers or police","c":"行動；任務","s":"The military commander organized a top-secret rescue operation to save the citizens trapped inside the remote zone.","t":"軍事指揮官組織了一次絕密的救援行動，以營救被困在偏遠地區內的公民。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"the ongoing factual processes, practical running, and day-to-day business management of a firm","c":"運營；運作","s":"The ambitious entrepreneur completely modernized the daily operation of the international corporation by deploying automated AI tools.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的企業家透過部署自動化人工智慧工具，徹底使這家國際公司的日常運營走向現代化。"},{"w":"entrepreneur","p":"n.","d":"a person who sets up a business or businesses, taking on financial risks in the hope of profit","c":"企業家；創業家","s":"Every young entrepreneur dreams of designing a customizable learning platform that can completely change the global educational landscape.","t":"每位年輕的企業家都夢想設計一個能夠徹底改變全球教育景觀的客製化學習平台。"},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies authorized to act as a single entity and recognized as such in law","c":"大企業；公司","s":"The international technology corporation decided to fund a new business expansion project to attract additional wealthy investors.","t":"這家國際科技公司決定資助一項全新的業務擴展計畫，以吸引更多富有的投資者。"},{"w":"go smoothly","p":"phr.","d":"to progress or happen without any problems, unexpected difficulties, or sudden interruptions","c":"進展順利；順利進行","s":"Thanks to the manager's meticulous lesson planning and organization, the entire product testing phase did go smoothly.","t":"幸虧經理細緻的計畫與組織，整個產品測試階段確實進展順利。"},{"w":"go badly","p":"phr.","d":"to happen in a way that is not successful or causes problems.","c":"進行得不順利","s":"Even when things would go badly for him, Kevin always tried his best to remain optimistic and keep smiling.","t":"即使事情對他來說進行得不順利，凱文總是盡全力保持樂觀並繼續微笑。"},{"w":"need badly","p":"phr.","d":"to require something very much or urgently.","c":"迫切需要","s":"The exhausted charity workers badly needed more volunteers to help distribute the food to the homeless people in the city.","t":"疲憊的慈善工作者迫切需要更多志工來幫忙發放食物給城市裡的無家可歸者。"},{"w":"harm","p":"v.","d":"cause physical injury, to injure.","c":"傷害","s":"Mean posts and comments of trolls harm the celebrity's reputation.","t":"酸民的尖酸刻薄的貼文漢留言傷害這個名人的名聲"},{"w":"harm","p":"n.","d":"physical injury, especially that which is deliberately inflicted; to injure.","c":"傷害","s":"My father was incredibly happy that there was no harm to his expensive new car after the severe thunderstorm.","t":"我父親非常高興，在嚴重的雷雨過後，他昂貴的新車沒有受到任何傷害。"},{"w":"do harm to","p":"phr.","d":"to cause physical or mental damage to someone or something.","c":"對...造成傷害","s":"The doctor warned that eating too much fast food and sugary snacks may eventually do harm to your stomach.","t":"醫生警告說，吃太多速食和含糖零食最終可能會對你的胃造成傷害。"},{"w":"do no harm to","p":"phr.","d":"to be completely safe and cause no damage or injury.","c":"不對...造成傷害","s":"I really don't know why Charles is so mad at me, because I have done no harm to him whatsoever.","t":"我真的不知道查爾斯為什麼生我的氣，因為我根本沒有對他造成傷害。"},{"w":"do more harm than good","p":"phr.","d":"to be damaging and not helpful in a situation.","c":"弊大於利","s":"I honestly think that continually pressuring Jerry to get a summer job will probably do more harm than good.","t":"我老實認為，不斷向傑瑞施壓要他去找一份暑期工作可能會弊大於利。"},{"w":"harmful","p":"adj.","d":"causing or likely to cause harm.","c":"有害的","s":"Releasing these toxic chemicals into the local river is incredibly harmful to the delicate ecosystem and the surrounding wildlife.","t":"將這些有毒化學物質排放到當地河流中，對脆弱的生態系統和周圍的野生動物是極其有害的。"},{"w":"harmless","p":"adj.","d":"not able or not likely to cause harm.","c":"無害的","s":"The large green snake might look incredibly frightening, but it is actually completely harmless to humans and pets.","t":"這條大綠蛇看起來可能非常嚇人，但牠對人類和寵物其實是完全無害的。"},{"w":"shortage","p":"n.","d":"a state or situation in which something needed cannot be obtained in sufficient amounts.","c":"短缺","s":"Due to the changing climate, major cities all over the world have been experiencing serious water shortage recently.","t":"由於氣候變遷，世界各地的主要城市最近一直經歷著嚴重的水資源短缺。"},{"w":"food shortage","p":"phr.","d":"a situation where there is not enough food for people in a region.","c":"糧食短缺","s":"The harsh winter drought destroyed most of the crops, leading to a terrible food shortage in the isolated farming village.","t":"嚴酷的冬季乾旱摧毀了大部分農作物，導致這個孤立的農村發生了可怕的糧食短缺。"},{"w":"a shortage of","p":"phr.","d":"a lack of a specific item or resource.","c":"...的短缺","s":"There was a sudden shortage of cashiers working today, so Marshall had to wait in a very long line.","t":"今天收銀員突然短缺，所以馬歇爾得排非常長的隊。"},{"w":"short","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of something.","c":"短缺的；不足的","s":"The hospital is severely short of experienced nursing staff, making it difficult to properly care for all the sick patients.","t":"醫院嚴重短缺經驗豐富的護理人員，導致很難適當地照顧所有生病的病患。"},{"w":"fall short of","p":"phr.","d":"to fail to meet an expectation or standard.","c":"未達到；不符合","s":"The company's final yearly profits unfortunately fell short of the ambitious expectations that the rich investors had originally set.","t":"該公司最終的年度利潤不幸地未達到富有的投資者最初設定的雄心勃勃的期望。"},{"w":"swell","p":"v.","d":"to become larger or rounder in size.","c":"腫脹；增加","s":"When Gina accidentally hurt her ankle during the game, it quickly swelled to twice the normal size and turned purple.","t":"當吉娜在比賽中不小心弄傷腳踝時，它迅速腫脹到正常大小的兩倍並變成紫色。"},{"w":"swollen","p":"adj.","d":"larger or rounder in size, typically as a result of an accumulation of fluid.","c":"腫大的","s":"After hiking in the humid jungle for ten hours, my feet were incredibly sore and completely swollen inside my boots.","t":"在潮濕的叢林裡徒步十個小時後，我的腳極度痠痛，且在靴子裡完全是腫大的。"},{"w":"swelling","p":"n.","d":"an abnormal enlargement of a part of the body.","c":"腫脹（處）","s":"You should immediately apply an ice pack to your injured knee to effectively reduce the painful swelling before tomorrow.","t":"你應該立刻在受傷的膝蓋上敷冰袋，以在明天之前有效地減少痛苦的腫脹。"},{"w":"fluid","p":"n. / adj.","d":"a substance that has no fixed shape; able to flow easily.","c":"液體；流暢的","s":"The professional ballet dancers had to carefully move their bodies in a completely fluid manner to match the classical music.","t":"專業的芭蕾舞者必須以完全流暢的方式小心地移動身體，以配合古典音樂。"},{"w":"body fluid","p":"phr.","d":"liquids originating from inside the bodies of living humans.","c":"體液","s":"Doctors must wear special protective gloves to prevent any dangerous contact with infected body fluid while treating the patients.","t":"醫生在治療病患時必須戴上特殊的防護手套，以防止與受感染的體液發生任何危險接觸。"},{"w":"fluid situation","p":"phr.","d":"a situation that is changing or likely to change.","c":"不穩定的局勢","s":"Because it is a highly fluid situation, the company has not yet finalized its exact marketing strategy for the upcoming year.","t":"因為這是一個高度不穩定的局勢，該公司尚未最終確定其來年的確切行銷策略。"},{"w":"leak","p":"v. / n.","d":"to accidentally lose or admit contents; a hole through which contents escape.","c":"漏水；洩漏","s":"The heavy rain constantly leaked through the old wooden roof and eventually flooded Pam's small kitchen during the terrible storm.","t":"在可怕的風暴中，大雨不斷地從舊木屋頂漏水，並最終淹沒了潘的小廚房。"},{"w":"leak information","p":"phr.","d":"to intentionally disclose secret or confidential information.","c":"洩漏資訊","s":"The angry former employee decided to anonymously leak confidential financial information to the press to severely damage the company's reputation.","t":"憤怒的前員工決定匿名向媒體洩漏機密財務資訊，以嚴重損害公司的聲譽。"},{"w":"lung","p":"n.","d":"each of the pair of organs situated within the rib cage, consisting of elastic sacs.","c":"肺臟","s":"It is a well-known biological fact that birds and mammals heavily rely on their lung to breathe the surrounding air.","t":"眾所周知的生物學事實是，鳥類和哺乳動物嚴重依賴牠們的肺臟來呼吸周圍的空氣。"},{"w":"at the top of one's lungs","p":"phr.","d":"as loudly as one's voice will allow.","c":"聲嘶力竭地","s":"The terrified children on the fast roller coaster were excitedly screaming at the top of their lungs during the steep drop.","t":"快速雲霄飛車上受驚的孩子們在陡降時正興奮地聲嘶力竭地尖叫。"},{"w":"lung cancer","p":"phr.","d":"a cancer that begins in the lungs and most often occurs in people who smoke.","c":"肺癌","s":"The doctor firmly explained that years of heavy smoking had drastically increased the old man's risk of developing lung cancer.","t":"醫生堅定地解釋說，多年的重度吸菸已急劇增加了這位老人罹患肺癌的風險。"},{"w":"kidney","p":"n.","d":"each of a pair of organs in the abdominal cavity excreting urine.","c":"腎臟","s":"Drinking enough fresh water every day is absolutely essential to ensure that your kidney can properly filter toxins from your blood.","t":"每天喝足夠的清水對於確保你的腎臟能適當地過濾血液中的毒素是絕對必要的。"},{"w":"liver","p":"n.","d":"a large lobed glandular organ in the abdomen of vertebrates, involved in many metabolic processes.","c":"肝臟","s":"Consuming massive amounts of alcohol over many years will severely damage your liver and lead to potentially fatal health conditions.","t":"多年來消耗大量酒精將嚴重損害你的肝臟並導致潛在致命的健康狀況。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing death.","c":"致命的","s":"Thankfully, Will's sudden and mysterious illness was not fatal, and he completely recovered after spending just two weeks in the hospital.","t":"幸好，威爾突然且神秘的疾病不是致命的，他在醫院只待了兩週就完全康復了。"},{"w":"fatal error","p":"phr.","d":"a serious mistake that causes a complete failure.","c":"致命的錯誤","s":"The inexperienced pilot made a completely fatal error during the heavy storm, which directly caused the small airplane to crash into the mountain.","t":"缺乏經驗的飛行員在暴風雨中犯了一個完全致命的錯誤，直接導致小飛機撞上山。"},{"w":"death toll","p":"phr.","d":"The total number of people who die in an accident, war, or natural disaster.","c":"死亡人數、死亡總數","s":"After the powerful earthquake struck the island, rescue teams worked day and night, but the death toll unfortunately continued to rise as more victims were found.","t":"在強震襲擊這座島嶼之後，救援隊日以繼夜地工作，但隨著發現更多罹難者，死亡人數不幸地持續上升。"},{"w":"mortality rate","p":"phr.","d":"The number of deaths in a particular group of people or during a specific period of time.","c":"死亡率","s":"Thanks to advanced medical technology and clean drinking water, the infant mortality rate in this country has dropped significantly over the past twenty years.","t":"多虧了先進的醫療科技和乾淨的飲用水，這個國家的嬰兒死亡率在過去二十年裡顯著下降。"},{"w":"lethal","p":"adj.","d":"Able to cause death; extremely dangerous or deadly.","c":"致命的","s":"The chemical factory accidentally leaked a lethal gas into the nearby village, forcing hundreds of residents to evacuate their homes immediately.","t":"這家化學工廠不小心將一種致命的氣體洩漏到附近的村莊，迫使數百名居民立刻撤離家園。"},{"w":"associate","p":"v.","d":"to connect someone or something in your mind with someone or something else.","c":"聯想；結交","s":"I don't think you should continue to associate with those aggressive people because they will constantly cause trouble for your career.","t":"我不認為你應該繼續與那些具攻擊性的人結交，因為他們會不斷地為你的職涯帶來麻煩。"},{"w":"associate ..with..","p":"phr.","d":"to make a mental connection between two things.","c":"把A和B聯想在一起","s":"Many people would naturally associate eating cold ice cream with the hot summer, but I personally love to eat it during winter too.","t":"許多人會自然地把吃冷冰淇淋和炎熱的夏天聯想在一起，但我個人在冬天也很喜歡吃。"},{"w":"be associated with","p":"adj.","d":"connected with something else.","c":"相關的","s":"Mitch actively wants to find a creative new job that is closely associated with modern interior design and architectural planning.","t":"米奇積極想找一份與現代室內設計和建築規劃密切相關的具創意的新工作。"},{"w":"association","p":"n.","d":"a connection or cooperative link between people or organizations.","c":"協會；聯想","s":"The historical neighborhood formed a strong community association to ensure that the ancient buildings would be protected from greedy property developers.","t":"這個歷史悠久的社區成立了一個強大的社區協會，以確保古老建築免受貪婪房地產開發商的破壞。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"n.","d":"a sum of money kept in a bank; to place or set down.","c":"存款；押金；存放","s":"The determined gold miner searched tirelessly for an entire year before he finally found a massive deposit of gold deep in the mountains.","t":"這位意志堅定的淘金者不知疲倦地尋找了整整一年，才終於在深山裡發現了巨大的黃金礦床（沉積）。"},{"w":"pay a deposit","p":"phr.","d":"to pay a sum of money as a first installment on a larger payment.","c":"付押金","s":"Steve unfortunately had to pay a very large deposit on the expensive sports car before the dealer would let him drive it home.","t":"史蒂夫不幸地必須為這輛昂貴的跑車付一大筆押金，然後經銷商才願意讓他把它開回家。"},{"w":"make a deposit","p":"phr.","d":"to put money into a bank account.","c":"存錢","s":"Tim generally spends half of the money he makes each month, and he goes to the local bank to make a deposit with the other half.","t":"提姆通常會花掉他每個月賺的一半的錢，然後去當地銀行把另一半存起來。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"v.","d":"To put money into a bank account for safekeeping.","c":"存款、存入","s":"After receiving his first paycheck from the new company, Mark immediately went to the bank to deposit the money into his savings account.","t":"在收到新公司的第一筆薪水後，馬克立刻去銀行把錢存入他的儲蓄帳戶。"},{"w":"withdraw money","p":"phr.","d":"To take money out of a bank account.","c":"提款、領錢","s":"Because the local night market only accepts cash, we need to find an ATM to withdraw money before we go there to buy some delicious street food.","t":"因為當地的夜市只收現金，所以我們在去那裡買美味的街頭小吃之前，需要找一台自動提款機來領錢。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"v.","d":"To drop or leave a layer of a substance, like sand or mud, on a surface over time.","c":"使沉澱、沉積","s":"When the heavy rain finally stopped, the flooding river began to slow down and deposit a thick layer of muddy sediment on the empty farmland.","t":"當大雨終於停歇時，氾濫的河水開始減緩，並在空曠的農田上沉積了一層厚厚的泥濘沉積物。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"n.","d":"A layer of a substance, such as rock, soil, or mud, that has been left naturally on a surface.","c":"沉澱物、沉積物","s":"The geologists studied the thick mineral deposit at the bottom of the ancient lake to learn more about the climate changes that happened millions of years ago.","t":"地質學家研究了古老湖底厚厚的礦物沉積物，以了解更多關於數百萬年前發生的氣候變遷。"},{"w":"mineral deposit","p":"phr.","d":"a concentration of naturally occurring solid material in the earth's crust.","c":"礦床","s":"The mining company heavily invested millions of dollars to extract the valuable mineral deposit that were discovered beneath the dense jungle.","t":"礦業公司投入數百萬美元來開採在茂密叢林下方發現的寶貴礦床。"},{"w":"fiber","p":"n.","d":"dietary material containing substances which are resistant to digestive enzymes.","c":"纖維","s":"Snacking regularly on fresh fruit and crunchy nuts is a highly effective way to get enough fiber in your daily diet.","t":"規律地把新鮮水果和脆堅果當零食吃，是在你日常飲食中獲得足夠纖維的一種非常有效的方法。"},{"w":"dietary fiber","p":"phr.","d":"the indigestible portion of food derived from plants.","c":"膳食纖維","s":"Whole wheat bread naturally contains much more dietary fiber than perfectly white bread, making it a significantly healthier choice for lunch.","t":"全麥麵包天然含有的膳食纖維比完美的白麵包多得多，使其成為午餐明顯更健康的選擇。"},{"w":"calcium","p":"n.","d":"a white metallic chemical element that occurs naturally in bone and teeth.","c":"鈣","s":"Drinking fresh milk every morning is a fantastic way to ensure your growing bones receive enough essential calcium to stay strong.","t":"每天早上喝鮮奶是確保你生長中的骨骼獲得足夠必需的鈣以保持強壯的絕佳方式。"},{"w":"protein","p":"n.","d":"a substance found in food that is necessary for the body to grow and be strong.","c":"蛋白質","s":"Chicken breast and hard-boiled eggs are excellent sources of lean protein, which is strictly required for building strong muscles after exercise.","t":"雞胸肉和水煮蛋是優質瘦蛋白質的極佳來源，這是在運動後建立強壯肌肉嚴格需要的。"},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a solid naturally occurring inorganic substance.","c":"礦物質","s":"This incredibly pure natural spring water contains many healthy minerals that are considered essential for maintaining an active human body.","t":"這種極度純淨的天然泉水含有許多健康的礦物質，這些礦物質被認為是維持活躍人體所必需的。"},{"w":"mineral water","p":"phr.","d":"water from a spring that contains dissolved minerals.","c":"礦泉水","s":"While dining at the expensive Italian restaurant, the fancy customers ordered an imported bottle of sparkling mineral water to pair with their rich meal.","t":"在昂貴的義大利餐廳用餐時，這些講究的顧客點了一瓶進口的氣泡礦泉水來搭配他們豐盛的一餐。"},{"w":"rich in minerals","p":"phr.","d":"containing a lot of minerals.","c":"富含礦物質","s":"The dark, fertile volcanic soil in this tropical region is incredibly rich in minerals, making it absolutely perfect for growing healthy coffee plants.","t":"這個熱帶地區黑暗肥沃的火山土壤極度富含礦物質，使其絕對適合種植健康的咖啡樹。"},{"w":"lighten","p":"v.","d":"to make or become lighter in weight, pressure, or severity.","c":"減輕；變亮","s":"The helpful teacher expertly lightened the difficult math problem by slowly solving it step-by-step on the blackboard for her confused students.","t":"樂於助人的老師在黑板上為她困惑的學生一步步慢慢解題，巧妙地減輕（簡化）了這道困難的數學題。"},{"w":"lighten up","p":"phr.","d":"to become more relaxed and less serious.","c":"放輕鬆","s":"James really needs to lighten up and relax a little bit because he has been taking his busy office job far too seriously lately.","t":"詹姆斯真的需要放輕鬆一點，因為他最近把他繁忙的辦公室工作看得太過嚴肅了。"},{"w":"lighten the load","p":"phr.","d":"to make a difficult situation easier to deal with.","c":"減輕負擔","s":"Hiring a highly efficient assistant will quickly lighten the load on the stressed manager and completely prevent him from quitting the company.","t":"僱用一位高效率的助理將迅速減輕這位壓力過大的經理的負擔，並完全防止他辭職。"},{"w":"lighten the mood","p":"phr.","d":"to make a situation less serious or tense.","c":"緩和氣氛","s":"When everyone was arguing in the hot conference room, Dave effectively told a funny joke to successfully lighten the mood.","t":"當大家在炎熱的會議室裡爭吵時，戴夫有效地講了一個好笑的笑話，成功地緩和了氣氛。"},{"w":"conclude","p":"v.","d":"to bring something to an end; to arrive at a judgment.","c":"結束；得出結論","s":"After carefully reviewing all the scientific evidence, the detective was forced to conclude that the suspect was completely innocent of the terrible crime.","t":"在仔細審查所有科學證據後，偵探被迫得出結論，該嫌疑犯對這起可怕的罪行是完全無辜的。"},{"w":"conclusion","p":"n.","d":"the end or finish of an event or process; a judgment or decision.","c":"結論","s":"Thinking deeply about his future career, Ian finally reached the logical conclusion that he truly wanted to be an international commercial pilot.","t":"深入思考他未來的職涯，伊恩最終得出了合乎邏輯的結論，他真正想成為一名國際商業飛行員。"},{"w":"in conclusion","p":"phr.","d":"lastly, to sum up.","c":"總而言之","s":"In conclusion, the environmental report clearly shows that we absolutely must reduce our daily carbon emissions to effectively save the beautiful planet.","t":"總而言之，這份環境報告清楚地顯示我們絕對必須減少日常碳排放量，以有效地拯救這顆美麗的星球。"},{"w":"reach the conclusion","p":"phr.","d":"to make a decision or judgement after considering all the information.","c":"得出結論","s":"It took the jury three long days of intense debate to finally reach the conclusion that the businessman had stolen the money.","t":"陪審團花了漫長三天的激烈辯論，才終於得出該商人偷了錢的結論。"},{"w":"jump to conclusions","p":"phr.","d":"to guess the facts about a situation without having enough information.","c":"妄下定論","s":"You shouldn't blindly jump to conclusions just because she was completely late for the meeting; she might have been stuck in bad traffic.","t":"你不應該只因為她開會完全遲到就盲目地妄下定論；她可能只是被困在糟糕的交通中。"},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"moderate in the amount.","c":"適度的","s":"Many top scientists deeply believe that developed countries have unfortunately only devoted modest resources to properly fighting global climate change.","t":"許多頂尖科學家深信，已開發國家不幸地只投入了適度的（少量的）資源來適當地對抗全球氣候變遷。"},{"w":"modestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a modest manner.","c":"謙虛地","s":"Despite winning the prestigious international award, the talented author modestly stated that she simply couldn't have successfully done it without her brilliant editor.","t":"儘管贏得了著名的國際獎項，這位才華洋溢的作家謙虛地表示，如果沒有她傑出的編輯，她根本不可能成功做到。"},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"humble in estimating one's own abilities or achievements, or relatively moderate in size","c":"謙虛的；端莊的；適度的","s":"Despite winning the national programming championship, the modest engineer remained quiet about his exceptional tech skills.","t":"儘管贏得了全國程式設計冠軍賽，這位謙虛的工程師對自己卓越的科技才能依然保持低調。"},{"w":"modesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality or state of being unassuming or moderate.","c":"謙遜","s":"Her unbelievable modesty prevents her from openly talking about her massive wealth, so most of her friends actually think she is quite poor.","t":"她令人難以置信的謙遜讓她無法公開談論她龐大的財富，所以她的大多數朋友其實都認為她相當窮。"},{"w":"moderate","p":"adj.","d":"average in amount, intensity, quality, or degree.","c":"中等的；適度的","s":"The experienced doctor strictly advised him to engage in moderate exercise daily rather than violently pushing himself too hard at the heavy gym.","t":"經驗豐富的醫生嚴格建議他每天進行適度的運動，而不是在繁重的健身房裡猛烈地過度逼迫自己。"},{"w":"humble","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing a modest or low estimate of one's own importance.","c":"謙卑的","s":"Even though Jon is arguably the most famous actor in Hollywood, he remains a deeply humble and incredibly friendly person to all his fans.","t":"即使喬恩可以說是好萊塢最著名的演員，他對所有粉絲仍然是一個極度謙卑的且極其友善的人。"},{"w":"arrogant","p":"adj.","d":"having or revealing an exaggerated sense of one's own importance or abilities.","c":"傲慢的","s":"The highly successful businessman was so ridiculously arrogant that he absolutely refused to listen to anyone else's professional opinions during the important meeting.","t":"這位非常成功的商人是如此荒謬地傲慢的，以至於在重要會議期間他絕對拒絕聽取任何其他人的專業意見。"},{"w":"arrogance","p":"n.","d":"The quality of being unpleasantly proud and thinking you are more important than others.","c":"傲慢、自大","s":"Although Kenny is an extremely talented piano player, his constant arrogance often annoys his classmates and makes it difficult for him to make close friends.","t":"雖然肯尼是一位極具天賦的鋼琴家，但他揮之不去的傲慢常常惹惱班上同學，也讓他很難交到知心的朋友。"},{"w":"snob","p":"n.","d":"A person who admires people with high social positions and looks down on those who are lower.","c":"勢利鬼、愛慕虛榮的人","s":"Amanda is such a snob that she refuses to speak to anyone who doesn't wear expensive designer clothes or drive a luxury sports car.","t":"阿曼達是個不折不扣的勢利鬼，她拒絕與任何不穿昂貴名牌衣服或不開豪華跑車的人說話。"},{"w":"show off","p":"phr.","d":"To behave in a way that is intended to attract attention or admiration from other people.","c":"炫耀、賣弄","s":"Whenever Ryan gets a perfect score on a math test, he always tries to show off to everyone in the classroom, which really irritates his peers.","t":"每當萊恩在數學考試中獲得滿分時，他總是在教室裡向每個人炫耀，這真的很讓他的同儕反感。"},{"w":"boast about","p":"phr.","d":"To speak too proudly about your own abilities, achievements, or possessions.","c":"自誇、誇耀","s":"Our wealthy neighbor loves to boast about his expensive trips abroad, but nobody likes to talk to him because he never listens to others.","t":"我們富裕的鄰居很喜歡誇耀他昂貴的國外旅行，但沒有人喜歡跟他聊天，因為他從不聽別人說話。"},{"w":"brag about","p":"phr.","d":"to speak too proudly, boastfully, or with excessive satisfaction about one's achievements or possessions","c":"吹噓...；誇耀...","s":"The arrogant contestant continuously bragged about his athletic records to impress the media representatives.","t":"這位傲慢的參賽者不斷吹噓自己的運動紀錄，以給媒體代表留下深刻印象。"},{"w":"flaunt","p":"v.","d":"to display something ostentatiously or proudly in public to intentionally provoke envy or admiration","c":"炫耀；張揚（動詞）","s":"It is considered highly unprofessional to flaunt one's personal wealth or corporate revenue during a serious labor strike.","t":"在嚴肅的工會 strike 期間，炫耀個人財富或公司營收被視為高度不專業的行為。"},{"w":"flex","p":"v.","d":"To show off your looks, wealth, or achievements in a boastful way (informal slang).","c":"炫耀、愛現（流行語）","s":"Many teenagers like to flex on social media by posting pictures of their expensive sneakers, even though their parents paid for them.","t":"許多青少年喜歡在社群媒體上炫耀，發布他們昂貴球鞋的照片，即使這些鞋子是他們父母付錢買的。"},{"w":"irritate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel annoyed, impatient, or angry, or to cause a part of the body to become sore","c":"使發怒；使惱火；使過敏","s":"The loud construction noise from the commercial area outside would consistently irritate the residents during their morning hours.","t":"外部商業區傳來的巨大施工噪音，在上午時段總是會使居民們感到惱火。"},{"w":"irritation","p":"n.","d":"the state of feeling annoyed or impatient, or a painful soreness in a specific part of the body","c":"惱怒；生氣；過敏不適","s":"The young entrepreneur expressed deep irritation when the critical automated server framework suddenly stopped functioning.","t":"當關鍵的自動化伺服器架構突然停止運作時，這位年輕的企業家表達了深切的惱怒。"},{"w":"irritating","p":"adj.","d":"causing annoyance, impatience, or mild anger through repetitive or undesirable actions","c":"令人惱火的；討厭的","s":"Every student agreed that filling out the poorly designed research questionnaire was an exceptionally irritating task.","t":"每個學生都同意，填寫那份設計不良的研究問卷是一項格外令人惱火的任務。"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"to frighten or threaten someone, typically in order to force them to do what one wants","c":"恐嚇；脅迫；嚇唬","s":"The aggressive gang attempted to intimidate the honest store owner into giving them a massive sum of money.","t":"那個具攻擊性的幫派企圖恐嚇這位誠實的店主，以強迫他給他們一大筆錢。"},{"w":"intimidating","p":"adj.","d":"causing one to feel frightened, nervous, or lacking in confidence due to scale or nature","c":"令人緊張的；嚇人的","s":"Moving away from a quiet suburb to start a new tech corporation in Taipei can be an intimidating experience.","t":"從寧靜的郊區搬走，並在台北創立一家新的科技大企業，可能會是一次令人緊張的經驗。"},{"w":"intimidation","p":"n.","d":"the action of intentionally frightening or threatening someone to force submissive behavior","c":"恐嚇；恫嚇；脅迫","s":"The unyielding dictator fiercely used military intimidation to crush any potential political opposition across the country.","t":"這位不屈服的獨裁者猛烈地利用軍事恐嚇，來鎮壓全國任何潛在的政治反對勢力。"},{"w":"attempt","p":"v.","d":"to make an effort to do, achieve, or complete a challenging task or scientific experiment","c":"企圖；嘗試（動詞）","s":"The medical research staff will attempt to isolate the highly invasive bacterial species during the controlled laboratory experiment.","t":"醫療研究人員將在受控的實驗室實驗中，嘗試分離出這種高度侵入性的細菌物種。"},{"w":"attempt","p":"n.","d":"an act of trying to achieve or complete something difficult, often used with collocations like make an attempt","c":"企圖；嘗試（名詞）","s":"The young entrepreneur made a bold attempt to modernize the daily operation of the traditional family corporation.","t":"這位年輕的企業家做出了一次大膽的嘗試，企圖使傳統家族大企業的日常運營走向現代化。"},{"w":"make an attempt to","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically try or endeavor to do something, especially a challenging task or project","c":"試圖去...；嘗試去...","s":"The dedicated medical staff will make an attempt to isolate the invasive bacterial species during the controlled laboratory experiment.","t":"盡責的醫療團隊將在受控的實驗室實驗中，嘗試分離出這種侵入性的細菌物種。"},{"w":"overdo","p":"v.","d":"to do, use, or carry to excess; exaggerate.","c":"做得過分；過度","s":"Expensive spices certainly add greatly to the delicious flavor of the hot soup, but you really shouldn't overdo it or you'll ruin it entirely.","t":"昂貴的香料確實能大大增加熱湯的美味，但你真的不應該過度使用，否則你會徹底毀了它。"},{"w":"go too far","p":"phr.","d":"to exceed the limits of what is reasonable or acceptable.","c":"做得太過分","s":"I usually completely tolerate your silly jokes, but this time you truly went too far by insulting my family members.","t":"我通常完全容忍你愚蠢的笑話，但這次你侮辱我的家人，真的做得太過分了。"},{"w":"overeat","p":"v.","d":"to eat too much.","c":"吃得過飽","s":"It is incredibly easy to accidentally overeat when you are happily enjoying a massive holiday feast with your beloved family and closest friends.","t":"當你快樂地與深愛的家人和最親密的朋友享受一頓豐盛的節日大餐時，不小心吃得過飽是極其容易的事。"},{"w":"overuse","p":"v.","d":"to use something too much or too often.","c":"過度使用","s":"Doctors frequently warn that if you continuously overuse antibiotics, the dangerous bacteria will quickly become highly resistant to the life-saving medicine.","t":"醫生經常警告，如果你持續過度使用抗生素，危險的細菌將很快對這種救命的藥物產生高度抗藥性。"},{"w":"overload","p":"v.","d":"to load with too great a burden or cargo.","c":"超載；負荷過多","s":"The ambitious manager completely overloaded the new employee with too many complex tasks, causing her to feel deeply stressed and constantly anxious.","t":"雄心勃勃的經理完全讓新員工負荷過多太多的複雜任務，導致她感到壓力極大且持續焦慮。"},{"w":"overweight","p":"adj.","d":"above a weight considered normal or desirable.","c":"超重的","s":"The veterinarian kindly informed us that our lazy dog is slightly overweight and needs to start walking outside in the park much more often.","t":"獸醫親切地通知我們，我們懶惰的狗有點超重的，需要開始更常去公園外面散步。"},{"w":"overwhelm","p":"v.","d":"To defeat someone completely, or to give someone too much of something to deal with.","c":"（數量、力量上）壓倒、使難以承受、使不知所措","s":"The massive amount of customer complaints after the product launch threatens to overwhelm the small support team, so the manager is hiring temporary workers.","t":"產品上市後大量的客戶投訴恐怕會壓倒這個小型的客服團隊，因此經理正在雇用臨時工。"},{"w":"be overwhelmed with","p":"phr.","d":"To receive or be faced with a huge number of physical things at once.","c":"被大量（某物）淹沒、收到多到無法應付的（某物）","s":"Following the celebrity's public announcement, the charity office was overwhelmed with hundreds of donation packages from supportive fans across the country.","t":"在該名人的公開聲明之後，慈善機構辦公室被來自全國支持粉絲的數百個捐贈包裹淹沒了。"},{"w":"be overwhelmed with workload","p":"phr.","d":"To have too much work to do, causing stress or a feeling of being unable to cope.","c":"被工作量壓得喘不過氣、工作量大到無法負荷","s":"Since two employees suddenly resigned last week, the remaining secretary is overwhelmed with workload, and she has to stay late every night to finish the reports.","t":"自從上週兩名員工突然辭職後，留下來的秘書被工作量壓得喘不過氣，她每天晚上都必須加班到很晚才能完成報告。"},{"w":"be overwhelmed with","p":"phr.","d":"To feel a sudden, very strong emotion that is difficult to control.","c":"內心充斥著（某種情緒）、被（某種情緒）淹沒","s":"When the young scientist won the prestigious international award, she was overwhelmed with joy and gave a tearful speech thanking her parents.","t":"當這名年輕的科學家贏得這項著名的國際獎項時，她心中充斥著喜悅，並發表了一段含淚感謝父母的演講。"},{"w":"overthrow","p":"v.","d":"To remove a leader or government from power by using force.","c":"推翻、打倒","s":"The rebel army managed to overthrow the cruel dictator after months of violent protests, and they immediately established a new democratic government.","t":"在數個月的暴力抗議之後，反叛軍成功推翻了殘暴的獨裁者，並立刻建立了一個新的民主政府。"},{"w":"overtake","p":"v.","d":"To catch up with and pass someone or something moving in the same direction.","c":"超車、超過、追上","s":"The professional racing driver managed to overtake his rival on the final lap of the race, which surprised the audience and won him the championship.","t":"這位職業賽車手在比賽的最後一圈成功超過了他的對手，這讓觀眾非常驚訝，也為他贏得了冠軍。"},{"w":"overcome","p":"v.","d":"To successfully control or deal with a problem, feeling, or difficult situation.","c":"克服、戰勝","s":"If you want to speak English fluently, you must overcome your fear of making mistakes and practice talking with native speakers as often as possible.","t":"如果你想流利地說英文，你必須克服對犯錯的恐懼，並儘可能經常與母語人士練習說話。"},{"w":"overcome a challenge","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully deal with a difficult task or situation that tests your abilities.","c":"克服挑戰、戰勝挑戰","s":"Although building a rocket required advanced technology, the young engineers managed to overcome a challenge through teamwork and months of hard work.","t":"雖然建造火箭需要先進的科技，但這群年輕的工程師透過團隊合作和數個月的努力，成功克服了挑戰。"},{"w":"overcome a shortcoming","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully correct or improve a weakness or fault in your character or ability.","c":"克服缺點、彌補不足","s":"Recognizing that he was often late, Jerry worked hard to overcome a shortcoming by setting multiple alarms on his phone every single night.","t":"意識到自己經常遲到後，傑瑞透過每天晚上在手機上設置多個鬧鐘，努力去克服這個缺點。"},{"w":"overcome a hardship","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully get through a period of severe suffering or difficult living conditions.","c":"熬過困境、克服艱難","s":"The poor family managed to overcome a hardship of losing their home after the flood because the local community provided them with food and shelter.","t":"水災過後，這戶貧困的家庭成功熬過了失去家園的困境，因為當地社區為他們提供了食物和庇護所。"},{"w":"overcome an obstacle","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully deal with something that blocks your progress or makes it difficult to achieve a goal.","c":"克服障礙、跨越阻礙","s":"The lack of funding was a major problem, but the research team managed to overcome an obstacle by presenting their brilliant project to rich investors.","t":"缺乏資金是一個主要問題，但研究團隊透過向富有的投資人展示他們出色的專案，成功克服了這個障礙。"},{"w":"overcome an adversity","p":"phr.","d":"To successfully deal with a very difficult, unlucky, or unpleasant situation.","c":"戰勝逆境、克服不幸","s":"Having lost both legs in a terrible accident, the brave athlete managed to overcome an adversity and eventually won a gold medal at the Paralympic Games.","t":"在一場可怕的事故中失去雙腿後，這位勇敢的運動員成功戰勝了逆境，並最終在帕拉林匹克運動會上贏得了金牌。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"transport – monumental","cards":[{"w":"transport","p":"v. / n.","d":"to carry goods or people from one place to another.","c":"運輸；運送","s":"The large cargo ships are specifically designed to safely transport thousands of heavy containers across the deep ocean.","t":"這些大型貨輪被專門設計來安全地跨越深海運輸數千個沉重的貨櫃。"},{"w":"transportation","p":"n.","d":"the action of transporting someone or something or the process of being transported.","c":"運輸；交通工具","s":"Because she doesn't own a car, Lisa relies entirely on public transportation to get to school every single morning.","t":"因為她沒有自己的車，麗莎每天早上完全依賴大眾運輸去上學。"},{"w":"public transportation","p":"phr.","d":"buses, trains, and other forms of transport that are available to the public.","c":"大眾運輸","s":"If you want to effectively reduce your daily carbon footprint, you should definitely start taking public transportation to work.","t":"如果你想有效地減少你每天的碳足跡，你絕對應該開始搭乘大眾運輸去上班。"},{"w":"means of transportation","p":"n.","d":"any system, vehicle, or method used for moving passengers or goods from one geographic location to another","c":"交通工具","s":"Utilizing public means of transportation like trains and buses can significantly minimize carbon emissions in crowded cities.","t":"利用火車和公車等大眾交通工具可以顯著減少擁擠城市的碳排放。"},{"w":"traffic congestion","p":"n.","d":"vehicles moving on a road or public highway.","c":"交通堵塞","s":"There was a traffic congestion on the highway today because a terrible accident blocked two major lanes.","t":"今天高速公路上有大量的車流，因為一場可怕的車禍堵住了兩個主要車道。"},{"w":"vehicle","p":"n.","d":"a thing used for transporting people or goods, especially on land.","c":"車輛；手段（媒介）","s":"There are far too many heavy vehicles on the road today, and that is rapidly causing the city's air quality to become significantly worse.","t":"今天路上的重型車輛實在太多了，而這正迅速導致城市的空氣品質變得明顯更糟。"},{"w":"electric vehicle","p":"phr.","d":"a vehicle which uses one or more electric motors for propulsion.","c":"電動車","s":"To help save the planet, the government is currently offering generous discounts to anyone who buys a clean, new electric vehicle.","t":"為了幫助拯救地球，政府目前正向任何購買乾淨全新電動車的人提供慷慨的折扣。"},{"w":"private vehicle","p":"n.","d":"a personal car, motorcycle, or transport device owned by an individual rather than used for public service","c":"私人車輛","s":"The smart apartment complex features a large automated garage designated specifically for each resident's private vehicle.","t":"這棟智慧公寓大樓擁有一個大型自動化車庫，專門供每位居民的私人車輛停放。"},{"w":"a vehicle for","p":"phr.","d":"a thing used to express, embody, or fulfill something.","c":"達成...的手段/媒介","s":"Most hardworking students intelligently view a university degree as an essential vehicle for eventually landing a highly successful and well-paying job.","t":"大多數努力的學生聰明地將大學學位視為最終獲得一份非常成功且高薪工作的重要手段。"},{"w":"depart from","p":"phr.","d":"to leave a specific place.","c":"從...出發/離開","s":"I unfortunately didn't meet Jack in person today because he had completely departed from his home very early this morning.","t":"我今天不幸地沒有親自見到傑克，因為他今天一大早就完全從家裡離開了。"},{"w":"depart for","p":"phr.","d":"to leave in order to go to a specific destination.","c":"出發前往...","s":"The ambitious boss is urgently packing her bags right now and will officially depart for Tokyo in less than four hours.","t":"雄心勃勃的老闆現在正緊急打包行李，並將在不到四小時內正式出發前往東京。"},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the action of leaving, typically to start a journey.","c":"離開；出發","s":"The angry passengers complained when they discovered that the busy train's time of departure had been unexpectedly delayed by thirty minutes.","t":"憤怒的乘客在發現這列繁忙火車的出發時間出乎意料地延誤了三十分鐘時，提出了抱怨。"},{"w":"arrive at","p":"phr.","d":"To reach a specific building, small place, or precise location.","c":"抵達、到達（特定地點/小地方）","s":"The tour bus will arrive at the hotel entrance at exactly eight o'clock, so please make sure you are waiting in the lobby.","t":"觀光巴士將在八點整抵達飯店門口，所以請確保您在大廳等候。"},{"w":"arrive in","p":"phr.","d":"To reach a large geographic area, such as a city, country, or town.","c":"抵達、到達（城市/國家/大地方）","s":"After a very long and exhausting flight across the ocean, the exchange students finally arrived in Tokyo to begin their winter study program.","t":"在經歷了一趟跨越海洋、漫長且令人筋疲力盡的飛行後，交換學生們終於抵達了東京，開始他們的冬季學習計畫。"},{"w":"arrival","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of arriving.","c":"抵達","s":"The excited children eagerly waited at the large airport gate for the safe arrival of their beloved grandparents from Canada.","t":"興奮的孩子們在大型機場登機門熱切地等待著他們深愛的祖父母從加拿大安全抵達。"},{"w":"estimated time of arrival","p":"phr.","d":"The time when a vehicle, plane, or person is expected to reach a destination.","c":"預計抵達時間","s":"Because the heavy snowstorm delayed our train, our estimated time of arrival has been changed from 6:00 p.m. to 8:30 p.m.","t":"因為大暴風雪延誤了我們的火車，我們的預計抵達時間已經從晚上六點更改為晚上八點半。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to bring something into existence.","c":"創造；建立","s":"The talented chef wanted to create a completely unique and delicious menu for the grand opening of his restaurant.","t":"這位才華洋溢的廚師想為他餐廳的盛大開幕創造一份完全獨特且美味的菜單。"},{"w":"creation","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of bringing something into existence.","c":"創造；發明","s":"The brilliant creation of the telephone made global communication much more convenient than anyone could have ever imagined.","t":"電話的卓越發明使全球通訊變得比任何人能想像的還要方便許多。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or involving the imagination or original ideas.","c":"有創意的","s":"The marketing team came up with a highly creative advertising campaign that quickly caught the attention of young consumers.","t":"行銷團隊提出了一個極具有創意的廣告活動，迅速引起了年輕消費者的注意。"},{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the use of the imagination or original ideas.","c":"創造力","s":"Teachers should always encourage their young students to express their natural creativity through engaging art and music projects.","t":"老師應該總是鼓勵年輕學生透過參與藝術和音樂專案來表達他們天生的創造力。"},{"w":"creature","p":"n.","d":"Any living being, such as an animal or insect, but not a plant.","c":"生物、動物","s":"Deep in the ocean, scientists discovered a strange creature that can glow in the dark to attract its food.","t":"在海洋深處，科學家們發現了一種能在黑暗中發光的奇特生物，以此來吸引牠的食物。"},{"w":"mythical creature","p":"phr.","d":"An imaginary animal or being from ancient stories and legends.","c":"神話生物、傳說中的生物","s":"The dragon is a famous mythical creature in many cultures, often representing power and wisdom in Eastern folklore.","t":"龍在許多文化中都是著名的神話生物，在東方民間傳說中通常代表著力量與智慧。"},{"w":"content creator","p":"n.","d":"A person who invents, makes, or produces informational knowledge","c":"內容創作者","s":"The talented content creator spent three days editing his travel video because he wanted to give his followers a high-quality experience.","t":"這位有才華的內容創作者花了三天時間剪輯他的旅遊影片，因為他想給他的追隨者們高質量的體驗。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activity done for enjoyment when one is not working.","c":"娛樂；休閒","s":"After a long and stressful week at the busy office, John usually plays golf for his weekend recreation.","t":"在繁忙的辦公室度過漫長且壓力大的一週後，約翰通常打高爾夫球作為他的週末休閒。"},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"Done for enjoyment or relaxation when you are not working.","c":"娛樂的、休閒的","s":"The city government built a new park with many recreational facilities, such as basketball courts and walking paths, for local residents.","t":"市政府建造了一座擁有許多休閒設施（例如籃球場和散步小徑）的新公園，供當地居民使用。"},{"w":"segment","p":"n. / v.","d":"each of the parts into which something is or may be divided.","c":"部分；分割","s":"A surprisingly small segment of this country's total population has unfortunately caught the terrible and highly infectious disease.","t":"令人驚訝的是，這個國家總人口中有一小部分不幸感染了這種可怕且高度傳染性的疾病。"},{"w":"market segment","p":"phr.","d":"a group of people who share one or more common characteristics for marketing purposes.","c":"市場區隔","s":"Our new cosmetic product is specifically designed to strongly appeal to a younger, more fashion-conscious market segment.","t":"我們的新化妝品專門設計來強烈吸引更年輕、更具時尚意識的市場區隔。"},{"w":"a segment of","p":"phr.","d":"a part or section of a whole.","c":"...的一部分","s":"Only a small segment of the movie was actually filmed outdoors, while the rest was completed in a studio.","t":"這部電影只有一小部分實際上是在戶外拍攝的，而其餘的都是在攝影棚內完成的。"},{"w":"dynasty","p":"n.","d":"a line of hereditary rulers of a country.","c":"朝代；王朝","s":"The knowledgeable historian explained that these incredibly beautiful paintings are originally from the powerful Ming dynasty.","t":"這位知識淵博的歷史學家解釋說，這些極其美麗的畫作最初來自強大的明朝（代）。"},{"w":"complete","p":"v.","d":"to finish making or doing","c":"完成","s":"You must carefully complete all the required safety training courses before you are officially allowed to operate the heavy machinery.","t":"在你被正式允許操作重型機械之前，你必須仔細完成所有必要的安全訓練課程。"},{"w":"complete","p":"adj.","d":"having all the necessary parts, elements, or steps, or being perfect and total in degree","c":"完全的；完整的","s":"The software engineering team managed to achieve complete control over the database after implementing the new automated security frameworks.","t":"在實施新的自動化安全架構後，軟體工程團隊成功實現了對資料庫的完全控制。"},{"w":"completion","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of finishing something.","c":"完成；完工","s":"Because of numerous unexpected delays, the massive building project took exactly ten years to finally achieve full completion.","t":"由於許多意想不到的延誤，這個龐大的建築專案花了整整十年才最終達成完全完工。"},{"w":"completely","p":"adv.","d":"totally; utterly.","c":"完全地","s":"After hiking through the dense jungle for eight hours without resting, the exhausted explorers were completely out of energy.","t":"在茂密的叢林中徒步八小時沒有休息後，疲憊的探險家完全地耗盡了精力。"},{"w":"achieve completion","p":"phr.","d":"to successfully finish a project or task.","c":"達成完工/完成","s":"The team worked diligently over the weekend so that the important software update could achieve completion before the deadline.","t":"團隊在週末勤奮地工作，以便這個重要的軟體更新能在截止日期前達成完工。"},{"w":"thorough","p":"adj.","d":"performed or written with great care, attention to detail, and a focus on leaving nothing incomplete","c":"徹底的；詳盡的","s":"The senior researcher requested a thorough evaluation of the participants' data to ensure the methodology was completely rigorous.","t":"高級研究員要求對參與者的數據進行徹底的評估，以確保研究方法完全嚴謹。"},{"w":"thoroughly","p":"adv.","d":"in a detailed, careful, and comprehensive manner that addresses every single part or aspect","c":"徹底地；詳盡地","s":"The medical board checked the patient's records thoroughly before authorizing the chief doctor to perform the major heart surgery.","t":"醫療委員會在授權主治醫生進行重大心臟手術之前，徹底地檢查了患者的紀錄。"},{"w":"milestone","p":"n.","d":"an action or event marking a significant change or stage in development.","c":"里程碑","s":"Our tech company reached an incredible milestone last year with the successful sale of our one millionth electronic product.","t":"我們的科技公司去年成功售出第一百萬件電子產品，達到了一個令人難以置信的里程碑。"},{"w":"reach a milestone","p":"phr.","d":"to achieve a significant stage in a process.","c":"達到里程碑","s":"The dedicated medical researchers will reach a major milestone if they can finally discover a cure for the disease.","t":"如果這些專注的醫學研究人員最終能發現該疾病的療法，他們將達到一個重大的里程碑。"},{"w":"historic milestone","p":"phr.","d":"an event of great historical importance.","c":"歷史性的里程碑","s":"Landing the first human on the surface of the moon was a historic milestone that completely changed space exploration forever.","t":"讓第一個人類登陸月球表面是一個徹底永遠改變太空探索的歷史性的里程碑。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"A famous building or object that is easily recognized and helps you know where you are.","c":"地標","s":"Taipei 101 is a famous landmark in Taiwan, and thousands of tourists visit it every year to enjoy the beautiful city view.","t":"台北101是台灣著名的地標，每年都有數千名遊客造訪，來欣賞美麗的城市景觀。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely important and marking a major change or turning point in history.","c":"里程碑式的、具重大歷史意義的","s":"The government signed a landmark agreement yesterday to reduce carbon emissions, which experts believe will greatly protect the environment.","t":"政府昨天簽署了一項具重大歷史意義的協議來減少碳排放，專家認為這將大大保護環境。"},{"w":"tourist destination","p":"phr.","d":"A place that many people travel to for a vacation or holiday.","c":"觀光勝地、旅遊目的地","s":"With its beautiful beaches and historic temples, Kyoto has become a popular tourist destination for travelers from all over the world.","t":"憑藉其美麗的海灘和歷史悠久的寺廟，京都已成為來自世界各地旅客的熱門旅遊目的地。"},{"w":"tourist attraction","p":"phr.","d":"A famous place that tourists like to visit, such as a museum, monument, or amusement park.","c":"觀光景點、旅遊景點","s":"The Eiffel Tower is a world-famous tourist attraction that draws millions of visitors to Paris every single year.","t":"艾菲爾鐵塔是世界聞名的觀光景點，每年都吸引數百萬名遊客前往巴黎。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"a sequence of continuous action in a play, movie, opera, or book; a landscape.","c":"場景；景色","s":"John unfortunately missed a highly crucial and dramatic scene in the movie when he quickly went to visit the crowded snack bar.","t":"當約翰迅速去擁擠的點心吧時，他不幸地錯過了電影中一個極其關鍵且戲劇性的場景。"},{"w":"crime scene","p":"n.","d":"the specific geographic location where an illegal act, violence, or offense has historically occurred","c":"犯罪現場","s":"The forensic investigators thoroughly examined the crime scene to collect valuable evidence before the military zone was closed.","t":"鑑識調查人員在軍事管制區關閉之前，徹底檢查了犯罪現場以蒐集寶貴的證據。"},{"w":"at the scene","p":"phr.","d":"being present right at the exact place where an event, accident, or specific incident occurred","c":"在現場","s":"The emergency medical technicians arrived quickly at the scene to provide immediate first aid to the domestic violence victims.","t":"緊急醫療技術人員迅速抵達現場，為家庭暴力受害者提供即時的急救。"},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural features of a landscape considered in terms of their appearance.","c":"風景；景色","s":"Before we safely drive back to the busy city, let's stop the car and take a beautiful picture of this magnificent scenery.","t":"在我們安全開車回到繁忙的城市之前，讓我們停下車，為這壯麗的風景拍張美麗的照片。"},{"w":"scenic","p":"adj.","d":"providing or relating to views of impressive or beautiful natural scenery.","c":"風景優美的","s":"The adventurous couple decided to slowly drive along the highly scenic coastal route to fully enjoy the absolutely breathtaking ocean views.","t":"這對喜歡冒險的夫婦決定沿著極其風景優美的沿海路線慢慢開車，以充分欣賞絕對令人驚嘆的海景。"},{"w":"scenic spot","p":"phr.","d":"A place known for its beautiful natural scenery, views, or landscapes.","c":"風景區、景點","s":"The travel guide recommends visiting this hidden scenic spot early in the morning so you can avoid the large crowds of noisy tourists.","t":"旅遊指南建議在一大早造訪這個隱藏的風景區（景點），這樣你就能避開大批吵鬧的遊客。"},{"w":"overlook the view","p":"v.","d":"take in the sight or natural scenery.","c":"俯瞰景色","s":"The expensive hotel suites at the top of the tall building overlook the view of the crystal clear blue ocean.","t":"在高聳建築頂端的昂貴飯店套房們俯瞰清澈的深藍色海洋景色。"},{"w":"sight-seeing / sightseeing","p":"n.","d":"The activity of visiting famous or interesting places, especially as a tourist.","c":"觀光、遊覽","s":"After finishing their important business meetings, the colleagues rented a car to do some sightseeing in the historic city center before flying back home.","t":"結束了重要的商務會議後，同事們租了一輛車在歷史悠久的市中心進行一些觀光（遊覽），然後才搭機返家。"},{"w":"go sightseeing","p":"phr.","d":"To travel around a place to see the interesting places and landmarks.","c":"去觀光、去遊覽","s":"If the weather is sunny tomorrow morning, we can go sightseeing along the beautiful coastline and take plenty of memorable photos.","t":"如果明天早上天氣晴朗，我們可以沿著美麗的海岸線去觀光，並拍下許多值得紀念的照片。"},{"w":"field trip","p":"n.","d":"a short journey made for pleasure, education, or physical exercise.","c":"郊遊；出遊","s":"Every single year, the generous technology company takes all of its hardworking employees on an exciting weekend field trip or an outing to the mountains.","t":"每一年，這家慷慨的科技公司都會帶領所有辛勤工作的員工到山裡進行一場刺激的週末出遊。"},{"w":"excursion","p":"n.","d":"A short journey or trip, usually for pleasure or education.","c":"（短途的）遠足、短途旅行","s":"Our high school organized a weekend excursion to the famous museum so that students could see the historical artifacts in person.","t":"我們的高中組織了一次去著名博物館的週末短途旅行（遠足），以便學生們能夠親自看到那些歷史文物。"},{"w":"expedition","p":"n.","d":"A long and carefully organized journey, often for scientific research or exploration.","c":"遠征、探險、考察隊","s":"The scientists planned a dangerous expedition to the Arctic to study how climate change is affecting the thick layers of ice.","t":"科學家們計畫了一次前往北極的危險考察（探險），以研究氣候變遷如何影響厚厚的冰層。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"To travel around a new place to learn about it or search for something.","c":"探索、探險、勘查","s":"When the tourists arrived at the ancient town, they decided to explore the narrow streets and discover hidden local shops.","t":"當遊客抵達這座古鎮時，他們決定去探索那些狹窄的街道並發掘隱藏的在地小店。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"The act of traveling through a place to learn about it or discover something new.","c":"探索、探測、研究","s":"Space exploration requires a massive amount of money and advanced technology, but it can help humans find potential resources on other planets.","t":"太空探索需要大量的資金和先進的科技，但它可以幫助人類在其他星球上尋找潛在的資源。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v. / n.","d":"to travel some distance between one's home and place of work on a regular basis.","c":"通勤","s":"Because of the terrible traffic, it usually takes Jane more than an hour to commute between her school and home.","t":"因為糟糕的交通，珍通常要花一個多小時在她的學校和家之間通勤。"},{"w":"commuter","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels some distance to work on a regular basis.","c":"通勤者","s":"During the incredibly busy morning rush hour, thousands of tired commuters pack tightly into the subway trains heading downtown.","t":"在極其繁忙的早晨尖峰時段，成千上萬疲憊的通勤者緊緊地擠進開往市中心的捷運列車中。"},{"w":"commuting","p":"n.","d":"the activity of traveling regularly between one's place of residence and place of work or study","c":"每日通勤；上下班往返","s":"Relying on public transit can significantly minimize the overall stress of daily commuting during the busy morning rush hour.","t":"在 busy morning rush hour 時段，依賴大眾運輸工具可以顯著減少每日通勤的整體壓力。"},{"w":"telecommute","p":"v.","d":"to work from home, making use of the internet, email, and the telephone.","c":"遠距辦公","s":"Thanks to highly advanced digital technology, many employees can now smoothly telecommute from the comfort of their own living rooms.","t":"多虧了高度先進的數位科技，許多員工現在可以順利地在自己舒適的客廳裡遠距辦公。"},{"w":"fulfill","p":"v.","d":"to bring to completion or reality; achieve or realize.","c":"實現；履行","s":"Unfortunately, lazy Bill never actually fulfilled my simple request to completely clean out the dirty garage on Sunday afternoon.","t":"不幸的是，懶惰的比爾從未實際履行我在星期天下午徹底清理骯髒車庫的簡單要求。"},{"w":"fulfill the dream","p":"phr.","d":"to achieve something that one has long desired.","c":"實現夢想","s":"Next year, courageous Lisa confidently plans to travel across India to finally fulfill the dream of seeing the world.","t":"明年，勇敢的麗莎自信地計畫穿越印度去旅行，以最終實現她看世界的夢想。"},{"w":"carry out the objective","p":"phr.","d":"to act upon and achieve one's aspirations.","c":"實踐目標","s":"It requires an immense amount of dedication and consistent hard work to successfully carry out the objective in reality.","t":"要在現實中成功實踐某人的目標，需要大量的奉獻精神和持續的努力工作。"},{"w":"fulfilling","p":"adj.","d":"making someone satisfied or happy because of fully developing their abilities.","c":"令人滿足的；有成就感的","s":"Teaching young children how to read and write is a highly fulfilling career that brings her a lot of daily joy.","t":"教導幼童如何閱讀和寫作是一份高度有成就感的職業，每天為她帶來許多快樂。"},{"w":"unfulfilled","p":"adj.","d":"not carried out or brought to completion.","c":"未實現的","s":"Despite achieving massive financial success, the wealthy businessman still felt deeply unfulfilled because he never pursued his artistic passions.","t":"儘管獲得了巨大的財務成功，這位富有的商人仍然感到深深的未實現的（不滿足的），因為他從未追求他的藝術熱情。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"the achievement of something desired, promised, or predicted.","c":"實現；滿足感","s":"After years of intense study and hard work, passing the medical exam brought him a deep sense of personal fulfillment.","t":"經過多年的密集學習和努力工作，通過醫學考試為他帶來了深深的個人滿足感。"},{"w":"scenic spot","p":"phr.","d":"A place known for its beautiful natural scenery, views, or landscapes.","c":"風景區、景點","s":"We stopped at a quiet scenic spot along the mountain highway to take pictures of the breathtaking green valley below.","t":"我們在山區公路旁一個安靜的風景區停了下來，拍下下方令人屏息的綠色山谷照片。"},{"w":"a sense of fulfillment","p":"phr.","d":"A feeling of happiness and deep satisfaction because you are doing something meaningful or useful.","c":"滿足感、成就感","s":"Volunteering at the local animal shelter gives Chloe a sense of fulfillment because she loves helping helpless dogs find new homes.","t":"在當地動物庇護所當志工帶給克洛伊一種滿足感，因為她喜歡幫助無助的狗狗找到新家。"},{"w":"a sense of achievement","p":"phr.","d":"A proud and happy feeling when you successfully complete something difficult through effort.","c":"成就感","s":"After studying hard for several months, passing the advanced English exam gave Leo a sense of achievement that made his parents very proud.","t":"在努力讀書幾個月之後，通過高級英文考試給了里歐一種成就感，這讓他的父母感到非常自豪。"},{"w":"a sense of accomplishment","p":"phr.","d":"A feeling of satisfaction from finishing a specific task or reaching a major goal.","c":"成就感","s":"Completing the twenty-kilometer marathon gave the young runner a sense of accomplishment, even though his legs were extremely sore and tired.","t":"完成這場二十公里的馬拉松給了這位年輕跑者一種成就感，儘管他的雙腿非常酸痛且疲憊。"},{"w":"timber","p":"n.","d":"wood prepared for use in building and carpentry.","c":"木材","s":"Because it has massive tropical forests, high-quality timber remains one of Brazil's biggest and most profitable international exports.","t":"因為擁有巨大的熱帶森林，高品質的木材仍然是巴西最大、最賺錢的國際出口產品之一。"},{"w":"lumber","p":"n.","d":"timber sawn into rough planks or otherwise partly prepared.","c":"木材（尤指鋸好的）","s":"My father happily bought a large amount of sturdy lumber from the hardware store in order to build a beautiful wooden porch.","t":"我父親高興地從五金行買了大量堅固的木材，為了建造一個美麗的木製門廊。"},{"w":"log","p":"n.","d":"a part of the trunk or a large branch of a tree that has fallen or been cut off.","c":"圓木；原木","s":"The strong lumberjacks worked tirelessly all day to efficiently transport these massive logs to the factory to safely make paper.","t":"強壯的伐木工人不知疲倦地工作了一整天，有效率地將這些巨大的圓木運送到工廠去安全地造紙。"},{"w":"express","p":"n./adj.","d":"a rapid and efficient postal or delivery service designed to transport packages or goods very quickly","c":"快遞；快捷的","s":"Utilizing the international express service allowed the ambitious entrepreneur to deliver the portable devices to global clients within 48 hours.","t":"利用國際快遞服務，讓這位雄心勃勃的企業家得以在 48 小時內將便攜式裝置送達全球客戶手中。"},{"w":"freight","p":"n.","d":"goods transported in bulk by truck, train, ship, or aircraft.","c":"貨物；貨運","s":"The experienced logistics manager explained that ground freight generally takes exactly twice the amount of time as flying things by air.","t":"經驗豐富的物流經理解釋說，陸路貨運通常需要整整兩倍於空運物品的時間。"},{"w":"cargo","p":"n.","d":"goods or merchandise carried on a large vehicle, such as a commercial ship, aircraft, or motor vehicle","c":"（大型交通工具裝載的）貨物","s":"The massive container ship slowly arrived at the port, carrying tons of valuable cargo from the international technology corporation.","t":"這艘巨大的貨櫃船緩慢抵達港口，載著來自這家國際科技公司價值不菲的貨物。"},{"w":"harbor","p":"n.","d":"a sheltered area of water next to the land where commercial ships or private boats can safely anchor","c":"港灣；港口","s":"The experienced captain carefully steered the large ocean vessel into the peaceful harbor before the severe winter storm arrived.","t":"在嚴重的冬季暴風雨來臨之前，經驗豐富的船長小心翼翼地將這艘大型海洋船隻駛入寧靜的港灣。"},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or city with a harbor where commercial ships load or unload cargo smoothly","c":"港口；港市","s":"The massive container ship slowly docked at the busy port, ready to unload tons of commercial goods.","t":"這艘巨大的貨櫃船緩慢停靠在繁忙的港口，準備卸下數噸的商業貨物。"},{"w":"import","p":"v.","d":"to bring goods, merchandise, or services into a country from abroad for commercial sale","c":"進口","s":"The international corporation plans to import luxury automobiles from Europe to satisfy the growing local demand.","t":"這家國際公司計劃從歐洲進口豪華汽車，以滿足日益增長的本地需求。"},{"w":"tariff","p":"n.","d":"a tax or duty imposed by a government on imported or exported goods to protect domestic industries","c":"關税","s":"The new government policy imposed a strict tariff on electronic products, causing significant friction in international trade.","t":"新政府政策對電子產品徵收嚴格的關稅，在國際貿易中引起了顯著的摩擦。"},{"w":"goods","p":"n.","d":"merchandise or possessions.","c":"貨物；商品","s":"The busy international port efficiently handles millions of tons of imported and exported goods from all around the globe daily.","t":"這個繁忙的國際港口每天有效率地處理數百萬噸來自全球各地的進出口貨物。"},{"w":"imported goods","p":"n.","d":"products, merchandise, or commodities that are brought into a country from a foreign nation","c":"進口貨物","s":"The customs officers thoroughly inspected all the imported goods to ensure they complied with national safety regulations.","t":"海關官員徹底檢查了所有進口貨物，以確保它們符合國家安全法規。"},{"w":"export","p":"v.","d":"to send goods, merchandise, or services to another country for international sale or trade","c":"出口","s":"Taiwan's technology sector continues to export high-quality electronic components and portable devices to markets worldwide.","t":"台灣的科技部門持續向全球市場出口高品質的電子元件與便攜式裝置。"},{"w":"exported goods","p":"n.","d":"products, merchandise, or commodities sent to a foreign country for commercial sale","c":"出口貨物","s":"The logistics company arranged for an express delivery service to transport the exported goods to the harbor safely.","t":"這家物流公司安排了快捷的快遞服務，以將這些出口貨物安全地運送到港灣。"},{"w":"commodity","p":"n.","d":"a raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold.","c":"商品；原物料","s":"The manager confidently stated that every single new item our factories can make is another valuable commodity we can effectively trade.","t":"經理自信地表示，我們工廠能製造的每一件新物品，都是我們可以有效交易的另一項有價值的商品。"},{"w":"product","p":"n.","d":"an article or substance that is manufactured or refined for sale.","c":"產品","s":"The highly innovative technology company is preparing to launch a revolutionary new product that will completely change the digital market.","t":"這家高度創新的科技公司正準備推出一款將徹底改變數位市場的革命性新產品。"},{"w":"fresh produce","p":"n.","d":"Fresh fruits and vegetables that are grown for food and sold to consumers.","c":"新鮮蔬果、生鮮農產品","s":"My mother always goes to the local traditional market early in the morning, and she always chooses the best fresh produce to cook a healthy dinner for our family.","t":"我母親總是在大清早去當地的傳統市場，而且她總是挑選最好的新鮮蔬果來為我們全家煮一頓健康的晚餐。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"To make, grow, or supply things, especially in large quantities.","c":"生產、製造、出產","s":"The factory has upgraded its machines, so it can now produce thousands of eco-friendly water bottles every day to meet the increasing demand.","t":"這家工廠已經升級了機器，因此現在每天可以生產數千個環保水瓶，以滿足日益增長的需求。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"Achieving a lot or producing a good amount of useful results.","c":"富有成效的、有生產力的","s":"Since she started planning her schedule every morning, Chloe has become much more productive and always finishes her assignments before dinner.","t":"自從她開始每天早上規劃自己的行程表以來，克洛伊變得富有成效得多，且總是在晚餐前完成她的作業。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"The rate at which a worker, company, or country completes tasks or produces goods.","c":"生產力、生產效率","s":"The manager introduced a new flexible working hours policy because he believed it would improve employee productivity and happiness.","t":"經理引入了新的彈性工作時間政策，因為他相信這能提升員工的生產力（生產效率）與幸福感。"},{"w":"merchandise","p":"n.","d":"Goods or products that are bought and sold in a business or store.","c":"商品、貨物","s":"The pop singer's official website offers a lot of exclusive merchandise, such as t-shirts, keychains, and posters for her loyal fans.","t":"這位流行歌手的官方網站為她的忠實粉絲提供了許多獨家商品，例如T恤、鑰匙圈和海報。"},{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to cease to support or look after; desert.","c":"放棄；拋棄","s":"When the old car suddenly broke down on the dark highway, the frustrated driver foolishly abandoned it on the side of the road.","t":"當這輛舊車在黑暗的高速公路上突然拋錨時，受挫的司機愚蠢地把它拋棄在路邊。"},{"w":"abandoned","p":"adj.","d":"having been deserted or cast off.","c":"被拋棄的；廢棄的","s":"The adventurous teenagers bravely decided to cautiously explore the creepy abandoned hospital that had been completely empty for twenty years.","t":"愛冒險的青少年勇敢地決定小心探索那家已經完全空了二十年、令人毛骨悚然的廢棄的醫院。"},{"w":"desert","p":"v.","d":"to leave a person, place, or organization in a way that is considered disloyal.","c":"離棄；擅離職守","s":"All of Steve's supposedly loyal friends cruelly deserted him when he lost his job and desperately needed their help the most.","t":"當史蒂夫失業且最極度需要他們的幫助時，所有他所謂忠誠的朋友都殘酷地離棄了他。"},{"w":"deserted","p":"adj.","d":"Empty of people; with no one there.","c":"荒涼的、空無一人的、被遺棄的","s":"The old amusement park has been deserted for years, and now the broken rides are covered in wild plants and weeds.","t":"這座舊遊樂園已經空無一人（被遺棄）多年了，現在損壞的遊樂設施都被野生植物和雜草覆蓋了。"},{"w":"desert","p":"n.","d":"A large, dry area of land with very little water or plants, usually covered with sand.","c":"沙漠","s":"Camels are perfectly adapted to live in the harsh desert, because they can travel for many days without drinking any water.","t":"駱駝完美地適應了在惡劣的沙漠中生活，因為牠們可以在不喝任何水的情況下旅行許多天。"},{"w":"dessert","p":"n.","d":"Sweet food eaten at the end of a meal.","c":"甜點","s":"Even though I was completely full after eating the large steak, I still ordered a delicious chocolate dessert because I have a sweet tooth.","t":"儘管吃完大牛排後我已經完全飽了，但我還是點了一份美味的巧克力甜點，因為我非常喜歡吃甜食。"},{"w":"quit","p":"v.","d":"to leave usually permanently.","c":"戒除:辭職；放棄","s":"The doctor strictly warned him that he must permanently quit smoking immediately for the sake of his failing physical health.","t":"醫生嚴格警告他，為了他不斷衰退的身體健康，他必須立刻永久地放棄吸菸。"},{"w":"motor","p":"n. / adj.","d":"a machine that supplies motive power for a vehicle or for some other device.","c":"馬達；汽車的","s":"The mechanic explained that my car would not start because there was obviously a serious mechanical problem with the expensive motor.","t":"技師解釋說我的車發不動了，因為顯然那個昂貴的馬達有嚴重的機械問題。"},{"w":"motorist","p":"n.","d":"the driver of an automobile.","c":"汽車駕駛","s":"The local police strongly advised every motorist to carefully slow down and drive safely during the unexpectedly heavy winter snowstorm.","t":"當地警方強烈建議每一位汽車駕駛在出乎意料的強烈冬季暴風雪中小心減速並安全駕駛。"},{"w":"motorcyclist","p":"n.","d":"a rider of a motorcycle.","c":"機車騎士","s":"The injured motorcyclist was rushed to the hospital after he unfortunately slipped on the wet road and heavily crashed into a tree.","t":"受傷的機車騎士在濕滑的道路上不幸滑倒並重重撞上樹後，被緊急送往醫院。"},{"w":"automobile","p":"n.","d":"a road vehicle, typically with four wheels, powered by an internal combustion engine or electric motor","c":"汽車","s":"Purchasing an electric automobile has become increasingly popular among city residents who want to reduce environmental pollution.","t":"在想要減少環境污染的城市居民中，購買電動汽車已經變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"w":"mobile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move or be moved freely and easily, or relating to wireless mobile technology","c":"可移動的；行動式的","s":"The technology corporation developed a new mobile application to help busy commuters track train schedules in real time.","t":"這家科技公司開發了一款全新的行動應用程式，以幫助忙碌的通勤族即時追蹤火車時刻表。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be easily carried or moved, especially because of being a lighter and smaller version than usual","c":"手提式的；便攜式的","s":"The experienced traveler always brings a portable charger to ensure his digital devices never run out of battery during long trips.","t":"經驗豐富的旅行者總是會帶一個便攜式充電器，以確保他的數位設備在長途旅行中絕不會耗盡電量。"},{"w":"portable charger","p":"n.","d":"a lightweight and compact external battery pack used to power electronics while traveling","c":"行動電源","s":"The experienced traveler always brings a portable charger to ensure his digital devices never run out of battery during long trips.","t":"經驗豐富的旅行者總是會帶一個便攜式充電器，以確保他的數位設備在長途旅行中絕不會耗盡電量。"},{"w":"portable device","p":"n.","d":"any small, lightweight electronic apparatus or gadget designed to be easily carried or operated by hand","c":"便攜式裝置；行動設備","s":"The software engineering firm specifically developed a new mobile application to run smoothly on every portable device.","t":"該軟體工程公司特別開發了一款全新的行動應用程式，以便在每台便攜式裝置上順利運行。"},{"w":"device","p":"n.","d":"a specialized mechanism, piece of equipment, or tool designed for a specific practical purpose","c":"裝置；設備；器具","s":"The tech corporation created an automated device to help busy commuters track their local public transit schedules in real time.","t":"這家科技公司創建了一個自動化裝置，以幫助忙碌的通勤族即時追蹤當地的公共運輸時刻表。"},{"w":"devise","p":"v.","d":"to carefully plan, invent, or design a complex methodology, strategy, or system through creative thinking","c":"構思；想出；設計","s":"The leading researcher spent several months attempting to devise a rigorous methodology to protect indigenous wild animal species.","t":"首席研究員花了幾個月的時間，試圖構思出一套嚴謹的研究方法來保護當地的野生動物物種。"},{"w":"mechanic","p":"n.","d":"a skilled worker who repairs and maintains automobile engines, heavy machinery, or mechanical devices","c":"技工；機械工","s":"The experienced mechanic thoroughly inspected the imported automobile to find the source of the engine failure.","t":"經驗豐富的技工徹底檢查了那輛進口汽車，以找出引擎故障的源頭。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, operated by, or caused by machinery, automated tools, or physical moving parts","c":"機械的；機械製的","s":"The international tech corporation devises advanced mechanical arms to increase efficiency in its automated factories.","t":"這家國際科技公司設計了先進的機械手臂，以提高其自動化工廠的效率。"},{"w":"manual","p":"n..","d":"a handbook of instructions","c":"使用手冊","s":"The technician checked the operation manual to learn how to fix the database errors on the new portable device.","t":"技術人員查看了操作手冊，以了解如何修復這台全新可攜式裝置上的資料庫錯誤。"},{"w":"manual","p":"adj.","d":"involving physical work done with hands rather than automated computers or electronic devices","c":"手工的；用手操作的","s":"The traditional workers had to endure long hours of heavy manual labor in the import warehouse before automated cranes were deployed.","t":"在部署自動化起重機之前，傳統工人必須在進口倉庫裡忍受長達數小時的沉重手工勞動。"},{"w":"manually","p":"adv.","d":"operated or done by a person using their hands directly, rather than by an automated system or machine","c":"用手地；手動地","s":"Because the automated database system suddenly failed, the logistics staff had to input every single zip code manually to sort the express packages.","t":"由於自動化資料庫系統突然故障，物流人員必須手動輸入每一個郵遞區號來為快捷包裹分類。"},{"w":"bless","p":"v.","d":"to ask for God's help and protection for someone or something.","c":"祝福；賜福","s":"The kind priest warmly blessed all of the hopeful people who had quietly gathered inside the beautifully decorated historical church.","t":"善良的神父溫暖地祝福了所有安靜地聚集在裝飾美麗的歷史教堂內滿懷希望的人們。"},{"w":"blessing","p":"n.","d":"God's favor and protection.","c":"祝福；幸事","s":"Discovering that the serious medical test results were completely negative was a true blessing for the terrified young woman and her family.","t":"發現嚴肅的醫學檢查結果完全是陰性的，對這位受驚的年輕女子及其家人來說是一件真正的幸事。"},{"w":"be blessed with","p":"phr.","d":"to have a lot of a good or desirable thing.","c":"有幸擁有...","s":"Eric is always blessed with an incredibly great job, a beautifully comfortable home, and a loving family that fully supports him.","t":"艾瑞克總是有幸擁有一份極好的工作、一個美麗舒適的家，以及一個完全支持他的充滿愛的家庭。"},{"w":"give his blessing","p":"phr.","d":"to give approval or support.","c":"給予准許/支持","s":"Ben's wealthy father finally decided to give his blessing for him to responsibly take a year off from medical school to travel independently.","t":"班富有的父親終於決定給予他的准許，讓他負責任地從醫學院休學一年去獨立旅行。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the arrangement of and relations between the parts or elements of something complex.","c":"結構；建築物","s":"The massive concrete parking structure is designed to easily hold up to 500 cars for people visiting the busy downtown shopping mall.","t":"這座巨大的混凝土停車建築物被設計來輕鬆容納多達500輛車，供參觀繁忙市中心購物中心的人們使用。"},{"w":"structural","p":"adj.","d":"of, relating to, or forming part of the structure of a building.","c":"結構的","s":"The powerful earthquake sadly caused severe structural damage to several historic buildings, making them completely unsafe for people to enter.","t":"強烈的地震令人遺憾地對幾座歷史建築造成了嚴重的結構的破壞，使人們進入其中完全不安全。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities.","c":"基礎建設","s":"The ambitious mayor promised to finally repair the city's aging infrastructure, which desperately needs better roads and safer bridges for the citizens.","t":"雄心勃勃的市長承諾將最終修復這座城市老舊的基礎建設，公民們極度需要更好的道路和更安全的橋樑。"},{"w":"monument","p":"n.","d":"a statue, building, or other structure erected to commemorate a famous or notable person or event.","c":"紀念碑","s":"The tall, majestic Statue of Liberty is widely considered one of America's most deeply famous and instantly recognizable historical monuments.","t":"高大雄偉的自由女神像被廣泛認為是美國最深具盛名且最能立即被認出的歷史紀念碑之一。"},{"w":"monumental","p":"adj.","d":"great in importance, extent, or size.","c":"具紀念性的；巨大的","s":"Rebuilding the completely destroyed city after the terrifying war was a truly monumental task that required everyone's persistent hard work and cooperation.","t":"在可怕的戰爭後重建被徹底摧毀的城市是一項真正巨大的任務，需要每個人的持續努力和合作。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"bulletproof – unprecedented","cards":[{"w":"bulletproof","p":"adj.","d":"designed to resist the penetration of bullets.","c":"防彈的","s":"The courageous police officer survived the dangerous shooting entirely because he was wearing a heavy bulletproof vest under his uniform.","t":"這名勇敢的警官之所以能在危險的槍擊事件中倖存，完全是因為他在制服下穿了一件沉重的防彈的背心。"},{"w":"fireproof","p":"adj.","d":"able to withstand fire or great heat.","c":"防火的","s":"Important government documents are typically stored securely inside a massive fireproof safe to ensure they are protected during an emergency.","t":"重要的政府文件通常安全地存放在一個巨大的防火的保險箱內，以確保它們在緊急情況下受到保護。"},{"w":"waterproof","p":"adj.","d":"impervious to water.","c":"防水的","s":"Ryan always carried a bright yellow waterproof jacket in his backpack just in case it suddenly rained during his long hike.","t":"萊恩總是在背包裡帶著一件亮黃色的防水的外套，以防在他長途徒步時突然下雨。"},{"w":"water-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"able to resist the penetration of water to some degree but not entirely.","c":"抗水的；防潑水的","s":"The new smart watch is water-resistant, meaning you can wear it while washing your hands, but you shouldn't swim with it.","t":"這款新的智慧型手錶是抗水的，這意味著你洗手時可以戴著它，但你不應該戴著它游泳。"},{"w":"heat-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"able to withstand high temperatures without being damaged.","c":"耐熱的","s":"When you are taking the hot baking pan out of the oven, make absolutely sure to use thick heat-resistant gloves.","t":"當你把熱烤盤從烤箱拿出來時，務必確保使用厚實的耐熱的手套。"},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to withstand the action or effect of.","c":"抵抗；忍住","s":"When I saw the delicious chocolate cake on the table, I simply couldn't resist eating a massive slice before dinner.","t":"當我看到桌上美味的巧克力蛋糕時，我就是無法忍住在晚餐前吃下一大塊。"},{"w":"resistant","p":"adj.","d":"offering resistance to something or someone.","c":"有抵抗力的；抗...的","s":"These specific vegetables were genetically engineered by scientists to be much more resistant to disease and harsh weather conditions.","t":"這些特定的蔬菜是由科學家進行基因工程改造的，對疾病和惡劣天氣條件更具有抵抗力的。"},{"w":"resistance","p":"n.","d":"the refusal to accept or comply with something.","c":"抵抗（力）；阻力","s":"Despite facing fierce political resistance from the conservative party, the new educational reform law was eventually passed by the government.","t":"儘管面臨來自保守黨激烈的政治阻力，新的教育改革法案最終還是被政府通過了。"},{"w":"severe","p":"adj.","d":"of something bad or undesirable: very great, intense, or harsh.","c":"嚴重的；嚴厲的","s":"The judge announced that the legal punishment for intentionally cheating on the important national exam would be extremely severe.","t":"法官宣布，故意在重要的國家考試中作弊的法律懲罰將會極度嚴厲的。"},{"w":"severely","p":"adv.","d":"to an undesirably great or intense degree.","c":"嚴重地","s":"The historic downtown area was severely damaged by the powerful earthquake, and it will cost billions of dollars to rebuild.","t":"歷史悠久的市中心地區被強烈地震嚴重地破壞，重建將花費數十億美元。"},{"w":"severity","p":"n.","d":"the fact or condition of being severe.","c":"嚴重性","s":"The inexperienced hikers completely underestimated the severity of the approaching winter storm and unfortunately became trapped on the mountain.","t":"缺乏經驗的登山客完全低估了逼近的冬季風暴的嚴重性，不幸地被困在山上。"},{"w":"severe storm","p":"phr.","d":"very bad and destructive weather.","c":"強烈風暴","s":"The local news station strongly advised all residents to stay safely indoors during the incredibly severe storm that was coming.","t":"當地新聞台強烈建議所有居民在即將到來的極其強烈風暴期間安全地待在室內。"},{"w":"severe pain","p":"phr.","d":"physical suffering or discomfort caused by illness or injury that is very intense.","c":"劇痛","s":"After heavily falling off his bicycle, Julian experienced severe pain in his right leg and had to visit the hospital.","t":"騎腳踏車重重摔倒後，朱利安的右腿感到劇痛，必須去醫院就診。"},{"w":"natural disaster","p":"phr.","d":"An extreme event like a flood, earthquake, or storm that causes great damage or loss of life.","c":"自然災害、天災","s":"The government has prepared emergency supply kits to ensure that citizens can survive if a major natural disaster strikes the region unexpectedly.","t":"政府已經準備了緊急物資包，以確保如果該地區意外遭受重大自然災害（天災）時，市民能夠存活下來。"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a prolonged period of abnormally low rainfall, leading to a shortage of water.","c":"乾旱","s":"We desperately hoped for much more rain this summer since our farming village had a terrible drought the previous year.","t":"我們極度希望今年夏天能下更多雨，因為我們的農村前一年發生了可怕的乾旱。"},{"w":"famine","p":"n.","d":"extreme scarcity of food.","c":"饑荒","s":"The prolonged lack of rain not only destroyed the crops but also caused a devastating famine across the entire African region.","t":"長期缺乏降雨不僅摧毀了農作物，還在整個非洲地區引發了毀滅性的饑荒。"},{"w":"wildfire","p":"n.","d":"a large, destructive fire that spreads quickly over woodland or brush.","c":"野火","s":"Driven by strong winds, the massive wildfire quickly destroyed thousands of acres of ancient forest in just a few short days.","t":"在強風的推波助瀾下，巨大的野火在短短幾天內迅速摧毀了數千英畝的古老森林。"},{"w":"mudslide","p":"n.","d":"a mass of mud and other earthy material that is falling or has fallen down a hillside.","c":"土石流","s":"Heavy rainfall over the weekend completely saturated the steep mountain, eventually triggering a dangerous mudslide that blocked the main highway.","t":"週末的強降雨完全浸透了陡峭的山體，最終引發了危險的土石流，堵塞了主要高速公路。"},{"w":"dust storm","p":"phr.","d":"a meteorological phenomenon common in arid and semi-arid regions.","c":"沙塵暴","s":"The travelers had to quickly cover their faces to protect their eyes and lungs when a sudden dust storm swept through the desert.","t":"當突如其來的沙塵暴席捲沙漠時，旅行者不得不迅速遮住臉以保護眼睛和肺部。"},{"w":"tsunami","p":"n.","d":"A giant ocean wave caused by an earthquake under the sea.","c":"海嘯","s":"Following a massive undersea earthquake, the coastal city issued an emergency warning because a destructive tsunami was rapidly approaching the shore.","t":"在一場巨大的海底地震之後，這座沿海城市發布了緊急警報，因為一場具破壞性的海嘯正迅速逼近海岸。"},{"w":"cyclone","p":"n.","d":"A violent tropical storm with very strong winds that rotate around a center.","c":"氣旋、熱帶風暴","s":"The powerful cyclone caused severe damage to the island nations in the Indian Ocean, tearing down power lines and destroying houses.","t":"這場強烈的氣旋對印度洋的島國造成了嚴重的破壞，扯斷了供電線路並摧毀了房屋。"},{"w":"typhoon","p":"n.","d":"A violent tropical storm with extremely strong winds and heavy rain that occurs in the Western Pacific.","c":"颱風","s":"Classes and work were canceled across Taiwan because a strong typhoon was expected to bring dangerous winds and flooding this weekend.","t":"全台停班停課，因為預計這週末一場強烈颱風將帶來危險的強風和洪水。"},{"w":"hurricane","p":"n.","d":"A violent tropical storm with extremely strong winds that occurs in the Atlantic Ocean.","c":"颶風","s":"Residents living near the Gulf of Mexico evacuated their homes before the massive hurricane made landfall with dangerous storm surges.","t":"居住在墨西哥灣附近的居民在這場巨大的颶風帶著危險的暴潮登陸之前，紛紛撤離了他們的家園。"},{"w":"tornado","p":"n.","d":"A violent, spinning column of air that stretches from a dark cloud to the ground.","c":"龍捲風","s":"The terrifying tornado ripped through the small town in just a few minutes, lifting cars into the air and damaging buildings.","t":"那場可怕的龍捲風在短短幾分鐘內席捲了這座小鎮，將汽車捲入空中並損毀了建築物。"},{"w":"landslide","p":"n.","d":"A large mass of rocks and earth that suddenly slides down a mountain or cliff.","c":"土石流、山崩","s":"After the heavy rainfall hit the mountain village, a sudden landslide blocked the main road and trapped many residents in their homes.","t":"在暴雨襲擊山村之後，一場突如其來的山崩（土石流）堵住了主要道路，將許多居民困在自己家中。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"Everything you can see when you look across a large area of land.","c":"風景、景色、自然景觀","s":"As the train moved through the countryside, passengers enjoyed the beautiful green landscape filled with rolling hills and traditional farms.","t":"當火車穿過鄉間時，乘客們欣賞著充滿起伏山丘和傳統農莊的蔚藍美麗綠色自然景觀（風景）。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"an overflow of a large amount of water beyond its normal limits.","c":"洪水","s":"After an entire week of continuous heavy rain, the anxious town next to the river began to seriously worry about flood.","t":"經過整整一星期的持續大雨，河邊焦慮的城鎮開始嚴重擔心洪水。"},{"w":"flood","p":"v.","d":"to cover or submerge a place with water in a flood.","c":"淹沒；氾濫","s":"The muddy waters of the river often flood the nearby low-lying fields and roads during the intensely wet rainy season.","t":"在極度潮濕的雨季，河流泥濘的河水經常淹沒附近低窪的田野和道路。"},{"w":"flooded","p":"adj.","d":"covered or submerged with water.","c":"被淹沒的","s":"The rescue workers bravely used small rubber boats to rescue the trapped families from their completely flooded homes in the valley.","t":"救援人員勇敢地使用小型橡皮艇，將受困家庭從山谷中完全被淹沒的家園中救出。"},{"w":"flash flood","p":"phr.","d":"a sudden local flood, typically due to heavy rain.","c":"山洪爆發","s":"You must never camp directly in a dry riverbed because a deadly flash flood can unexpectedly happen without any warning whatsoever.","t":"你絕不能直接在乾涸的河床露營，因為致命的山洪爆發可能會在沒有任何警告的情況下出乎意料地發生。"},{"w":"flood the market","p":"phr.","d":"to bring a huge number of things to a place to sell.","c":"充斥市場","s":"Cheaper electronic products from overseas competitors have begun to flood the market and seriously threaten our local technology businesses.","t":"來自海外競爭對手較便宜的電子產品已經開始充斥市場，並嚴重威脅我們當地的科技企業。"},{"w":"toll","p":"n.","d":"the number of deaths, casualties, or injuries arising from particular circumstances.","c":"傷亡人數","s":"The tragic earthquake was so incredibly destructive that the exact death toll has not yet been accurately counted by officials.","t":"這場悲慘的地震如此具毀滅性，以至於官方尚未準確統計出確切的死亡傷亡人數。"},{"w":"pay a toll","p":"phr.","d":"to pay a fee to use a particular road or bridge.","c":"付通行費","s":"The angry drivers had to wait in a long line just to pay a toll to cross the newly built suspension bridge.","t":"憤怒的駕駛必須排很長的隊，只為了付通行費以穿過新建的吊橋。"},{"w":"take a toll on","p":"phr.","d":"to have a bad effect on someone or something over a long period.","c":"對...造成傷害","s":"Chronic sleep deprivation and social media addiction take a toll on many teenagers' mental and physical health.","t":"慢性睡眠缺乏和社群媒體成癮症傷害很多青少年的身心健康"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities needed for the operation of a society.","c":"基礎建設","s":"A significant portion of the infrastructure in this old industrial city is outdated and desperately needs to be completely repaired.","t":"這座古老工業城市中很大一部分的基礎建設已經過時，極度需要徹底修復。"},{"w":"public infrastructure","p":"phr.","d":"facilities and systems serving a country, city, or area.","c":"公共基礎建設","s":"The ambitious new mayor promised to dramatically improve the public infrastructure by building modern hospitals and better public schools.","t":"雄心勃勃的新市長承諾將透過建造現代化醫院和更好的公立學校來大幅改善公共基礎建設。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to reduce to a state of ruin or destroy.","c":"毀壞；破壞","s":"The expensive library book is completely ruined because you carelessly left it outside all night in the pouring rain.","t":"這本昂貴的圖書館書籍完全被毀壞了，因為你粗心地把它留在外面淋了一整晚的傾盆大雨。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"n.","d":"the physical destruction or disintegration of something.","c":"毀滅；廢墟","s":"The famous ancient Roman temple is now only a pile of ruin, but it still attracts thousands of fascinated tourists daily.","t":"著名的古羅馬神廟現在只是一堆廢墟，但它每天仍然吸引著數以千計著迷的遊客。"},{"w":"ruins","p":"n. pl.","d":"The broken parts that remain after a building or city has been destroyed.","c":"廢墟、遺跡","s":"Many tourists travel to Greece every year to walk through the ancient ruins of the Parthenon and take photos of the historic stone pillars.","t":"每年都有許多遊客前往希臘，在帕德嫩神廟的古老廢墟（遺跡）中漫步，並拍攝歷史悠久的石柱照片。"},{"w":"in a state of ruin","p":"phr.","d":"in a completely broken or destroyed condition.","c":"處於毀滅狀態","s":"Years of terrible executive decisions and widespread corruption ultimately left the historical company in a state of financial ruin.","t":"多年來糟糕的高層決策和普遍的貪腐，最終讓這家歷史悠久的公司處於財務毀滅狀態。"},{"w":"the remains of","p":"phr.","d":"The parts of something that are left after the rest has been destroyed, used, or taken away.","c":"…的殘骸、…的遺留物","s":"After the terrible forest fire was finally put out, the rangers found the remains of a burnt tent left behind by the careless campers.","t":"在可怕的森林大火終於被撲滅後，巡邏員發現了被粗心露營客留下的燒毀帳篷殘骸。"},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to put an end to the existence of something by damaging or attacking it.","c":"摧毀","s":"The aggressive military forces completely destroyed the enemy's main supply base, making it impossible for them to continue the war.","t":"具攻擊性的軍隊徹底摧毀了敵人的主要補給基地，使他們無法繼續戰爭。"},{"w":"destructive","p":"adj.","d":"Causing a large amount of severe damage, harm, or destruction.","c":"具破壞性的、毀滅性的","s":"The government warned that the upcoming typhoon could have a highly destructive effect on coastal villages, urging everyone to evacuate immediately.","t":"政府警告說，即將來臨的颱風可能對沿海村莊造成極具破壞性的影響，並敦促每個人立刻撤離。"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"The act or process of destroying something so badly that it cannot be fixed.","c":"破壞、毀滅、摧毀","s":"The sudden explosion at the chemical factory caused widespread destruction to the surrounding neighborhood, shattering windows a mile away.","t":"化學工廠突如其來的爆炸對周邊社區造成了廣泛的破壞，甚至震碎了一英里外的窗戶。"},{"w":"damage","p":"v.","d":"To harm, break, or spoil something physically.","c":"損害、損壞、破壞","s":"If you don't use a sturdy phone case to protect your new smartphone, you might accidentally damage its fragile screen when you drop it.","t":"如果你不用一個堅固的保護殼來保護你的新智慧型手機，當你不小心摔到它時，可能會損壞它脆弱的螢幕。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n. [U]","d":"Physical harm caused to something, making it less attractive, useful, or valuable.","c":"損害、損失、破壞","s":"The heavy hailstorm caused severe damage to the farmer's fruit crop, forcing him to lower his selling prices for the season.","t":"沉重的冰雹對農夫的水果作物造成了嚴重的損害，迫使他不得不降低該季的售價。"},{"w":"deal... damage","p":"phr.","d":"To cause harm or damage to someone or something, often used in games or combat contexts.","c":"造成…傷害、施加…破壞","s":"In the final round of the video game tournament, Leo's character managed to deal massive damage to the enemy boss, winning the match instantly.","t":"在電子遊戲錦標賽的決賽中，里歐的角色成功對敵方大頭目造成了巨大的傷害，立刻贏得了比賽。"},{"w":"do damageharm to","p":"phr.","d":"To cause physical, mental, or environmental harm or injury to someone or something.","c":"對…造成損害/傷害","s":"Spending too many hours staring at a computer screen in a completely dark room will definitely do serious damage/harm to your eyesight.","t":"在完全黑暗的房間裡花太多時間盯著電腦螢幕，絕對會對你的視力造成嚴重的損害（傷害）。"},{"w":"damaging","p":"adj.","d":"Causing social, financial, or physical harm or trouble.","c":"有害的、造成破壞的","s":"Spreading false rumors about the local restaurant on social media can be extremely damaging to its business and long-term reputation.","t":"在社群媒體上散布關於當地餐廳的謠言，可能對其業務和長期聲譽造成極其有害的（造成破壞的）影響。"},{"w":"harmful","p":"adj.","d":"Causing or likely to cause damage, pain, or injury.","c":"有害的、致傷的","s":"Many doctors warn that feeding young children too much sugary food and soda can be highly harmful to their developing teeth.","t":"許多醫生警告說，讓幼兒吃太多含糖食物和汽水，可能對他們發育中的牙齒非常有害。"},{"w":"harmless","p":"adj.","d":"Completely safe and not able or likely to cause any hurt, pain, or damage.","c":"無害的","s":"Don't be afraid of that little garter snake in the backyard; it is completely harmless and actually helps catch annoying garden pests.","t":"不要害怕後院的那條小束帶蛇；牠完全是無害的，而且實際上還能幫忙捕捉惱人的花園害蟲。"},{"w":"emergency","p":"n.","d":"a serious, unexpected, and often dangerous situation requiring immediate action.","c":"緊急情況","s":"The flight attendant instructed the passengers that, in a real emergency, they must quickly push the red button above their seats.","t":"空服員指示乘客，在真正的緊急情況下，他們必須迅速按下座位上方的紅色按鈕。"},{"w":"emergency room","p":"phr.","d":"the department of a hospital that provides immediate treatment for acute illnesses and trauma.","c":"急診室","s":"After badly breaking his arm during the football game, Mark was immediately rushed to the nearest emergency room for surgical treatment.","t":"在足球比賽中嚴重摔斷手臂後，馬克立刻被送往最近的急診室接受外科治療。"},{"w":"state of emergency","p":"phr.","d":"a situation of national danger or disaster in which a government suspends normal procedures.","c":"緊急狀態","s":"The president officially declared a national state of emergency after the devastating hurricane completely destroyed several coastal cities in the south.","t":"在毀滅性的颶風徹底摧毀南部幾個沿海城市後，總統正式宣布進入全國緊急狀態。"},{"w":"emergency landing","p":"phr.","d":"an unplanned landing by an aircraft due to a crisis.","c":"緊急降落","s":"One of the airplane's engines suddenly caught fire, forcing the skilled pilot to make a dangerous emergency landing in a cornfield.","t":"飛機的一個引擎突然起火，迫使技術高超的飛行員在玉米田裡進行危險的緊急降落。"},{"w":"kilometer","p":"n.","d":"a metric unit of measurement equal to 1,000 meters.","c":"公里","s":"The highly energetic people participating in the charity race had to continuously run 10 kilometer in the extreme summer heat.","t":"參加慈善路跑精力充沛的人們，必須在極端的夏日酷暑中連續跑10公里。"},{"w":"centimeter","p":"n.","d":"a metric unit of length, equal to one hundredth of a meter.","c":"公分","s":"The exotic green snake that we discovered hiding in the garden bushes was around 90 centimeter long and looked quite dangerous.","t":"我們在花園灌木叢中發現藏著的奇特綠蛇大約90公分長，看起來相當危險。"},{"w":"kilogram","p":"n.","d":"the SI unit of mass, equivalent to 1,000 grams.","c":"公斤","s":"To bake this massive birthday cake for the party, you will definitely need at least one kilogram of fine white flour.","t":"為了烤這個派對用的大型生日蛋糕，你絕對需要至少一公斤的優質白麵粉。"},{"w":"modify","p":"v.","d":"to make partial or minor changes to something.","c":"修改","s":"The clever marketing team thoroughly modified their business proposal to much better meet the demanding client's specific professional needs.","t":"聰明的行銷團隊徹底修改了他們的商業提案，以更好地滿足要求嚴格的客戶特定的專業需求。"},{"w":"genetically modified","p":"phr.","d":"containing genetic material that has been artificially altered.","c":"基因改造的","s":"Many modern environmentalists firmly believe that growing genetically modified crops might have unforeseen and potentially dangerous effects on local ecosystems.","t":"許多現代環保人士堅信，種植基因改造的農作物可能對當地生態系統產生不可預見且潛在危險的影響。"},{"w":"modification","p":"n.","d":"the action of modifying something.","c":"修改；改變","s":"The structural engineer suggested a slight modification to the building's original design to ensure it could withstand strong earthquake tremors.","t":"結構工程師建議對建築物的原始設計進行輕微的修改，以確保它能承受強烈的地震震動。"},{"w":"alter","p":"v.","d":"to change or cause to change in character or composition.","c":"改變","s":"She had to carefully alter her beautiful wedding dress because she had surprisingly lost a significant amount of weight recently.","t":"她必須小心地改變（修改）她美麗的婚紗，因為她最近令人驚訝地減輕了大量的體重。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n./adj.","d":"a choice limited to one of two or more possibilities, or describing something available as another choice","c":"替代方案；可替代的","s":"Utilizing public commuting options provides a green alternative to driving a private vehicle in congested urban areas.","t":"在擁擠的都市區域中，利用大眾通勤工具為駕駛私人車輛提供了一種綠色的替代方案。"},{"w":"amend","p":"v.","d":"to formally modify, alter, or update a legal document, contract, policy, or legislative bill","c":"修訂；修改（法律/文件）","s":"The international corporation decided to amend its operational safety policy to thoroughly protect all its warehouse workers.","t":"這家國際公司決定修訂其營運安全政策，以徹底保護其所有倉庫工人。"},{"w":"amendment","p":"n.","d":"a formal or official change, modification, or addition made to a constitution, statute, or contract","c":"修訂案；修正條款","s":"The progressive politicians proposed a new tariff amendment to support domestic technology manufacturing companies.","t":"進步派政治人物提出了一項新的關稅修正案，以支持國內的科技製造公司。"},{"w":"make an amendment","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically perform or introduce a formal modification to a law, rule, or contract","c":"進行修訂；做出修改","s":"The legal committee will make an amendment the trade agreement to ensure both ports operate smoothly under the new laws.","t":"法律委員會將對該貿易協定進行修訂，以確保兩個港口在新法律下都能順利運作。"},{"w":"repair","p":"v.","d":"to fix, restore, or mend something that is damaged, broken, split, or not functioning correctly","c":"修復；修理（動詞）","s":"The skilled mechanic will attempt to repair the mechanical arm that suddenly failed on the automated production line.","t":"技術熟練的技工將嘗試修復在自動化生產線上突然故障的機械手臂。"},{"w":"repair","p":"n.","d":"the factual act or process of fixing something that is broken, damaged, or completely worn out","c":"修理；修補（名詞）","s":"After thoroughly inspecting the imported automobile, the technician estimated that the engine repair would take three days.","t":"在徹底檢查那輛進口汽車後，技術人員估計引擎修理將需要三天的時間。"},{"w":"process","p":"n.","d":"a series of actions or steps taken in order to achieve a particular end.","c":"過程","s":"Jeremy excitedly visited a local dairy factory and carefully watched the fascinating step-by-step process of making delicious chocolate ice cream.","t":"傑瑞興奮地參觀了一家當地的乳製品工廠，並仔細觀看了製作美味巧克力冰淇淋引人入勝的逐步過程。"},{"w":"in the process of","p":"phr.","d":"doing something currently.","c":"在...的過程中","s":"The ambitious software company is currently in the process of developing a highly advanced application for learning foreign languages quickly.","t":"這家雄心勃勃的軟體公司目前正在開發一款用於快速學習外語的高度先進應用程式的過程中。"},{"w":"process","p":"v.","d":"to perform a series of mechanical or chemical operations on something.","c":"處理；加工","s":"The busy customer service representative explained that it can take up to three weeks for the company to process your request.","t":"忙碌的客服代表解釋說，公司最多可能需要三個星期的時間來處理你的請求。"},{"w":"processed","p":"adj.","d":"having been subjected to a special process or treatment.","c":"加工過的","s":"You should definitely try to avoid eating highly processed meats if you genuinely want to improve your long-term cardiovascular health.","t":"如果你真的想改善你長期的心血管健康，你絕對應該試著避免吃高度加工過的肉類。"},{"w":"processed food","p":"phr.","d":"food that has been altered from its natural state for safety reasons or convenience.","c":"加工食品","s":"Nutritionists consistently warn that a daily diet consisting entirely of cheap processed food will inevitably lead to severe weight gain.","t":"營養學家不斷警告，完全由廉價加工食品組成的日常飲食不可避免地會導致嚴重的體重增加。"},{"w":"fortify","p":"v.","d":"to strengthen a place with defensive works so as to protect it against attack.","c":"強化；加強","s":"The determined president fortified his political campaign promises with his bold new policies aimed at improving the country's weak economy.","t":"意志堅定的總統以旨在改善國家疲弱經濟的大膽新政策，強化了他的政治競選承諾。"},{"w":"fortification","p":"n.","d":"a defensive wall or other reinforcement built to strengthen a place.","c":"防禦工事；強化","s":"The ancient Roman soldiers spent several grueling months building a massive stone fortification to protect their city from foreign invaders.","t":"古羅馬士兵花了幾個月艱苦的時間建造一座巨大的石頭防禦工事，以保護他們的城市免受外國入侵者的侵害。"},{"w":"fortress","p":"n.","d":"a heavily protected and impenetrable building.","c":"堡壘","s":"The heavily armed rebels retreated to a hidden mountain fortress where they could safely regroup and plan their next major attack.","t":"全副武裝的叛軍撤退到一座隱藏的山區堡壘，在那裡他們可以安全地重組並計畫下一次重大攻擊。"},{"w":"inject","p":"v.","d":"to drive or force a liquid into a person's body with a syringe.","c":"注射；注入","s":"The experienced nurse carefully injected the life-saving drug into Kyle's arm while he bravely looked away to ignore the pain.","t":"經驗豐富的護士小心地將救命藥物注射進凱爾的手臂，同時他勇敢地把頭轉開以忽略疼痛。"},{"w":"injection","p":"n.","d":"an instance of injecting or being injected.","c":"注射；打針","s":"The frightened child started crying loudly the moment he saw the doctor preparing the sharp needle for his annual injection.","t":"受驚的孩子一看到醫生準備銳利的針頭要為他進行年度打針時，就開始大聲哭了起來。"},{"w":"eject","p":"v.","d":"to force or throw something out, typically in a violent or sudden way.","c":"彈出；逐出","s":"The fighter pilot was forced to immediately eject from the burning aircraft just seconds before it crashed into the dark ocean.","t":"戰鬥機飛行員被迫在燃燒的飛機墜入黑暗海洋的前幾秒鐘立刻從中彈出。"},{"w":"inject money into","p":"phr.","d":"to provide funds to a project or business.","c":"向...注資","s":"The ambitious investors are planning to inject money into the new wearable device, hoping it dominates the global market.","t":"雄心勃勃的投資者正計畫向這款新的穿戴式裝置注資數百萬美元，希望它能主導全球市場。"},{"w":"object to","p":"v.","d":"to say something to express one's disapproval or disagreement.","c":"反對","s":"The angry neighbors strongly object to the controversial plan of building a massive, noisy chemical factory right next to their homes.","t":"憤怒的鄰居強烈反對就在他們家旁邊建造一座巨大、吵雜的化學工廠的具爭議性計畫。"},{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"a sheet, quantity, or thickness of material, typically one of several.","c":"層","s":"Traditional Italian lasagna is usually made from thick layer of rich meat sauce, fresh pasta, and delicious melted mozzarella cheese.","t":"傳統的義大利千層麵通常是由厚厚數層濃郁的肉醬、新鮮的義大利麵和美味的融化莫札瑞拉起司製成的。"},{"w":"layer","p":"v.","d":"to arrange in a layer or layers.","c":"把...分層","s":"The incredibly skilled pastry chef carefully layered the huge birthday cake with rich chocolate, sweet vanilla, and fresh strawberry cream.","t":"技巧極其高超的糕點師傅小心地把巨大的生日蛋糕塗上濃郁巧克力、甜香草和新鮮草莓鮮奶油分層。"},{"w":"ozone layer","p":"phr.","d":"a layer in the earth's stratosphere containing a high concentration of ozone.","c":"臭氧層","s":"The progressive environmental policy aims to effectively stop harmful chemicals from continually destroying the Earth's delicate and protective ozone layer.","t":"漸進的環保政策旨在有效地阻止有害化學物質不斷破壞地球脆弱且具保護作用的臭氧層。"},{"w":"technique","p":"n.","d":"a way of carrying out a particular task.","c":"技巧；技術","s":"These beautiful clay pots were perfectly made by the artist using a brand new technique she learned during her trip.","t":"這些美麗的陶罐是由這位藝術家使用她在旅行中學到的一種全新技巧完美製作而成的。"},{"w":"technical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a particular subject, art, or craft, or its techniques.","c":"技術上的","s":"The brilliant engineering team unexpectedly ran into several major technical problems, so the highly anticipated speech unfortunately started very late.","t":"才華洋溢的工程團隊出乎意料地遇到了幾個重大的技術上的問題，所以這場備受期待的演講不幸地很晚才開始。"},{"w":"technically","p":"adv.","d":"according to the facts or exact meaning of something.","c":"嚴格來說；技術上","s":"While tomatoes are commonly treated as vegetables in cooking, technically, they are actually categorized as a fruit by expert botanists.","t":"雖然番茄在烹飪中通常被當作蔬菜處理，但嚴格來說，它們實際上被專家植物學家歸類為水果。"},{"w":"technique","p":"n.","d":"skill","c":"技巧","s":"The famous movie director is widely known for the camera technique used in his intense and realistic action films.","t":"這位著名的電影導演以其在緊張逼真的動作片中使用的晃動鏡頭技巧而廣為人知。"},{"w":"predict","p":"v.","d":"to say or estimate that a specified thing will happen in the future.","c":"預測","s":"Even with modern technology, scientists cannot yet accurately predict exactly when and where a massive, destructive earthquake will finally happen.","t":"即使擁有現代科技，科學家仍然無法準確地預測一場巨大且具毀滅性的地震究竟何時何地會最終發生。"},{"w":"prediction","p":"n.","d":"a thing predicted; a forecast.","c":"預言；預測","s":"The famous economist's bold prediction about the sudden stock market crash unfortunately turned out to be completely and devastatingly true.","t":"這位著名經濟學家關於股市突然崩盤的大膽預測，不幸地被證明是完全且具毀滅性的真實。"},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be predicted.","c":"可預測的","s":"The plot of that romantic comedy movie was incredibly boring and highly predictable, as I knew exactly how it would end.","t":"那部浪漫喜劇電影的情節極度無聊且高度可預測的，因為我完全知道它會如何結束。"},{"w":"forecast","p":"n.","d":"a prediction or estimate of future events, especially coming weather.","c":"預報","s":"Before setting sail across the treacherous ocean, the cautious captain carefully listened to the detailed weather forecast on the radio.","t":"在航行穿越危險的海洋之前，謹慎的船長仔細聆聽了收音機上詳細的天氣預報。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"to intensify, increase, or further improve the quality, value, or extent of.","c":"提升；加強","s":"The professional photographer cleverly used advanced computer software to significantly enhance the colors and sharpness of the beautiful wedding photos.","t":"專業攝影師巧妙地使用先進的電腦軟體來顯著提升美麗婚禮照片的顏色和清晰度。"},{"w":"enhanced","p":"adj.","d":"intensified, increased, or further improved in quality.","c":"增強的；改良的","s":"The brand new military aircraft is fully equipped with highly enhanced radar systems to detect enemy targets from much further away.","t":"全新的軍用飛機配備了高度增強的雷達系統，能從更遠的地方偵測到敵方目標。"},{"w":"enhancement","p":"n.","d":"an increase or improvement in quality, value, or extent.","c":"提升；增強","s":"Scientific studies clearly show that those who exercise regularly experience significant enhancement in both their physical health and mental abilities.","t":"科學研究清楚地顯示，那些規律運動的人在身體健康和心智能力方面都經歷了顯著的提升。"},{"w":"improvement","p":"n.","d":"an example of improving or being improved.","c":"改善；進步","s":"After practicing speaking Spanish for an hour every single day, there was a massive improvement in his overall conversational fluency.","t":"在每天練習說西班牙語一小時後，他整體的會話流利度有了巨大的進步。"},{"w":"prehistoric","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or denoting the period before written records.","c":"史前的","s":"While digging deeply in the ancient cave, the excited archaeologists discovered several mysterious prehistoric tools carved out of animal bone.","t":"在古老洞穴深處挖掘時，興奮的考古學家發現了幾件由動物骨頭雕刻而成的神祕史前的工具。"},{"w":"primitive","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, denoting, or preserving the character of an early stage in the historical development of something","c":"原始的；遠古的","s":"The leading anthropologist thoroughly analyzed the primitive tools found at the ancient crime scene to understand how the tribe historically survived.","t":"首席人類學家徹底分析了在古老犯罪現場發現的原始工具，以了解該部落在歷史上是如何生存的。"},{"w":"sophisticated","p":"adj.","d":"having a high degree of complexity, refinement, or advanced development in technology, system, or taste","c":"精密的；複雜先進的；老練的","s":"The software engineering team deployed a sophisticated database system to monitor the day-to-day business operations of the company.","t":"軟體工程團隊部署了一套精密先進的資料庫系統，以監控公司的日常業務運作。"},{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","d":"never done, known, or experienced before in history, representing a completely new situation","c":"空前的；前所未有的","s":"The international corporation achieved unprecedented success last year, breaking all previous sales records for portable electronic devices.","t":"這家國際公司去年取得了前所未有的成功，打破了以往所有可攜式電子裝置的銷售紀錄。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"nation – unavailable","cards":[{"w":"nation","p":"n.","d":"a large body of people united by common descent, history, culture, or language.","c":"國家","s":"The president delivered an inspiring speech, urging the entire nation to remain completely united during the ongoing economic crisis.","t":"總統發表了激勵人心的演說，敦促整個國家在持續的經濟危機中保持完全團結。"},{"w":"national","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or characteristic of a nation.","c":"國家的；全國的","s":"Tomorrow is a highly anticipated national holiday, which means that all banks and public schools will be closed.","t":"明天是一個備受期待的國家的假日，這意味著所有銀行和公立學校都將關閉。"},{"w":"nationality","p":"n.","d":"the status of belonging to a particular nation.","c":"國籍","s":"Even though Leslie has lived in the United States for her entire life, she officially holds Canadian nationality.","t":"儘管萊斯莉一生都住在美國，她官方持有的是加拿大國籍。"},{"w":"dual nationality","p":"phr.","d":"the status of being a citizen of two different countries.","c":"雙重國籍","s":"Because his parents were born in different countries, the young man was incredibly lucky to possess dual nationality.","t":"因為他的父母出生在不同的國家，這個年輕人極其幸運地擁有雙重國籍。"},{"w":"internationally","p":"adv.","d":"in, between, or among many different nations.","c":"國際地","s":"The famous author is internationally recognized for her brilliant novels that explore the complex nature of human relationships.","t":"這位著名作家因其探討人際關係複雜本質的才華洋溢的小說而在國際地受到認可。"},{"w":"state","p":"n.","d":"a nation or territory considered as an organized political community under one government","c":"國家；州","s":"The progressive law firm advised the international corporation on how to comply with the trade regulations of each foreign state.","t":"這家進步派法律事務所就如何遵守每個外國國家的貿易法規，向這家國際公司提供建議。"},{"w":"state-run","p":"adj.","d":"operated, managed, or funded directly by the government or official authorities of a country","c":"國營的；政府開辦的","s":"The newly elected president promised to thoroughly modernize the state-run railway system to improve daily commuting for all citizens.","t":"新當選的總統承諾徹底使國營鐵路系統走向現代化，以改善所有公民的每日通勤。"},{"w":"state","p":"v.","d":"to express something definitely, clearly, and formally in speech or in a written legal document","c":"陳述；聲明（動詞）","s":"The contract terms clearly state that all imported goods must be assessed by customs officers before entering the port.","t":"合約條款明確陳述，所有進口貨物在進入港口前都必須接受海關官員的評估。"},{"w":"statement","p":"n.","d":"a definite or official expression of something in speech or writing, or a formal account of facts","c":"聲明；陳述（名詞）","s":"The ambitious entrepreneur issued an official statement to reassure the wealthy investors that the business expansion was going smoothly.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的企業家發表了一份正式聲明，以向富有的投資者們保證業務擴展正順利進行。"},{"w":"make a statement","p":"phr.","d":"to provide an official, formal oral or written account of facts, typically to the public or authorities","c":"發表聲明；陳述","s":"The leading researcher decided to make a statement to the press after his scientific experiment yielded highly accurate data.","t":"首席研究員在他的科學實驗產出高度準確的數據後，決定向媒體發表聲明。"},{"w":"proclaim","p":"v.","d":"to announce or declare something officially, publicly, and proudly, especially a major victory or law","c":"宣告；宣佈；讚揚","s":"The victorious general arrived at the capital to proclaim the complete defeat of the oppressive invading army.","t":"獲勝的將軍抵達首都，宣告徹底擊敗了那支殘暴的入侵軍隊。"},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to formally, solemnly, or officially state a fact, intention, or legal condition to the public","c":"宣布；宣告；申報","s":"The government intends to declare the heavily damaged forest region a protected zone to save the endangered wild species.","t":"政府打算宣布這片受損嚴重的森林區域為保護區，以拯救瀕危的野生學名物種。"},{"w":"declare war","p":"phr.","d":"to officially or formally announce that a state of military conflict exists between countries","c":"宣戰","s":"The unyielding dictator fiercely chose to declare war on the neighboring state after the peace talks failed completely.","t":"在和平談判完全失敗後，這位不屈服的獨裁者猛烈地選擇向鄰國宣戰。"},{"w":"declaration","p":"n.","d":"a formal, official, or explicit announcement of an intention, political state, or legal fact","c":"宣告；宣言；申報書","s":"The historic declaration of independence was celebrated by the citizens throughout the vast territory of the newly formed country.","t":"這份歷史性的獨立宣言，受到了這個新成立國家廣大領土上所有公民的慶祝。"},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"to have as belonging to one; own.","c":"擁有","s":"According to the ancient legend, this mysterious silver ring is said to possess strange and highly dangerous magical powers.","t":"根據古老的傳說，這枚神祕的銀色戒指據說擁有奇怪且高度危險的魔法力量。"},{"w":"possession","p":"n.","d":"the state of having, owning, or controlling something.","c":"擁有；所有物","s":"The police officer quickly arrested the nervous young man for the illegal possession of dangerous and stolen weapons.","t":"警察迅速以非法擁有危險的被盜武器為由，逮捕了那名緊張的年輕人。"},{"w":"worldly possessions","p":"phr.","d":"physical things that someone owns, as opposed to spiritual values.","c":"世俗財產","s":"When the terrible wildfire destroyed their neighborhood, the family tragically lost all their worldly possessions, but they survived safely.","t":"當可怕的野火摧毀了他們的社區時，這家人悲慘地失去了所有世俗財產，但他們安全地倖存了下來。"},{"w":"spiritual","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or affecting the human spirit or soul as opposed to material or physical things.","c":"精神上的；心靈的","s":"After experiencing a serious personal crisis, Abby decided to focus entirely on her spiritual development and inner peace this year.","t":"在經歷了一次嚴重的個人危機後，艾比決定今年完全專注於她的精神上的發展和內心的平靜。"},{"w":"spiritually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to the human spirit or soul.","c":"精神上地","s":"Many people find that practicing daily meditation and deep breathing exercises leaves them feeling significantly healthier and spiritually fulfilled.","t":"許多人發現，練習每日冥想和深呼吸運動讓他們感覺明顯更健康且在精神上地獲得滿足。"},{"w":"spirit","p":"n.","d":"the nonphysical part of a person which is the seat of emotions and character.","c":"精神；靈魂","s":"Despite losing the difficult championship game, the young athletes maintained a remarkably strong and positive team spirit throughout the tournament.","t":"儘管輸掉了艱難的冠軍賽，這些年輕運動員在整個錦標賽中保持了異常堅強且積極的團隊精神。"},{"w":"physical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the body as opposed to the mind.","c":"身體的；物理的","s":"The strict doctor firmly reminded his patient that maintaining excellent physical health is absolutely essential for a long life.","t":"嚴格的醫生堅定地提醒他的病患，保持極佳的身體的健康對於長壽是絕對必要的。"},{"w":"imperial","p":"adj.","d":"relating to an empire or an emperor.","c":"帝國的；皇帝的","s":"The wealthy imperial family was tragically forced to leave the grand palace and hide away safely after the violent war broke out.","t":"富有的皇（帝國）的家族在暴力的戰爭爆發後，悲慘地被迫離開宏偉的宮殿並安全地躲藏起來。"},{"w":"imperialism","p":"n.","d":"a policy of extending a country's power and influence through diplomacy or military force.","c":"帝國主義","s":"The history professor passionately discussed how 19th-century imperialism profoundly changed the economic and cultural landscapes of many African nations.","t":"歷史教授充滿熱情地討論了19世紀的帝國主義如何深刻地改變了許多非洲國家的經濟和文化景觀。"},{"w":"emperor","p":"n.","d":"a sovereign ruler of great power and rank, especially one ruling an empire.","c":"皇帝","s":"The powerful Roman emperor commanded a vast and incredibly loyal army that successfully conquered many distant foreign lands.","t":"強大的羅馬皇帝指揮著一支龐大且極度忠誠的軍隊，成功征服了許多遙遠的外國土地。"},{"w":"empire","p":"n.","d":"an extensive group of states or countries under a single supreme authority.","c":"帝國","s":"At the absolute height of its power, the ancient empire spanned across three continents and controlled vital international trade routes.","t":"在其權力的絕對巔峰時期，這個古老的帝國橫跨三大洲並控制著至關重要的國際貿易路線。"},{"w":"imperial palace","p":"phr.","d":"the official residence of an emperor or empress.","c":"皇宮","s":"Thousands of curious tourists eagerly visit the beautiful imperial palace every single day to admire its magnificent traditional architecture.","t":"每天都有成千上萬好奇的遊客熱切地參觀這座美麗的皇宮，以欣賞其壯麗的傳統建築。"},{"w":"bloom","p":"v. / n.","d":"to produce flowers; a flower, especially one cultivated for its beauty.","c":"開花；花朵","s":"My grandmother's beautiful garden is definitely most attractive when the red roses are fully blooming in the early spring.","t":"我祖母美麗的花園絕對是在初春紅玫瑰完全開花時最迷人。"},{"w":"in bloom","p":"phr.","d":"with the flowers fully open.","c":"盛開中","s":"We decided to take a long walk through the colorful park because all the spring flowers were perfectly in bloom.","t":"我們決定在色彩繽紛的公園裡散步很久，因為所有的春季花朵都在完美地盛開中。"},{"w":"full bloom","p":"phr.","d":"the stage of a flower being completely open.","c":"全盛時期；完全綻放","s":"The magnificent cherry trees in the mountain valley finally reached full bloom yesterday, attracting hundreds of professional photographers.","t":"山谷中壯麗的櫻花樹昨天終於達到了完全綻放，吸引了數百名專業攝影師。"},{"w":"blooming / thriving","p":"adj.","d":"producing flowers; flourishing.","c":"盛開的；繁榮的","s":"The successful business owner proudly looked out over his incredibly profitable and rapidly thriving international technology company.","t":"這位成功的企業主自豪地俯瞰著他那極其有利可圖且正在迅速繁榮的國際科技公司。"},{"w":"blossom","p":"n. / v.","d":"a flower or a mass of flowers; to produce flowers.","c":"花朵；開花","s":"The ancient cherry tree standing right next to our wooden house was completely covered in beautiful pink blossom this morning.","t":"站在我們木屋正旁邊的那棵古老櫻花樹，今早完全被美麗的粉紅色花朵覆蓋了。"},{"w":"cherry blossom","p":"phr.","d":"the flower of a cherry tree, famous for blooming beautifully in spring.","c":"櫻花","s":"Thousands of excited tourists travel to Japan every spring specifically to view the stunningly beautiful cherry blossom slowly falling down.","t":"每年春天，成千上萬興奮的遊客專程前往日本，只為了觀賞令人驚豔的美麗櫻花緩緩落下。"},{"w":"in blossom","p":"phr.","d":"flowering.","c":"盛開中","s":"The entire scenic mountain valley looks absolutely magical when the millions of wild apple trees are finally perfectly in blossom.","t":"當數百萬棵野生蘋果樹終於完美地在盛開中時，整個風景優美的山谷看起來絕對充滿魔力。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the quality or state of being physically strong.","c":"力量；優點","s":"The exhausted warehouse worker had to use all his remaining physical strength just to safely lift the incredibly heavy wooden box.","t":"疲憊的倉庫工人必須用盡他剩餘的所有身體力量，只為了安全地舉起那個極其沉重的木箱。"},{"w":"inner strength","p":"phr.","d":"mental and emotional toughness or resilience.","c":"內在力量","s":"Surviving such a terrible and heartbreaking tragedy requires an incredible amount of inner strength and endless support from close family.","t":"在如此可怕且令人心碎的悲劇中倖存下來，需要令人難以置信的內在力量以及來自親密家人的無盡支持。"},{"w":"strengths and weaknesses","p":"phr.","d":"the good and bad qualities of a person or thing.","c":"優缺點","s":"Before the difficult job interview, Randall carefully compiled a detailed list of his professional strengths and weaknesses to present clearly.","t":"在困難的工作面試之前，藍道仔細編寫了一份他專業優缺點的詳細清單以清楚地呈現。"},{"w":"strengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make or become stronger.","c":"加強；鞏固","s":"The government officially passed a new law designed to significantly strengthen the strict environmental protections for our polluted oceans.","t":"政府正式通過了一項新法律，旨在顯著加強對我們受污染海洋的嚴格環境保護。"},{"w":"throne","p":"n.","d":"a ceremonial chair for a sovereign, bishop, or similar figure.","c":"王座","s":"The majestic king and beautiful queen sat proudly on their golden throne in the incredibly grand and highly decorated palace.","t":"雄偉的國王和美麗的王后自豪地坐在極其宏偉且高度裝飾的宮殿裡金色的王座上。"},{"w":"heir to the throne","p":"phr.","d":"the person next in line to become the monarch.","c":"王位繼承人","s":"The birth of the healthy baby boy was celebrated widely because he was the official heir to the throne of the country.","t":"這個健康男嬰的誕生被廣泛慶祝，因為他是這個國家官方的王位繼承人。"},{"w":"refer to","p":"phr.","d":"to mention or allude to; to look at a source of information.","c":"提及；參考","s":"If you have any serious questions about how to fix this broken refrigerator, please closely refer to the attached instruction manual.","t":"如果你對於如何修理這台壞掉的冰箱有任何嚴重的問題，請仔細參考附上的說明書。"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"the action of mentioning or alluding to something.","c":"參考；提及","s":"The professor made a brief but incredibly insightful reference to the ancient Roman Empire during his complex history lecture today.","t":"教授在今天複雜的歷史講課中，對古羅馬帝國做了一個簡短但極具洞察力的提及。"},{"w":"refer to...as","p":"phr.","d":"To call or describe someone or something by a specific name or title.","c":"把…稱為、將…稱作","s":"Because he is always willing to help others, many citizens refer to the kind doctor as a local hero.","t":"因為他總是樂於助人，許多市民把這位善良的醫生稱為當地的英雄。"},{"w":"view...as","p":"phr.","d":"To think about or consider someone or something in a particular way.","c":"把…視為、將…看作","s":"The strict manager tends to view mistakes as valuable opportunities for employees to learn and grow.","t":"這位嚴格的經理傾向於把錯誤視為員工學習與成長的寶貴機會。"},{"w":"see...as","p":"phr.","d":"To consider or regard someone or something in a specific way.","c":"把…看作、將…視為","s":"Many young children see their parents as real-life superheroes who can solve any problem in the world.","t":"許多幼童把他們的父母看作現實生活中的超級英雄，能夠解決世界上任何問題。"},{"w":"regard...as","p":"phr.","d":"To think of someone or something with a specific feeling or opinion.","c":"把…視為、認為…是","s":"Historians generally regard this ancient document as one of the most important texts in human history.","t":"歷史學家普遍把這份古代文獻視為人類歷史上最重要的文本之一。"},{"w":"consider...to be","p":"phr.","d":"To have a particular opinion about someone or something; to believe someone or something has a certain quality.","c":"認為…是、把…視為","s":"Most experts consider regular exercise to be the most effective way to maintain good physical and mental health.","t":"大多數專家認為規律運動是維持身心健康最有效的方法。"},{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"a system of money in general use in a particular country.","c":"貨幣","s":"You should always make absolutely sure you have some local currency with you when you independently travel to a foreign country.","t":"當你獨立前往外國旅行時，你總是應該絕對確保身上帶有一些當地的貨幣。"},{"w":"currency rate","p":"phr.","d":"the value of one currency for the purpose of conversion to another.","c":"匯率","s":"The international businessman checks the daily currency rate religiously to perfectly ensure his global company doesn't lose any profits.","t":"這位國際商人虔誠地檢查每日的匯率，以完美地確保他的全球公司不會損失任何利潤。"},{"w":"currency exchange","p":"phr.","d":"a business or service that changes one country's money for another.","c":"貨幣兌換","s":"We urgently need to find a secure currency exchange counter at the busy airport so we can quickly buy train tickets.","t":"我們急需在繁忙的機場找到一個安全的貨幣兌換櫃台，這樣我們才能迅速購買火車票。"},{"w":"foreign currency","p":"phr.","d":"the money used in a country other than one's own.","c":"外幣","s":"The conservative bank charges an incredibly high fee if you ever try to withdraw foreign currency from their automated teller machines.","t":"如果你試圖從他們的自動櫃員機提取外幣，這家保守的銀行會收取極高昂的手續費。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to fasten or join one thing to another.","c":"貼上；附加","s":"Rick carefully attached the important medical note to the kitchen fridge with a heavy magnet so his wife would definitely see it.","t":"瑞克小心地用一塊重磁鐵將重要的醫療紙條貼（附加）在廚房冰箱上，這樣他妻子絕對會看到它。"},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"an extra part or extension that is or can be attached to something.","c":"附件；依戀","s":"Please effectively download the detailed PDF attachment in my email so you can properly review the updated financial figures tonight.","t":"請有效地在我的電子郵件中下載詳細的PDF附件，這樣你今晚就可以適當地審查更新的財務數據。"},{"w":"attached","p":"adj.","d":"joined, fastened, or connected to something.","c":"附上的；依戀的","s":"The newly hired assistant completely forgot to include the critically important attached document when she bravely sent the email to the boss.","t":"新聘請的助理在勇敢地發送電子郵件給老闆時，完全忘記包含極其重要的附上的文件。"},{"w":"emotional attachment","p":"phr.","d":"a strong feeling of affection or loyalty towards someone or something.","c":"情感依戀","s":"The lonely old man has a deep emotional attachment to that broken watch because his beloved late grandfather gave it to him.","t":"那位孤獨的老人對那隻壞掉的手錶有著深深的情感依戀，因為那是由他深愛的已故祖父送給他的。"},{"w":"be attached to","p":"phr.","d":"To be joined or sent together with an email message as a separate digital file.","c":"隨信附上、附帶於（電子郵件）","s":"The detailed PDF report is attached to the email I sent you this morning, so please review the file carefully before our afternoon meeting.","t":"今天早上我發給您的電子郵件中隨信附上了詳細的 PDF 報告，因此請在我們下午的會議之前仔細審閱該檔案。"},{"w":"be attached to","p":"phr.","d":"To feel a strong emotional connection, affection, or loyalty to someone or something.","c":"依戀…、對…有深厚的感情","s":"Having lived in the old countryside house for over ten years, the elderly couple was deeply attached to the neighborhood and refused to move to the city.","t":"在這棟鄉間老房子住了十多年，這對年邁的夫婦對這個社區深具感情（非常依戀），並拒絕搬到城市。"},{"w":"detached","p":"adj.","d":"Emotionally distant, cool, or not showing any personal involvement or feelings.","c":"不帶感情的、冷漠的、超然的","s":"The judge remained completely detached throughout the emotional trial, focusing only on the cold facts presented by both lawyers.","t":"在這場充滿情緒張力的審判中，法官始終保持完全超然（不帶感情），只專注於雙方律師提出的冰冷事實。"},{"w":"reputation","p":"n.","d":"the beliefs or opinions that are generally held about someone or something.","c":"名聲","s":"The arrogant politician knew that his professional reputation would be seriously at risk if he unfortunately failed to win his court case.","t":"傲慢的政治人物知道，如果他不幸未能在官司中勝訴，他的專業名聲將處於嚴重的危險之中。"},{"w":"have a reputation for","p":"phr.","d":"to be known for a particular quality or characteristic.","c":"以...聞名/有...的名聲","s":"My parents' newly opened Italian restaurant has an excellent reputation for serving incredibly good and highly inexpensive food to local customers.","t":"我父母新開的義大利餐廳以為當地顧客提供極好且非常便宜的食物有極佳的名聲（聞名）。"},{"w":"drag somebody's reputation through the mud","p":"phr.","d":"to publicly ruin or deeply damage someone's good name.","c":"使某人名譽掃地","s":"The angry journalist deliberately wrote a false article that cruelly dragged the innocent mayor's reputation through the mud during the election.","t":"憤怒的記者故意寫了一篇虛假的文章，在選舉期間殘酷地使無辜市長的名譽掃地。"},{"w":"reputable","p":"adj.","d":"having a good reputation.","c":"聲譽卓著的","s":"If you ever want to safely invest your valuable money, you should absolutely find a highly reputable and experienced financial advisor.","t":"如果你曾經想要安全地投資你寶貴的金錢，你絕對應該找一位高度聲譽卓著的且經驗豐富的財務顧問。"},{"w":"reputed","p":"adj.","d":"generally believed to be a certain way, though not necessarily proven.","c":"據說的；被普遍認為的","s":"The mysteriously quiet man who just moved in next door is the reputed leader of a highly dangerous international criminal organization.","t":"剛搬到隔壁的神祕安靜男子，是高度危險的國際犯罪組織的據說的首領。"},{"w":"plant stem","p":"phr.","d":"the structural axis of a plant.","c":"植物莖幹","s":"The biology students eagerly studied how vital nutrients travel swiftly upward through the plant stem to reach the delicate green leaves.","t":"生物系學生熱切地研究了重要的營養物質如何迅速向上穿過植物莖幹以到達嬌嫩的綠葉。"},{"w":"stem from","p":"phr.","d":"to be caused by or originate from something.","c":"源自於","s":"The psychologist explained that Anna's irrational fear of heights deeply stemmed from a terrifying experience she unfortunately had as a young child.","t":"心理學家解釋說，安娜對高處不理性的恐懼深深源自於她小時候不幸有過的一次可怕經歷。"},{"w":"derive from","p":"phr.","d":"to obtain or originate from a specified source.","c":"源自於；從...衍生出","s":"Many of the most commonly used English words actually derive from ancient Latin, which fascinates the brilliant linguistics professor entirely.","t":"許多最常用的英語單字實際上源自於古老的拉丁語，這讓那位才華洋溢的語言學教授完全著迷。"},{"w":"originate from","p":"phr.","d":"To come from a particular place, time, or situation; to have a specific beginning.","c":"源自、發源於","s":"Many delicious traditional dishes in Taiwan originally originated from the early immigrant communities who brought their local cooking styles to the island.","t":"許多美味的台灣傳統料理最初源自早期的移民社群，他們將當地的烹飪風格帶到了這座島上。"},{"w":"result from","p":"phr.","d":"To be caused by something else (Effect + result from + Cause).","c":"起因於、由…所造成","s":"The severe flooding in the downtown area did not result from a lack of drainage systems, but rather from the unprecedented amount of heavy rainfall.","t":"市中心的嚴重水災並非起因於排水系統的缺乏，而是由前所未有的特大豪雨所造成的。"},{"w":"result in","p":"phr.","d":"To cause a particular situation or outcome to happen (Cause + result in + Effect).","c":"導致、造成、結果是","s":"Staying up late every night to play video games will eventually result in poor academic performance and extreme fatigue during the daytime.","t":"每晚熬夜打電子遊戲最終會導致學業成績不佳以及白天的極度疲勞。"},{"w":"as a result of","p":"phr.","d":"Because of something that has happened (Used before a noun phrase cause).","c":"由於…的結果、因為","s":"As a result of the sudden cancelation of the morning flight, hundreds of frustrated passengers had to spend the night sleeping on the airport floor.","t":"由於早上班機突然取消的結果，數百名感到沮喪的乘客不得不躺在機場地板上過夜。"},{"w":"as a result","p":"phr.","d":"Therefore; because of something that was just mentioned (Used to introduce the effect).","c":"因此、結果","s":"The young athlete trained intensely for four hours every single day; as a result, he broke the national record and won the gold medal.","t":"這位年輕的運動員每天都密集訓練四個小時；因此，他打破了全國紀錄並贏得了金牌。"},{"w":"eternal","p":"adj.","d":"lasting or existing forever; without end or beginning.","c":"永恆的","s":"Some religious people deeply believe that after a person's death, they will peacefully go on to live an eternal life in heaven.","t":"一些有宗教信仰的人深信，在人死後，他們將平靜地在天堂過著永恆的生命。"},{"w":"eternal youth","p":"phr.","d":"the state of looking or feeling young forever.","c":"青春永駐","s":"Many wealthy people strongly desiring eternal youth frequently use all sorts of expensive cosmetic products to make their skin look artificially younger.","t":"許多強烈渴望青春永駐的富人經常使用各種昂貴的化妝產品，以讓他們的皮膚看起來人工地更年輕。"},{"w":"eternity","p":"n.","d":"infinite or unending time.","c":"永恆；漫長的時間","s":"Waiting anxiously in the crowded hospital room for the crucial medical test results honestly felt like an absolute eternity to the terrified mother.","t":"在擁擠的醫院病房焦急地等待關鍵的醫學檢查結果，對這位受驚的母親來說，老實說感覺就像是絕對的永恆。"},{"w":"immortal","p":"adj.","d":"living forever; never dying or decaying.","c":"不朽的；長生不老的","s":"According to ancient legends, the powerful Greek gods were completely immortal, but their daily actions still came across as very human sometimes.","t":"根據古老的傳說，強大的希臘神祇是完全長生不老的，但他們日常的行為有時仍然表現得非常像人類。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"Lasting for a long time or forever; not temporary.","c":"永久的、固定的、長期的","s":"After working as a temporary freelancer for two years, David was thrilled to finally receive an offer for a permanent position at the marketing company.","t":"在擔任了兩年的兼職接案人員後，大衛興高采烈地終於獲得了這家行銷公司固定（永久）職位的錄取通知。"},{"w":"permanently","p":"adv.","d":"In a way that lasts forever or for a very long time without changing.","c":"永久地、長期地","s":"Because of the severe spine injury he suffered in the accident, the doctor warned that the athlete's left leg might be permanently damaged.","t":"由於他在事故中受到的嚴重脊椎傷勢，醫生警告說這位運動員的左腿可能會永久地受損。"},{"w":"for good","p":"phr.","d":"Forever; permanently.","c":"永遠地、永久地","s":"Tired of the cold winter weather and crowded streets, the family decided to leave New York for good and move to a sunny beach town in Florida.","t":"厭倦了寒冬的天氣和擁擠的街道，這戶人家決定永遠地離開紐約，搬到佛羅里達州一個陽光明媚的海灘小鎮。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"Lasting for only a short or limited time; not permanent.","c":"暫時的、臨時的","s":"The store set up a temporary counter near the entrance to sell holiday gifts, but it will be removed once the Christmas season is over.","t":"這家店在入口附近設置了一個暫時的（臨時的）櫃檯來販售節日禮物，但一旦聖誕節結束，它就會被拆除。"},{"w":"temporarily","p":"adv.","d":"For a short or limited time; not permanently.","c":"暫時地、臨時地","s":"Due to a sudden power outage caused by the lightning strike, the office computer network is temporarily unavailable until the technicians fix the system.","t":"由於雷擊導致的突發停電，辦公室的電腦網路在技術人員修復系統之前將暫時地無法使用。"},{"w":"glory","p":"n.","d":"high renown or honor won by notable achievements.","c":"榮耀","s":"The brilliant general rightfully earned immense national glory through his incredibly courageous achievements during the long and brutally destructive war.","t":"這位才華洋溢的將軍透過他在漫長且極具毀滅性的戰爭中極其勇敢的成就，理所當然地贏得了巨大的國家榮耀。"},{"w":"glory days","p":"phr.","d":"a period in the past when something or someone was highly successful.","c":"光輝歲月","s":"The retired professional athletes frequently meet at the local bar to nostalgically talk about their incredible glory days from twenty years ago.","t":"退休的職業運動員經常在當地酒吧聚會，懷舊地談論他們二十年前令人難以置信的光輝歲月。"},{"w":"glorious","p":"adj.","d":"having, worthy of, or bringing fame or admiration.","c":"輝煌的；壯麗的","s":"We eventually reached the incredibly high mountain peak exactly in time to witness a truly glorious and colorful sunset over the ocean.","t":"我們最終正好及時抵達極其高聳的山峰，見證了海洋上空一場真正壯麗的且色彩繽紛的日落。"},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"v.","d":"to give up something valued for the sake of other considerations.","c":"犧牲","s":"Dedicated Kim bravely sacrificed her entire personal life in order to achieve massive success in her highly demanding corporate job.","t":"盡責的金勇敢地犧牲了她整個私人生活，為了在她要求極高的企業工作中取得巨大的成功。"},{"w":"make a sacrifice","p":"n.","d":"The act of giving up something valuable to help someone else or to achieve an important goal.","c":"犧牲、奉獻","s":"The devoted parents make a significant financial sacrifice to send their daughter to a prestigious university overseas, working extra hours every week.","t":"這對無私的父母為了送女兒去國外著名的大學念書，做出了巨大的經濟犧牲，每週都額外加班工作。"},{"w":"make a sacrifice","p":"phr.","d":"to give up something important or valuable.","c":"做出犧牲","s":"Poor Maggie had to make a sacrifice just to afford to send her smart son to the incredibly expensive private school.","t":"可憐的瑪姬必須做出許多痛苦的個人犧牲，只為了負擔得起送她聰明的兒子去那所極其昂貴的私立學校。"},{"w":"ultimate sacrifice","p":"phr.","d":"the act of giving one's life for a cause.","c":"最終的犧牲（指捐軀）","s":"The whole nation silently honored the brave soldiers who unfortunately made the ultimate sacrifice while fiercely defending their beloved country from invaders.","t":"整個國家默默地向那些在猛烈保衛深愛國家免受入侵者侵害時，不幸做出最終的犧牲的勇敢士兵致敬。"},{"w":"esteem","p":"n. / v.","d":"respect and admiration, typically for a person.","c":"尊重；評價","s":"Talented Tiger Woods is widely esteemed by millions of fans as being undoubtedly one of the best and most famous golfers in the world.","t":"才華洋溢的老虎伍茲被數百萬粉絲廣泛評價（尊重）為無疑是世界上最好、最著名的高爾夫球手之一。"},{"w":"esteemed","p":"adj.","d":"highly respected or admired.","c":"受人尊敬的","s":"The incredibly esteemed scientist was formally invited to the grand university to deliver a highly complex speech about his groundbreaking medical research.","t":"這位極度受人尊敬的科學家正式被邀請到宏偉的大學，就他突破性的醫學研究發表一場高度複雜的演講。"},{"w":"self-esteem","p":"n.","d":"confidence in one's own worth or abilities; self-respect.","c":"自尊","s":"Constantly criticizing your young children for making tiny mistakes will undoubtedly cause them to quickly develop severely low self-esteem.","t":"不斷批評你年幼的孩子犯了微小的錯誤，無疑會導致他們迅速發展出嚴重低下的自尊。"},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea, impression, or feeling known or understandable to someone.","c":"傳達","s":"Sensitive Carl elegantly conveyed his deepest and most complex romantic feelings through the incredibly beautiful poetry he wrote for his girlfriend.","t":"敏感的卡爾透過他為女友寫的極其美麗的詩歌，優雅地傳達了他最深刻、最複雜的浪漫情感。"},{"w":"convey a message","p":"phr.","d":"to successfully communicate a thought or idea.","c":"傳達訊息","s":"The powerful movie utilized dark colors and somber music to effectively convey a clear message about the tragic consequences of violent war.","t":"這部強而有力的電影利用深色調和憂鬱的音樂，有效地傳達了一個關於暴力戰爭悲慘後果的清晰訊息。"},{"w":"conveyor","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that transports or communicates something.","c":"傳達者；運輸工具","s":"The highly energetic teacher proudly acted as a passionate conveyor of valuable historical knowledge to her young, eager students during the class.","t":"這位精力充沛的老師在課堂上自豪地扮演著為她年輕、熱切的學生充滿熱情地傳達（者）寶貴歷史知識的角色。"},{"w":"conveyor belt","p":"phr.","d":"a continuous moving band of fabric, rubber, or metal used for transporting objects.","c":"輸送帶","s":"The damaged suitcases slowly rolled along the noisy conveyor belt as the exhausted passengers waited impatiently at the busy international airport.","t":"當疲憊的乘客在繁忙的國際機場不耐煩地等待時，受損的行李箱緩慢地沿著吵雜的輸送帶滾動。"},{"w":"delicate","p":"adj.","d":"very fine in texture or structure; of intricate workmanship or quality.","c":"精緻的；脆弱的","s":"These extremely delicate white plates are made of fine, expensive china and will easily break if you carelessly drop them on the hard floor.","t":"這些極其精緻的白盤是由優質昂貴的瓷器製成的，如果你粗心地把它們掉在硬地板上，很容易就會碎。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a choice or expensive food.","c":"佳餚；珍饈","s":"In some adventurous foreign countries, eating fried insects is considered a rare culinary delicacy that many curious international tourists eagerly want to try.","t":"在一些愛冒險的外國國家，吃油炸昆蟲被認為是一種罕見的烹飪佳餚，許多好奇的國際遊客都熱切地想嘗試。"},{"w":"delicately","p":"adv.","d":"in a very careful or finely skilled manner.","c":"精緻地；小心翼翼地","s":"The highly experienced surgeon delicately successfully removed the tiny tumor without causing any permanent damage to the patient's surrounding healthy tissues.","t":"經驗極其豐富的外科醫生小心翼翼地成功移除了微小的腫瘤，而沒有對病患周圍的健康組織造成任何永久性的損傷。"},{"w":"firm","p":"adj.","d":"having a solid, almost unyielding surface or structure.","c":"堅固的；堅定的","s":"Unlike the incredibly soft and fragile pillows on my bed, this new mattress is perfectly firm and provides excellent support for my back.","t":"不同於我床上極度柔軟脆弱的枕頭，這張新床墊非常堅固的，能為我的背部提供極好的支撐。"},{"w":"is firmly convinced that","p":"phr.","d":"completely certain and holding a powerful, unyielding belief that something is absolutely true","c":"堅信...；確信...","s":"The leading researcher is firmly convinced that implementing a more rigorous methodology will yield highly accurate data for the experiment.","t":"首席研究員堅信，實施更嚴謹的研究方法將為該實驗帶來高度準確的數據。"},{"w":"law firm","p":"n.","d":"a business partnership formed by lawyers to advise clients about their legal rights and represent them in court","c":"法律事務所","s":"The prestigious law firm decided to amend its operational contract to handle complex international trade disputes more efficiently.","t":"這家聲譽卓著的法律事務所決定修訂其營運合約，以更有效率地處理複雜的國際貿易糾紛。"},{"w":"accounting firm","p":"n.","d":"a company that provides professional services such as auditing, tax preparation, and financial tracking","c":"會計師事務所","s":"The ambitious entrepreneur hired a local accounting firm to thoroughly evaluate the corporation's import and tariff expenses.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的企業家雇用了一家當地的會計師事務所，以徹底評估公司的進口與關稅支出。"},{"w":"evaluate","p":"v.","d":"to form an idea of the amount, number, or value of something after careful appraisal","c":"評估；評價（動詞）","s":"The leading researcher needs to evaluate the scientific data thoroughly before presenting the methodology to the international board.","t":"首席研究員需要在向國際委員會展示研究方法之前，徹底評估科學數據。"},{"w":"evaluation","p":"n.","d":"the making of a judgment about the amount, number, or value of something; assessment","c":"評估；評價（名詞）","s":"The prestigious law firm requested a thorough evaluation of the new trade policy to protect their client's corporation.","t":"這家聲譽卓著的法律事務所要求對新的貿易政策進行徹底的評估，以保護他們客戶的公司。"},{"w":"evaluated","p":"adj./v-pt","d":"having been judged or calculated carefully regarding worth, quality, or significance","c":"被評估的；已評估的","s":"The exported goods were carefully evaluated by customs officers at the port to ensure compliance with international regulations.","t":"這些出口貨物在港口接受了海關官員的仔細評估，以確保符合國際法規。"},{"w":"assess","p":"v.","d":"to officially judge or decide the amount, value, quality, or importance of a situation or tax","c":"評定；評估；核定（動詞）","s":"The accounting firm will systematically assess the financial risks associated with the upcoming business expansion project.","t":"會計師事務所將系統性地評估與即將進行的業務擴展計畫相關的財務風險。"},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"the factual act of judging or deciding the amount, value, quality, or importance of something","c":"評定；評估（名詞）","s":"The government's environmental assessment revealed that the invasive species was heavily damaging the local agricultural ecosystem.","t":"政府的環境評估顯示，這種侵入性物種正嚴重破壞當地的農業生態系統。"},{"w":"assessed","p":"adj./v-pt","d":"evaluated or officially charged with a specific value, property tax, or level of performance","c":"被評定的；已評估的","s":"The total tariff assessed on the imported electronics caused the young entrepreneur to alter his pricing strategy completely.","t":"對進口電子產品所評定的總關稅，促使這位年輕的企業家完全改變了他的定價策略。"},{"w":"access","p":"v.","d":"to open, obtain, or gain entry to a specific digital file, database, secure network, or physical location","c":"讀取；進入；接近（動詞）","s":"Users can smoothly access the online testing platform by entering their registered student name and password.","t":"使用者透過輸入他們註冊的學生姓名與密碼，即可順利登入線上測驗平台。"},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"the right, opportunity, or physical means to approach, enter, or make use of something","c":"進入的權利；通道；路徑（名詞）","s":"The remote mountain village historically had limited access to modern medical facilities before the new highway was constructed.","t":"在新公路修築之前，這座偏遠的山村在歷史上接觸現代醫療設施的機會非常有限。"},{"w":"gain access to","p":"phr.","d":"to successfully manage to enter a secure physical area or retrieve protected digital data","c":"獲得...的進入權；取得（資料）","s":"The clever hacker made a bold attempt to gain access to the secure database framework of the international technology corporation.","t":"這名聰明的駭客做出大膽的嘗試，企圖獲取該國際科技公司安全資料庫架構的存取權。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to approach, enter, obtain, use, or understand for various individuals or devices","c":"可接近的；可進入的；易懂的","s":"The tech company devises responsive web layouts to ensure the online dictionary modal is fully accessible on mobile devices.","t":"這家科技公司設計了響應式網頁版面，以確保線上字典彈窗在行動裝置上完全可以順利使用。"},{"w":"available","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used, obtained, or accessed smoothly, or being free to do something or meet someone","c":"可獲得的；可利用的；有空的","s":"The accounting firm will thoroughly check all the available financial resources before funding the business expansion project.","t":"會計師事務所將在資助業務擴展計畫之前，徹底檢查所有可利用的財務資源。"},{"w":"unavailable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be used, obtained, or accessed at the moment, or being too busy to attend a meeting","c":"無法獲得的；沒空的","s":"Because the automated network server was temporarily unavailable, the software engineering team had to fix the error manually.","t":"由於自動化網路伺服器暫時無法使用，軟體工程團隊必須手動修復該錯誤。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"therapy – depressed","cards":[{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"treatment intended to relieve or heal a disorder.","c":"治療；療法","s":"Doris severely hurt her muscles while playing sports, so she needed intensive physical therapy to help heal them.","t":"朵莉絲在做運動時嚴重拉傷了肌肉，所以她需要密集的物理治療來幫助復原。"},{"w":"physical therapy","p":"phr.","d":"the treatment of disease, injury, or deformity by physical methods such as massage or exercise.","c":"物理治療","s":"After his serious car accident, the young man had to attend physical therapy twice a week for several months.","t":"在嚴重的車禍後，這名年輕人必須連續幾個月每週參加兩次物理治療。"},{"w":"ancient","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the very distant past and no longer in existence.","c":"古老的","s":"The ambitious university professor was extremely excited when he discovered the ruined buildings of a magnificent ancient city.","t":"當這位雄心勃勃的大學教授發現一座宏偉古老的城市的建築遺跡時，他感到極度興奮。"},{"w":"elderly","p":"adj.","d":"old or aging.","c":"年長的","s":"Tim is a very devoted son who makes sure to visit his elderly parents every single Sunday morning.","t":"提姆是個非常孝順的兒子，他確保每個星期天早上都會去探望他年長的父母。"},{"w":"the elderly","p":"n.","d":"old people considered as a group.","c":"年長者（集合名詞）","s":"The local government recently started a brand new social program specifically designed to care for the elderly in our community.","t":"當地政府最近啟動了一個全新的社會計畫，專門設計來照顧我們社區的年長者。"},{"w":"aged","p":"adj.","d":"having lived for a specified length of time; having grown old.","c":"...歲的；年老的","s":"Mike dutifully looks after his aged parents who can no longer comfortably take care of themselves at home.","t":"麥克盡責地照顧他那無法再舒適地在家自理的年老的父母。"},{"w":"middle-aged","p":"adj.","d":"Being in the period of life between youth and old age, typically from about 40 to 60 years old.","c":"中年的","s":"The middle-aged man decided to join a local marathon to stay healthy and energetic as he approached his fifties.","t":"這位中年的男子決定參加當地的馬拉松比賽，以便在接近五十歲時保持健康與活力。"},{"w":"middle class","p":"n. [C]","d":"A social group between the rich and the poor, including professional and business people.","c":"中產階級","s":"Most families living in this suburban neighborhood belong to the middle class, earning a stable income and owning their homes.","t":"居住在這個郊區社區的大多數家庭都屬於中產階級，擁有穩定的收入並擁有自己的房子。"},{"w":"ageing / aging","p":"adj.","d":"Becoming older, or showing signs of growing old.","c":"變老的、高齡化的、老化的","s":"The government is building more nursing homes to provide better medical care for the country's aging population.","t":"政府正在建造更多養老院，以便為該國高齡化的（變老的）人口提供更好的醫療照護。"},{"w":"ageing society","p":"n.","d":"A society where the average age of the population increases because of falling birth rates and longer life-spans.","c":"高齡化社會","s":"Taiwan has officially become an ageing society, which means there are fewer young workers to support the retired population.","t":"台灣已正式成為一個高齡化社會，這意味著能扶養退休人口的年輕勞動力變少了。"},{"w":"senior","p":"n. / adj.","d":"an older person; of a more advanced age.","c":"年長者；資深的","s":"The local movie theater kindly offers much cheaper movie tickets to students and senior during the weekday afternoons.","t":"當地電影院親切地在平日下午為學生和年長者提供便宜許多的電影票。"},{"w":"senior citizen","p":"n.","d":"An older person, usually someone who has retired from work (often over 65).","c":"老年人、銀髮族","s":"Every senior citizen living in this city can take public transportation for free by showing their special identity card.","t":"居住在這座城市的每位老年人（銀髮族）大只要出示他們的特殊身分證，就可以免費搭乘大眾運輸。"},{"w":"is senior to","p":"phr.","d":"To have a higher rank, position, or status than someone else in an organization or company.","c":"職位比…高、資歷比…深","s":"Although Marcus is much younger than Kevin, he is senior to Kevin because he was promoted to manager last year.","t":"雖然馬庫斯比凱文年輕得多，但在公司裡他的職位比凱文高（資歷比凱文深），因為他去年被晉升為經理。"},{"w":"is junior to","p":"phr.","d":"To have a lower rank, position, or status than someone else in an organization or company.","c":"職位比…低、資歷比…淺","s":"Since Chloe just joined the accounting department last week, she is junior to everyone else in terms of work experience.","t":"由於克洛伊上週才加入會計部，就工作經驗而言，她的職位比其他人低（資歷比其他人淺）。"},{"w":"limit","p":"v. n.","d":"a point or level beyond which something does not or may not extend or pass.","c":"限制；極限","s":"If you genuinely want to lose some extra weight, you must set a limit the amount of sweet food you eat.","t":"如果你真的想減掉一些多餘的體重，你必須嚴格制定醣類攝取限制量和限制你吃的甜食數量。"},{"w":"set a speed limit","p":"phr.","d":"to establish a legal maximum or minimum speed allowed for vehicles traveling on a specific road","c":"設定速限","s":"The city council decided to set a speed limit along the busy residential area to minimize traffic accidents and ensure pedestrian safety.","t":"市議會決定沿著繁忙的住宅區設定速限，以減少交通事故並確保行人安全。"},{"w":"limitation","p":"n.","d":"a limiting rule or circumstance; a restriction.","c":"限制；極限","s":"His only noticeable limitation as a professional fashion model is that he is actually a little bit too short.","t":"他作為職業時裝模特兒唯一明顯的限制，是他實際上稍微太矮了一點。"},{"w":"strict limitation","p":"phr.","d":"a severe or unyielding restriction.","c":"嚴格的限制","s":"Because of the terrible water shortage, the city council imposed a strict limitation on washing cars and watering gardens.","t":"因為可怕的水資源短缺，市議會對洗車和澆花實施了嚴格的限制。"},{"w":"restrict","p":"v.","d":"to put a limit on someone or something, or to keep something within strict legal boundaries","c":"限制；限定（動詞）","s":"The government decided to restrict civilian access to the military zone to protect top-secret scientific experiments.","t":"政府決定限制平民進入軍事管制區，以保護絕密的科學實驗。"},{"w":"restriction","p":"n.","d":"an official rule, statute, or law that limits what people can do or how a total system operates","c":"限制（名詞）","s":"The prestigious law firm thoroughly evaluated the new trade restriction imposed on imported goods at the port.","t":"這家聲譽卓著的法律事務所徹底評估了港口對進口貨物所施加的新貿易限制。"},{"w":"ban ...from","p":"phr.","d":"to officially or legally forbid someone from doing something, entering a place, or using a service","c":"禁止...做...","s":"The strict city council intends to ban private vehicles from entering the crowded commercial area during rush hours.","t":"嚴格的市議會打算在尖峰時段禁止私人車輛進入擁擠的商業區。"},{"w":"lift the ban","p":"phr.","d":"to officially remove or cancel a legal prohibition or restriction that was previously established","c":"解除禁令","s":"The president decided to lift the ban on foreign technology products after the trade agreement went smoothly.","t":"在貿易協定順利進行後，總統決定解除對外國科技產品的禁令。"},{"w":"prohibit","p":"v.","d":"to officially or legally forbid something by a law, rule, statue, or authoritative decree","c":"禁止；不准（動詞）","s":"New traffic regulations strictly prohibit the parking of any private vehicle along the narrow streets of the residential area.","t":"新的交通法規嚴格禁止在住宅區的狹窄街道上停放任何私人車輛。"},{"w":"prohibit ...from","p":"phr.","d":"to formally prevent or legally stop an individual or group from doing a specific activity","c":"禁止...做...","s":"The strict company policy will prohibit unauthorized staff from gaining access to the secure database framework of the corporation.","t":"公司嚴格的政策將禁止未經授權的人員獲取公司安全資料庫架構的存取權。"},{"w":"inhibit...from","p":"phr.","d":"to prevent, slow down, or hinder someone or something from making progress or developing naturally","c":"阻礙...做...；抑制...","s":"Extreme winter weather will heavily inhibit the logistics workers from delivering the express cargo to the harbor.","t":"極端寒冬的天氣將嚴重阻礙物流工人將快捷貨物運送到港口。"},{"w":"inhibition","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of embarrassment or worry that prevents you from saying or doing what you truly want","c":"拘束；顧忌；壓抑","s":"The student successfully overcame her initial inhibition and made an active attempt to state her opinion clearly.","t":"這名學生成功克服了她起初的顧忌，並大膽嘗試清楚地陳述她的觀點。"},{"w":"refrain from","p":"phr.","d":"to intentionally choose to stop oneself from doing something, especially an undesirable habit","c":"克制不去做...；忍住...","s":"All participants in the scientific experiment must refrain from smoking before the leading researcher begins the assessment.","t":"在首席研究員開始評估之前，科學實驗的所有參與者都必須克制不去吸菸。"},{"w":"restraint","p":"n.","d":"controlled behavior, self-control, or a legal/physical restriction that limits someone's freedom or actions","c":"克制；抑制；約束（名詞）","s":"The police officers exercised remarkable restraint when dealing with the highly aggressive protesters at the crime scene.","t":"警員在犯罪現場應對極具攻擊性的抗議者時，表現出了驚人的克制。"},{"w":"exercise control","p":"phr.","d":"to actively direct, influence, or manage the behavior, operation, or development of something","c":"施加控制；進行管理 (補充)","s":"The central bank attempts to exercise strict control over the national currency to prevent sudden inflation in the market.","t":"中央銀行試圖對國家貨幣實施嚴格控制，以防止市場上突然發生通貨膨脹。"},{"w":"exercise self-discipline","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically control one's own desires, emotions, and behaviors to achieve long-term goals","c":"展現自律；實踐自我克制","s":"The ambitious student needs to exercise self-discipline to study for the standardized exam instead of playing video games.","t":"這名雄心勃勃的學生需要展現自律來準備標準化考試，而不是玩電子遊戲。"},{"w":"exercise caution","p":"phr.","d":"to be purposefully careful and alert in order to avoid potential danger, mistakes, or accidents","c":"保持謹慎；格外小心","s":"Drivers must exercise caution when navigating the narrow and slippery mountain roads during a severe winter storm.","t":"在嚴重的冬季暴風雨中行駛於狹窄且濕滑的山路時，駕駛人必須保持謹慎。"},{"w":"exercise patience","p":"phr.","d":"to intentionally remain calm and controlled while waiting for something or dealing with difficulties","c":"保持耐心","s":"The leading researcher reminded his young assistants to exercise patience while waiting for the scientific data to compile.","t":"首席研究員提醒他的年輕助手們，在等待科學數據彙編時要保持耐心。"},{"w":"exercise the authority","p":"phr.","d":"to officially use legal power, command, or directional control over an organization or state","c":"行使公權力；行使職權","s":"The newly appointed military commander decided to exercise the authority to restrict civilian access to the critical crime scene.","t":"新上任的軍事指揮官決定行使職權，限制平民進入關鍵的犯罪現場。"},{"w":"exercise civil rights","p":"phr.","d":"to formally use or apply a legal prerogative, freedom, or privilege guaranteed by the law","c":"行使公民權利","s":"All citizens are heavily encouraged to exercise civil rights to vote in the upcoming presidential election and referendum next month.","t":"所有公民都被強烈鼓勵在下個月即將舉行的總統大選和公投中行使投票權。"},{"w":"election","p":"n.","d":"a formal and organized choice by vote of a person for a political office or other position","c":"選舉","s":"The progressive political party urged every single citizen to exercise their legal right to vote in the upcoming presidential election.","t":"進步派政黨敦促每一位公民在即將到來的總統選舉中行使他們的合法投票權。"},{"w":"referendum","p":"n.","d":"a general vote by the electorate on a single political question which has been referred to them for a direct decision","c":"公民投票；公投","s":"The government decided to conduct a national referendum to let citizens directly determine whether to alter the existing tariff laws.","t":"政府決定舉行全民公投，讓公民直接決定是否修改現行的關稅法律。"},{"w":"practice a religious ritual","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically perform a traditional ceremony, custom, or service associated with a faith","c":"履行宗教儀式","s":"The local tribe gathered at the ancient temple to practice a religious ritual to pray for a bountiful autumn harvest.","t":"當地部落聚集在古老的寺廟裡履行宗教儀式，以祈求秋季豐收。"},{"w":"practice law","p":"phr.","d":"to officially work as a professional lawyer or legal advisor within a specific legislative framework","c":"執業（律師）；從事法律工作","s":"After passing the rigorous bar exam, the progressive lawyer decided to practice law at a prestigious international law firm.","t":"在通過嚴格的律師資格考試後，這位進步派律師決定在一家聲譽卓著的國際法律事務所執業。"},{"w":"practice medicine","p":"phr.","d":"to officially work as a qualified medical doctor, treating patients and prescribing therapies","c":"執業（醫生）；從事醫療工作","s":"The skilled surgeon obtained her official license and began to practice medicine in a remote rural community that lacked facilities.","t":"這位技術熟練的外科醫生獲得了她的正式執照，並開始在一個缺乏設施的偏遠農村社區從事醫療工作。"},{"w":"perform a surgery","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically carry out a medical operation on a patient to treat a physical injury or illness","c":"進行手術","s":"The experienced chief surgeon will perform a surgery tomorrow morning to repair the patient's severely damaged mechanical heart.","t":"經驗豐富的總外科醫生將於明天上午進行手術，以修復患者嚴重受損的機械心臟。"},{"w":"perform a duty","p":"phr.","d":"to actively execute, fulfill, or carry out a moral obligation, legal responsibility, or assigned task","c":"履行職責；執行任務","s":"Every loyal police officer is fully expected to perform a duty with complete integrity and protect local communities.","t":"每位忠誠的警員都被充分期望能以完全正直的態度履行職責，並保護當地社群。"},{"w":"perform an act of kindness","p":"phr.","d":"to intentionally do a helpful, generous, or considerate action for another individual without expecting reward","c":"做出善行","s":"Even a small gesture can make a significant difference when you perform an act of kindness for a complete stranger.","t":"當你為一個完全陌生的人做出善行時，即使是一個小小的舉動也能帶來重大的改變。"},{"w":"conduct an experiment","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically organize and carry out a scientific test or trial to discover or verify facts","c":"進行實驗","s":"The software engineering team plans to conduct an experiment to assess whether the new automated system operates smoothly.","t":"軟體工程團隊計劃進行一項實驗，以評估這個新的自動化系統是否運作順利。"},{"w":"conduct a research project","p":"phr.","d":"to professionally organize, manage, and execute a systematic academic investigation or deep study","c":"主導研究計畫","s":"The leading university received a massive government grant to conduct a research project on endangered wild animal species.","t":"這所頂尖大學獲得了巨額的政府補助，以主導一項關於瀕危野生動物物種的研究計畫。"},{"w":"conduct a survey","p":"phr.","d":"to systematically gather specific opinions, data, or facts from a targeted group of participants","c":"進行調查","s":"The marketing firm decided to conduct a survey to evaluate consumer satisfaction regarding the new portable devices.","t":"這家行銷公司決定進行一項調查，以評估消費者對這款全新便攜式裝置的滿意度。"},{"w":"conduct an interview","p":"phr.","d":"to formally host, guide, and ask questions during a structured meeting with a prospective candidate","c":"舉辦面試","s":"The human resources department will conduct an interview tomorrow to assess the applicant's mechanical engineering skills.","t":"人力資源部門明天將進行面試，以評估應徵者的機械工程技能。"},{"w":"conduct an orchestra","p":"phr.","d":"to actively direct and coordinate the performance of a large musical group using hand gestures or a baton","c":"指揮交響樂團","s":"The world-renowned musician was invited to conduct an orchestra during the international charity concert next weekend.","t":"這位世界聞名的音樂家受邀在下週末的國際慈善音樂會上指揮交響樂團。"},{"w":"conduct heat","p":"phr.","d":"to efficiently transmit thermal energy or warmth directly through a specific material or substance","c":"傳導熱","s":"Copper and aluminum are highly valued in manufacturing because they can conduct heat much faster than plastic materials.","t":"銅和鋁在製造業中受到高度重視，因為它們傳導熱的速度比塑膠材料快得多。"},{"w":"conduct electricity","p":"phr.","d":"to efficiently allow an electrical current or energy flow to pass smoothly through a physical substance","c":"導電","s":"Pure water itself is a poor conductor, but dissolved minerals allow the liquid to conduct electricity very efficiently.","t":"純水本身是個不良導體，但溶解的礦物質能讓這種液體非常高效地導電。"},{"w":"hold a ceremony","p":"phr.","d":"to formally organize and conduct a traditional, official, or ritualistic public event","c":"舉行儀式；舉辦典禮","s":"The indigenous tribe gathered near the ancient harbor to hold a ceremony to pray for a bountiful and safe fishing season.","t":"原住民部落聚集在古老的港口附近舉行儀式，以祈求豐收且安全的捕魚季節。"},{"w":"throw a party","p":"phr.","d":"to informally organize, host, and fund a celebratory social gathering for friends or colleagues","c":"舉辦派對；辦宴會","s":"The ambitious entrepreneur decided to throw a party to celebrate the international corporation's successful business expansion.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的企業家決定舉辦一場派對，以慶祝這家國際公司的業務擴展圓滿成功。"},{"w":"notice","p":"v.","d":"to become aware of; the fact of observing or paying attention to something.","c":"注意（到）","s":"Did you happen to notice that Sarah was wearing a completely different dress when she returned from the bathroom?","t":"你有碰巧注意到莎拉從洗手間回來時穿著一件完全不同的洋裝嗎？"},{"w":"notice","p":"n.","d":"A written or printed announcement or warning displayed for everyone to see.","c":"公告、通知、啟事","s":"The school principal put up a large notice next to the main entrance to inform students that the annual sports day has been postponed.","t":"校長在主入口旁張貼了一份大型公告，以通知學生年度運動會已延期。"},{"w":"noticeable","p":"adj.","d":"easily seen or noticed; clear or apparent.","c":"明顯的；引人注目的","s":"After he finally left his stressful home environment, there was a highly noticeable change in his overall daily attitude.","t":"在他終於離開壓力沉重的家庭環境後，他整體的日常態度有了非常明顯的改變。"},{"w":"bulletin","p":"n.","d":"A short official statement or news report about an important matter of public interest.","c":"（官方的）簡報、公告、新聞快報","s":"The hospital issued a regular medical bulletin regarding the president's health condition to keep the anxious public informed.","t":"醫院發布了關於總統健康狀況的定期醫療簡報（公告），以讓焦慮的公眾知情。"},{"w":"bulletin board","p":"phr.","d":"A board on a wall where people can pin notices, advertisements, or messages.","c":"佈告欄、公告欄","s":"Students frequently check the bulletin board in the hallway to see the latest updates about club activities and school events.","t":"學生們經常查看走廊上的佈告欄，以了解社團活動和學校事件的最新動態。"},{"w":"apparent","p":"adj.","d":"clearly visible or understood; obvious.","c":"明顯的；顯而易見的","s":"It was quite apparent to everyone in the room that the nervous man was lying about his true identity.","t":"房間裡的每個人都很明顯的看出這個緊張的男人在說謊掩飾他的真實身分。"},{"w":"obvious","p":"adj.","d":"Easy to see, recognize, or understand.","c":"明顯的、顯而易見的","s":"It was obvious to everyone in the room that Leo was nervous, because his hands were shaking violently during the presentation.","t":"房間裡的每個人都很明顯地看出里歐很緊張，因為他在簡報時雙手抖得很厲害。"},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"open to more than one interpretation; having a double meaning.","c":"模稜兩可的","s":"The politician's completely ambiguous answer to the journalist's serious question left the entire audience feeling extremely confused and frustrated.","t":"這位政治人物對記者嚴肅問題完全模稜兩可的回答，讓全場觀眾感到極度困惑和沮喪。"},{"w":"vague","p":"adj.","d":"Not clear, definite, or specific in thought, expression, or details.","c":"模糊的、含糊的、不明確的","s":"The detective found the witness's description of the suspect very vague, as she could only remember that he was wearing a dark jacket.","t":"偵探發現證人對嫌犯的描述非常含糊（模糊），因為她只記得他穿著一件深色外套。"},{"w":"blurry","p":"adj.","d":"Not clear or sharp, especially when referring to images, photos, or vision.","c":"模糊的、（影像）不清晰的","s":"Because Chloe accidentally moved her hand while clicking the shutter, the photo she took of the beautiful sunset turned out completely blurry.","t":"因為克洛伊在按下快門時不小心動了手，她拍的那張美麗落日的照片結果完全是模糊的。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"Existing as an idea, feeling, or quality rather than a physical or material object.","c":"抽象的","s":"Truth and justice are abstract concepts that can be difficult for young children to understand, as they usually prefer concrete examples they can see.","t":"真理和正義是幼童可能很難理解的抽象概念，因爲他們通常更喜歡看得見的具體例子。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"space or equipment necessary for doing something.","c":"設施；機構","s":"When the man suddenly collapsed on the street, the ambulance rushed him directly to a nearby medical facility.","t":"當那名男子突然在街上倒下時，救護車將他直接送往附近的醫療機構。"},{"w":"medical facility","p":"phr.","d":"a place where healthcare is provided.","c":"醫療機構","s":"In rural areas, it can sometimes take hours to drive a sick patient to the nearest fully equipped medical facility.","t":"在鄉村地區，有時可能需要開車數小時才能將生病的病患送到最近且設備齊全的醫療機構。"},{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make an action or process easy or easier.","c":"促進；使便利","s":"The new interactive teaching software is specifically designed to deeply facilitate faster and more effective learning for young children.","t":"這個新的互動教學軟體專門設計來深入促進幼童更快、更有效的學習。"},{"w":"wheelchair","p":"n.","d":"a chair fitted with wheels for use as a means of transport by a person who is unable to walk.","c":"輪椅","s":"The poor old man unfortunately can't walk anymore and desperately needs a wheelchair just to get around his house.","t":"可憐的老人不幸地再也無法走路，極度需要一張輪椅才能在他的房子裡四處走動。"},{"w":"wheelchair bound","p":"adj.","d":"unable to walk and thus forced to use a wheelchair.","c":"必須坐輪椅的","s":"Despite being entirely wheelchair bound for most of his adult life, the inspiring man managed to write three brilliant books.","t":"儘管在他的成年生活中大多是完全必須坐輪椅的，這位激勵人心的人還是成功寫出了三本才華洋溢的書。"},{"w":"motorized wheelchair","p":"phr.","d":"a wheelchair propelled by an electric motor.","c":"電動輪椅","s":"Thanks to his highly advanced motorized wheelchair, the disabled veteran can easily navigate the busy city streets completely by himself.","t":"多虧了他高度先進的電動輪椅，這位殘障的退伍軍人能完全靠自己輕鬆地在繁忙的城市街道上穿梭。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"reciprocal action or influence; communication.","c":"互動","s":"Because Carol doesn't have any classes with Sam, they unfortunately don't have much personal interaction during the long school day.","t":"因為卡蘿沒有和山姆同班的課，他們在漫長的上學日中不幸地沒有多少個人的互動。"},{"w":"interact with","p":"v.","d":"to act in such a way as to have an effect on another; to communicate.","c":"互動；交流","s":"The friendly kindergarten teacher always strongly encourages her shy students to confidently interact with each other during outdoor playtime.","t":"友善的幼稚園老師總是強烈鼓勵她害羞的學生在戶外遊戲時間自信地互相互動。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing a two-way flow of information between a computer and a computer-user; responding to a user's input.","c":"互動式的","s":"The fascinating science museum features many brilliant interactive exhibits that brilliantly allow children to physically test out physics principles.","t":"迷人的科學博物館擁有許多出色的互動式的展覽，出色地讓孩子們能實際測試物理原理。"},{"w":"social interaction","p":"phr.","d":"the process of acting and reacting to the people around us.","c":"社交互動","s":"Maintaining regular and positive social interaction is incredibly important for preserving an elderly person's mental health and overall happiness.","t":"維持規律且積極的社交互動，對於保存年長者的心理健康和整體幸福感極其重要。"},{"w":"magical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, using, or resembling magic.","c":"魔法的；神奇的","s":"The beautifully decorated theme park creates a truly magical experience for young children visiting it for the very first time.","t":"裝飾美麗的主題樂園為第一次造訪的幼童創造了真正神奇的體驗。"},{"w":"magically","p":"adv.","d":"by or as if by magic.","c":"如魔法般地；神奇地","s":"During the impressive performance, the floating cup appeared to magically hover completely unsupported right above the wooden desk.","t":"在令人印象深刻的表演中，漂浮的杯子似乎神奇地完全無支撐地盤旋在木製書桌正上方。"},{"w":"miracle","p":"n.","d":"an extraordinary and welcome event that is not explicable by natural or scientific laws and is considered to be the work of a divine agency","c":"奇蹟","s":"The chief surgeon stated that it was a complete miracle that the patient survived such a severe heart failure during the operation.","t":"主治醫生聲稱，病人在手術過程中經歷了如此嚴重的生命心臟衰竭卻能活下來，完全是一個奇蹟。"},{"w":"miraculous","p":"adj.","d":"occurring through divine or extraordinary intervention; highly improbable and extraordinarily wonderful","c":"奇蹟般的；不可思議的","s":"The injured athlete made a miraculous recovery just a few weeks before the highly anticipated international programming tournament.","t":"這名受傷的運動員在備受期待的國際程式設計大賽舉行前幾週，做出了奇蹟般的康復。"},{"w":"miraculously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that resembles or suggests a miracle; extraordinarily, unexpectedly, or completely by chance","c":"奇蹟般地","s":"Despite driving through a severe winter storm on the narrow mountain road, the entire family miraculously arrived home safely without any accidents.","t":"儘管在狹窄的山路上開車穿過嚴重的冬季暴風雨，全家人依然奇蹟般地安全抵達家門，沒有發生任何意外。"},{"w":"appear magically","p":"phr.","d":"to suddenly show up as if brought by magic.","c":"神奇地出現","s":"Just when we desperately needed a taxi in the pouring rain, one seemed to appear magically right at the corner.","t":"正當我們在傾盆大雨中極度需要計程車時，一輛計程車似乎神奇地出現在轉角處。"},{"w":"transform","p":"v.","d":"to make a thorough or dramatic change in the form, appearance, or character of.","c":"改變；改造","s":"Buying that expensive new modern furniture completely transformed their dark and boring living room into a bright, stylish space.","t":"買下那套昂貴的新現代家具，徹底將他們黑暗無聊的客廳改造成一個明亮、時尚的空間。"},{"w":"transform a into b","p":"phr.","d":"to completely change one thing into another.","c":"把A變成B","s":"The ambitious city government officially plans to successfully transform a into b a beautiful large shopping complex.","t":"雄心勃勃的市政府正式計畫成功地把廢棄的舊工廠建築變成一個美麗的大型購物中心。"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a thorough or dramatic change in form or appearance.","c":"轉變；變形","s":"The butterfly's miraculous physical transformation from a tiny, creeping caterpillar is widely considered one of nature's most beautiful processes.","t":"蝴蝶從一隻微小爬行的毛毛蟲發生的奇蹟般物理轉變，被廣泛認為是自然界最美麗的過程之一。"},{"w":"convert","p":"v.","d":"to cause to change in form, character, or function.","c":"轉換；改變","s":"The wealthy businessman decided to expensively convert his massive basement into a fully equipped private cinema for his family.","t":"富有的商人決定花大錢將他巨大的地下室改裝（轉換）成一個設備齊全的家庭私人電影院。"},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest from work or engage in an enjoyable activity so as to become less tired or anxious.","c":"放鬆","s":"After successfully finishing his incredibly difficult final exams, Ian finally had the opportunity to just sit down and relax.","t":"在成功完成極其困難的期末考後，伊恩終於有機會直接坐下來放鬆。"},{"w":"relaxation","p":"n.","d":"the state of being free from tension and anxiety.","c":"放鬆；消遣","s":"Exhausted Sasha firmly told me that she specifically wants her upcoming summer vacation to be entirely about rest and relaxation.","t":"疲憊的莎夏堅定地告訴我，她特別希望即將到來的暑假能完全是關於休息和放鬆。"},{"w":"relaxed","p":"adj.","d":"free from tension and anxiety; at ease.","c":"放鬆的；從容的","s":"The manager's calm and highly relaxed leadership style surprisingly helps the entire office remain highly productive during stressful deadlines.","t":"經理平靜且高度從容的領導風格，出人意料地幫助整個辦公室在充滿壓力的截止日期期間保持高生產力。"},{"w":"relaxing","p":"adj.","d":"reducing tension or anxiety.","c":"令人放鬆的","s":"Getting a professional deep tissue massage after a terribly stressful week at work is arguably the most relaxing experience possible.","t":"在工作了極度充滿壓力的一週後，接受專業的深層組織按摩可以說是可能最令人放鬆的體驗了。"},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"the state of being stretched tight; mental or emotional strain.","c":"緊張；拉力","s":"The unbearable physical tension in his sore shoulders finally began to disappear after he took a long, hot shower.","t":"在洗了個舒服的熱水澡後，他痠痛肩膀上難以忍受的身體緊張（緊繃）終於開始消失了。"},{"w":"presence","p":"n.","d":"the state or fact of existing, occurring, or being present in a place or thing.","c":"出席；存在","s":"You don't have to come to the party, but your pleasant presence would undoubtedly make everyone there incredibly happy.","t":"你不必來參加派對，但你令人愉快的出席無疑會讓在那裡的每個人都非常高興。"},{"w":"in the presence of","p":"phr.","d":"in front of or existing with someone else.","c":"在...的面前","s":"Naughty Ted surprisingly always acts extremely well-behaved and polite whenever he is in the presence of his strict parents.","t":"頑皮的泰德令人驚訝地每當他在他嚴格父母的面前時，總是表現得極度守規矩且有禮貌。"},{"w":"present","p":"adj.","d":"existing or occurring now; in a particular place.","c":"在場的；現在的","s":"The principal demanded to ensure that every single senior student was actually physically present in the auditorium for the speech.","t":"校長要求確保每一位高三學生實際上都確實在場於禮堂聆聽演講。"},{"w":"absence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being away from a place or person.","c":"缺席；不在","s":"The manager noted that John's continued and entirely unexplained absence from the important weekly meetings was becoming a serious issue.","t":"經理指出，約翰持續且完全無法解釋的對重要週會的缺席，正成為一個嚴重的問題。"},{"w":"orphan","p":"n. / v.","d":"a child whose parents are dead; to make a child an orphan.","c":"孤兒；使成為孤兒","s":"The generous charity specifically works hard to securely provide safe housing and good food for every homeless orphan in the city.","t":"這家慷慨的慈善機構特別努力為城市裡每一位無家可歸的孤兒穩妥地提供安全的住所和良好的食物。"},{"w":"orphanage","p":"n.","d":"a residential institution for the care and education of orphans.","c":"孤兒院","s":"Poor John sadly grew up in a crowded local orphanage after his loving parents tragically passed away in a car accident.","t":"可憐的約翰在他充滿愛的父母於車禍中悲慘離世後，令人遺憾地在擁擠的當地孤兒院長大。"},{"w":"express","p":"v.","d":"to convey a thought or feeling in words or by gestures and conduct.","c":"表達","s":"Because the quiet man was not naturally express, I simply didn't know what he actually wanted from the store.","t":"因為這個安靜的男人天生不擅表達，我根本不知道他實際上想從店裡得到什麼。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"effectively conveying thought or feeling.","c":"富於表情的；善於表達的","s":"The incredibly talented actor's highly expressive face perfectly communicated his deep sorrow without him ever needing to speak a word.","t":"這位才華洋溢的演員極其富於表情的臉龐，完美地傳達了他深深的悲傷，而不需要他說出任何一個字。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"the process of making known one's thoughts or feelings.","c":"表達；表情","s":"Writing incredibly beautiful poetry was her absolute favorite form of emotional expression whenever she felt lonely or deeply misunderstood.","t":"每當她感到孤單或深深被誤解時，寫出極其美麗的詩是她絕對最喜歡的情感表達形式。"},{"w":"talkative","p":"adj.","d":"fond of or given to talking.","c":"健談的；多話的","s":"Unlike her exceptionally quiet sister, Maria is a highly talkative person who can easily chat with complete strangers for hours.","t":"不同於她異常安靜的妹妹，瑪麗亞是個極其健談的人，可以輕鬆地與完全陌生的人聊上幾個小時。"},{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"done by people acting as a group.","c":"集體的；共同的","s":"Rebuilding the completely destroyed town after the terrible earthquake clearly required an immense collective effort from every single surviving citizen.","t":"在可怕的地震後重建被徹底摧毀的城鎮，顯然需要每一位倖存公民付出巨大的集體的努力。"},{"w":"tense","p":"adj.","d":"stretched tight or unable to relax; causing anxiety.","c":"緊張的；緊繃的","s":"Alice unfortunately feels extremely tense most of the time because her demanding corporate job is very difficult and highly stressful.","t":"艾莉絲不幸地大部分時間都感到極度緊張的，因為她要求極高的企業工作非常困難且壓力極大。"},{"w":"feel tense","p":"phr.","d":"to experience physical or emotional tightness.","c":"感到緊張","s":"It is completely natural to feel incredibly tense and anxious right before delivering an important speech to a large, silent audience.","t":"在向大批安靜的觀眾發表重要演講之前，感到極度緊張和焦慮是完全自然的。"},{"w":"tense mood","p":"phr.","d":"a heavily strained atmosphere.","c":"緊張的氣氛","s":"The unpredictable tense mood in the dark room was palpable as the angry family awkwardly ate their dinner in complete silence.","t":"當這個憤怒的家庭在完全的沉默中尷尬地吃著晚餐時，黑暗房間裡不可預測的緊張的氣氛是顯而易見的。"},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of fear, distrust, or anxiety caused by tight relationships or unresolved conflict","c":"緊張（關係）；局勢緊張","s":"The rising political tension between the two neighbouring countries forced the international border to close temporarily.","t":"兩國之間日益加劇的政治緊張關係迫使國際邊界暫時關閉。"},{"w":"relieve tension","p":"phr.","d":"to reduce mental or emotional strain.","c":"緩解緊張","s":"Engaging in regular deep breathing exercises can effectively relieve the terrible physical tension that builds up during a long workday.","t":"進行規律的深呼吸運動可以有效地緩解在漫長工作日中累積的可怕身體緊張。"},{"w":"intensive","p":"adj.","d":"involving a high degree of concentrated effort, massive resources, or energy within a short time","c":"密集的；集中的","s":"The engineering team underwent intensive training to master the newly deployed automated server frameworks.","t":"工程團隊接受了密集的培訓，以掌握新部署的自動化伺服器架構。"},{"w":"intensive course","p":"n.","d":"a highly concentrated educational program designed to teach extensive knowledge very quickly","c":"密集課程","s":"Joining an intensive course in asset management helped the young intern quickly fulfill his professional potential.","t":"參加資產管理的密集課程幫助這位年輕實習生迅速發揮了他的專業潛力。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to cause pain, distress, or difficulty to become less severe or serious.","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"Gus cautiously took some expensive prescription medicine to quickly relieve the sharp, shooting pain in his lower back.","t":"葛斯謹慎地吃了一些昂貴的處方藥，以迅速緩解他下背部劇烈刺痛的疼痛。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of reassurance and relaxation following release from anxiety or distress.","c":"如釋重負；解脫","s":"Joe immediately felt a huge sense of deep relief after the experienced doctor told him he would definitely recover completely.","t":"在經驗豐富的醫生告訴他絕對會完全康復後，喬立刻感到了一種巨大的深深的如釋重負。"},{"w":"relieved","p":"adj.","d":"no longer feeling distressed or anxious; reassured.","c":"感到寬慰的","s":"The terribly worried parents were visibly relieved when the brave police officer safely brought their missing little boy back home.","t":"當勇敢的警察安全地把他們失蹤的小男孩帶回家時，極度擔憂的父母明顯地感到寬慰的。"},{"w":"anxiety","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry, nervousness, or unease, typically about an imminent event.","c":"焦慮","s":"Poor Chris has tragically suffered from crippling anxiety for much of his difficult adult life, making it hard to socialize.","t":"可憐的克里斯在他艱難的成年生活中大部分時間都悲慘地遭受嚴重焦慮的折磨，使他難以社交。"},{"w":"anxious","p":"adj.","d":"experiencing worry, nervousness, or unease.","c":"焦慮的；渴望的","s":"The young job applicant felt incredibly anxious and sweaty while sitting quietly in the cold waiting room before his interview.","t":"年輕的求職者在面試前安靜地坐在寒冷的候診室時，感到極度焦慮的且流汗。"},{"w":"anxiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a manner resulting from or revealing anxiety.","c":"焦急地","s":"The loving mother stood by the window and completely anxiously watched the dark street, waiting for her teenage daughter's return.","t":"慈愛的母親站在窗邊，完全焦急地看著黑暗的街道，等待著她十幾歲的女兒歸來。"},{"w":"anxiety disorder","p":"phr.","d":"a mental health disorder characterized by feelings of worry or fear.","c":"焦慮症","s":"It is highly recommended to seek professional psychological help if you constantly suspect you might officially have an anxiety disorder.","t":"如果你不斷懷疑自己可能正式患有焦慮症，強烈建議尋求專業心理協助。"},{"w":"depression","p":"n.","d":"a persistent mental health condition characterized by severe long-term sadness, low energy, and loss of interest","c":"憂鬱症；沮喪","s":"The experienced counselor provided professional guidance to help the young student overcome her severe academic depression.","t":"經驗豐富的輔導老師提供了專業的指導，以幫助這名年輕學生克服她嚴重的學業沮喪。"},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling deeply sad, hopeless, and discouraged about life or a specific unfortunate situation","c":"感到憂鬱的；沮喪的","s":"Feeling heavily depressed after the sudden business failure, the ambitious entrepreneur decided to take a short break to restore his energy.","t":"在突如其來的商業失敗後感到非常沮喪，這位雄心勃勃的企業家決定休個短假以恢復精力。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"sensation – exposition","cards":[{"w":"sensation","p":"n.","d":"a physical feeling or perception resulting from something that happens to or comes into contact with the body.","c":"感覺；轟動","s":"The young girl felt a strange and uncomfortable sensation when the freezing cold wind unexpectedly blew past her.","t":"當冰冷的寒風出乎意料地吹過她身旁時，這個年輕女孩感到一種奇怪且不舒服的感覺。"},{"w":"strange sensation","p":"phr.","d":"an unusual physical or mental feeling.","c":"奇怪的感覺","s":"Being out on a large boat for the very first time is a strange sensation that certainly takes some getting used to.","t":"第一次乘坐大船出海是一種肯定需要一些時間來適應的奇怪的感覺。"},{"w":"sensational","p":"adj.","d":"causing great public interest and excitement.","c":"轟動的；極好的","s":"The new science fiction movie is truly sensational and has quickly received thousands of highly positive reviews online.","t":"這部新的科幻電影真的是極好的（轟動的），並已迅速在網路上獲得了數千條高度正面的評論。"},{"w":"create a sensation","p":"phr.","d":"to cause a lot of excitement or interest.","c":"引起轟動","s":"The incredibly talented young singer managed to create a sensation with her absolutely breathtaking performance at the summer music festival.","t":"這位才華洋溢的年輕歌手憑藉她在夏季音樂節上絕對令人驚嘆的表演，成功地引起了轟動。"},{"w":"drift","p":"v. / n.","d":"to be carried slowly by a current of air or water.","c":"漂流；大意","s":"The broken wooden raft drifted continuously for several days before it was finally spotted by a large passing cargo ship.","t":"破碎的木筏連續漂流了好幾天，才終於被一艘路過的大型貨輪發現。"},{"w":"drift off to sleep","p":"phr.","d":"to gradually fall asleep.","c":"漸漸入睡","s":"Because she was incredibly tired from working all day, Nancy quickly drifted off to sleep during the boring history movie.","t":"因為她工作了一整天極度疲倦，南西在無聊的歷史電影中很快就漸漸入睡了。"},{"w":"fade","p":"v.","d":"to gradually grow faint and disappear.","c":"褪色；消退","s":"The bright red paint on my father's old car has completely faded after being left out in the hot sun for years.","t":"我父親舊車上鮮豔的紅漆，在烈日下曝曬多年後已經完全褪色了。"},{"w":"fade away","p":"phr.","d":"to gradually disappear completely.","c":"逐漸消失","s":"As the warm morning sun slowly rose over the mountains, the thick white fog on the peaceful lake eventually faded away.","t":"隨著溫暖的晨光慢慢從群山升起，平靜湖面上濃濃的白霧最終逐漸消失了。"},{"w":"vanish","p":"v.","d":"to disappear suddenly and completely.","c":"消失","s":"Many beautiful and endangered animals could unfortunately vanish forever as a direct and tragic result of ongoing global climate change.","t":"作為持續的全球氣候變遷直接且悲慘的結果，許多美麗且瀕臨絕種的動物可能不幸地永遠消失。"},{"w":"disappear","p":"v.","d":"to cease to be visible.","c":"消失","s":"The frightened wild rabbit managed to quickly disappear into the dark and dense forest before the careful hunter could even catch it.","t":"那隻受驚的野兔設法迅速消失在黑暗茂密的森林裡，讓小心翼翼的獵人甚至來不及抓住牠。"},{"w":"murmur","p":"n. / v.","d":"a soft, indistinct sound made by a person or group of people speaking quietly or at a distance.","c":"低語聲；喃喃自語","s":"Before the highly anticipated movie officially started, the large theater was completely filled with a low murmur from the excited audience.","t":"在這部備受期待的電影正式開始前，大型影廳裡完全充滿了興奮觀眾的低沉低語聲。"},{"w":"whisper","p":"v. / n.","d":"to speak very softly using one's breath without one's vocal cords.","c":"耳語；小聲說話","s":"The two naughty students had to cautiously whisper to each other in the silent library so they wouldn't disturb anyone studying.","t":"兩個頑皮的學生必須在安靜的圖書館裡小心翼翼地對彼此耳語，這樣他們才不會打擾到任何正在學習的人。"},{"w":"drone","p":"v. / n.","d":"to make a continuous low humming sound; to speak tediously.","c":"嗡嗡聲；單調地說","s":"The incredibly boring professor continued to drone on for two long hours about an outdated topic that absolutely no one was interested in.","t":"這位極度無聊的教授繼續用單調的聲音講了兩個漫長的小時，談論一個絕對沒有人感興趣的過時話題。"},{"w":"drone","p":"n","d":"manless flying gadget","c":"無人機","s":"The invading nation lauched thousands of drones to attack the military bases of the neighboring country.","t":"入侵的國家發射很多無人機去攻擊鄰近國家的軍事基地"},{"w":"enclose","p":"v.","d":"to surround or close off on all sides.","c":"圍住；附上","s":"The rich and famous businessman decided to completely enclose his large private property with a tall and highly secure metal fence.","t":"這位富有且著名的商人決定用一道高大且高度安全的金屬圍欄將他的大型私人財產完全圍住。"},{"w":"disclose","p":"v.","d":"to make secret or new information known.","c":"揭露；公開","s":"The reputable bank strictly refuses to secretly disclose any sensitive private information about its loyal customers to the general public.","t":"這家聲譽卓著的銀行嚴格拒絕向大眾秘密揭露任何關於其忠誠顧客的敏感私人資訊。"},{"w":"enclosure","p":"n.","d":"an area that is sealed off with an artificial or natural barrier.","c":"圍欄；圈地","s":"The dangerous and powerful lions at the city zoo are kept safely inside a massive glass and steel enclosure for everyone's protection.","t":"為了每個人的安全，市立動物園裡危險且強大的獅子被安全地飼養在一個巨大的玻璃和鋼製圍欄內。"},{"w":"enclosed","p":"adj.","d":"surrounded or closed off on all sides; included with a letter or package.","c":"隨函附上的；封閉的","s":"Please carefully and thoroughly review the highly important enclosed documents before you sign the legal contract and mail it back.","t":"在您簽署法律合約並將其寄回之前，請仔細且徹底地審查極其重要的隨函附上的文件。"},{"w":"precious","p":"adj.","d":"of great value; not to be wasted or treated carelessly.","c":"珍貴的","s":"These old black-and-white photos of your beloved grandparents are incredibly precious, so you really must take excellent care of them.","t":"這些你深愛祖父母的舊黑白照片是極其珍貴的，所以你真的必須好好照顧它們。"},{"w":"priceless","p":"adj.","d":"so precious that its value cannot be determined.","c":"無價的","s":"The ancient golden artifact found deep inside the hidden tomb is totally priceless and undoubtedly belongs in a secure national museum.","t":"在隱藏陵墓深處發現的古代黃金工藝品是完全無價的，且無疑屬於安全的國家博物館。"},{"w":"worthless","p":"adj.","d":"having no real value or use.","c":"毫無價值的","s":"Because the complex machine is completely broken and utterly unrepairable, it is now entirely worthless to the frustrated factory owners.","t":"因為這台複雜的機器完全壞了且完全無法修理，它現在對沮喪的工廠老闆來說完全是毫無價值的。"},{"w":"precious metal","p":"phr.","d":"a rare, naturally occurring metallic chemical element of high economic value.","c":"貴金屬","s":"Gold and silver are highly valued precious metal that have successfully been used as standard currency for thousands of human generations.","t":"黃金和白銀是高度珍貴的貴金屬，已經成功地被數千代人類用作標準貨幣。"},{"w":"extraordinary","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or remarkable.","c":"非凡的；出色的","s":"It took an absolutely extraordinary effort for the highly dedicated salesperson to finally reach her incredibly ambitious annual sales goal.","t":"這位非常敬業的銷售員花了絕對非凡的努力，才終於達成她極具野心的年度銷售目標。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; outstanding.","c":"卓越的；例外的","s":"The young girl consistently showed an exceptional talent for playing the classical piano, deeply impressing all of her experienced music teachers.","t":"這個年輕女孩不斷展現出彈奏古典鋼琴的卓越的天賦，深深打動了她所有經驗豐富的音樂老師。"},{"w":"phenomenon","p":"n. [C]","d":"Something that exists or happens, especially something that is studied because it is unusual or interesting.","c":"現象","s":"The rapid growth of social media shopping is a recent economic phenomenon that has completely changed how brands sell products to young consumers.","t":"社群媒體購物的快速增長是近期的一種經濟現象，它完全改變了品牌向年輕消費者銷售產品的方式。"},{"w":"natural phenomenon","p":"phr.","d":"An event or occurrence in the physical world that is not created by humans, such as a rainbow or volcanic eruption.","c":"自然現象","s":"A solar eclipse is a fascinating natural phenomenon where the moon passes between the sun and Earth, temporarily blocking the sunlight.","t":"日食是一種迷人的自然現象，此時月球穿過太陽和地球之間，暫時阻擋了陽光。"},{"w":"phenomenal","p":"adj.","d":"very remarkable; extraordinary.","c":"驚人的；非凡的","s":"The new internet software startup experienced phenomenal growth during its very first year, making the young founders incredibly wealthy overnight.","t":"這家新的網路軟體新創公司在其第一年就經歷了驚人的成長，讓年輕的創辦人們一夜暴富。"},{"w":"ordinary","p":"adj.","d":"with no special or distinctive features; normal.","c":"普通的","s":"Despite his immense worldwide wealth and incredible fame, the highly successful actor actually prefers to live a surprisingly ordinary and quiet life.","t":"儘管擁有巨大的全球財富和令人難以置信的名氣，這位非常成功的演員實際上更喜歡過著令人驚訝的普通的和平靜生活。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the arrangement of and relations between the parts or elements of something complex.","c":"結構；建築物","s":"The highly complex structure of the human brain actively allows us to process detailed information in incredibly fast and fascinating ways.","t":"人類大腦高度複雜的結構，主動讓我們能以極其快速且迷人的方式處理詳細資訊。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities needed for the operation of a society.","c":"基礎建設","s":"The ambitious city mayor heavily invested billions of dollars in upgrading the aging infrastructure to better support the rapidly growing local population.","t":"雄心勃勃的市長投入了數十億美元來升級老舊的基礎建設，以更好地支持快速增長的當地人口。"},{"w":"structural damage","p":"phr.","d":"physical harm that impairs the function or integrity of a structure.","c":"結構性損壞","s":"The terrifying winter storm caused significant structural damage to several vulnerable houses located directly along the highly exposed coastline.","t":"可怕的冬季風暴對直接位於高度暴露海岸線上的幾棟脆弱房屋造成了重大的結構性損壞。"},{"w":"endeavor","p":"n. / v.","d":"an attempt to achieve a goal; to try hard to do or achieve something.","c":"努力；嘗試","s":"Climbing that highly dangerous, snow-covered mountain completely without an experienced guide will undoubtedly be a very difficult and risky endeavor.","t":"在完全沒有經驗豐富嚮導的情況下攀登那座極其危險、被雪覆蓋的山，無疑將是一次非常困難且冒險的嘗試。"},{"w":"endeavor","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to do or achieve something.","c":"努力；盡力","s":"You should always strictly endeavor to avoid making common grammar and spelling mistakes when carefully writing a professional business report.","t":"在仔細撰寫專業商業報告時，你應該總是嚴格地努力避免犯下常見的文法和拼字錯誤。"},{"w":"successful endeavor","p":"phr.","d":"an attempt or project that achieves its goals.","c":"成功的嘗試","s":"Launching the brand new smartphone application proved to be a highly successful endeavor that quickly generated millions of dollars in total profit.","t":"推出這款全新的智慧型手機應用程式被證明是一次高度成功的嘗試，迅速創造了數百萬美元的總利潤。"},{"w":"erect","p":"v.","d":"to construct a building, wall, or other structure.","c":"建立；豎立","s":"The proud city council officially decided to gracefully erect a large bronze monument in the central park to honor its brave founder.","t":"自豪的市議會正式決定在中央公園優雅地豎立一座大型青銅紀念碑，以紀念其勇敢的建立者。"},{"w":"erection","p":"n.","d":"the action of erecting a structure or object.","c":"建造；設立","s":"The surprisingly rapid erection of the brand new suspension bridge greatly improved the daily heavy traffic flow between the two busy cities.","t":"全新吊橋令人驚訝地快速建造，極大地改善了這兩座繁忙城市之間每天繁重的交通流量。"},{"w":"put up","p":"phr.","d":"to construct or erect something.","c":"建造；搭起","s":"The highly dedicated construction workers quickly managed to put up the temporary wooden fence before the incredibly heavy rain finally started.","t":"非常敬業的建築工人迅速在極大的暴雨最終開始之前，設法搭起了臨時的木製圍欄。"},{"w":"construct","p":"v.","d":"to build or erect something, typically a building, road, or machine.","c":"建造；構成","s":"The massive international company officially plans to construct a highly advanced new factory in the rural area to provide more local jobs.","t":"這家龐大的國際公司正式計畫在鄉村地區建造一座高度先進的新工廠，以提供更多當地就業機會。"},{"w":"rival","p":"n. / v.","d":"a person or thing competing with another for the same objective; to equal or be compared with.","c":"競爭對手；與...匹敵","s":"The highly successful and wealthy technology company currently faces a fierce new rival that is efficiently producing much cheaper electronic devices.","t":"這家非常成功且富有的科技公司目前面臨著一個猛烈的新競爭對手，該對手正高效率地生產便宜許多的電子設備。"},{"w":"rival","p":"v.","d":"to be or seem to be equal or comparable to.","c":"與...匹敵","s":"The highly impressive quality of the digital camera in this modern cell phone can easily rival that of a very expensive regular camera.","t":"這款現代手機中數位相機令人印象深刻的品質，可以輕鬆地與非常昂貴的一般相機匹敵。"},{"w":"rivalry","p":"n.","d":"competition for the same objective or for superiority in the same field.","c":"競爭；敵對","s":"There is an incredibly long and deeply intense rivalry between the two local high school football teams during the competitive sports season.","t":"在競爭激烈的體育賽季中，兩所當地高中美式足球隊之間有著令人難以置信的漫長且極度激烈的競爭。"},{"w":"competitor","p":"n.","d":"an organization or country that is engaged in commercial or economic competition with others.","c":"競爭者","s":"In order to remain highly profitable, the global business must constantly and carefully monitor every major competitor in the competitive international market.","t":"為了保持高利潤，這家全球企業必須不斷且仔細地監控競爭激烈的國際市場中每一個主要的競爭者。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"someone who competes against or fights another in a contest, game, or argument.","c":"對手","s":"The highly skilled and muscular boxer carefully studied his strong opponent for several weeks before the important championship match finally took place.","t":"這位技術高超且肌肉發達的拳擊手在重要的冠軍賽最終舉行前，仔細研究了他強大的對手好幾個星期。"},{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal religious or public occasion, typically one celebrating a particular event or anniversary.","c":"儀式；典禮","s":"The beautiful women in the traditional ceremony wore long robes of pure white, and the proud men wore brightly colored red ones.","t":"傳統儀式中美麗的女人們穿著純白色的長袍，而自豪的男人們則穿著色彩鮮豔的紅色長袍。"},{"w":"rite","p":"n.","d":"a religious or other solemn ceremony or act.","c":"儀式；慣例","s":"The ancient indigenous tribe joyfully performs a highly special religious rite every single spring to warmly celebrate the return of the pleasant weather.","t":"古老的原住民部落每年春天都會歡樂地舉行一個非常特別的宗教儀式，以溫暖地慶祝宜人天氣的回歸。"},{"w":"ritual","p":"n.","d":"a religious or solemn ceremony consisting of a series of actions performed according to a prescribed order.","c":"儀式；習慣","s":"Having a quiet and relaxing cup of coffee on the sunny balcony is my absolute favorite morning ritual before starting the busy day.","t":"在陽光明媚的陽台上安靜放鬆地喝杯咖啡，是我在開始忙碌一天之前絕對最喜歡的早晨儀式（習慣）。"},{"w":"religious ritual","p":"n.","d":"a religious ceremony or practice to worship gods","c":"宗教儀式","s":"The priest of the aboriginal tribe practices the conventional religious ritual to worship to the gods for good fortune.","t":"原住民部落的祭司舉行傳統的宗教儀式，向神明祈求好運。"},{"w":"stand on ceremony","p":"phr.","d":"to insist on formal behavior.","c":"拘泥於禮節","s":"You really don't have to stand on ceremony at this incredibly casual house party; just wear comfortable clothing and totally relax.","t":"在這個極其休閒的家庭派對上，你真的不必拘泥於禮節；只要穿著舒適的衣服並完全放鬆即可。"},{"w":"opening ceremony","p":"phr.","d":"the formal event that marks the beginning of a larger event or festival.","c":"開幕典禮","s":"The spectacular opening ceremony of the massive international sports event featured incredible traditional dancing and a surprisingly large colorful fireworks display.","t":"這場大型國際體育賽事壯觀的開幕典禮，以令人難以置信的傳統舞蹈和令人驚訝的盛大彩色煙火表演為特色。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a forcible overthrow of a government or social order; a dramatic and wide-reaching change in the way something works.","c":"革命","s":"The rapid and completely unexpected development of the global internet has completely created a massive revolution in the way we communicate daily.","t":"全球網際網路迅速且完全出乎意料的發展，已經徹底在我們日常溝通的方式上創造了一場巨大的革命。"},{"w":"revolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"involving or causing a complete or dramatic change.","c":"革命性的","s":"The brilliant scientist's totally revolutionary new theory completely changed how modern physicists fundamentally understand the complex and mysterious nature of the universe.","t":"這位才華洋溢科學家完全革命性的新理論，徹底改變了現代物理學家對宇宙複雜神秘本質的根本理解。"},{"w":"revolutionize","p":"v.","d":"to change something radically or fundamentally.","c":"徹底改變","s":"The amazing invention of the highly affordable modern automobile managed to totally revolutionize personal transportation and complicated urban planning around the entire world.","t":"極度負擔得起的現代汽車的驚人發明，成功地徹底改變了全世界的個人交通和複雜的城市規劃。"},{"w":"revolve","p":"v.","d":"to move in a circle on a central axis.","c":"旋轉；圍繞","s":"The knowledgeable and friendly astronomy teacher carefully explained how all the rocky planets in our solar system naturally revolve around the glowing sun.","t":"知識淵博且友善的天文學老師仔細解釋了我們太陽系中所有岩石行星如何自然地圍繞著發光的太陽旋轉。"},{"w":"cultural revolution","p":"phr.","d":"a fundamental change in the cultural values and practices of a society.","c":"文化大革命","s":"The sudden and incredibly dramatic cultural revolution in the ancient country significantly changed its historical art, modern music, and traditional social values forever.","t":"這個古老國家突然且極其戲劇性的文化大革命，顯著地永遠改變了它的歷史藝術、現代音樂和傳統社會價值觀。"},{"w":"creak","p":"n.","d":"a harsh scraping or squeaking sound.","c":"嘎吱聲；發出嘎吱聲","s":"The incredibly loud and spooky creak of the old wooden door as I entered the dark room immediately woke my sleeping parents up.","t":"當我進入黑暗的房間時，老木門極其響亮且令人毛骨悚然的嘎吱聲立刻吵醒了熟睡的父母。"},{"w":"creak","p":"v.","d":"to make a harsh, high-pitched sound when being moved or when pressure or weight is applied.","c":"發出嘎吱聲","s":"Mary walked as gently and quietly as she possibly could, but the aged wooden floor still creaked loudly and annoyingly under her heavy feet.","t":"瑪麗盡可能輕柔且安靜地走，但老舊的木地板在她沉重的腳下仍然大聲且煩人地發出嘎吱聲。"},{"w":"renew","p":"v.","d":"to resume an activity after an interruption; to re-establish.","c":"更新；重新燃起","s":"Watching the highly exciting television documentary about the vast, deep ocean has completely renewed my long-forgotten childhood interest in sailing large boats.","t":"觀看這部關於廣闊深海極其刺激的電視紀錄片，已經徹底重新燃起了我被遺忘已久的童年對駕駛大船的興趣。"},{"w":"resume","p":"v.","d":"to begin to do or pursue something again after a pause or interruption.","c":"恢復；繼續","s":"The exciting professional baseball game will officially resume tomorrow afternoon as soon as the incredibly heavy and dangerous thunderstorm finally passes safely.","t":"刺激的職業棒球比賽將在極其強烈且危險的雷雨終於安全過去後，於明天下午正式恢復（繼續）。"},{"w":"renewable","p":"adj.","d":"not depleted when used.","c":"可再生的","s":"Powerful solar and wind power are naturally excellent sources of renewable energy that can significantly help human beings protect the delicate natural environment.","t":"強大的太陽能和風能天然是可再生的能源的極佳來源，可以顯著幫助人類保護脆弱的自然環境。"},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of receiving something sent, given, or inflicted; a formal social occasion held to welcome someone.","c":"接待；歡迎會","s":"The victorious and highly respected king was given a truly grand and exciting reception upon safely arriving back at the heavily guarded large stone castle.","t":"勝利且備受尊敬的國王在安全返回戒備森嚴的大型石頭城堡時，受到了一場真正盛大且令人興奮的接待（歡迎會）。"},{"w":"reception desk","p":"phr.","d":"a desk or area in a hotel, office, etc., where visitors are received and directed.","c":"接待櫃檯","s":"When you are completely packed and fully ready to leave the luxury hotel, please kindly remember to leave your electronic room key at the main reception desk.","t":"當您完全打包好並準備離開豪華飯店時，請親切地記得將您的電子房卡留在主要的接待櫃檯。"},{"w":"receptionist","p":"n.","d":"a person employed in an office or other establishment to answer the telephone, deal with clients, and greet visitors.","c":"接待員","s":"The highly friendly and incredibly helpful receptionist quickly answered the loudly ringing telephone and efficiently directed the important business call to the busy general manager.","t":"這位非常友善且極度樂於助人的接待員迅速接起了大聲響鈴的電話，並高效率地將這通重要的商業電話轉接給忙碌的總經理。"},{"w":"grand reception","p":"phr.","d":"a large, impressive formal party or celebration.","c":"盛大的招待會","s":"The happily newly married young couple beautifully hosted a truly grand reception for absolutely all their beloved family members and closest lifelong friends to warmly celebrate.","t":"這對快樂新婚的年輕夫婦美麗地舉辦了一場真正的盛大的招待會，讓他們所有深愛的家人和最親密的一生摯友溫暖地慶祝。"},{"w":"gown","p":"n.","d":"a long elegant dress worn on formal occasions.","c":"禮服；長袍","s":"The incredibly famous Hollywood actress confidently and gracefully walked down the long red carpet wearing a stunning and outrageously expensive red silk gown.","t":"這位極其著名的好萊塢女演員自信優雅地走在長長的紅地毯上，穿著一件令人驚豔且昂貴得離譜的紅色絲綢禮服。"},{"w":"wedding gown","p":"phr.","d":"a dress worn by a bride on her wedding day.","c":"婚紗","s":"My extremely talented and patient mother spent several long, tiring months carefully hand-making my lovely older sister's completely beautiful white lace wedding gown.","t":"我極具才華且耐心的母親花了幾個月漫長疲憊的時間，小心翼翼地手工製作了我可愛的姊姊那件完全美麗的白色蕾絲婚紗。"},{"w":"evening gown","p":"phr.","d":"a long, formal dress worn for evening events.","c":"晚禮服","s":"The wealthy and important guests were strictly required by the exclusive invitation to either wear a formal black suit or a beautiful long evening gown to the party.","t":"獨家邀請函嚴格要求這些富有且重要的客人，必須穿著正式的黑色西裝或美麗的長晚禮服參加派對。"},{"w":"cigar","p":"n.","d":"a cylinder of tobacco rolled in tobacco leaves for smoking.","c":"雪茄","s":"Proud American fathers historically and often happily give out highly expensive cigar to their close male friends when a healthy new baby is finally born.","t":"驕傲的美國父親在健康的新嬰兒終於誕生時，在歷史上且經常快樂地向他們親密的男性朋友分發極其昂貴的雪茄。"},{"w":"cigarette","p":"n.","d":"a thin cylinder of finely cut tobacco rolled in paper for smoking.","c":"香菸","s":"Consistently smoking a cigarette every single day is a very unhealthy and highly dangerous bad habit that can eventually lead to severely serious and deadly lung diseases.","t":"每天持續抽香菸是一個非常不健康且高度危險的壞習慣，最終可能導致嚴重且致命的肺部疾病。"},{"w":"light a cigar","p":"phr.","d":"to ignite a cigar for smoking.","c":"點燃雪茄","s":"The extremely wealthy and successful businessman confidently used a heavy, solid gold lighter to slowly light a cigar right after officially closing the massive corporate deal.","t":"這位極度富有且成功的商人在正式完成龐大的企業交易後，自信地使用一個沉重的純金打火機緩慢地點燃雪茄。"},{"w":"smoke a cigar","p":"phr.","d":"to inhale and exhale the smoke of a cigar.","c":"抽雪茄","s":"My retired grandfather absolutely loves to peacefully sit on the quiet wooden back porch and smoke a cigar while slowly reading the detailed morning newspaper.","t":"我退休的祖父絕對喜歡平靜地坐在安靜的木製後廊上，一邊抽雪茄一邊慢慢閱讀詳細的晨報。"},{"w":"lessen","p":"v.","d":"to make or become less; to diminish.","c":"減少；減輕","s":"Consistently maintaining a healthy and regular daily exercise routine can significantly lessen your overall personal risk of developing many highly serious long-term physical illnesses.","t":"持續維持健康規律的日常運動習慣，可以顯著減少你個人罹患許多極其嚴重的長期身體疾病的整體風險。"},{"w":"decrease","p":"v.","d":"to make or become smaller or fewer in size, amount, intensity, or degree.","c":"減少","s":"The highly innovative company successfully managed to drastically decrease its massive production costs by highly automating the complicated manufacturing process in the new factory.","t":"這家高度創新的公司透過將新工廠中複雜的製造過程高度自動化，成功設法大幅減少了其龐大的生產成本。"},{"w":"enlarge","p":"v.","d":"to make or become bigger or more extensive.","c":"擴大","s":"We are actively planning to expensively enlarge our incredibly small and cramped kitchen early next year so we can finally have much more comfortable space to cook daily.","t":"我們正積極計畫在明年初花大錢擴大我們極其狹小擁擠的廚房，這樣我們終於能有舒適許多的空間來進行日常烹飪。"},{"w":"expand","p":"v.","d":"to become or make larger or more extensive.","c":"擴張","s":"The highly ambitious and rapidly growing international corporation actively plans to quickly expand its profitable retail business into several brand new and economically developing countries.","t":"這家極具野心且快速成長的國際企業積極計畫將其有利可圖的零售業務，迅速擴張到幾個全新且經濟正在發展的國家。"},{"w":"nonetheless","p":"adv.","d":"in spite of that; nevertheless.","c":"儘管如此","s":"Mike is currently seriously ill with aggressive cancer, but nonetheless, he courageously and persistently continues to work incredibly hard at his highly demanding and stressful office job.","t":"麥克目前罹患了嚴重的侵襲性癌症，但儘管如此，他依然勇敢且堅持不懈地在他要求極高且充滿壓力的辦公室工作中極其努力地工作。"},{"w":"nevertheless","p":"adv.","d":"in spite of that; notwithstanding; all the same.","c":"然而；儘管如此","s":"The surprisingly heavy and sudden rain made the steep mountain hiking trail extremely muddy and highly dangerous; nevertheless, we firmly decided to safely finish the long journey together.","t":"令人驚訝的突發大雨讓陡峭的登山步道變得極度泥濘且高度危險；然而（儘管如此），我們堅定地決定一起安全地完成這趟漫長的旅程。"},{"w":"however","p":"adv.","d":"used to introduce a statement that contrasts with or seems to contradict something that has been said previously.","c":"然而","s":"The incredibly expensive downtown restaurant has genuinely beautiful artistic decorations and exceptionally great service; however, the actual served food is quite surprisingly disappointing and completely tasteless.","t":"這家極其昂貴的市中心餐廳擁有真正美麗的藝術裝飾和異常出色的服務；然而，實際提供的食物卻相當令人驚訝地令人失望且完全沒有味道。"},{"w":"exposition","p":"n.","d":"a comprehensive description and explanation of an idea or theory; a large public exhibition.","c":"詳細闡述；博覽會","s":"The highly knowledgeable history teacher passionately provided a highly detailed and truly fascinating exposition on the complex and hidden political causes of the devastating global world war.","t":"知識非常淵博的歷史老師充滿熱情地對這場毀滅性全球世界大戰複雜且隱藏的政治原因，提供了一場極度詳細且真正引人入勝的詳細闡述。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"apparent – broaden one's horizons","cards":[{"w":"apparent","p":"adj.","d":"clearly visible or understood; obvious.","c":"明顯的","s":"Because his bedroom was completely messed up, it was quite apparent that someone had secretly been sleeping on his bed.","t":"因為他的臥室完全被弄亂了，很明顯的有人偷偷睡在他的床上。"},{"w":"apparently","p":"adv.","d":"as far as one knows or can see.","c":"顯然地","s":"The sky is incredibly dark and cloudy today, so apparently it is going to rain very heavily later this afternoon.","t":"今天天空極其黑暗且多雲，所以顯然地今天下午晚些時候會下大雨。"},{"w":"obvious","p":"adj.","d":"easily perceived or understood; clear, self-evident, or apparent.","c":"明顯的","s":"After watching him completely fail to hit the baseball, it was painfully obvious that he had never played the game before.","t":"在看著他完全打不到棒球後，令人痛苦地明顯的是他以前從未玩過這個遊戲。"},{"w":"obviously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easily perceived or understood.","c":"明顯地","s":"The strict teacher noticed that Evan obviously hadn't studied very hard, since he miserably failed the difficult exam.","t":"嚴格的老師注意到伊凡顯然沒有很用功讀書，因為他悽慘地沒通過這場困難的考試。"},{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"to strengthen or support physically or mentally.","c":"維持","s":"In order to properly sustain rapid economic growth, the developing country must heavily invest in its public transportation systems immediately.","t":"為了適當地維持快速的經濟成長，這個發展中國家必須立刻大力投資其大眾運輸系統。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be maintained at a certain rate or level.","c":"永續的","s":"Dedicated environmental researchers are actively looking for sustainable methods of producing clean electricity for the rapidly growing modern city.","t":"盡責的環境研究人員正積極為快速發展的現代城市尋找生產乾淨電力的永續的方法。"},{"w":"unsustainable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be maintained at the current rate or level.","c":"無法永續的","s":"Relying entirely on expensive and highly polluting fossil fuels is a completely unsustainable way to generate electricity for future generations.","t":"完全依賴昂貴且高污染的化石燃料，對後代來說是一種完全無法永續的發電方式。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to be maintained at a certain rate or level.","c":"永續性","s":"The modern international company places a strong emphasis on environmental sustainability by efficiently using recycled materials for all their products.","t":"這家現代國際公司透過在其所有產品中高效率地使用回收材料，強烈強調環境的永續性。"},{"w":"sustainable development","p":"phr.","d":"economic development that is conducted without depletion of natural resources.","c":"永續發展","s":"The ambitious new mayor promised to passionately promote sustainable development by building several massive solar power plants just outside the city.","t":"雄心勃勃的新市長承諾，將透過在城市外圍建造幾座大型太陽能發電廠來熱情推動永續發展。"},{"w":"technical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a particular subject, art, or craft, or its techniques.","c":"技術的；專業的","s":"The dense scientific article contained far too many complex technical terms that the average reader simply could not understand correctly.","t":"這篇密集的科學文章包含太多複雜的專業的（技術的）術語，一般讀者根本無法正確理解。"},{"w":"technically","p":"adv.","d":"according to the facts or exact meaning of something; strictly.","c":"嚴格來說；技術上","s":"Although the red tomato is widely considered a vegetable in cooking, technically it is actually classified as a sweet fruit by scientists.","t":"雖然紅番茄在烹飪中被廣泛認為是蔬菜，但嚴格來說，它實際上被科學家歸類為甜水果。"},{"w":"technical problem","p":"phr.","d":"an issue arising from the mechanical or electronic operation of a system.","c":"技術問題","s":"Because the engineering team experienced an unexpected technical problem, the highly anticipated educational speech unfortunately started very late.","t":"因為工程團隊經歷了出乎意料的技術問題，這場備受期待的教育演講不幸地很晚才開始。"},{"w":"technical support","p":"phr.","d":"a service provided to users of technology products or services.","c":"技術支援","s":"If you honestly cannot fix the broken software yourself, you should probably contact technical support to get some professional assistance quickly.","t":"如果你真的無法自己修復壞掉的軟體，你可能應該聯絡技術支援以迅速獲得一些專業協助。"},{"w":"technical term","p":"phr.","d":"a word that has a specific meaning within a specific field of expertise.","c":"專業術語","s":"The brilliant professor explained the complex technical term in simple language so that all the beginner students could easily understand it.","t":"這位才華洋溢的教授用簡單的語言解釋了複雜的專業術語，讓所有初學者都能輕鬆理解。"},{"w":"unconventional","p":"adj.","d":"not based on or conforming to what is generally done or believed.","c":"非傳統的；非常規的","s":"When dealing with highly complex modern business issues, sometimes unconventional solutions are actually the most effective way to solve them.","t":"在處理高度複雜的現代商業問題時，有時非傳統的解決方案實際上是解決它們最有效的方法。"},{"w":"conventional","p":"adj.","d":"based on or in accordance with what is generally done or believed.","c":"傳統的；常規的","s":"Instead of following conventional methods of farming, the young farmer decided to creatively grow his healthy vegetables indoors using advanced technology.","t":"這位年輕農夫沒有遵循傳統的耕作方法，而是決定創造性地使用先進技術在室內種植健康的蔬菜。"},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"a large meeting of people with a shared interest.","c":"大會；慣例","s":"The famous international technology company holds a massive annual convention to proudly announce its newest electronic products to the eager public.","t":"這家著名的國際科技公司每年舉辦一次大型大會，向熱切的大眾自豪地宣布其最新的電子產品。"},{"w":"unconventionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not based on what is generally done or believed.","c":"非傳統地","s":"The extremely popular new pop artist dresses incredibly unconventionally, which brilliantly helps her strongly stand out from other boring musicians.","t":"這位極受歡迎的新流行歌手穿著極其非傳統地，這出色地幫助她在其他無聊的音樂家中強烈地脫穎而出。"},{"w":"document","p":"n.","d":"a piece of written, printed, or electronic matter that provides information or evidence.","c":"文件","s":"Pat had to quickly prepare several highly important legal documents to give to his expensive lawyer before the difficult trial officially started.","t":"派特必須迅速準備幾份極其重要的法律文件，以便在艱難的審判正式開始前交給他昂貴的律師。"},{"w":"document","p":"v.","d":"to record (something) in written, photographic, or other form.","c":"記錄","s":"The strict safety inspector officially documented several dangerous violations at the factory and ordered the angry owners to fix them immediately.","t":"嚴格的安全檢查員官方記錄了工廠的幾項危險違規行為，並命令憤怒的老闆立即修復。"},{"w":"documentary","p":"n.","d":"a movie or a television or radio program that provides a factual record or report.","c":"紀錄片","s":"The fascinating television documentary beautifully explored the mysterious deep ocean and the incredibly unique creatures that live completely in the darkness.","t":"這部引人入勝的電視紀錄片美麗地探索了神祕的深海，以及完全生活在黑暗中極其獨特的生物。"},{"w":"documented","p":"adj.","d":"recorded in written, photographic, or other form.","c":"有記錄的","s":"The ambitious historical researcher carefully studied the well documented evidence to write a completely accurate book about the powerful ancient empire.","t":"雄心勃勃的歷史研究員仔細研究了充分有記錄的證據，以寫出一本關於強大古代帝國完全準確的書。"},{"w":"pest","p":"n.","d":"a destructive insect or other animal that attacks crops, food, livestock, etc.","c":"害蟲；有害動物","s":"The aggressive farmer bought a special chemical spray that will effectively keep mice and other destructive pests from entering your cozy home.","t":"具攻擊性的農夫買了一種特殊的化學噴霧，能有效地防止老鼠和其他具破壞性的有害動物（害蟲）進入你舒適的家。"},{"w":"pesticide","p":"n.","d":"a substance used for destroying insects or other organisms harmful to cultivated plants or to animals.","c":"殺蟲劑","s":"To successfully protect the valuable summer crops from hungry insects, the workers carefully sprayed a powerful pesticide over the entire green field.","t":"為了成功保護寶貴的夏季農作物免受飢餓昆蟲的侵害，工人們小心地在整個綠色田野上噴灑了強效的殺蟲劑。"},{"w":"pest control","p":"phr.","d":"the regulation or management of a species defined as a pest.","c":"害蟲防治","s":"When we suddenly discovered hundreds of dangerous spiders hiding in the dark basement, we immediately called a professional pest control company.","t":"當我們突然發現數百隻危險的蜘蛛隱藏在黑暗的地下室時，我們立刻打電話給專業的害蟲防治公司。"},{"w":"agricultural pest","p":"phr.","d":"an insect or animal that is detrimental to farming.","c":"農業害蟲","s":"The tiny green bug is a widely well-known agricultural pest that can unfortunately completely destroy an entire field of healthy wheat in days.","t":"這種綠色小蟲是一種廣為人知的農業害蟲，不幸地能在幾天內徹底摧毀整片健康的麥田。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n.","d":"an advantage or profit gained from something.","c":"好處；益處","s":"There are undoubtedly many great benefits to living in a big, modern city, such as convenient public transportation and excellent international restaurants.","t":"住在現代化大城市無疑有許多巨大的好處，例如便利的大眾運輸和極佳的國際餐廳。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"v.","d":"to receive an advantage; profit.","c":"對...有益","s":"Eating lots of fresh sweet fruits and crisp green vegetables every single day will significantly benefit your overall long-term physical health.","t":"每天吃許多新鮮甜美的水果和清脆的綠色蔬菜，將顯著對你整體的長期身體健康有益。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"favorable or advantageous; resulting in good.","c":"有益的","s":"Taking essential organic vitamins daily is widely believed by doctors to be highly beneficial to maintaining a strong and healthy human immune system.","t":"醫生廣泛認為每天服用必需的有機維生素對維持強壯健康的免疫系統是高度有益的。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"a financial gain, especially the difference between the amount earned and the amount spent.","c":"利潤","s":"If the struggling local retail store doesn't make a positive profit by the end of the month, we will inevitably go completely out of business.","t":"如果這家苦苦掙扎的當地零售店在月底前沒有獲得正向的利潤，我們將不可避免地徹底倒閉。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to make great efforts to achieve or obtain something.","c":"努力；奮鬥","s":"If you genuinely want to eventually succeed in this highly competitive industry, you must constantly strive to do much better than your rivals.","t":"如果你真的想在這個競爭激烈的產業中最終取得成功，你必須不斷努力做得比你的競爭對手好很多。"},{"w":"endeavor","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to do or achieve something.","c":"努力；盡力","s":"The dedicated project manager will strictly endeavor to heavily improve the uncomfortable daily working conditions for absolutely all of his tired employees.","t":"盡責的專案經理將嚴格努力大幅改善他所有疲憊員工不舒服的日常工作環境。"},{"w":"strive for","p":"phr.","d":"to make a great effort to achieve something.","c":"為...奮鬥","s":"The passionate Olympic athletes always intensely strive for absolute physical perfection during their grueling daily training sessions before the international games.","t":"熱情的奧運選手在國際比賽前艱苦的日常訓練中，總是強烈地為絕對的身體完美而奮鬥。"},{"w":"endeavor","p":"n.","d":"an attempt to achieve a goal.","c":"努力；嘗試","s":"Starting a brand new international technology business entirely from scratch is a highly challenging endeavor that strongly requires lots of money and extreme patience.","t":"完全從零開始創立一家全新的國際科技企業是一項極具挑戰性的嘗試，強烈需要大量資金和極度的耐心。"},{"w":"swap","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an exchange of.","c":"交換","s":"Because he really didn't like the dark, boring color, Brad happily swapped his brown winter jacket for a brand new one in a much brighter color.","t":"因為他真的不喜歡那種深沉無聊的顏色，布萊德高興地把他的棕色冬裝外套交換成一件顏色亮得多的全新外套。"},{"w":"swap","p":"n.","d":"an act of exchanging one thing for another.","c":"交換","s":"The two close childhood friends warmly agreed to a fair swap of their absolute favorite video games so they could both enthusiastically play something completely new.","t":"兩個親密的兒時玩伴熱情地同意公平交換他們絕對最喜歡的電玩遊戲，這樣他們就能熱情地玩一些全新的東西。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"v.","d":"to give something and receive something of the same kind in return.","c":"更換；交換","s":"The highly dissatisfied customer quickly returned to the busy clothing store to aggressively exchange the incredibly small shirt for a much larger size.","t":"極度不滿的顧客迅速回到繁忙的服飾店，積極地將極其小的襯衫更換成大得多的尺寸。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"n.","d":"an act of giving one thing and receiving another in return.","c":"交流；交換","s":"The incredibly exciting international student exchange program allows brave teenagers to comfortably live and study in a completely different foreign country for a year.","t":"極其令人興奮的國際學生交換計畫，允許勇敢的青少年在一個完全不同的外國國家舒適地生活和學習一年。"},{"w":"ethical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to moral principles or the branch of knowledge dealing with these.","c":"道德的；倫理的","s":"It would absolutely not be ethical for a trusted professional company to secretly share an employee's highly personal information with other greedy corporations.","t":"讓一家受信任的專業公司秘密地與其他貪婪的企業分享員工高度個人化的資訊，絕對是不道德的。"},{"w":"unethical","p":"adj.","d":"not morally correct.","c":"不道德的","s":"The greedy and arrogant businessman was heavily fined by the strict government for his highly unethical and completely illegal corporate marketing practices.","t":"貪婪且傲慢的商人因其高度不道德的且完全非法的企業行銷手法，被嚴格的政府處以重罰。"},{"w":"ethic","p":"n.","d":"a set of moral principles.","c":"道德規範；職業道德","s":"Because she naturally has an incredibly strong work ethic, Mary consistently stays at the busy office until the difficult job is completely finished.","t":"因為她天生有著令人難以置信的強烈工作職業道德，瑪麗始終留在繁忙的辦公室直到困難的工作完全結束。"},{"w":"ethically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to moral principles.","c":"合乎道德地","s":"The highly popular modern clothing brand proudly claims that all of its comfortable cotton shirts are completely ethically produced without ever using cheap child labor.","t":"這個極受歡迎的現代服飾品牌自豪地聲稱，其所有舒適的棉質襯衫都是完全合乎道德地生產的，從未使用廉價童工。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"one of two or more available possibilities.","c":"替代方案；選擇","s":"Delicious frozen strawberry yogurt is widely considered a highly popular and healthy low-fat alternative to eating traditional, heavy chocolate ice cream during the hot summer.","t":"在炎熱的夏天，美味的冷凍草莓優格被廣泛認為是吃傳統厚重巧克力冰淇淋的一種極受歡迎且健康的低脂替代方案。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"adj.","d":"available as another possibility.","c":"替代的","s":"Because Donna strictly doesn't eat any meat whatsoever, she always has to intelligently find alternative sources of rich protein to stay physically healthy and strong.","t":"因為唐娜嚴格不吃任何肉類，她總是必須聰明地尋找富含蛋白質的替代的來源，以保持身體健康強壯。"},{"w":"alternatively","p":"adv.","d":"as another option or possibility.","c":"或者；要不然","s":"We could easily take the incredibly fast express train to the busy city, or alternatively, we could cheaply rent a small car and drive there ourselves.","t":"我們可以輕鬆地搭乘極快的特快列車前往繁忙的城市，或者，我們可以便宜地租一輛小車自己開車去那裡。"},{"w":"have no alternative but to","p":"phr.","d":"to be forced to do something because there are no other choices.","c":"除了...別無選擇","s":"Because it is absolutely terrible and highly dangerous weather outside, we have no alternative but to completely cancel the exciting championship baseball game today.","t":"因為外面是絕對可怕且高度危險的天氣，我們今天除了完全取消刺激的棒球冠軍賽別無選擇。"},{"w":"alternative energy","p":"phr.","d":"energy generated in ways that do not deplete natural resources or harm the environment.","c":"替代能源","s":"In order to safely protect our beautiful and delicate planet, global governments must heavily invest billions of dollars in clean alternative energy like wind and solar power.","t":"為了安全保護我們美麗且脆弱的星球，全球政府必須大力投資數十億美元在風能和太陽能等乾淨的替代能源上。"},{"w":"consequently","p":"adv.","d":"as a result.","c":"因此；結果","s":"Jack unfortunately broke his right arm during soccer practice; consequently, he had to sadly drop out of the highly anticipated regional tennis tournament.","t":"傑克在足球練習時不幸摔斷了右臂；因此，他不得不悲傷地退出備受期待的區域網球錦標賽。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result or effect of an action or condition.","c":"後果","s":"You really should deeply think carefully about the serious consequence before you bravely do something that might eventually turn out to be incredibly dangerous.","t":"在你勇敢地做一些最終可能變得極其危險的事情之前，你真的應該深入仔細思考嚴重的後果。"},{"w":"therefore","p":"adv.","d":"for that reason; consequently.","c":"因此","s":"The highly nervous student completely forgot to set his loud alarm clock; therefore, he was incredibly late for his highly important university final exam.","t":"極度緊張的學生完全忘記設定他大聲的鬧鐘；因此，他極其重要的大學期末考遲到了非常久。"},{"w":"as a consequence","p":"phr.","d":"as a result of something.","c":"因此；結果","s":"The violent and unpredictable summer storm completely destroyed the only old bridge, and as a consequence, the small rural town was totally isolated for several days.","t":"猛烈且不可預測的夏季風暴徹底摧毀了唯一的老橋，結果（因此），這個鄉村小鎮完全被孤立了好幾天。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"a general direction in which something is developing or changing.","c":"趨勢；潮流","s":"I really enjoy peacefully reading popular modern fashion magazines to easily find out about the latest exciting clothing trend for the upcoming hot summer season.","t":"我非常喜歡平靜地閱讀受歡迎的現代時尚雜誌，以輕鬆了解即將到來的炎熱夏季最新令人興奮的服裝趨勢。"},{"w":"trend","p":"v.","d":"to change or develop in a general direction.","c":"趨向","s":"Modern American consumers have been steadily trending toward significantly healthier daily eating habits over the past two long and incredibly busy decades.","t":"在過去漫長且極其忙碌的二十年裡，現代美國消費者一直在穩定地趨向明顯更健康的日常飲食習慣。"},{"w":"trendy","p":"adj.","d":"very fashionable or up to date in style or influence.","c":"時髦的","s":"The highly popular new Italian restaurant in the busy downtown area is incredibly trendy and consistently attracts lots of young, fashionable college students every single night.","t":"繁忙市中心極受歡迎的義大利新餐廳極其時髦的，且每晚持續吸引許多年輕、時尚的大學生。"},{"w":"currently trending","p":"phr.","d":"widely discussed or popular on the internet at the present time.","c":"目前正流行","s":"That incredibly funny short video of a cleverly dancing cat is currently trending on YouTube and effortlessly has millions of enthusiastic viewers worldwide.","t":"那部聰明跳舞的貓的極其搞笑短片目前正在YouTube上流行，且輕鬆地擁有全球數百萬熱情的觀眾。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"yielding profit or financial gain.","c":"有利可圖的；賺錢的","s":"We had a highly profitable afternoon happily selling our old, gently used secondhand clothes to interested buyers at the crowded outdoor flea market.","t":"我們度過了一個高度賺錢的下午，在擁擠的戶外跳蚤市場快樂地將我們舊的、輕度使用的二手衣服賣給有興趣的買家。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"a financial gain.","c":"利潤","s":"The ambitious global technology company successfully generated a massive financial profit during the exceptionally busy and highly competitive holiday shopping season last year.","t":"雄心勃勃的全球科技公司在去年異常繁忙且競爭高度激烈的假日購物季期間，成功創造了巨大的財務利潤。"},{"w":"profitably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that yields profit or financial gain.","c":"獲利地","s":"The highly experienced and intelligent business manager knows exactly how to proudly and profitably run a large retail store in an incredibly competitive international market.","t":"經驗非常豐富且聰明的商業經理完全知道如何在極具競爭的國際市場中自豪且獲利地經營一家大型零售店。"},{"w":"lucrative","p":"adj.","d":"producing a great deal of profit.","c":"賺錢的；有利可圖的","s":"Writing successful mobile computer software can definitely be an incredibly lucrative career that effectively allows young programmers to easily earn massive amounts of money quickly.","t":"編寫成功的行動電腦軟體絕對是一項極其賺錢的職業，能有效地讓年輕程式設計師輕鬆快速地賺取大量金錢。"},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"able to adapt or be adapted to many different functions or activities.","c":"多用途的；多才多藝的","s":"Strong and incredibly cheap plastic is a highly versatile material that is frequently and cleverly used to easily make many different common household products.","t":"堅固且極其便宜的塑膠是一種高度多用途的材料，經常被巧妙地用來輕鬆製作許多不同的常見家庭用品。"},{"w":"versatility","p":"n.","d":"ability to adapt or be adapted to many different functions or activities.","c":"多功能性","s":"The amazing versatility of the advanced modern smartphone allows users to take beautiful pictures, browse the internet, and send instant messages.","t":"先進的現代智慧型手機驚人的多功能性，有效地讓使用者能輕鬆拍出美麗的照片、瀏覽網路並安全地發送即時訊息。"},{"w":"highly versatile","p":"phr.","d":"extremely capable of doing many things well.","c":"非常多才多藝的","s":"The incredibly talented young musician is absolutely highly versatile, perfectly and confidently playing the classical piano, the electric guitar, and the loud drums at concerts.","t":"這位才華洋溢的年輕音樂家絕對是非常多才多藝的，能在演唱會上完美自信地彈奏古典鋼琴、電吉他和響亮的鼓。"},{"w":"roast","p":"v.","d":"to cook (food, especially meat) by prolonged exposure to heat in an oven or over a fire.","c":"烘烤","s":"For our grand and highly anticipated holiday dinner, my wonderful mother traditionally roasts some incredibly delicious chicken and fresh green vegetables in the hot oven.","t":"為了我們盛大且備受期待的節日晚餐，我極好的母親傳統上會在熱烤箱裡烘烤一些極其美味的雞肉和新鮮的綠色蔬菜。"},{"w":"bake","p":"v.","d":"to cook (food) by dry heat without direct exposure to a flame, typically in an oven.","c":"烘焙","s":"The highly skilled and incredibly patient pastry chef woke up extremely early to carefully bake several fresh loaves of crusty bread and sweet chocolate cookies.","t":"技術高超且極具耐心的糕點師傅極早起床，小心翼翼地烘焙了幾條新鮮的脆皮麵包和甜巧克力餅乾。"},{"w":"boil","p":"v.","d":"to reach or cause to reach the temperature at which it bubbles and turns to vapor.","c":"煮沸","s":"If you effectively boil the dirty and dangerous water from the remote river for at least ten full minutes, it will be completely safe for you to drink.","t":"如果你有效地將偏遠河流中骯髒危險的水煮沸至少整整十分鐘，你喝起來就會完全安全。"},{"w":"fry","p":"v.","d":"to cook (food) in hot fat or oil, typically in a shallow pan.","c":"油炸；煎","s":"The incredibly busy and exhausted cook decided to quickly fry some eggs and thick bacon in the hot oily pan for a classic, heavy American breakfast.","t":"極其忙碌且疲憊的廚師決定在熱油鍋裡快速煎一些雞蛋和厚培根，做一頓經典厚重的傳統美式早餐。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook (something) using a grill.","c":"燒烤","s":"During the long, warm summer months, my outgoing father absolutely loves to confidently grill thick, juicy steaks and large beef burgers in the sunny backyard.","t":"在漫長溫暖的夏季月份裡，我外向的父親絕對喜歡在陽光明媚的後院自信地燒烤厚實多汁的牛排和大型牛肉漢堡。"},{"w":"steam","p":"v.","d":"to cook (food) by heating it in steam from boiling water.","c":"蒸","s":"If you want to efficiently and perfectly retain the healthy vitamins in your fresh green vegetables, you should lightly steam them instead of heavily boiling them.","t":"如果你想有效完美地保留新鮮綠色蔬菜中健康的維生素，你應該稍微蒸一下它們，而不是重度水煮它們。"},{"w":"horizon","p":"n.","d":"the line at which the earth's surface and the sky appear to meet.","c":"地平線","s":"As the deeply romantic and quiet evening approached, we peacefully sat on the soft sandy beach and silently watched the glowing sun set beautifully on the horizon.","t":"隨著深深浪漫且安靜的傍晚來臨，我們平靜地坐在柔軟的沙灘上，默默地看著發光的太陽在地平線上美麗地落下。"},{"w":"on the horizon","p":"phr.","d":"imminent or just becoming apparent.","c":"即將到來；在地平線上","s":"With the incredibly difficult and highly important final math test finally on the horizon, nervous Ralph started diligently studying much more every single night.","t":"隨著極其困難且高度重要的期末數學考試終於即將到來，緊張的拉爾夫開始每天晚上更加勤奮地學習。"},{"w":"around the corner","p":"phr.","d":"very near.","c":"即將到來；在轉角處","s":"The incredibly exciting and joyful winter holiday season is right around the corner, so you should definitely start thoughtfully buying your colorful gifts immediately.","t":"極其令人興奮和歡樂的冬季假日季節就在轉角處（即將到來），所以你絕對應該立刻開始深思熟慮地購買你色彩繽紛的禮物。"},{"w":"broaden one's horizons","p":"phr.","d":"to expand one's range of interests, activities, and knowledge.","c":"開闊眼界","s":"Ambitious Michelle desperately wanted to peacefully travel to historical Europe so she could successfully broaden her horizons and eagerly learn all about completely different foreign cultures.","t":"雄心勃勃的蜜雪兒極度想平靜地去歷史悠久的歐洲旅行，這樣她就能成功地開闊她的眼界，並熱切地學習所有關於完全不同的外國文化。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"lean – coverage","cards":[{"w":"lean","p":"adj.","d":"thin and healthy; to incline or bend from a vertical position.","c":"精瘦的；傾靠","s":"Rebecca works out vigorously at the gym every single day so that she can eventually get a perfectly lean body.","t":"蕾貝卡每天都在健身房精力充沛地鍛鍊，這樣她最終就能擁有一個完美精瘦的身體。"},{"w":"lean meat","p":"phr.","d":"meat that contains low amounts of fat.","c":"瘦肉","s":"Health experts highly recommend eating lean meat rather than fatty cuts to effectively maintain a perfectly balanced daily diet.","t":"健康專家強烈建議吃瘦肉而不是肥肉，以有效地維持完美均衡的日常飲食。"},{"w":"lean","p":"v.","d":"To slope or bend your body in a particular direction.","c":"傾身、屈身、傾斜","s":"The excited fans had to lean forward over the metal railing to get a closer look at their favorite singer on the stage.","t":"興奮的粉絲們不得不向前傾身越過金屬圍欄，以便更近距離地看一眼舞台上他們最喜愛的歌手。"},{"w":"lean against","p":"phr.","d":"To rest your body or an object against something for support.","c":"斜靠在…上、倚靠著","s":"Tired after a long day of walking around the city, Marcus decided to lean against the brick wall while waiting for his Uber to arrive.","t":"在城市裡走了一整天感到疲倦後，馬庫斯決定在等待他的 Uber 抵達時斜靠在磚牆上。"},{"w":"skinny","p":"adj.","d":"unattractively or unusually thin.","c":"皮包骨的；極瘦的","s":"Because she hasn't been eating properly lately, the stray dog looks dangerously skinny and desperately needs good food.","t":"因為牠最近沒有好好進食，這隻流浪狗看起來危險地皮包骨的，且極度需要好的食物。"},{"w":"chubby","p":"adj.","d":"plump and rounded.","c":"微胖的","s":"Nick decided to start exercising regularly after he suddenly noticed he was getting a little bit chubby around his stomach.","t":"尼克在突然注意到自己肚子周圍變得有點微胖的之後，決定開始規律地運動。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"pleasingly graceful and stylish in appearance or manner.","c":"優雅的","s":"Mary wants to buy an incredibly elegant and expensive dress to wear to the grand theater in London this weekend.","t":"瑪麗想買一件極其優雅的且昂貴的洋裝，這個週末穿去倫敦的宏偉劇院。"},{"w":"graceful","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing grace or elegance.","c":"優美的","s":"Professional ballet dancers always move their bodies in a completely graceful manner when they are performing on the large stage.","t":"專業芭蕾舞者在大型舞台上表演時，總是能以完全優美的方式移動他們的身體。"},{"w":"elegance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being graceful and stylish in appearance or manner.","c":"優雅","s":"The famous royal palace is widely known for its breathtaking elegance and its beautifully decorated historical dining rooms.","t":"這座著名的皇宮以其令人驚嘆的優雅和裝飾美麗的歷史悠久餐廳而廣為人知。"},{"w":"elegantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a graceful and stylish manner.","c":"優雅地","s":"The wealthy young lady was elegantly dressed in a long silk gown as she confidently entered the crowded ballroom tonight.","t":"這位富有的年輕女士今晚自信地進入擁擠的舞廳時，穿著一襲長絲綢禮服，打扮得非常優雅地。"},{"w":"athletic","p":"adj.","d":"physically strong, fit, and active.","c":"有運動細胞的；運動的","s":"Drew is not very athletic, so he usually doesn't join us when we energetically play volleyball on the sunny beach.","t":"德魯不是很有運動細胞的，所以當我們在陽光明媚的海灘上充滿活力地打排球時，他通常不會加入我們。"},{"w":"athlete","p":"n.","d":"a person who is proficient in sports and other forms of physical exercise.","c":"運動員","s":"The highly dedicated Olympic athlete must train extremely hard every single day to compete at the highest international level.","t":"這位非常敬業的奧運運動員必須每天極其刻苦地訓練，才能在最高的國際水準上競爭。"},{"w":"twist","p":"v. / n.","d":"to injure a joint by wrenching it; an unexpected development.","c":"扭傷；轉折","s":"Betty accidentally twisted her fragile left knee while joyfully roller skating with her close friends in the public park.","t":"貝蒂在公園裡和親密的朋友快樂地溜直排輪時，不小心扭傷了她脆弱的左膝。"},{"w":"twisted","p":"adj.","d":"forced out of its natural or proper shape.","c":"扭曲的","s":"The violent and completely destructive tornado left a path of completely twisted metal and broken trees across the entire town.","t":"猛烈且完全具毀滅性的龍捲風在整個城鎮留下了一條完全扭曲的金屬和斷樹的軌跡。"},{"w":"twists and turns","p":"phr.","d":"complicated dealings or circumstances.","c":"迂迴曲折","s":"People really love to watch dramatic soap operas because the complicated stories are completely filled with unexpected twists and turns.","t":"人們真的很喜歡看充滿戲劇性的肥皂劇，因為複雜的故事完全充滿了出乎意料的迂迴曲折。"},{"w":"take another twist","p":"phr.","d":"to have a new, unexpected development.","c":"出現另一個轉折","s":"The mysterious bank robbery story took another twist yesterday when the police suddenly discovered that the banker's wife was involved.","t":"這起神祕的銀行搶劫案昨天出現另一個轉折，警方突然發現銀行家的妻子也牽涉其中。"},{"w":"fad","p":"n.","d":"an intense and widely shared enthusiasm for something, especially one that is short-lived.","c":"一時的狂熱；短暫的流行","s":"Many people wrongly and foolishly believed that the creation of the global internet was just a temporary and silly fad.","t":"許多人錯誤且愚蠢地認為，全球網際網路的創造只是一種暫時且愚蠢的一時的狂熱。"},{"w":"fashion","p":"n.","d":"a popular trend, especially in styles of dress and ornament or manners of behavior.","c":"流行；時尚","s":"The colorful 1980s look is officially the exciting new fashion for this upcoming fall season among young and trendy consumers.","t":"色彩繽紛的1980年代造型正式成為即將到來的秋季中，年輕且時髦的消費者之間令人興奮的新流行（時尚）。"},{"w":"frenzy","p":"n.","d":"A state of wild excitement, madness, or uncontrolled activity.","c":"瘋狂、狂熱","s":"The release of the limited-edition sneakers created a shopping frenzy among teenagers, causing the store to sell out in minutes.","t":"這款限量版球鞋的發售在青少年中引發了一股購物狂熱（瘋狂），導致店家在幾分鐘內就售罄。"},{"w":"be crazy about","p":"phr.","d":"To be extremely interested in, enthusiastic about, or in love with someone or something.","c":"對…瘋狂、非常迷戀…","s":"Ever since she attended their live concert last year, Emily is completely crazy about this indie rock band.","t":"自從去年參加了他們的現場演唱會後，艾米莉就完全迷戀這支獨立搖滾樂團。"},{"w":"fashionable","p":"adj.","d":"Popular at a particular time; following the latest style of clothing, behavior, or ideas.","c":"時髦的、流行的","s":"Wearing oversized denim jackets and vintage sneakers has become highly fashionable among university students this season.","t":"在本季的大學生中，穿著寬大牛仔外套和復古球鞋已變得非常時髦（流行）。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n. [C]","d":"A general direction in which something is developing, changing, or becoming popular.","c":"趨勢、潮流","s":"There is a growing trend toward remote work worldwide, as more companies realize that employees can remain productive at home.","t":"全球正出現一股走向遠距工作的新趨勢（潮流），因為越來越多的公司意識到員工在家也能保持高效率。"},{"w":"buzz","p":"n. [sing.]","d":"A strong feeling of excitement, or a lot of activity and noisy talk around a new product or event.","c":"興奮、熱烈的討論、轟動","s":"The opening of the new futuristic theme park has created a huge buzz on social media, with everyone sharing videos of the rides.","t":"新前衛主題樂園的開幕在社群媒體上引發了巨大的熱烈討論（轟動），每個人都在分享遊樂設施的影片。"},{"w":"phenomenon","p":"n. [C]","d":"Something that exists or happens, especially something that is studied because it is unusual or interesting.","c":"現象","s":"The sudden popularity of short video apps among young children is a global phenomenon that teachers and parents are closely watching.","t":"短影音軟體在幼童間的突然流行是一種全球性的現象，教師和家長正密切關注著。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the quality or state of being physically strong.","c":"力量","s":"It takes a massive amount of physical and mental strength to safely climb that dangerously high snow-covered mountain.","t":"安全攀登那座危險且被雪覆蓋的高山，需要大量的身心力量。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"to intensify, increase, or further improve the quality, value, or extent of.","c":"提升","s":"The ambitious manager introduced a clever new training program designed to significantly enhance the team's overall daily working performance.","t":"雄心勃勃的經理推出了一個聰明的新訓練計畫，旨在顯著提升團隊整體的日常工作表現。"},{"w":"lengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make or become longer.","c":"加長","s":"The dedicated tailor had to carefully lengthen the beautiful dress because it was surprisingly much too short for the tall bride.","t":"盡責的裁縫師必須仔細地將這件美麗的洋裝加長，因為對高挑的新娘來說它令人驚訝地太短了。"},{"w":"pulse","p":"n. / v.","d":"a rhythmical throbbing of the arteries; to throb rhythmically.","c":"脈搏；搏動","s":"Your rapid resting pulse will naturally slow down a lot when you feel very relaxed after taking a warm bath.","t":"當你在泡完熱水澡感到非常放鬆時，你快速的靜息脈搏自然會減慢很多。"},{"w":"impulse","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong and unreflective urge or desire to act.","c":"衝動","s":"The hungry shopper had a sudden impulse to buy every single chocolate bar displayed right next to the checkout counter.","t":"飢餓的購物者突然有一種衝動，想買下陳列在結帳櫃檯旁邊的每一塊巧克力棒。"},{"w":"on impulse","p":"phr.","d":"suddenly and without forethought.","c":"衝動地","s":"On impulse, the exhausted woman suddenly bought some sweet candy that she saw near the busy store's cash register.","t":"衝動地，這名疲憊的女子突然買了一些她在繁忙商店收銀機附近看到的甜糖果。"},{"w":"impulsive","p":"adj.","d":"Acting or done suddenly without thinking carefully about the results or consequences.","c":"衝動的","s":"Since Leo tends to be very impulsive when he is stressed, he often makes shopping decisions that he later regrets.","t":"由於里歐在壓力大時往往非常衝動，他經常做出事後會後悔的購物決定。"},{"w":"impulsive shopping","p":"phr.","d":"The act of buying things suddenly without planning or thinking about whether you really need them.","c":"衝動購物","s":"E-commerce apps use flash sales and countdown timers to encourage impulsive shopping among young consumers.","t":"電子商務應用程式利用閃購和倒數計時器，來刺激年輕消費者進行衝動購物。"},{"w":"shopping spree","p":"phr.","d":"A short period of time spent buying a lot of things, often spending a large amount of money.","c":"瘋狂購物、瘋狂採購","s":"After receiving her annual bonus, Chloe went on a massive shopping spree at the luxury department store.","t":"在領到年終獎金後，克洛伊去那家奢華的百貨公司進行了一場大瘋狂購物。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"Required by a law or a rule; that must be done.","c":"強制性的、必修的、義務的","s":"In Taiwan, elementary and junior high school education is compulsory for all children under a certain age.","t":"在台灣，對於達到特定年齡的所有兒童而言，國小與國中教育都是義務的（強制性的）。"},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adj.","d":"Ordered by authority; officially or legally required.","c":"強制性的、法定的、義務的","s":"Attending the orientation session is mandatory for all new employees so they can understand the company rules.","t":"參加新生訓練對所有新員工來說都是強制性的（義務的），以便他們了解公司規定。"},{"w":"emphasis","p":"n.","d":"special importance, value, or prominence given to something.","c":"強調；重點","s":"The main emphasis of this advanced university course will be strictly exploring recent European history and its complex political conflicts.","t":"這門進階大學課程的主要重點將嚴格探討近期的歐洲歷史及其複雜的政治衝突。"},{"w":"emphasize","p":"v.","d":"to give special importance or prominence to something in speaking or writing.","c":"強調","s":"Our strict English teacher frequently likes to deeply emphasize the absolute importance of thoroughly memorizing all the daily vocabulary words.","t":"我們嚴格的英文老師經常喜歡深深強調徹底背誦所有每日單字的絕對重要性。"},{"w":"put emphasis on","p":"phr.","d":"to give special attention or importance to something.","c":"把重點放在...","s":"The successful international company always puts great emphasis on effective teamwork rather than solely celebrating individual talents during major projects.","t":"這家成功的國際公司在重大專案中總是把極大的重點放在有效的團隊合作上，而不是僅僅慶祝個人才華。"},{"w":"lay emphasis on","p":"phr.","d":"to give special importance to something.","c":"將重點放在...","s":"The strict university professor tends to lay emphasis on completing original research rather than simply reading the old textbook.","t":"這位嚴格的大學教授傾向於將重點放在完成原創研究上，而不是僅僅閱讀舊教科書。"},{"w":"bodily","p":"adj.","d":"of or concerning the body.","c":"身體的","s":"Many terrified passengers on the crashed bus unfortunately suffered highly serious bodily injuries and had to visit the hospital.","t":"墜毀巴士上許多受驚的乘客不幸遭受了極其嚴重的身體的傷害，必須去醫院就診。"},{"w":"bodily function","p":"phr.","d":"an organic process that takes place in the body.","c":"身體機能","s":"Drinking enough fresh water every single day is absolutely essential for effectively maintaining every normal bodily function in humans.","t":"每天喝足夠的新鮮水，對於有效維持人類所有正常的身體機能絕對是必不可少的。"},{"w":"consistent","p":"adj.","d":"acting or done in the same way over time, especially so as to be fair or accurate.","c":"始終如一的；一致的","s":"The highly popular Italian restaurant always delivers consistent quality, ensuring that every single customer leaves feeling completely full and happy.","t":"這家極受歡迎的義大利餐廳總是提供始終如一的品質，確保每一位顧客離開時都感到完全飽足和快樂。"},{"w":"inconsistent","p":"adj.","d":"not staying the same throughout.","c":"不一致的","s":"Because his daily studying habits were incredibly inconsistent, the frustrated student unfortunately failed his difficult final math exam again.","t":"因為他每天的讀書習慣極度不一致的，這位沮喪的學生不幸地再次沒有通過他困難的數學期末考。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"in every case or on every occasion; invariably.","c":"一貫地","s":"The dedicated marathon runner consistently wakes up extremely early every morning to complete her rigorous and exhausting outdoor training.","t":"這位盡責的馬拉松跑者一貫地每天極早起床，以完成她嚴格且令人疲憊的戶外訓練。"},{"w":"consistency","p":"n.","d":"consistent behavior or treatment.","c":"一致性","s":"Maintaining perfect consistency in your professional work is truly the best way to earn the deep respect of your demanding boss.","t":"在你的專業工作中保持完美的一致性，確實是贏得你要求嚴格的老闆深深尊重的最佳方式。"},{"w":"compatible with","p":"phr.","d":"Able to exist, work, or be used together successfully without causing problems.","c":"與…相容的、能共處的","s":"These new software updates are not compatible with older computer operating systems, so you might need to upgrade your device first.","t":"這些新的軟體更新與舊的電腦作業系統不相容，所以您可能需要先升級您的裝置。"},{"w":"constant","p":"adj.","d":"Staying the same; fixed and never-changing over a period of time.","c":"恆定的、不變的","s":"To bake the perfect soufflé, you must keep the oven at a constant temperature throughout the entire cooking process.","t":"為了烘焙出完美的舒芙蕾，您必須在整個烹飪過程中將烤箱保持在恆定的（不變的）溫度。"},{"w":"constant","p":"adj.","d":"Happening all the time or repeatedly; frequent and continuous.","c":"持續不斷的、經常發生的","s":"The old office building requires constant repairs due to its leaking roof and broken water pipes.","t":"這棟老舊的辦公大樓因為屋頂漏水和水管破裂，需要持續不斷的（經常性的）維修。"},{"w":"constantly","p":"adv.","d":"All the time, or very often; continuously and repeatedly.","c":"不斷地、時常地、持續地","s":"The successful technology company is constantly inventing new products to stay ahead of its competitors in the market.","t":"這家成功的科技公司正在不斷地（持續地）研發新產品，以在市場上保持領先競爭對手。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"to be greater in number or size than a quantity, number, or other measurable thing.","c":"超過","s":"Please ensure that you do not carelessly exceed the strict speed limit when you are driving on this dangerous highway.","t":"當你行駛在這條危險的高速公路上時，請確保你不要粗心地超過嚴格的速限。"},{"w":"exceedingly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; to a very great degree.","c":"極其；非常","s":"The tall young boy is exceedingly strong and should easily be able to make the competitive high school football team.","t":"這個高大的年輕男孩非常強壯，應該能輕易地加入競爭激烈的高中美式足球隊。"},{"w":"enormously","p":"adv.","d":"to a very great degree or extent; considerably.","c":"巨大地；非常","s":"The highly anticipated science fiction movie was enormously popular, quickly earning millions of dollars at the busy international box office.","t":"這部備受期待的科幻電影非常（巨大地）受歡迎，迅速在繁忙的國際票房賺進了數百萬美元。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"v.","d":"an advantage or profit gained from something; to receive an advantage.","c":"益處；對...有益","s":"Living in a large modern city will significantly benefit your professional career by providing many excellent and unique networking opportunities.","t":"居住在現代化的大城市，透過提供許多極好且獨特的建立人脈機會，將顯著對你的職業生涯有益。"},{"w":"benefit from","p":"phr. v.","d":"To get an advantage, profit, or helpful result from something.","c":"從…獲益、得益於","s":"Many local businesses will greatly benefit from the new subway line, as it brings thousands of potential customers to the area every day.","t":"許多在地商家將大大從這條新地鐵線獲益（得益於此），因為它每天為該地區帶來數千名潛在客戶。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"An advantage, profit, or helpful effect that you get from something.","c":"好處、利益、優勢","s":"Regular exercise offers numerous health benefits, including a stronger heart, reduced stress, and better sleep quality.","t":"規律運動帶來許多健康好處（利益），包括更強壯的心臟、減輕壓力和更好的睡眠品質。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"favorable or advantageous; resulting in good.","c":"有益的","s":"Taking daily Vitamin C supplements is widely believed by medical experts to be highly beneficial to a person's complex immune system.","t":"醫學專家廣泛認為，每天服用維生素C補充劑對一個人複雜的免疫系統是高度有益的。"},{"w":"helpful","p":"adj.","d":"giving or ready to give help.","c":"有幫助的","s":"The experienced teacher provided some incredibly helpful advice that allowed the struggling student to finally pass the difficult exam.","t":"經驗豐富的老師提供了一些極其有幫助的建議，讓這位苦苦掙扎的學生終於通過了困難的考試。"},{"w":"stiff","p":"adj.","d":"not easily bent or changed in shape; rigid.","c":"僵硬的；拘謹的","s":"Dan had to uncomfortably sleep on the hard wooden floor, and he understandably felt very stiff the next early morning.","t":"丹必須不舒服地睡在堅硬的木地板上，可以理解地，他在隔天清晨感到非常僵硬的。"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"capable of bending easily without breaking; able to be easily modified.","c":"靈活的；有彈性的","s":"Mary is very lucky to have a highly flexible work schedule that perfectly lets her carefully manage her own free time.","t":"瑪麗非常幸運能擁有高度有彈性的工作時間表，完美地讓她能仔細管理自己的空閒時間。"},{"w":"inflexible","p":"adj.","d":"unwilling to change or compromise.","c":"缺乏彈性的","s":"The strict manager was completely inflexible regarding the company rules, absolutely refusing to allow any employees to leave early today.","t":"這位嚴格的經理在公司規定方面完全是缺乏彈性的，絕對拒絕允許任何員工今天提早下班。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of bending easily without breaking.","c":"靈活性","s":"Practicing gentle yoga every single day will significantly increase your physical flexibility and help effectively prevent dangerous sports injuries.","t":"每天練習溫和的瑜珈將顯著增加你身體的靈活性，並幫助有效地預防危險的運動傷害。"},{"w":"sharpen","p":"v.","d":"to make or become sharp or sharper.","c":"使鋒利；增進","s":"Actively learning a complex new foreign language can effectively help you successfully sharpen your mind and improve your daily memory.","t":"積極學習一門複雜的新外語，能有效地幫助你成功增進你的心智並改善你的日常記憶。"},{"w":"sharp","p":"adj.","d":"having an edge or point that is able to cut or pierce something.","c":"鋒利的","s":"You should definitely be very careful when washing that incredibly sharp knife because it can easily cut your wet hands.","t":"在清洗那把極度鋒利的刀時，你絕對要非常小心，因為它很容易割傷你濕漉漉的手。"},{"w":"pencil sharpener","p":"phr.","d":"a device for sharpening a pencil by rotating a cutter around its point.","c":"削鉛筆機","s":"The young student quickly asked his busy teacher if he could borrow the electric pencil sharpener to fix his broken pencil.","t":"年輕的學生迅速問他忙碌的老師，是否可以借用電動削鉛筆機來修好他斷掉的鉛筆。"},{"w":"fatigue","p":"n. / v.","d":"extreme tiredness resulting from mental or physical exertion or illness.","c":"疲勞","s":"The unbearable physical fatigue in the exhausted runner's heavy legs unfortunately caused him to drastically slow down near the finish line.","t":"筋疲力盡的跑者沉重雙腿上難以忍受的身體疲勞，不幸地導致他在終點線附近大幅減速。"},{"w":"fatigued","p":"adj.","d":"cause someone to feel exhausted.","c":"疲勞的","s":"She was severely fatigued by a nasty and lingering case of the winter flu, forcing her to stay warmly in bed.","t":"她因感染了嚴重且揮之不去的冬季流感而感到極度疲勞的，迫使她溫暖地待在床上。"},{"w":"boost","p":"n. / v.","d":"a source of help or encouragement leading to increase or improvement.","c":"提升；促進","s":"When I am feeling incredibly tired in the morning, I always deeply drink hot black coffee to give myself a boost.","t":"當我在早上感到極度疲倦時，我總是深喝熱黑咖啡來給自己一個提升。"},{"w":"increase","p":"n. / v.","d":"a rise in the size, amount, or degree of something.","c":"增加","s":"The struggling company urgently needs to drastically increase its annual sales if it wants to completely avoid total financial ruin.","t":"這家苦苦掙扎的公司如果想完全避免徹底的財務崩潰，就急需大幅增加其年度銷售額。"},{"w":"ego","p":"n.","d":"a person's sense of self-esteem or self-importance.","c":"意識；自尊心","s":"The incredibly harsh and completely unforgiving online critic really hurt the famous young actor's fragile ego with his terrible review.","t":"這位極其嚴厲且完全不寬容的線上評論家，用他糟糕的評論真的傷害了這位著名年輕演員脆弱的自尊心。"},{"w":"dignity","p":"n. [U]","d":"The quality of being worthy of honor or respect, or a calm and serious manner.","c":"尊嚴、莊嚴","s":"Even after losing his job unexpectedly, Marcus maintained his dignity by accepting the situation calmly and refusing to blame others.","t":"即使意外失去工作，馬庫斯依然透過冷靜接受現狀且拒絕指責他人，來維持他的尊嚴。"},{"w":"self-esteem","p":"n. [U]","d":"The feeling of being satisfied with your own character, abilities, and value; self-respect.","c":"自尊（心）","s":"Getting bullied at school can severely damage a teenager's self-esteem-self-esteem, making them feel worthless and isolated.","t":"在學校遭受霸凌會嚴重損害青少年的自尊心，使他們感到自己毫無價值且孤立無援。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n. [U]","d":"A feeling of trust or belief in your own abilities, or in someone else's reliability.","c":"信心、自信","s":"Practicing his presentation in front of a mirror multiple times gave Leo the confidence he needed to speak clearly on stage.","t":"在鏡子前多次練習簡報，給了里歐在舞台上清晰發言所需的信心（自信）。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"Feeling sure about your own abilities or certain that something will happen successfully.","c":"有信心的、有自信的","s":"Chloe spent months studying for the TOEFL exam, so she feels completely confident that she will get a high score.","t":"克洛伊花了幾個月的時間準備托福考試，因此她對自己能獲得高分感到非常有信心（有自信）。"},{"w":"disappointed","p":"adj.","d":"sad or displeased because someone or something has failed to fulfill one's hopes or expectations.","c":"失望的","s":"I was incredibly disappointed to sadly hear that you probably won't be joining us for the exciting dinner party tonight.","t":"聽到你今晚可能不會加入我們刺激的晚宴，我感到極其失望的。"},{"w":"disappoint","p":"v.","d":"to fail to fulfill the hopes or expectations of someone.","c":"令人失望","s":"The lazy student's terrible final test scores will undoubtedly disappoint his hardworking parents who paid for his expensive private tutors.","t":"這位懶惰學生糟糕的期末考成績，無疑會讓他那支付了昂貴私人導師費用的辛勤父母感到令人失望。"},{"w":"disappointment","p":"n.","d":"sadness or displeasure caused by the nonfulfillment of one's hopes or expectations.","c":"失望","s":"To her immense disappointment, the heavily promoted new romantic movie turned out to be incredibly boring and completely poorly written.","t":"讓她極度失望的是，這部被大力宣傳的新浪漫電影結果卻是極其無聊且劇本寫得非常糟糕。"},{"w":"be disappointed in","p":"phr.","d":"to feel sadness or displeasure toward someone.","c":"對(某人)感到失望","s":"The hardworking father is deeply disappointed in his teenage son for completely failing his classes and lying about his grades.","t":"辛勤的父親對他那完全不及格並在成績上說謊的青少年兒子感到深深的失望。"},{"w":"be disappointed with","p":"phr.","d":"to feel sadness or displeasure toward something.","c":"對(某事物)感到失望","s":"We are truly disappointed with the terrible quality of the expensive restaurant's cold food and completely unhelpful customer service.","t":"我們真的對這家昂貴餐廳冷掉食物的可怕品質和完全沒有幫助的客戶服務感到失望。"},{"w":"healthful","p":"adj.","d":"having or conducive to good health.","c":"有益健康的","s":"After recovering from her serious illness, Jane completely committed herself to strictly living a much more healthful and active lifestyle.","t":"從重病康復後，珍完全致力於嚴格過著一種更有益健康的且活躍的生活方式。"},{"w":"healthy","p":"adj.","d":"in a good physical or mental condition; in good health.","c":"健康的","s":"Eating lots of dark green vegetables and frequently exercising outdoors is the absolute best way to stay perfectly healthy forever.","t":"多吃深綠色蔬菜並經常在戶外運動，是永遠保持完美健康的絕對最佳方式。"},{"w":"stay healthy","p":"phr.","d":"To maintain good physical and mental well-being by eating well and exercising.","c":"保持健康","s":"Eating a balanced diet and getting enough sleep every night are essential ways to stay healthy throughout the stressful school year.","t":"均衡飲食和每晚充足的睡眠是在充滿壓力的學年中保持健康的重要方法。"},{"w":"stay in shape","p":"phr.","d":"To keep your body lean, strong, and healthy through regular physical exercise.","c":"保持體態、保持身材","s":"Many people join gyms or go jogging in the park to stay in shape, ensuring they look and feel their best.","t":"許多人加入健身房或去公園慢跑以保持體態（保持身材），確保自己看起來和感覺起來都是最佳狀態。"},{"w":"stay fit","p":"phr.","d":"To keep your body strong and physically healthy, especially through regular exercise.","c":"保持健美、保持體能良好","s":"You don't need expensive equipment to stay fit; just doing basic bodyweight exercises at home can make a huge difference.","t":"你不需要昂貴的設備來保持健美（保持良好的體能狀態）；只需在家做基本的自重訓練就能帶來巨大的改變。"},{"w":"health","p":"n. [U]","d":"The condition of a person's body or mind, and whether they are sick or well.","c":"健康（狀況）","s":"Regular checkups are important because they allow doctors to monitor your overall health and catch potential medical issues early.","t":"定期檢查非常重要，因為它們能讓醫生監控你的整體健康（狀況）並儘早發現潛在的醫療問題。"},{"w":"health benefit","p":"phr.","d":"A positive or helpful effect that a specific food, activity, or habit has on a person's well-being.","c":"健康益處","s":"Drinking green tea offers a significant health benefit because it contains rich antioxidants that protect your cells from damage.","t":"喝綠茶帶來顯著的健康益處，因為它含有能保護細胞免受損害的豐富抗氧化劑。"},{"w":"health concern","p":"phr.","d":"A medical issue, condition, or problem that causes worry or requires professional attention.","c":"健康顧慮、健康隱憂","s":"High blood pressure is a serious health concern that can lead to heart disease if it is not managed properly with medicine and diet.","t":"高血壓是一個嚴重的健康顧慮（隱憂），如果沒有透過藥物和飲食妥善控制，可能會導致心臟病。"},{"w":"public health","p":"phr.","d":"The health of the population as a whole, especially as monitored and protected by the government.","c":"公共衛生、公眾健康","s":"During the flu season, the government promotes public health by providing free vaccinations to senior citizens and young children.","t":"在流感季節，政府透過向老年人和幼童提供免費疫苗接種來提升公共衛生（公眾健康）。"},{"w":"healthcare","p":"n. [U]","d":"The set of services provided by medical professionals to maintain or restore physical and mental health.","c":"醫療保健、醫療服務","s":"The government is working to improve the quality of healthcare in rural areas so that everyone can have access to good doctors.","t":"政府正在努力提高農村地區的醫療保健（醫療服務）品質，以便每個人都能看得到好醫生。"},{"w":"healthcare system","p":"phr.","d":"The organization of people, institutions, and resources that deliver medical care services to a population.","c":"醫療保健體制、醫療系統","s":"Taiwan's National Health Insurance is widely praised as an efficient healthcare system that provides affordable medical care to all citizens.","t":"台灣的全民健康保險被廣泛讚譽為一個高效的醫療保健體制（醫療系統），為所有國民提供負擔得起的醫療服務。"},{"w":"insure","p":"v.","d":"To buy or provide insurance for someone or something to protect against financial loss.","c":"為…投保、給…保險","s":"It is illegal to drive a car on public roads if you do not insure the vehicle against potential accidents.","t":"如果你沒有為車輛投保以防範潛在的意外，在公共道路上開車是違法的。"},{"w":"insurance","p":"n. [U]","d":"An arrangement where you pay a company regular money and they pay for your costs if you have an accident, illness, or loss.","c":"保險","s":"Before going on a backpacking trip across Europe, it is wise to buy travel insurance to cover any unexpected medical emergencies.","t":"在前往歐洲進行背包客旅行之前，購買旅遊保險以支付任何突發的醫療緊急狀況是明智的。"},{"w":"health insurance","p":"phr.","d":"A type of insurance that pays for medical and surgical expenses incurred by the insured person.","c":"健康保險、醫療保險","s":"Many employees consider comprehensive health insurance to be the most important benefit when choosing a new job.","t":"許多員工在選擇新工作時，將完善的健康保險（醫療保險）視為最重要的福利。"},{"w":"insurance policy","p":"phr.","d":"An official contract or document that details the conditions and items covered by an insurance agreement.","c":"保險單、保險契約","s":"You should read the terms of your insurance policy carefully to understand exactly what kinds of damage are covered.","t":"你應該仔細閱讀你的保險單（保險契約）條款，以確切了解哪些種類的損害是在理賠範圍內。"},{"w":"coverage","p":"n. [U]","d":"The amount of protection or the specific risks included in an insurance plan.","c":"保險範圍、保險保障","s":"Basic medical plans usually don't include dental coverage, so patients have to pay for regular teeth cleanings out of pocket.","t":"基本的醫療計劃通常不包含牙科保險範圍，因此患者必須自費進行定期洗牙。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"battery – work miracles","cards":[{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"a container consisting of one or more cells, in which chemical energy is converted into electricity.","c":"電池","s":"After playing the exciting video game for several hours, the battery in his wireless controller completely died.","t":"在玩了幾個小時刺激的電玩遊戲後，他無線控制器的電池完全沒電了。"},{"w":"dead battery","p":"phr.","d":"a battery that no longer has electrical charge.","c":"沒電的電池","s":"I was planning to quickly call my boss, but unfortunately my smartphone currently has a completely dead battery.","t":"我本來打算迅速打電話給我的老闆，但不幸的是我的智慧型手機目前有一顆完全沒電的電池。"},{"w":"charge the battery","p":"phr.","d":"to replenish the electrical power in a battery.","c":"為電池充電","s":"Before we finally leave for our long weekend camping trip, you must remember to fully charge the battery of the flashlight.","t":"在我們最終出發去漫長的週末露營旅行之前，你必須記得為手電筒為電池充電（把電池充滿電）。"},{"w":"rechargeable battery","p":"phr.","d":"a type of electrical battery which can be charged, discharged into a load, and recharged many times.","c":"充電電池","s":"To help responsibly protect the environment and save some money, you should consider using a rechargeable battery for your daily electronic devices.","t":"為了負責任地幫助保護環境並省點錢，你應該考慮為你的日常電子設備使用充電電池。"},{"w":"portable charger","p":"n. [C]","d":"A small external device used to charge electronic items when you are away from a wall outlet.","c":"行動電源","s":"I always keep a portable charger in my backpack so I can power up my phone during long trips.","t":"我總是在背包裡放一個行動電源，這樣在長途旅行中就能給手機充電。"},{"w":"charge","p":"v.","d":"To pass electricity into a device or battery to store power for future use.","c":"給…充電","s":"Remember to charge your wireless earphones tonight so they don't run out of power tomorrow.","t":"記得今晚給你的無線耳機充電，這樣明天才不會沒電。"},{"w":"charge","p":"v.","d":"To ask an amount of money for a service, activity, or item.","c":"收費、索價","s":"Most luxury hotels charge a premium price for high-speed Wi-Fi access in the guest rooms.","t":"大多數奢華飯店在客房內提供高速網路時都會收取高昂的費用。"},{"w":"charge","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"The amount of money that you have to pay for a service or a product.","c":"費用、價錢","s":"There is an extra charge for modifying your flight ticket details just three days before departure.","t":"在出發前三天修改機票細節需要額外支付一筆費用。"},{"w":"free of charge","p":"phr.","d":"Without having to pay any money; completely free.","c":"免費地、不收費地","s":"The museum offers guided tours free of charge every Saturday morning to all visitors.","t":"這家博物館每週六早上向所有遊客免費提供導覽服務。"},{"w":"be in charge of","p":"phr.","d":"To be responsible for a group of people, a project, or a specific activity.","c":"負責…、掌管…","s":"Chloe will be in charge of organizing the annual company banquet this year.","t":"克洛伊今年將負責籌辦公司的一年一度尾牙晚宴。"},{"w":"charge","p":"v.","d":"To rush forward quickly and suddenly, often in an attack or out of excitement.","c":"猛衝、向前衝","s":"As soon as the store doors opened for the anniversary sale, the eager crowd began to charge inside.","t":"週年慶特賣會的店門一打開，熱切的人群便開始向前猛衝進去。"},{"w":"fee","p":"n. [C]","d":"An amount of money paid for a professional service, exam, or official privilege.","c":"費用、服務費、規費","s":"To maintain your gym membership active, you must pay a monthly fee by the first of each month.","t":"為了保持健身房會員資格有效，你必須在每月一號前支付月費。"},{"w":"service fee","p":"phr.","d":"An additional charge made for a particular service, often added to a restaurant bill.","c":"服務費","s":"Many dining establishments in Taipei automatically add a ten percent service fee to the final bill.","t":"許多餐廳會自動在最終帳單上加收百分之十的服務費。"},{"w":"admission(s) fee","p":"phr.","d":"The fee paid to enter a place like a museum, theater, historical site, or theme park.","c":"門票、入場費","s":"The historic palace charges a small admission fee to help cover the costs of building maintenance.","t":"這座歷史悠久的宮殿收取少許入場費（門票），以協助支付建築維護的成本。"},{"w":"shipping fee","p":"phr.","d":"The money paid to transport large items or products, usually over longer distances or overseas.","c":"運費（船運/空運商品等）","s":"Buying items from international websites often involves a high shipping fee and potential import taxes.","t":"從國際網站購買商品通常涉及高昂的運費以及潛在的進口稅。"},{"w":"delivery fee","p":"phr.","d":"The cost charged by a company to bring goods, food, or packages directly to your door.","c":"外送費、配送費","s":"Ordering food through mobile apps during a heavy rainstorm might require a higher delivery fee.","t":"在暴風雨中透過手機應用程式點餐可能需要支付較高的外送費（配送費）。"},{"w":"fare","p":"n. [C]","d":"The price you pay to travel on public transportation, such as a bus, train, or plane.","c":"票價、（車、船、機）費","s":"The local government decided to raise the public bus fare by two dollars starting next month.","t":"當地政府決定從下個月開始將公車票價調高兩元。"},{"w":"flight fare airfare","p":"phr. / n.","d":"The price of a ticket for traveling by airplane.","c":"機票票價、航空票價","s":"Booking your summer vacation tickets early will help you secure a much cheaper flight fare airfare.","t":"提早預訂暑假假期的機票將有助於你取得更便宜的機票票價。"},{"w":"taxi fare","p":"phr.","d":"The amount of money you pay for a ride in a taxi cab.","c":"計程車車資","s":"Marcus split the taxi fare with his coworkers since they were all traveling to the same conference center.","t":"馬庫斯和他的同事平分了計程車車資，因為他們全都要前往同一個會議中心。"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting or intended to last or remain unchanged indefinitely.","c":"永久的","s":"The experienced doctor sadly informed Tony that the large scars on his face would likely not be completely permanent.","t":"經驗豐富的醫生遺憾地通知東尼，他臉上的大疤痕很可能不會是完全永久的。"},{"w":"permanently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that lasts or remains unchanged indefinitely.","c":"永久地","s":"After suffering from a terrible sports injury, the professional athlete was unfortunately forced to permanently retire from the competitive game.","t":"在遭受可怕的運動傷害後，這位職業運動員不幸被迫永久地從競爭激烈的比賽中退休。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for only a limited period of time; not permanent.","c":"暫時的","s":"Frank is currently working at a difficult temporary job just to make some extra money before he officially goes to college.","t":"法蘭克目前正在做一份困難的暫時的工作，只是為了在他正式上大學前多賺點錢。"},{"w":"eternal","p":"adj.","d":"lasting or existing forever; without end or beginning.","c":"永恆的","s":"Some deeply religious people firmly believe that their souls will peacefully live an eternal life in heaven after they die.","t":"一些非常虔誠的人堅信，他們死後靈魂將在天堂平靜地過著永恆的生活。"},{"w":"everlasting","p":"adj.","d":"lasting forever or a very long time.","c":"持久的；永恆的","s":"The young couple gave each other golden rings as a beautiful symbol of their deep and everlasting love for one another.","t":"這對年輕夫婦互相贈送金戒指，作為他們彼此深厚且持久的（永恆的）愛的象徵。"},{"w":"magnet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of iron that has its component atoms so ordered that the material exhibits properties of magnetism.","c":"磁鐵","s":"I quickly used a colorful magnet to securely attach my important summer class schedule to the front door of the refrigerator.","t":"我迅速用一塊色彩鮮豔的磁鐵，將我重要的暑期課程表牢牢地貼在冰箱的前門上。"},{"w":"magnetic","p":"adj.","d":"exhibiting or relating to magnetism.","c":"有吸引力的；磁性的","s":"Because she naturally has a highly magnetic personality, everyone at the crowded party instantly wanted to become her best friend.","t":"因為她天生有著極具有吸引力的（磁性的）個性，擁擠派對上的每個人都立刻想成為她最好的朋友。"},{"w":"magnetic field","p":"phr.","d":"a region around a magnetic material or a moving electric charge within which the force of magnetism acts.","c":"磁場","s":"The knowledgeable astronomy teacher thoroughly explained that Jupiter's massive magnetic field is surprisingly twenty thousand times stronger than Earth's.","t":"知識淵博的天文學老師詳細解釋說，木星巨大的磁場令人驚訝地比地球強兩萬倍。"},{"w":"insert","p":"v.","d":"to place, fit, or thrust something into another thing.","c":"插入","s":"David carefully inserted several shiny silver coins into the old vending machine and successfully bought a cold can of soda.","t":"大衛小心地將幾枚閃亮的銀幣插入這台舊自動販賣機中，並成功買到了一罐冰汽水。"},{"w":"insertion","p":"n.","d":"the action of inserting something.","c":"插入","s":"The delicate medical operation requires the highly precise insertion of a tiny camera completely into the patient's damaged heart.","t":"這項精密的醫療手術需要將微型攝影機極其精確地插入病患受損的心臟中。"},{"w":"capsule","p":"n.","d":"a small case or container, especially a round or cylindrical one.","c":"膠囊","s":"This strong bitter medicine comes in the form of a small capsule and must be swallowed whole with a large glass of water.","t":"這種強效的苦藥是小膠囊的形狀，必須搭配一大杯水整個吞下。"},{"w":"time capsule","p":"phr.","d":"a container storing a selection of objects chosen as being typical of the present time, buried for discovery in the future.","c":"時空膠囊","s":"The excited elementary school students buried a sealed time capsule containing modern photographs and letters for future generations to find.","t":"興奮的小學生埋下了一個密封的時空膠囊，裡面裝著現代照片和信件，留待後代去發現。"},{"w":"capsule hotel","p":"phr.","d":"a hotel system with extremely small rooms intended to provide cheap overnight accommodation.","c":"膠囊旅館","s":"Because he was traveling on a very strict budget, the tired tourist decided to sleep comfortably in a cheap capsule hotel downtown.","t":"因為他的旅行預算非常嚴格，疲憊的遊客決定在市中心一家便宜的膠囊旅館舒適地睡覺。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"advice or information aimed at resolving a problem or difficulty, especially as given by someone in authority.","c":"指導；引導","s":"We desperately need some highly expert guidance on how to successfully handle the aggressive reporters waiting outside the main building.","t":"我們極度需要一些高度專業的指導，來了解如何成功應對在主建築物外等待的具攻擊性的記者。"},{"w":"under the guidance of","p":"phr.","d":"being directed or helped by someone.","c":"在...的指導下","s":"Under the guidance of her experienced personal trainer, Jane finally managed to successfully lose ten pounds in just two months.","t":"在她經驗豐富的私人教練的指導下，珍終於成功地在短短兩個月內減掉了十磅。"},{"w":"guide","p":"n.","d":"to show or indicate the way to someone; a person who advises or shows the way to others.","c":"引導；嚮導","s":"The friendly local guide safely led the curious tourists through the dark and extremely dangerous caves located deep in the mountains.","t":"友善的當地嚮導安全地帶領好奇的遊客穿過位於深山中黑暗且極其危險的洞穴。"},{"w":"tour guide","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person whose job is to show tourists around places of interest and give them information.","c":"導遊","s":"The friendly tour guide led the group through the ancient temple, explaining the history of each statue.","t":"這位友善的導遊帶領團隊穿過這座古老的寺廟，解釋每座雕像的歷史。"},{"w":"guide","p":"v.","d":"To show someone the way to a place, or to help them understand how to do something.","c":"引導、帶路、指導","s":"The experienced mentor will guide the new interns through their first week of complex projects at the company.","t":"這位經驗豐富的導師將引導新實習生度過他們在公司的第一週複雜專案。"},{"w":"lead","p":"v.","d":"To go in front of a group of people or animals to show them the way or direction.","c":"帶領、引領、領路","s":"The brave captain will lead his team onto the field for the championship game tonight.","t":"這位勇敢的隊長今晚將帶領他的球隊進入球場進行冠軍賽。"},{"w":"lead to","p":"phr. v.","d":"To cause something to happen as a final result; to result in a particular situation.","c":"導致、造成","s":"Making regular mistakes on financial reports can lead to serious problems during the end-of-year audit.","t":"在財務報告上經常出錯可能會導致年終審計期間的嚴重問題。"},{"w":"leadership","p":"n. [U]","d":"The position of being a leader, or the ability to guide, manage, and inspire a group of people.","c":"領導能力、領導地位","s":"Under the strong leadership of the new CEO, the technology company doubled its profits within a single year.","t":"在新任執行長強大的領導能力下，這家科技公司在短短一年內利潤翻倍。"},{"w":"direct","p":"v.","d":"To control, manage, or give official orders and instructions to a group of people or an activity.","c":"指揮、引導、指示","s":"Police officers had to direct traffic at the busy intersection after the traffic lights broke down suddenly.","t":"在交通號誌突然故障後，警員們不得不忙碌的十字路口指揮交通。"},{"w":"direct","p":"v.","d":"To tell the actors, musicians, and camera operators what to do in order to make a movie, show, or video.","c":"導演、執導（影片/電影）","s":"Spielberg was chosen to direct the new sci-fi movie because of his incredible storytelling skills.","t":"史匹柏因其驚人的敘事技巧而被選中來執導這部新的科幻電影。"},{"w":"director","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person who is in charge of making a movie, play, or video, telling actors how to play their parts.","c":"導演","s":"The movie director asked the lead actress to repeat the emotional scene to get the perfect shot.","t":"電影導演要求女主角重拍那場情感豐富的戲，以獲得最完美的鏡頭。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"The position or path towards which someone or something moves, faces, or points.","c":"方向、方位","s":"If you walk in the wrong direction, you will end up at the train station instead of the museum.","t":"如果你走錯了方向，你最終會走到火車站而不是博物館。"},{"w":"in all directions","p":"phr.","d":"Moving away from a central point towards every possible side, way, or area.","c":"朝四面八方、向各個方向","s":"When the loud firecracker exploded in the park, the frightened pigeons flew off in all directions.","t":"當巨大的鞭炮在公園爆炸時，受驚的鴿子朝四面八方飛散。"},{"w":"direct","p":"adj.","d":"Going straight from one point to another without stopping, turning, or changing path.","c":"直接的、直達的","s":"Taking a direct flight from Taipei to Los Angeles saves a lot of travel time compared to having a long layover.","t":"與中途長時間停留相比，搭乘從台北到洛杉磯的直達（直接）航班可以節省大量的旅行時間。"},{"w":"indirect","p":"adj.","d":"Not happening or done in a straight way, or not immediately caused by something.","c":"間接的、迂迴的","s":"High stress at work can be an indirect cause of severe sleep problems and poor eating habits.","t":"工作壓力大可能是嚴重睡眠問題和不良飲食習慣的間接原因。"},{"w":"external","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to or forming the outer surface or structure of something.","c":"外用的；外部的","s":"The pharmacist strictly warned the patient that this special medical skin cream is absolutely for external use only and should not be eaten.","t":"藥劑師嚴格警告病患，這種特殊的醫療護膚霜絕對僅供外用的，不應食用。"},{"w":"exterior","p":"adj. / n.","d":"forming, situated on, or relating to the outside of something; the outer surface or structure.","c":"外部（的）","s":"The talented designer painted the entire exterior of the beautiful modern house with an incredibly bright and cheerful yellow color.","t":"才華洋溢的設計師用極其明亮歡快的黃色，粉刷了這棟美麗現代房屋的整個外部。"},{"w":"outer","p":"adj.","d":"outside; external.","c":"外面的；外部的","s":"During the terribly cold winter storm, the hiker wore a thick waterproof jacket as his strong outer layer of protective clothing.","t":"在極其寒冷的冬季風暴中，登山客穿著一件厚實的防水外套作為他堅固的外面的防護衣物。"},{"w":"internal","p":"adj.","d":"of or situated on the inside.","c":"內部的","s":"The severe car accident unfortunately caused massive internal bleeding, requiring the injured driver to undergo immediate and highly dangerous emergency surgery.","t":"這起嚴重的車禍不幸造成了大量的內部的出血，需要受傷的駕駛立刻接受極其危險的緊急手術。"},{"w":"externally","p":"adv.","d":"with reference to the outer surface or structure of something; outside.","c":"外部地","s":"The grand historic building has been completely restored externally, but the entire inside still needs a significant amount of repair work.","t":"這座宏偉的歷史建築在外部地已經完全修復，但整個內部仍然需要大量的維修工作。"},{"w":"fetch","p":"v.","d":"to go for and then bring back (someone or something) for someone.","c":"拿來；去取","s":"The energetic young dog eagerly ran across the huge green park and quickly fetched the wooden stick for its loving owner.","t":"充滿活力的年輕小狗熱切地跑過巨大的綠色公園，迅速為牠充滿愛心的主人拿來了木棍。"},{"w":"far-fetched","p":"adj.","d":"unlikely and unconvincing; implausible.","c":"牽強的；難以置信的","s":"The desperate student's excuse for not completing his difficult math homework sounded incredibly far-fetched and completely unbelievable to the strict teacher.","t":"這名絕望的學生沒有完成困難數學作業的藉口，在嚴格的老師聽來極其牽強的且完全難以置信。"},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the possibility or likelihood of some future event occurring.","c":"前景；可能性","s":"Allan diligently did absolutely everything he possibly could in order to effectively improve his future career prospect in the banking industry.","t":"艾倫勤奮地做了他可能做的絕對一切，以有效地改善他未來在銀行業的職業前景。"},{"w":"prospective","p":"adj.","d":"expected or expecting to be something particular in the future.","c":"潛在的；預期的","s":"The ambitious real estate agent spent the entire afternoon showing the beautifully decorated modern apartment to several wealthy prospective buyers.","t":"雄心勃勃的房地產仲介花了整個下午，向幾位富有的潛在的買家展示這間裝潢美麗的現代公寓。"},{"w":"outlook","p":"n.","d":"a person's point of view or general attitude to life; a view of the future.","c":"前景；觀點","s":"Despite facing numerous difficult challenges, the optimistic team maintained a highly positive outlook regarding the final outcome of the complicated project.","t":"儘管面臨許多困難的挑戰，這支樂觀的團隊對這項複雜專案的最終結果仍然保持著高度積極的前景（觀點）。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"achieving maximum productivity with minimum wasted effort or expense.","c":"有效率的","s":"Debbie is an incredibly efficient and hardworking manager who absolutely never wastes any valuable time during the busy workday.","t":"黛比是一位極其有效率的且辛勤工作的經理，在繁忙的工作日裡絕對從不浪費任何寶貴的時間。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the state or quality of being efficient.","c":"效率","s":"The newly installed computer software successfully improved the overall efficiency of the entire office, allowing everyone to finish tasks much faster.","t":"新安裝的電腦軟體成功改善了整個辦公室整體的效率，讓每個人都能更快完成任務。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that achieves maximum productivity with minimum wasted effort or expense.","c":"有效率地","s":"The highly trained rescue team worked extremely efficiently to safely evacuate all the terrified residents from the burning apartment building.","t":"訓練有素的救援小組極其有效率地工作，將所有驚恐的居民從燃燒的公寓大樓中安全撤離。"},{"w":"inefficient","p":"adj.","d":"not achieving maximum productivity; wasting or failing to make the best use of time or resources.","c":"沒效率的","s":"Using an extremely old and slow computer to properly edit these massive video files is highly inefficient and incredibly frustrating.","t":"使用極其老舊且緩慢的電腦來適當地編輯這些龐大的影片檔案，是高度沒效率的且極度令人沮喪的。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"successful in producing a desired or intended result.","c":"有效的","s":"Taking this strong prescription medicine daily is widely considered the most effective way to completely cure your terrible throat infection.","t":"每天服用這種強效處方藥被廣泛認為是完全治癒你可怕喉嚨感染最有效的方法。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"producing or able to produce large amounts of goods, crops, or other commodities.","c":"多產的；有生產力的","s":"After enjoying a surprisingly relaxing weekend, the rested employees had a highly productive Monday morning at the busy corporate office.","t":"在享受了一個令人驚訝的放鬆週末後，休息過的員工在繁忙的企業辦公室度過了一個高度有生產力的星期一早晨。"},{"w":"agent","p":"n.","d":"a substance that brings about a chemical or physical effect; a person who acts on behalf of another.","c":"媒介；代理人","s":"Fresh lemons can effectively be used as a natural cleaning agent to quickly get rid of terrible smells inside the dirty refrigerator.","t":"新鮮檸檬可以有效地用作天然清潔媒介（劑），以迅速去除骯髒冰箱內的可怕氣味。"},{"w":"agency","p":"n.","d":"a business or organization established to provide a particular service.","c":"機構；代理處","s":"The ambitious young actor finally signed an exclusive contract with a highly prestigious talent agency located right in the center of Hollywood.","t":"這位雄心勃勃的年輕演員終於與一家位於好萊塢正中心的極具聲望的星探機構簽訂了獨家合約。"},{"w":"secret agent","p":"phr.","d":"a person employed by a government to obtain secret information or conduct operations.","c":"特務；秘密情報員","s":"The thrilling new action movie is about a highly skilled secret agent who is desperately trying to completely stop an evil global organization.","t":"這部驚險的新動作片講述了一位技術高超的特務，他正拚命地試圖徹底阻止一個邪惡的全球組織。"},{"w":"real estate agent","p":"phr.","d":"a person who sells and rents out buildings and land for clients.","c":"房地產仲介","s":"The friendly and knowledgeable real estate agent carefully showed the wealthy family five beautifully designed modern homes near the private beach.","t":"友善且知識淵博的房地產仲介仔細地向這個富裕的家庭展示了五棟位於私人海灘附近、設計美麗的現代住宅。"},{"w":"mend","p":"v.","d":"to repair (something that is broken or damaged).","c":"修理；癒合","s":"Sarah urgently needs to undergo a complex medical surgery to properly mend her terribly broken collarbone before the important sports competition.","t":"莎拉急需進行一項複雜的醫療手術，以便在重要的體育比賽前適當地癒合（修復）她嚴重斷裂的鎖骨。"},{"w":"amend","p":"v.","d":"to make minor changes in a text in order to make it fairer, more accurate, or more up-to-date.","c":"修改；修訂","s":"The strict government officially decided to carefully amend the extremely outdated environmental law to better protect the beautiful natural forests.","t":"嚴格的政府正式決定仔細修改極度過時的環境法律，以更好地保護美麗的自然森林。"},{"w":"mend one's ways","p":"phr.","d":"to improve one's habits or behavior.","c":"改過自新","s":"After many foolish years of carelessly fooling around, John finally realized his terrible mistakes and firmly decided to mend his ways.","t":"經過許多年粗心大意地鬼混後，約翰終於意識到自己可怕的錯誤，並堅定地決定要改過自新。"},{"w":"mend fences","p":"phr.","d":"to try to repair a relationship that has been damaged.","c":"修復關係","s":"After the stressful corporate merger was finally complete, the senior management successfully mended fences with their bitter former business rivals.","t":"在充滿壓力的企業合併終於完成後，高階管理層成功地與他們昔日痛苦的商業競爭對手修復了關係。"},{"w":"surgery","p":"n.","d":"the medical treatment of bodily injuries or diseases by incision or manipulation.","c":"外科手術","s":"The friendly doctor happily informed me that my elderly father's complex knee surgery went incredibly well and he will recover fully.","t":"友善的醫生高興地通知我，我年邁父親複雜的膝蓋外科手術進行得非常順利，他將會完全康復。"},{"w":"plastic surgery","p":"phr.","d":"the process of reconstructing or repairing parts of the body, especially by the transfer of tissue.","c":"整形手術","s":"The wealthy Hollywood actor secretly flew to a completely private medical clinic in Europe to undergo highly expensive plastic surgery.","t":"這位富有的好萊塢男演員秘密飛往歐洲一家完全私人的醫療診所，接受極其昂貴的整形手術。"},{"w":"surgeon","p":"n.","d":"a medical practitioner qualified to practice surgery.","c":"外科醫生","s":"The highly skilled and intensely focused surgeon successfully transplanted a healthy heart into the dangerously sick four-year-old boy yesterday morning.","t":"這位技術高超且高度專注的外科醫生昨天早上成功地將一顆健康的心臟移植到病情危險的四歲男孩體內。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"an act of surgery performed on a patient.","c":"手術；操作","s":"Because the patient was in intense physical pain, the doctor recommended a dangerous back operation to permanently fix the completely ruined muscles.","t":"因為病患正處於劇烈的身體疼痛中，醫生建議進行一項危險的背部手術，以永久修復完全毀損的肌肉。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The act, process, or method of working, running, or controlling something.","c":"操作、運作、運轉","s":"Reading the instruction manual carefully is necessary for the safe operation of this heavy factory equipment.","t":"仔細閱讀說明手冊對於安全操作（運作）這台重型工廠設備是必要的。"},{"w":"operate on a patient","p":"phr.","d":"To perform a medical surgery or cut on someone to cure an illness or injury.","c":"為病人動手術、幫病人開刀","s":"The experienced surgeon had to operate on a patient who suffered a severe injury from the car accident immediately.","t":"這位經驗豐富的外科醫生必須立刻為一位在車禍中受重傷的病人動手術（開刀）。"},{"w":"operate a machine","p":"phr.","d":"To control, run, or work a piece of equipment or mechanism safely.","c":"操作機器","s":"New factory workers must undergo intensive training before they are allowed to operate a machine on their own.","t":"新工廠員工在被允許獨自操作機器之前，必須接受密集訓練。"},{"w":"business operation","p":"phr.","d":"The day-to-day activities, processes, and functions that a company performs to make a profit.","c":"商業營運、企業運作","s":"The global shipping crisis has severely disrupted the normal business operation of many international trading companies.","t":"全球航運危機已嚴重打亂了許多國際貿易公司的正常商業營運（企業運作）。"},{"w":"sensor","p":"n.","d":"a device which detects or measures a physical property and records, indicates, or otherwise responds to it.","c":"感測器","s":"The highly advanced and extremely sensitive motion sensor instantly detected a dangerous intruder sneaking around the dark and quiet office building.","t":"高度先進且極其敏感的動作感測器，立刻偵測到一名危險的入侵者在黑暗安靜的辦公大樓周圍偷偷摸摸。"},{"w":"sensory","p":"adj.","d":"of or relating to sensation or the physical senses; transmitted or perceived by the senses.","c":"感官的","s":"The fascinating interactive children's museum uses bright lights, loud sounds, and completely different textures to provide a deeply engaging sensory experience.","t":"迷人的互動兒童博物館利用明亮的燈光、巨大的聲音和完全不同的紋理來提供深度參與的感官的體驗。"},{"w":"sense","p":"n.","d":"a faculty by which the body perceives an external stimulus; to perceive by a sense.","c":"感覺；感官","s":"Because dogs naturally have a highly acute sense of smell, they can easily locate hidden food from incredibly far away distances.","t":"因為狗天生有極其敏銳的嗅覺感官，牠們可以輕鬆地從極遠的距離找到隱藏的食物。"},{"w":"a keen sense of smell","p":"phr.","d":"A sharp, highly developed, or very good ability to notice or recognize odors and scents.","c":"敏銳的嗅覺","s":"Rescue dogs are chosen for their jobs because they have a keen sense of smell that allows them to track missing people easily.","t":"搜救犬被選中來執行工作是因為牠們擁有敏銳的嗅覺，這讓牠們依循氣味就能輕鬆地追蹤失蹤人員。"},{"w":"sense","p":"v.","d":"To feel, realize, or become aware of something without being told directly.","c":"感覺到、察覺、意識到","s":"Cats can often sense an impending earthquake or weather change long before humans notice anything unusual.","t":"貓通常能在人類注意到任何異常之前很久，就感覺到（察覺）即將發生的地震或天氣變化。"},{"w":"sensible","p":"adj.","d":"Showing good judgment; practical, wise, and reasonable.","c":"明智的、合理的、懂事的","s":"It is a sensible decision to save a portion of your monthly income for emergencies rather than spending it all immediately.","t":"將每月收入的一部分存起來以備不時之需，而不是立刻全部花掉，這是一個明智的決定。"},{"w":"sensitive","p":"adj.","d":"Easily hurt, damaged, or affected by something; or easily offended or upset by what people say.","c":"敏感的、易受影響的","s":"People with sensitive skin need to be careful when choosing skincare products, as certain ingredients can cause redness.","t":"擁有敏感的肌膚的人在選擇保養品時需要格外小心，因為某些成分可能會導致皮膚發紅。"},{"w":"be sensitive to","p":"phr.","d":"To be easily affected by or highly responsive to something (like light, sound, cold, or criticism).","c":"對…敏感、對…敏銳","s":"My teeth are very sensitive to cold food, so I always experience a sharp pain whenever I bite into an ice cream cone.","t":"我的牙齒對冰冷的食物非常敏感，所以每當我咬冰淇淋甜筒時，總會感到一陣銳痛。"},{"w":"potential","p":"n.","d":"latent qualities or abilities that may be developed and lead to future success; having the capacity to develop into something in the future.","c":"潛力；潛在的","s":"Jeremy is a highly ambitious young man completely full of incredible potential who will undoubtedly achieve massive global success someday.","t":"傑瑞米是一個極具野心且完全充滿令人難以置信潛力的年輕人，總有一天無疑會取得巨大的全球成功。"},{"w":"potential","p":"adj.","d":"Possible, or able to develop into something or happen in the future.","c":"潛在的、可能的","s":"The product development team is analyzing potential problems that might arise before they launch the new software next month.","t":"產品開發團隊正在分析下個月推出新軟體前可能出現的潛在問題。"},{"w":"potential customer","p":"phr.","d":"A person who might buy a product or service from a business in the future.","c":"潛在客戶","s":"Giving out free samples at the front door of the bakery is a great way to attract a potential customer who passes by.","t":"在麵包店門口發放免費試用品是吸引路過潛在客戶的好方法。"},{"w":"target audience","p":"phr.","d":"The specific group of people that an advertisement, product, or program is aimed at.","c":"目標客群、目標觀眾","s":"The clothing brand's target audience consists mainly of university students and young adults who love vintage styles.","t":"這個服飾品牌的目標客群（目標觀眾）主要由熱愛復古風格的大學生和年輕人組成。"},{"w":"potential threat","p":"phr.","d":"A person, thing, or situation that is likely to cause harm, danger, or damage in the future.","c":"潛在威脅","s":"Cybersecurity experts warn that using the same password for multiple websites poses a serious potential threat to personal privacy.","t":"網路安全專家警告，在多個網站上使用相同的密碼會對個人隱私構成嚴重的潛在威脅。"},{"w":"potential risk","p":"phr.","d":"A possibility of something bad, dangerous, or harmful happening as a result of an action or decision.","c":"潛在風險","s":"Before investing all his savings into the new business venture, Marcus carefully evaluated every potential risk.","t":"在將所有積蓄投入這項新創事業之前，馬庫斯仔細評估了每一個潛在風險。"},{"w":"potentially","p":"adv.","d":"with the capacity to develop or happen in the future.","c":"潛在地；可能地","s":"The strict doctor warned her that mixing those two strong medicines together could potentially be extremely dangerous for her weak heart.","t":"嚴格的醫生警告她，將這兩種強效藥物混合在一起，可能地（潛在地）對她虛弱的心臟極其危險。"},{"w":"possibility","p":"n.","d":"a thing that may happen or be the case.","c":"可能性","s":"There is a very strong possibility that the rapidly approaching winter storm will heavily delay completely all of the international flights today.","t":"迅速逼近的冬季風暴有非常強烈的可能性會嚴重延誤今天所有國際航班。"},{"w":"miracle","p":"n.","d":"a surprising and welcome event that is not explicable by natural or scientific laws and is considered to be the work of a divine agency.","c":"奇蹟","s":"It is an absolute miracle that you somehow weren't seriously hurt when that massive heavy truck aggressively hit your tiny car.","t":"當那輛巨大的重型卡車猛烈撞擊你微小的汽車時，你不知怎麼的竟然沒有受重傷，這絕對是個奇蹟。"},{"w":"miraculous","p":"adj.","d":"occurring through divine or supernatural intervention, or manifesting such power.","c":"奇蹟般的","s":"Following a deeply terrible and highly destructive car crash, the young woman surprisingly made a completely miraculous recovery in just three weeks.","t":"在經歷了一場極其可怕且具高度破壞性的車禍後，這名年輕女子令人驚訝地在短短三週內取得了完全奇蹟般的康復。"},{"w":"work miracles","p":"phr.","d":"to bring about extremely good results.","c":"創造奇蹟","s":"Many people strongly believe that this specific kind of expensive essential oil can effortlessly work miracles on highly severe sleeping problems.","t":"許多人堅信，這種特定種類的昂貴精油能毫不費力地在極其嚴重的睡眠問題上創造奇蹟。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"trace – unemployment rate","cards":[{"w":"trace","p":"v.","d":"to find or discover by investigation; a mark, object, or other indication of the existence or passing of something.","c":"追蹤","s":"The experienced police detectives worked tirelessly to carefully trace the mysterious email back to the person who originally sent it.","t":"經驗豐富的警探不知疲倦地工作，以仔細地將這封神祕的電子郵件追蹤回最初發送它的人。"},{"w":"trace something's roots","p":"phr.","d":"to find the origin of something.","c":"追溯...的根源","s":"The knowledgeable historians have successfully traced the ancient roots of this fascinating story back to a popular Greek myth.","t":"知識淵博的歷史學家已成功將這個迷人故事的古老根源追溯到一個受歡迎的希臘神話。"},{"w":"trace","p":"v.","d":"To copy a drawing or pattern by drawing over its lines on a transparent sheet.","c":"描摹、照著描","s":"The young art student used a piece of thin paper to trace the beautiful drawing from the ancient textbook so that she could practice her shading techniques.","t":"這位年輕的美術系學生用了一張薄紙來描摹這本古老教科書上的美麗畫作，以便她能練習自己的陰影技巧。"},{"w":"trace","p":"n.","d":"A sign, mark, or object showing that something has existed or happened.","c":"痕跡、蹤跡","s":"The police searched the entire house carefully, but they could not find any trace of the thief who broke into the building last night.","t":"警方仔細搜尋了整棟房子，但他們找不到任何昨晚闖入大樓的竊賊的痕跡（蹤跡）。"},{"w":"follow the trace","p":"phr.","d":"To find or chase someone or something by looking at the marks or signs they left behind.","c":"順著痕跡尋找、追蹤蹤跡","s":"The experienced hunters decided to follow the trace of the wild bear in the snow, hoping to find its hidden cave before sunset.","t":"經驗豐富的獵人們決定在雪地裡順著野熊的痕跡尋找，希望能在日落前找到牠隱蔽的洞穴。"},{"w":"traces of","p":"phr.","d":"marks, objects, or other indications of the existence of something.","c":"...的痕跡","s":"The terrified campers quickly packed their tents after they shockingly found fresh traces of dangerous bear activity in their backyard.","t":"受驚的露營者在令人震驚地發現他們後院有危險熊活動的新鮮痕跡後，迅速收拾了他們的帳篷。"},{"w":"track","p":"v.","d":"To follow the movements or progress of someone or something, especially by using electronics or signs.","c":"追蹤、記錄...的進展","s":"Online shoppers can use the mobile app to track their packages in real time, so they know exactly when the delivery guy will arrive.","t":"線上購物者可以使用手機應用程式即時追蹤他們的包裹，這樣他們就能確切知道送貨員何時會到達。"},{"w":"track","p":"n.","d":"A rough path or road made by people or animals, or a mark left by a wheel or foot.","c":"跑道、小徑、足跡","s":"The athletes lined up on the running track and waited for the starting gun, because they all wanted to win the gold medal this afternoon.","t":"運動員們在跑步跑道上排好隊，等待起跑槍響，裝因為他們今天下午都想贏得金牌。"},{"w":"keep track of","p":"phr.","d":"To continue to know about where someone or something is, or how something is changing.","c":"記錄、掌握...的動態","s":"It is necessary for college students to keep track of their expenses every week, otherwise they might run out of pocket money before the month ends.","t":"大學生每週記錄（掌握）自己的花銷是必要的，否則他們可能會在月底前就把零用錢花光。"},{"w":"railway","p":"n.","d":"A system of tracks on which trains travel, or the organization that operates them.","c":"鐵路、鐵道","s":"The government is building a new high-speed railway to connect the remote mountain villages with the big cities, which will make travel much more convenient.","t":"政府正在建造一條新的高速鐵路，將偏遠的山村與大城市連接起來，這將使交通變得更加便利。"},{"w":"path","p":"n.","d":"A narrow track or way made for walking, or a line along which something moves.","c":"小徑、小路","s":"We followed a narrow path through the thick forest, and it finally led us to a beautiful secret waterfall that few people knew about.","t":"我們沿著一條穿過茂密森林的狹窄小徑前行，它最終引導我們來到了一個很少人知道的美麗秘密瀑布。"},{"w":"idiom","p":"n.","d":"a group of words established by usage as having a meaning not deducible from those of the individual words.","c":"慣用語；成語","s":"\"It's raining cats and dogs\" is a very popular English idiom that is frequently used to say it's raining heavily.","t":"「下傾盆大雨」是一個非常受歡迎的英文慣用語，經常被用來表示雨下得很大。"},{"w":"heel","p":"n.","d":"the back part of the human foot below the ankle.","c":"腳跟；鞋跟","s":"Poor Chloe accidentally cut her right heel on some broken glass that was unfortunately hidden deep in the soft sand.","t":"可憐的克洛伊不小心在不幸隱藏在柔軟沙子深處的一些碎玻璃上割傷了她的右腳跟。"},{"w":"high heels","p":"phr.","d":"women's shoes in which the heels are raised high off the ground.","c":"高跟鞋","s":"Because she isn't used to wearing expensive high heels, Janice's feet hurt terribly after walking around the party all night.","t":"因為她不習慣穿昂貴的高跟鞋，珍妮絲在派對上走了一整晚後腳痛得要命。"},{"w":"fall head over heels for","p":"phr.","d":"To fall deeply and completely in love with someone.","c":"徹底愛上、為...神魂顛倒","s":"Although they only met a few weeks ago at a summer camp, Ethan completely fell head over heels for Olivia because of her kind heart and wonderful sense of humor.","t":"雖然他們幾週前才在夏令營認識，但伊森因為奧莉維亞善良的心和極佳的幽默感而徹底愛上了她。"},{"w":"nowadays","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time, in contrast with the past.","c":"現今；如今","s":"Nowadays, younger people usually spend several continuous hours a day staring at their computers and ignoring their tired family members.","t":"現今，較年輕的人通常每天花連續幾個小時盯著他們的電腦，並忽略了他們疲憊的家人。"},{"w":"recently","p":"adv.","d":"at a recent time; not long ago.","c":"最近","s":"I haven't seen my busy sister recently, as she has been constantly working late nights at the large corporate office.","t":"我最近沒見到我忙碌的妹妹，因為她一直在大型企業辦公室持續深夜加班。"},{"w":"lately","p":"adv.","d":"recently; not long ago.","c":"最近；近來","s":"Has the demanding manager been acting strangely lately, or is he just stressed about the incredibly tight project deadlines?","t":"這位要求嚴格的經理最近表現得奇怪嗎，還是他只是對極其緊迫的專案截止日期感到壓力？"},{"w":"these days","p":"phr.","d":"used to talk about the present time, in comparison with the past.","c":"如今；現在","s":"Finding a cheap and comfortable apartment in the crowded city center is becoming incredibly difficult to do these days.","t":"如今，在擁擠的市中心找到一間便宜且舒適的公寓正變得極其困難。"},{"w":"the latest","p":"phr.","d":"The newest or most recent item, news, or product.","c":"最新的、最近的","s":"Have you read the article about the latest smartphone from that tech company, which features a revolutionary battery that can last for three days?","t":"你讀了關於那家科技公司最新智慧型手機的文章嗎？它配備了能持續使用三天的革命性電池。"},{"w":"the last","p":"phr.","d":"The final one, or the one right before the present moment.","c":"最後的、上一個的","s":"We must hurry to the station because this is the last train leaving for Taipei tonight, or we will have to take an expensive taxi.","t":"我們必須趕快去車站，開往台北的最後一班列車，否則我們就必須搭昂貴的計程車了。"},{"w":"the latter","p":"phr.","d":"The second of two people or things that have just been mentioned.","c":"後者（兩者之中的第二個）","s":"Tina likes both playing the piano and painting, but she spends more time on the latter because she wants to become a professional artist.","t":"蒂娜喜歡彈鋼琴和畫畫，但她花更多時間在後者上，因為她想成為一名專業的藝術家。"},{"w":"enormous","p":"adj.","d":"very large in size, quantity, or extent.","c":"巨大的","s":"As the terrifying winter storm rapidly approached, the quiet beach was heavily buffeted by absolutely enormous and destructive ocean waves.","t":"隨著可怕的冬季風暴迅速逼近，安靜的海灘受到了絕對巨大的且具破壞性的海浪的猛烈衝擊。"},{"w":"grand","p":"adj.","d":"magnificent and imposing in appearance, size, or style.","c":"宏偉的；盛大的","s":"The victorious army officially held a truly grand and colorful parade right through the center of the completely ruined city.","t":"勝利的軍隊正式在徹底毀壞的城市中心舉行了一場真正宏偉的且色彩繽紛的遊行。"},{"w":"tremendous","p":"adj.","d":"very great in amount, scale, or intensity.","c":"極大的；巨大的","s":"The dedicated student successfully put a tremendous amount of effort into his final project and ultimately received the highest grade.","t":"盡責的學生成功地在他期末專案上投入了極大的努力，並最終獲得了最高分。"},{"w":"massive","p":"adj.","d":"Very large, heavy, and solid; huge.","c":"巨大的、大量的","s":"The company suffered a massive loss because their main factory caught fire last week, forcing them to cancel many orders.","t":"該公司上週因主要工廠失火而遭受巨大的損失，迫使他們取消了許多訂單。"},{"w":"magnificent","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely beautiful, impressive, or grand.","c":"壯麗的、宏偉的","s":"When we reached the top of the mountain, we saw a magnificent view of the ocean that made us forget how tired we were.","t":"當我們到達山頂時，我們看到了壯麗的海景，這讓林們忘記了自己有多累。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"Extremely interesting and attractive.","c":"迷人的、引人入勝的","s":"The museum tour guide shared many fascinating stories about ancient Egypt, so all the students listened carefully without getting bored.","t":"博物館導遊分享了許多關於古埃及的迷人故事，所以所有學生都認真聽講，一點也不覺得無聊。"},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"Unusual or surprising in a way that causes people to take notice.","c":"非凡的、值得注意的","s":"Kevin showed a remarkable talent for playing the violin at a young age, and he won his first international competition yesterday.","t":"凱文在年紀還小的時候就展現了非凡的小提琴天賦，並在昨天贏得了他的第一場國際比賽。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"Much better than average; unusual and outstanding.","c":"傑出的、異常優秀的","s":"Because of her exceptional performance during the training program, the manager decided to give Linda a promotion and a higher salary.","t":"由於她在培訓計劃期間傑出的表現，經理決定給琳達升職並加薪。"},{"w":"distinguished","p":"adj.","d":"Successful, authoritative, and commanding great respect.","c":"卓越的、著名的","s":"The university invited a distinguished professor to give a speech about climate change, and the main auditorium was completely packed with students.","t":"這所大學邀請了一位卓越的教授發表關於氣候變遷的演講，主禮堂完全擠滿了學生。"},{"w":"celebrated","p":"adj.","d":"Famous and praised by many people.","c":"著名的、馳名的","s":"This restaurant is a celebrated spot for local seafood, so you usually have to book a table several weeks in advance.","t":"這家餐廳是著名的在地海鮮餐廳，所以你通常必須提前幾週訂位。"},{"w":"noted","p":"adj.","d":"Well-known and respected for a particular quality or ability.","c":"有名的、著名的","s":"Mr. Wang is a noted expert in computer science, and he has written several textbooks that are used all over the country.","t":"王先生是著名的電腦科學專家，他寫了幾本在全國各地使用的教科書。"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"Famous and respected for something specific.","c":"有名的、聲譽卓著的","s":"The French chef is renowned for his delicious desserts, which attract thousands of food lovers to his bakery every single month.","t":"這位法國廚師以其美味的甜點而聞名，這每個月都吸引了數千名美食愛好者光顧他的烘焙坊。"},{"w":"glamorous","p":"adj.","d":"Especially attractive, exciting, and connected with wealth or success.","c":"迷人的、光鮮亮麗的","s":"Many young people think that working in the fashion industry is a glamorous job, but it actually requires a lot of hard work.","t":"許多年輕人認為在時尚界工作是一份光鮮亮麗的工作，但它實際上需要付出很多努力。"},{"w":"lavish","p":"adj.","d":"Large in amount, expensive, and impressive.","c":"奢華的、豪華的","s":"The rich businessman hosted a lavish party at a five-star hotel to celebrate his company's anniversary, inviting hundreds of important guests.","t":"這位富商在一家五星級飯店舉辦了一場奢華的派對來慶祝公司週年，邀請了數百位重要貴賓。"},{"w":"lush","p":"adj.","d":"Growing thickly and strongly; green and healthy.","c":"茂盛的、草木聰蘢的","s":"After raining heavily for several days, the valley became filled with lush green grass and beautiful flowers that attracted many tourists.","t":"連續幾天降下大雨後，山谷裡長滿了茂盛的綠草和美麗的花朵，吸引了許多遊客。"},{"w":"significant","p":"adj.","d":"Large or important enough to have a noticeable effect.","c":"顯著的、重要的","s":"Regular exercise and a balanced diet can make a significant difference to your overall health, so you should start today.","t":"規律運動和均衡飲食能對你的整體健康產生顯著的改變，所以你今天就應該開始。"},{"w":"significantly","p":"adv.","d":"In a way that is large or important enough to be noticed.","c":"顯著地、相當地","s":"The new train system has significantly reduced travel time between the two cities, making it much easier for people to commute.","t":"新的鐵路系統顯著地減少了兩座城市之間的交通時間，使人們通勤變得更加容易。"},{"w":"considerable","p":"adj.","d":"Great in amount, size, or importance.","c":"相當大（多）的","s":"The government spent a considerable amount of money on building the new library, but the local citizens think it was worth it.","t":"政府在建造新圖書館上花費了相當多的資金，但當地市民資源認為這是值得的。"},{"w":"considerably","p":"adv.","d":"Much or a lot; to a large degree.","c":"相當地、非常","s":"The price of vegetables increased considerably after the typhoon hit the island, causing many families to complain about the high costs.","t":"颱風襲擊該島後，蔬菜價格相當地上漲，導致許多家庭抱怨生活成本過高。"},{"w":"rapid","p":"adj.","d":"Happening or moving very quickly.","c":"快速的、迅速的","s":"Thanks to the rapid development of technology, people can now connect with their friends instantly no matter where they live.","t":"多虧了科技的快速發展，現在不論人們住在哪裡，都能立即與朋友取得聯絡。"},{"w":"rapidly","p":"adv.","d":"Very quickly; at a fast rate.","c":"迅速地、很快地","s":"The water level in the river rose rapidly during the heavy storm, so the police advised everyone to stay away from the banks.","t":"暴風雨期間河川水位迅速地上漲，因此警方建議大家遠離河岸。"},{"w":"moderate","p":"adj.","d":"Neither too much nor too little; average in amount or intensity.","c":"適度的、中等的","s":"Doctors recommend that doing a moderate amount of exercise every week can help protect your heart and reduce daily stress.","t":"醫生建議每週進行適度的運動量可以幫助保護心臟並減輕日常壓力。"},{"w":"moderately","p":"adv.","d":"To a medium degree; not excessively.","c":"適度地、普通地","s":"Although the new restaurant is only moderately priced, the food they serve is of high quality and tastes absolutely delicious.","t":"雖然這家新餐廳的價位算適度地（價位中等），但他們供應的食物品質很高且味道絕對美味。"},{"w":"slight","p":"adj.","d":"Small in amount or degree; not noticeably big.","c":"輕微的、微小的","s":"There was a slight delay in the flight schedule due to the bad weather, but all passengers arrived safely at their destination.","t":"由於惡劣的天氣，航班行程出現了輕微的延誤，但所有乘客都安全抵達了目的地。"},{"w":"slightly","p":"adv.","d":"A little bit; to a small degree.","c":"稍微、輕微地","s":"This year's exam was slightly more difficult than last year's, but most students still passed because they studied very hard.","t":"今年的考試比去年的稍微難了一點，但大多數學生因為非常努力複習，所以還是通過了。"},{"w":"outer","p":"adj.","d":"outside; external.","c":"外面的；外部的","s":"The teacher carefully drew two shapes and noted that the outer circle was significantly bigger than the inner circle.","t":"老師仔細地畫了兩個形狀，並指出外面的圓圈明顯比裡面的圓圈大。"},{"w":"inner","p":"adj.","d":"situated inside or further in; internal.","c":"內部的；裡面的","s":"The frightened child nervously hid deep inside the dark and completely silent inner room of the massive abandoned wooden house.","t":"受驚的孩子緊張地躲在巨大廢棄木屋黑暗且完全安靜的裡面的（內部的）房間深處。"},{"w":"outer edge","p":"phr.","d":"the outside boundary or surface of something.","c":"外緣","s":"The brave explorers cautiously walked along the steep outer edge of the dangerous mountain cliff while looking at the sea.","t":"勇敢的探險家小心翼翼地沿著危險山崖陡峭的外緣行走，同時看著大海。"},{"w":"outer surface","p":"phr.","d":"the external layer or outside part.","c":"外表面","s":"The protective outer surface of the advanced spacecraft is completely designed to safely withstand the intense heat during re-entry.","t":"先進太空船具保護性的外表面完全被設計來安全地承受重返大氣層時的強烈高溫。"},{"w":"deceive","p":"v.","d":"to cause someone to believe something that is not true.","c":"欺騙","s":"Sue's unfaithful boyfriend foolishly promised that he would never ever deceive her again, but she simply didn't trust him anymore.","t":"蘇不忠的男友愚蠢地承諾他絕對不會再欺騙她，但她就是不再信任他了。"},{"w":"deceptive","p":"adj.","d":"giving an appearance or impression different from the true one; misleading.","c":"欺騙性的","s":"The highly deceptive advertisement smoothly made the incredibly cheap product seem much more valuable than it actually was in reality.","t":"這個極具欺騙性的廣告順利地讓這個極其便宜的產品看起來比現實中實際上有價值許多。"},{"w":"deception","p":"n.","d":"the action of deceiving someone.","c":"欺騙；騙局","s":"The intelligent detective quickly realized that the criminal's complex story was entirely based on cleverly planned lies and dark deception.","t":"聰明的警探迅速意識到，罪犯複雜的故事完全是基於巧妙計畫的謊言和黑暗的騙局。"},{"w":"trick","p":"v. / n.","d":"a cunning or skillful act or scheme intended to deceive or outwit someone.","c":"欺騙；詭計","s":"I still honestly can't believe that my supposed best friends completely tricked me into coming to this extremely boring party.","t":"我老實說仍然不敢相信我所謂的最好朋友們完全欺騙（拐騙）我來參加這個極其無聊的派對。"},{"w":"trick someone into ving","p":"phr.","d":"To make someone do something by deceiving or lying to them.","c":"誘騙某人做...、騙某人去做某事","s":"The online scammer tried to trick the old man into sending money by pretending to be his long-lost friend on social media.","t":"網路詐騙犯在社群媒體上假裝成老先生失散多年的朋友，試圖誘騙他匯款。"},{"w":"trick","p":"n.","d":"A clever action used to deceive someone, either as a joke or a scam.","c":"把戲、詭計、惡作劇","s":"The magician performed an amazing trick with a deck of cards, and nobody in the audience could figure out how he did it.","t":"這位魔術師用一副撲克牌表演了一個令人驚嘆的把戲，現場觀眾沒有人能弄清楚他是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"play a trick on","p":"phr.","d":"To deceive or cheat someone as a joke or a prank.","c":"捉弄某人、對某人惡作劇","s":"On April Fools' Day, the mischievous students decided to play a trick on their homeroom teacher by hiding her favorite chalk.","t":"在愚人節那天，那些調皮的學生決定藏起班導師最喜歡的粉筆來捉弄她。"},{"w":"naive","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lack of experience, wisdom, or judgment.","c":"天真的；幼稚的","s":"The young and highly naive student completely trusted the friendly stranger who secretly wanted to steal his expensive new smartphone.","t":"年輕且極其天真的學生完全信任了那個暗中想偷他昂貴新智慧型手機的友善陌生人。"},{"w":"act naively","p":"phr.","d":"to behave in a foolishly simple or gullible way.","c":"表現得天真","s":"You simply cannot afford to act so naively when you are formally negotiating such an incredibly important and valuable contract.","t":"當你正式談判如此極其重要且有價值的合約時，你根本承受不起表現得如此天真的後果。"},{"w":"aware","p":"adj.","d":"having knowledge or perception of a situation or fact.","c":"意識到的","s":"The strict principal made absolutely sure that every single student was fully aware of the brand new school safety regulations.","t":"嚴格的校長絕對確保每一位學生都完全意識到了全新的學校安全規定。"},{"w":"be aware of","p":"phr.","d":"Knowing or realizing something; having knowledge or consciousness.","c":"意識到、注意到、知道","s":"Drivers must be aware of the speed limits on the highway, because the police often set up speed cameras to catch reckless drivers.","t":"駕駛人必須注意到高速公路上的速度限制，因為警方經常設置測速照相機來捕捉魯莽的駕駛。"},{"w":"beware","p":"v.","d":"be cautious and alert to the dangers of.","c":"當心；提防","s":"When you cautiously walk in these dark and dense woods, you should always beware of dangerous and highly venomous snakes.","t":"當你在這些黑暗茂密的樹林裡小心翼翼地行走時，你應該總是當心危險且具劇毒的蛇。"},{"w":"beware of","p":"phr.","d":"to be careful of something.","c":"當心...","s":"The bright yellow traffic sign clearly warned the tired drivers to heavily beware of the unexpected sharp curve up ahead.","t":"明亮的黃色交通標誌清楚地警告疲憊的駕駛要高度當心前方出乎意料的急轉彎。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or perception of a situation or fact.","c":"意識；察覺","s":"The massive environmental campaign successfully raised global awareness about the tragic destruction of the beautiful and delicate ancient rainforests.","t":"大型的環保活動成功提升了全球對美麗且脆弱的古老雨林遭到悲慘破壞的意識。"},{"w":"raise the awareness of","p":"phr.","d":"To increase people's knowledge or understanding about an important issue.","c":"提高...的意識、喚起對...的關注","s":"The school decided to host an Earth Day event to raise the awareness of environmental protection among young students.","t":"學校決定舉辦地球日活動，以提高年輕學生對環境保護的意識。"},{"w":"raise the question","p":"phr.","d":"To mention a topic or doubt that needs to be discussed or considered.","c":"提出問題、引發疑問","s":"The sudden change in the company's policy might raise the question of whether the manager plans to cut down the employees' benefits.","t":"公司政策的突然改變可能會引發經理是否計畫削減員工福利的疑問。"},{"w":"raise the issue","p":"phr.","d":"To bring up a problem or topic so that people can talk about it.","c":"提出議題、提出問題（討論）","s":"During the monthly meeting, the sales team decided to raise the issue of declining customer satisfaction over the past quarter.","t":"在月會期間，銷售團隊決定提出過去一季顧客滿意度下降的議題。"},{"w":"raise funds","p":"phr.","d":"To collect money for a specific purpose, especially for a charity or project.","c":"籌措資金、募款","s":"The local charity group organized a charity concert to raise funds for the families who lost their homes in the recent earthquake.","t":"當地的慈善團體舉辦了一場慈善音樂會，為在近期地震中失去家園的家庭籌措資金。"},{"w":"raise children","p":"phr.","d":"To take care of kids and help them grow up until they are adults.","c":"養育小孩、撫養子女","s":"It can be very challenging for working parents to raise children while maintaining a full-time job in a busy city like Taipei.","t":"對於雙薪父母來說，在像台北這樣繁忙的城市裡，一邊維持全職工作一邊養育小孩是非常具有挑戰性的。"},{"w":"raise hands","p":"phr.","d":"To lift hands up in the air to ask a question or show agreement.","c":"舉手","s":"The teacher told the students to raise hands if they knew the answer, but nobody in the classroom volunteered to speak.","t":"老師告訴學生們如果知道答案就舉手，但教室裡沒有人自願發言。"},{"w":"get a raise","p":"phr.","d":"To receive an increase in the amount of money you earn from your job.","c":"加薪、獲得調薪","s":"After working hard and completing several successful projects this year, Sharon finally managed to get a raise from her boss.","t":"在今年努力工作並完成了幾個成功的專案之後，莎倫終於成功從她老闆那裡獲得加薪。"},{"w":"moreover","p":"adv.","d":"as a further matter; besides.","c":"此外；而且","s":"This delicious hot soup is much less expensive than that greasy hamburger; moreover, it is significantly healthier and more nutritious.","t":"這碗美味的熱湯比那個油膩的漢堡便宜得多；而且（此外），它明顯更健康、更有營養。"},{"w":"furthermore","p":"adv.","d":"in addition; besides.","c":"此外；而且","s":"The newly hired employee is highly intelligent and consistently works hard; furthermore, he is incredibly friendly to all his colleagues.","t":"新聘請的員工非常聰明且始終努力工作；此外，他對所有同事都極其友善。"},{"w":"in addition","p":"phr.","d":"as an extra person, thing, or circumstance.","c":"此外","s":"In addition to providing excellent medical benefits, the generous company also surprisingly offers its workers four weeks of paid vacation.","t":"此外（除了...之外）提供極佳的醫療福利，這家慷慨的公司令人驚訝地還為其員工提供四週的帶薪休假。"},{"w":"additionally","p":"adv.","d":"as an extra factor or circumstance.","c":"此外","s":"The luxurious hotel room features a beautifully comfortable bed, and additionally, it has a truly magnificent view of the ocean.","t":"豪華的飯店房間配有漂亮舒適的床，此外，它還擁有真正壯麗的海景。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement reached by each side making concessions; to weaken or harm.","c":"妥協；損害","s":"The strict boss finally compromise, generously giving all the exhausted workers extra paid holidays but absolutely no permanent salary raise.","t":"嚴格的老闆終於妥協了，慷慨地給予所有疲憊的員工額外的帶薪休假，但絕對沒有永久加薪。"},{"w":"reach a compromise","p":"phr.","d":"to come to an agreement where both sides make concessions.","c":"達成妥協","s":"The two extremely stubborn businessmen finally managed to reach a fair compromise after having an incredibly long and stressful meeting.","t":"在經歷了一場極其漫長且充滿壓力的會議後，兩位極度固執的商人終於設法達成了一個公平的妥協。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"v.","d":"to accept standards that are lower than is desirable.","c":"損害；危及","s":"Continuously smoking heavy cigarettes severely compromises your physical health by slowly and permanently damaging your vital heart and lungs.","t":"持續抽濃菸會透過緩慢且永久地破壞你重要的心臟和肺部，嚴重損害你的身體健康。"},{"w":"give and take","p":"phr.","d":"mutual concessions and compromises.","c":"互相讓步；妥協","s":"Any healthy and deeply romantic relationship naturally requires a certain amount of give and take to successfully survive difficult challenges.","t":"任何健康且深刻浪漫的關係自然需要一定程度的互相讓步，才能成功地在困難的挑戰中倖存下來。"},{"w":"defeat","p":"v.","d":"win a victory over someone in a battle or other contest.","c":"擊敗","s":"The skilled blue team successfully defeated the aggressive red team in the highly competitive and incredibly exciting championship football game.","t":"技巧高超的藍隊在競爭高度激烈且極其刺激的美式足球冠軍賽中，成功地擊敗了具攻擊性的紅隊。"},{"w":"defeat","p":"n.","d":"an instance of defeating or being defeated.","c":"失敗；戰敗","s":"The confident players on the national baseball team were deeply upset and crying after their terrible and completely unexpected defeat.","t":"國家棒球隊充滿自信的球員們在經歷了可怕且完全出乎意料的失敗後，感到深深的沮喪並哭了起來。"},{"w":"defeated","p":"adj.","d":"demoralized and overcome by adversity.","c":"覺得挫敗的；被擊敗的","s":"After failing the difficult medical exam for the third time, the exhausted student understandably felt completely defeated and totally hopeless.","t":"在第三次未能通過困難的醫學考試後，疲憊的學生可以理解地感到完全被擊敗的（覺得挫敗的）且完全絕望。"},{"w":"suffer a defeat","p":"phr.","d":"to lose in a battle, contest, or election.","c":"遭受失敗","s":"The powerful military forces unfortunately suffered a devastating defeat during the long and brutally cold winter battle in the mountains.","t":"強大的軍隊在深山中漫長且殘酷寒冷的冬季戰鬥中，不幸地遭受了一場毀滅性的失敗。"},{"w":"tragic","p":"adj.","d":"causing or characterized by extreme distress or sorrow.","c":"悲慘的；悲劇的","s":"The incredibly tragic and heartbreaking love story of Romeo and Juliet is widely known by millions of emotional people worldwide.","t":"羅密歐與茱麗葉極其悲慘的且令人心碎的愛情故事，被全世界數百萬充滿情感的人廣為人知。"},{"w":"tragically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves or causes extreme distress or sorrow.","c":"悲慘地","s":"The brilliant and highly popular young musician tragically died in a terrible car accident when he was only twenty years old.","t":"這位才華洋溢且極受歡迎的年輕音樂家，在他只有二十歲時悲慘地死於一場可怕的車禍。"},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"an event causing great suffering, destruction, and distress.","c":"悲劇；災難","s":"It will certainly be an incredibly long time before the completely destroyed island eventually recovers from the terrifying natural tragedy.","t":"在這座被徹底摧毀的島嶼最終從可怕的自然悲劇（災難）中復原之前，肯定還需要極其漫長的時間。"},{"w":"comic","p":"adj.","d":"causing or meant to cause laughter.","c":"喜劇的；滑稽的","s":"Instead of watching a dark drama, the tired family decided to watch a lighthearted and highly comic movie to relax completely.","t":"疲憊的家庭沒有看黑暗的戲劇，而是決定看一部輕鬆且高度喜劇的電影來徹底放鬆。"},{"w":"comedy","p":"n.","d":"A movie, play, or show that is funny and makes people laugh.","c":"喜劇、喜劇片","s":"We decided to watch a popular comedy at the movie theater last night because we needed a good laugh after a stressful week of final exams.","t":"我們昨天晚上決定去電影院看一部熱門的喜劇，因為在經歷了壓力很大的期末考週之後，我們需要好好大笑一場。"},{"w":"comedian","p":"n.","d":"A person whose job is to entertain people by making them laugh.","c":"喜劇演員、脫口秀演員","s":"The famous comedian told many funny jokes during the live show, which made the entire audience laugh out loud throughout the evening.","t":"那位著名的喜劇演員在現場表演中講了許多搞笑的笑話，這讓全場觀眾整晚都大笑不止。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"a traditional story concerning the early history of a people or explaining some natural or social phenomenon.","c":"神話；迷思","s":"Every ancient culture has its own fascinating traditional myth about how the vast and complex world was originally created miraculously.","t":"每個古老的文化都有其自身迷人的傳統神話，講述廣闊且複雜的世界最初是如何奇蹟般地被創造出來的。"},{"w":"mythical","p":"adj.","d":"occurring in or characteristic of myths or folk tales.","c":"神話的；虛構的","s":"The brave and strong hero heroically fought against an incredibly dangerous and fire-breathing mythical dragon to safely save the beautiful princess.","t":"勇敢強壯的英雄英勇地與一隻極度危險且會噴火的神話的龍戰鬥，以安全地拯救美麗的公主。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"a traditional story sometimes popularly regarded as historical but unauthenticated.","c":"傳說；傳奇人物","s":"According to the famous old legend, courageous Robin Hood cleverly stole money from the rich and generously gave it to the poor.","t":"根據著名古老的傳說，勇敢的羅賓漢聰明地從富人那裡偷錢，並慷慨地把它分給窮人。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"A commonly believed story or idea that is actually false.","c":"迷思、錯誤的看法、神話","s":"Many people still believe the myth that drinking coffee stunts your growth, but scientific studies have proven that this idea is completely wrong.","t":"許多人仍然相信喝咖啡會阻礙發育的迷思，但科學研究已經證明這種觀念是完全錯誤的。"},{"w":"popular myth","p":"phr.","d":"a widely held but false belief or idea.","c":"普遍的迷思","s":"The brilliant scientist wrote a detailed book to carefully debunk the popular myth that eating chocolate constantly causes bad skin.","t":"這位才華洋溢的科學家寫了一本詳細的書，以仔細揭穿不斷吃巧克力會導致皮膚變差的普遍的迷思。"},{"w":"debunk a myth","p":"phr.","d":"To prove that a commonly believed story or idea is false.","c":"揭穿迷思、破除迷思","s":"The doctor wrote an article to debunk a myth about fad diets, explaining that starving yourself is actually very dangerous for your health.","t":"醫生寫了一篇文章來揭穿關於盲目減肥的迷思，並解釋挨餓對你的身體健康實際上是非常危險的。"},{"w":"validate the fact","p":"phr.","d":"To prove or confirm that a statement or piece of information is true.","c":"證實事實、確認事實","s":"Scientists need to conduct multiple experiments to validate the fact before they can publish their new discovery in a famous medical journal.","t":"科學家需要進行多次實驗來證實事實，然後才能將他們的新發現發表在著名的醫學期刊上。"},{"w":"mystery","p":"n.","d":"Something that is difficult or impossible to understand or explain.","c":"謎、神秘的事物","s":"The sudden disappearance of the ancient civilization remains a total mystery, as archaeologists have found very few clues to explain what happened to them.","t":"這個古老文明的突然消失仍然是一個未解之謎，因為考古學家發現了極少能解釋他們究竟發生了什麼事的線索。"},{"w":"mysterious","p":"adj.","d":"Strange, unknown, or difficult to understand or explain.","c":"神秘的、難以理解的","s":"A mysterious package arrived at my house this morning without a return address, so I was afraid to open it until my parents came home.","t":"今天早上一個神秘的包裹寄到了我家，上面沒有寄件人地址，所以我不敢打開它，直到我父母回家。"},{"w":"curiosity","p":"n.","d":"a strong desire to know or learn something.","c":"好奇心；奇特的事物","s":"Most energetic young children naturally possess a lot of intense curiosity about the completely unknown things that physically surround them.","t":"大多數精力充沛的幼童天生對物理上圍繞他們完全未知的事物擁有許多強烈的好奇心。"},{"w":"out of curiosity","p":"phr.","d":"because of a desire to know or learn something.","c":"出於好奇","s":"Merely out of curiosity, the deeply fascinated children carefully opened the large wooden box to see what was hidden inside.","t":"僅僅出於好奇，深深著迷的孩子們仔細地打開了那個大木箱，想看看裡面藏了什麼。"},{"w":"curiosity killed the cat","p":"phr.","d":"being inquisitive about other people's affairs may get you into trouble.","c":"好奇心害死貓","s":"You really shouldn't secretly investigate your demanding boss's highly private financial matters, because you know that curiosity killed the cat.","t":"你真的不應該秘密調查你要求嚴格老闆高度私人的財務問題，因為你知道好奇心害死貓。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"eager to know or learn something.","c":"好奇的","s":"The incredibly curious tourist couldn't stop asking the tired local guide dozens of complex questions about the town's hidden history.","t":"這位極度好奇的遊客忍不住問了疲憊的當地導遊幾十個關於該鎮隱藏歷史的複雜問題。"},{"w":"be curious about","p":"phr.","d":"Wanting to know or learn more about something.","c":"對...感到好奇","s":"Young children are naturally curious about the world around them, so they always ask their parents a lot of questions.","t":"幼小的孩童天生對周遭的世界感到好奇，所以他們總是會問父母許多問題。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"Showing a lot of excitement and interest in something.","c":"熱情的、熱心的","s":"The students were very enthusiastic about the upcoming school trip, and they spent the whole afternoon discussing what to pack.","t":"學生們對即將到來的學校旅行感到非常熱情，他們花了整個下午討論要打包什麼行李。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"A strong feeling of excitement and interest in an activity.","c":"熱情、熱忱","s":"Although the project was difficult, Mary never lost her enthusiasm and she continued to work hard until it was completely finished.","t":"雖然這個專案很困難，但瑪麗從未失去她的熱情，她繼續努力工作直到它完全完成。"},{"w":"passion","p":"n.","d":"A very strong feeling of love, interest, or enthusiasm for an activity.","c":"熱愛、強烈的愛好","s":"David has a true passion for photography, so he spends all his weekends taking beautiful pictures of birds in the local park.","t":"大衛對攝影有著真正的熱愛，所以他把所有的週末都花在當地的公園裡拍攝鳥類的漂亮照片。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"Having or showing strong feelings of enthusiasm or love for something.","c":"熱情的、熱愛的","s":"The young chef is extremely passionate about cooking, and he hopes to open his own Italian restaurant in Taipei next year.","t":"這位年輕的廚師對烹飪極具熱情，他希望明年能在台北開一家屬於自己的義式餐廳。"},{"w":"companion","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal with whom one spends a lot of time or with whom one travels.","c":"同伴；伴侶","s":"The brave medieval hero and his loyal companion had many incredibly dangerous and exciting adventures together while traveling the kingdom.","t":"勇敢的中世紀英雄和他忠誠的同伴在遊歷王國時，一起經歷了許多極其危險且刺激的冒險。"},{"w":"traveling companion","p":"phr.","d":"someone you travel with.","c":"旅伴","s":"I genuinely hope to eventually find a highly reliable and extremely fun traveling companion to comfortably travel through Europe with me next summer.","t":"我真心希望能最終找到一位高度可靠且極其有趣的旅伴，明年夏天能舒服地和我一起去歐洲旅行。"},{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"The state of being with someone so they do not feel lonely.","c":"陪伴、作伴","s":"After her husband passed away, Mrs. Lin adopted a cute little dog because she really needed some company during those long, quiet evenings.","t":"在她丈夫過世後，林太太領養了一隻可愛的小狗，因為在那些漫長而安靜的夜晚，她真的很需要一些陪伴。"},{"w":"keep someone company","p":"phr.","d":"To spend time with someone so that they are not alone.","c":"陪伴某人","s":"Because Sarah was feeling sick and had to stay home alone, her best friend went over to keep her company for the entire afternoon.","t":"因為莎拉覺得不舒服且必須獨自待在家裡，她最好的朋友過去陪伴她度過了一整個下午。"},{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"A business organization that makes money by selling goods or services.","c":"公司","s":"After graduating from university, Jason started working for a famous technology company that develops educational software for high school students across the country.","t":"大學畢業後，傑森開始為一家著名的科技公司工作，該公司為全國的高中生開發教育軟體。"},{"w":"accompany","p":"v.","d":"To go somewhere with someone as a companion or escort.","c":"陪同、陪伴","s":"Children under the age of twelve are not allowed to enter the museum unless an adult can accompany them during the entire visit.","t":"十二歲以下的兒童不允許進入這家博物館，除非有成年人能在整個參觀期間陪同他們。"},{"w":"be accompanied by","p":"phr.","d":"To go together with someone or happen together with something else.","c":"由...陪同、伴隨著...","s":"The president will be accompanied by his wife and several important officials during his official visit to Japan next week.","t":"總統下週正式訪問日本期間，將由他的妻子和幾位重要官員陪同。"},{"w":"colleague","p":"n.","d":"a person with whom one works in a profession or business.","c":"同事","s":"The friendly manager happily invited absolutely all of his hardworking office colleague to a grand dinner to enthusiastically celebrate the massive success.","t":"友善的經理快樂地邀請了他所有辛勤工作的辦公室同事參加一場盛大的晚宴，以熱情地慶祝巨大的成功。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in an undertaking with another or others.","c":"夥伴；合夥人","s":"Wealthy Bruce is currently looking for an experienced and highly trustworthy business partner to help completely fund his brand new startup company.","t":"富有的布魯斯目前正在尋找一位經驗豐富且極度值得信賴的商業夥伴（合夥人），以幫助完全資助他全新的新創公司。"},{"w":"manager","p":"n.","d":"A person who is in charge of a department, business, or team.","c":"經理、主管","s":"The hotel manager apologized to the guests for the loud noise and offered them a free breakfast the next morning.","t":"飯店經理向賓客因巨大的噪音而致歉，並在隔天早上為他們提供免費的早餐。"},{"w":"manage","p":"v.","d":"To be in control of a business, team, organization, or time.","c":"管理、經營","s":"Mr. Lin has to manage a large team of software engineers, so he always arrives at the office early to plan their daily tasks.","t":"林先生必須管理一個由軟體工程師組成的大型團隊，因此他總是提早到達辦公室來規劃他們每日的任務。"},{"w":"manage to v","p":"phr.","d":"To succeed in doing something difficult, especially after trying hard.","c":"設法做到...、成功做到...","s":"Although the project was extremely difficult, the team managed to finish it just a few hours before the strict deadline.","t":"雖然這個專案非常困難，但團隊還是設法在嚴格的截止日期前幾個小時完成了它。"},{"w":"supervise","p":"v.","d":"To watch a person or activity to make sure everything is done correctly and safely.","c":"監督、指導","s":"The science teacher must supervise the students while they are doing chemistry experiments, because some of the liquids can be dangerous.","t":"自然老師在學生做化學實驗時必須監督他們，因為某些液體可能具有危險性。"},{"w":"supervisor","p":"n.","d":"A person who is in charge of a group of people or an area of work.","c":"主管、監工","s":"If you want to take a day off next week, you need to get permission from your supervisor before submitting the application form.","t":"如果你下週想請一天假，你在提交申請表之前需要先得到你主管的允許。"},{"w":"monitor","p":"v.","d":"To check, watch, or test something regularly to see how it progresses.","c":"監測、監控","s":"Doctors use special machines to monitor the patient's heartbeat after the long surgery, ensuring that there are no unexpected problems.","t":"醫生在漫長的手術後使用特殊機器來監測病人的心跳，以確保不會出現意外的問題。"},{"w":"monitor","p":"n.","d":"A screen that shows information or images, or a device used for checking something.","c":"顯示器、螢幕","s":"The graphic designer decided to buy a larger computer monitor because it would help him see the details of his drawings more clearly.","t":"這位平面設計師決定買一個更大的電腦顯示器（螢幕），因為這將能幫助他更清楚地看見他畫作的細節。"},{"w":"employ","p":"v.","d":"To pay someone to work for your company or organization.","c":"雇用","s":"The new international restaurant plans to employ thirty local workers, which will create many great job opportunities for young people in this town.","t":"這家新的國際餐廳計畫雇用三十名當地員工，這將為這個小鎮的年輕人創造許多棒的工作機會。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"A person who is paid to work for someone else or a company.","c":"員工、雇員","s":"Every employee in this company receives a special bonus at the end of the year if the sales targets are successfully achieved.","t":"如果銷售目標成功達成，這家公司的每位員工在年底都會收到一筆特別的獎金。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"A person or organization that pays people to work for them.","c":"雇主、老闆","s":"A good employer should provide a safe working environment and treat all workers fairly, rather than just focusing on making profits.","t":"一位好雇主應該要提供安全的工作環境並公平對待所有勞工，而不是僅僅專注於賺取利潤。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"The state of having a paid job, or the act of employing someone.","c":"就業、工作","s":"It is difficult for university graduates to find stable employment during an economic crisis, so many choose to continue their studies instead.","t":"在經濟危機期間，大學畢業生很難找到穩定的工作（就業機會），因此許多人選擇繼續他們的學業。"},{"w":"employment rate","p":"phr.","d":"The percentage of the working-age population that currently has a paid job.","c":"就業率","s":"The government announced that the employment rate has increased this year because several new factories opened and hired thousands of citizens.","t":"政府宣布今年的就業率有所上升，因為幾家新工廠開業並雇用了數千名市民。"},{"w":"unemployment rate","p":"phr.","d":"The percentage of people in the workforce who do not have a job but are looking for one.","c":"失業率","s":"When the economy is weak, the unemployment rate usually goes up because many businesses are forced to close down or reduce their staff.","t":"當經濟疲軟時，失業率通常會上升，因為許多企業被迫倒閉或縮減員工人數。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"collapse – justice","cards":[{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down or give way suddenly.","c":"倒塌；崩潰","s":"It is incredibly lucky that absolutely no one was driving on the old bridge when it suddenly collapsed.","t":"令人難以置信的幸運是，當那座舊橋突然倒塌時，絕對沒有人在上面開車。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"n.","d":"an instance of a structure falling down or giving way.","c":"倒塌；崩潰","s":"The catastrophic bridge collapse unfortunately claimed the innocent lives of several unsuspecting commuters early this rainy morning.","t":"災難性的橋樑倒塌不幸地在今天這個下雨的清晨奪走了幾位毫無防備的通勤者無辜的生命。"},{"w":"colony collapse disorder","p":"phr.","d":"a phenomenon in which worker bees from a beehive abruptly disappear.","c":"蜂群崩壞症候群","s":"Many dedicated environmental scientists are actively studying colony collapse disorder to understand why the vital bee populations are vanishing.","t":"許多盡責的環境科學家正積極研究蜂群崩壞症候群，以了解為什麼至關重要的蜜蜂群體正在消失。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"To suddenly fall down, cave in, or fail completely due to weakness, damage, or illness.","c":"倒塌、崩潰、暈倒","s":"The old wooden bridge might collapse if too many heavy trucks try to drive over it at the same time.","t":"如果有太多重型卡車同時試圖開過去，這座老舊的木橋可能會倒塌。"},{"w":"the economy collapses","p":"phr.","d":"A situation where a country's financial, banking, and business systems fail completely and suddenly.","c":"經濟崩潰","s":"Financial experts warn that if the government cannot control inflation, the economy collapses, leading to mass unemployment.","t":"金融專家警告，如果政府無法控制通貨膨脹，經濟就會崩潰，進而導致大規模失業。"},{"w":"a building collapses","p":"phr.","d":"A structure suddenly falling down or caving in because of an earthquake, weak foundation, or severe damage.","c":"建築物倒塌","s":"Rescue teams rushed to the downtown area after a building collapsed during the powerful earthquake.","t":"在那次強烈地震中一棟建築物倒塌後，搜救隊迅速趕往市中心區域。"},{"w":"someone collapses","p":"phr.","d":"A person suddenly falling down and often becoming unconscious because they are very sick, exhausted, or weak.","c":"（人）暈倒、不支倒地","s":"The office worker collapsed at her desk due to extreme exhaustion after working for twenty-four hours straight.","t":"那位上班族在連續工作二十四小時後，因極度力竭而在辦公桌前不支倒地（暈倒）。"},{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in or occupy a place or environment.","c":"居住於","s":"Several extremely dangerous and highly venomous snakes are known to actively inhabit this dark and mysterious mountain cave.","t":"幾種極度危險且具劇毒的蛇已知積極居住於這個黑暗神祕的山洞中。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural home or environment of an animal, plant, or other organism.","c":"棲息地","s":"While some highly resilient animals can easily live in dry desert habitat, others desperately need lush forests.","t":"雖然一些適應力極強的動物可以輕鬆地生活在乾燥的沙漠棲息地，但其他動物極度需要茂盛的森林。"},{"w":"natural habitat","p":"phr.","d":"the natural environment in which a species or organism lives.","c":"自然棲息地","s":"Cutting down the ancient trees will completely destroy the natural habitat of many rare and beautiful wild birds.","t":"砍伐這些古老的樹木將徹底摧毀許多稀有且美麗的野鳥的自然棲息地。"},{"w":"habitant","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person or animal that lives in a particular place; a resident or inhabitant.","c":"居民、居住者","s":"The local community center provides free language classes to help every new habitant adapt to the neighborhood.","t":"當地社區中心提供免費的語言課程，以幫助每一位新居民適應這個社區。"},{"w":"habitable","p":"adj.","d":"Suitable, safe, or good enough for people or animals to live in.","c":"適合居住的、可居住的","s":"Due to severe flooding and toxic mold, the ground floor of the apartment building is temporarily not habitable.","t":"由於嚴重的洪水和有毒霉菌，這棟公寓大樓的一樓暫時不適合居住。"},{"w":"inhabitable","p":"adj.","d":"Suitable for living in. (Note: This means the same as \"habitable,\" NOT the opposite).","c":"適合居住的、可居住的（**注意：**字根來自 inhabit，意思與 habitable 相同，並非相反詞）","s":"Environmentalists are working hard to protect the wetlands and keep them inhabitable for rare bird species.","t":"環保人士正努力保護這片濕地，以讓它們維持適合珍稀鳥類居住的狀態。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj.","d":"exceptionally good or great; remarkable.","c":"非凡的；單一的","s":"He is a truly singular musician whose incredibly brilliant classical work is entirely beyond compare in this modern century.","t":"他是一位真正非凡的音樂家，其極其才華洋溢的古典作品在這個現代世紀完全無與倫比。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj. / n.","d":"Relating to a word form that refers to only one person, thing, or concept.","c":"單數的、單數形","s":"The English teacher reminded the class that a singular subject like \"he\" or \"she\" requires a verb with an \"s\" in the present tense.","t":"英文老師提醒全班，像 \"he\" 或 \"she\" 這樣的單數主詞，在現在式中需要搭配字尾加 \"s\" 的動詞。"},{"w":"plural","p":"adj. / n.","d":"Relating to a word form that refers to more than one person, thing, or concept.","c":"複數的、複數形","s":"Most English nouns can be changed into their plural forms simply by adding an \"s\" or \"es\" to the end of the word.","t":"大多數的英文名詞只需在字尾加上 \"s\" 或 \"es\"，就能轉換成它們的複數型態。"},{"w":"except (for)","p":"prep.","d":"Not including someone or something.","c":"除了…之外（不包含）","s":"The amusement park is open every day except for Christmas Day, when it closes for annual maintenance.","t":"這座主題樂園除了聖誕節當天之外每天都開放，聖誕節當天會關閉進行年度維護。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person or thing that is not included in a general statement or does not follow a rule.","c":"例外","s":"Most students in the class passed the difficult exam, with the sole exception of Leo, who missed the test due to illness.","t":"班上大多數學生都通過了這場艱難的考試，唯一的例外是里歐，他因病缺考。"},{"w":"no exception","p":"phr.","d":"Following the same rule or behaving in the same way as everyone or everything else.","c":"也不例外","s":"All new employees must attend the safety training session, and the new managers are no exception.","t":"所有新員工都必須參加安全培訓課程，新任經理們也不例外。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; outstanding.","c":"卓越的；例外的","s":"The strict international company only tolerates employee lateness in highly exceptional circumstances, such as severe weather emergencies.","t":"這家嚴格的國際公司只有在高度例外的情況下（例如嚴重的惡劣天氣緊急情況）才容許員工遲到。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing creativity or inventiveness.","c":"富有想像力的","s":"The highly imaginative young boy creatively made up an incredibly fun and complex new game for all his friends.","t":"這個極其富有想像力的年輕男孩，為他所有的朋友充滿創意地發明了一個極其有趣且複雜的新遊戲。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the faculty or action of forming new ideas, or images or concepts of external objects not present to the senses.","c":"想像力","s":"Reading fantastic adventure novels every night greatly helps young children actively develop their growing intelligence and colorful imagination.","t":"每晚閱讀奇妙的冒險小說，極大地幫助幼童積極發展他們成長中的智力和豐富多彩的想像力。"},{"w":"imaginable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to be conceived or imagined.","c":"可想像得到的","s":"The luxury hotel offers the most incredibly comfortable beds and absolutely every high-end amenity imaginable for its wealthy guests.","t":"這家豪華飯店為其富有的客人提供最極度舒適的床鋪和絕對所有可想像得到的高端設施。"},{"w":"imaginary","p":"adj.","d":"existing only in the imagination.","c":"虛構的；想像中的","s":"The fascinating bedtime story was about a magical and completely imaginary land where clever animals could fluently talk.","t":"這個迷人的床邊故事是關於一個神奇且完全虛構的土地，在那裡聰明的動物可以流利地說話。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"working or produced by machines or machinery.","c":"機械的","s":"The expensive store warranty unfortunately only covers internal mechanical problems, so you must pay for any exterior cosmetic damage.","t":"昂貴的商店保固不幸地只涵蓋內部的機械的問題，所以你必須為任何外部的裝飾性損壞付費。"},{"w":"mechanism","p":"n.","d":"a system of parts working together in a machine.","c":"機械裝置；機制","s":"The complex locking mechanism on the heavy steel safe is specifically designed to completely prevent any dangerous robberies.","t":"沉重鋼製保險箱上複雜的鎖定機械裝置，是專門設計來完全防止任何危險的搶劫。"},{"w":"mechanic","p":"n.","d":"a person who repairs and maintains machinery.","c":"技工","s":"The highly experienced car mechanic skillfully fixed the broken engine in less than two surprisingly short hours.","t":"經驗非常豐富的汽車技工在不到兩個令人驚訝的短暫小時內，巧妙地修好了壞掉的引擎。"},{"w":"equip","p":"v.","d":"to supply with the necessary items for a particular purpose.","c":"裝備；配備","s":"The generous military general made absolutely sure to securely equip each brave soldier with a heavy, reliable gun.","t":"慷慨的將軍絕對確保安全地為每一位勇敢的士兵裝備一把沉重可靠的槍。"},{"w":"be equipped with","p":"phr.","d":"to be provided with a particular feature or equipment.","c":"配備有...","s":"My expensive brand new sports car is fully equipped with a highly advanced GPS device for safe modern navigation.","t":"我昂貴的全新跑車完全配備有一個高度先進的GPS裝置，用於安全的現代導航。"},{"w":"equipment","p":"n.","d":"the necessary items for a particular purpose.","c":"設備；器材","s":"The dedicated hospital recently purchased several million dollars worth of advanced medical equipment to better treat sick patients.","t":"這家盡責的醫院最近購買了價值數百萬美元的先進醫療設備，以更好地治療生病的病患。"},{"w":"wrap up","p":"phr.","d":"to conclude or finish something.","c":"結束；包好","s":"I have to leave in exactly five minutes, so we seriously need to wrap up this boring meeting quickly.","t":"我必須在剛好五分鐘後離開，所以我們真的需要迅速結束這場無聊的會議。"},{"w":"wrapping","p":"n.","d":"paper or soft material used to cover or enclose something.","c":"包裝紙","s":"We urgently need to buy some colorful wrapping paper tonight to beautifully cover the expensive holiday gifts for the children.","t":"我們今晚急需買一些色彩鮮豔的包裝紙，來美麗地包裝給孩子們的昂貴節日禮物。"},{"w":"unwrap","p":"v.","d":"to remove the wrapping from something.","c":"拆開","s":"The excited little boy couldn't wait to happily unwrap his massive birthday present the moment he finally woke up.","t":"興奮的小男孩一醒來就等不及要快樂地拆開他巨大的生日禮物。"},{"w":"secure","p":"v.","d":"to protect against threats; make safe.","c":"使安全；獲得","s":"The brilliant software engineer successfully designed a program that effectively secures the entire office computer system from destructive viruses.","t":"才華洋溢的軟體工程師成功設計了一個程式，有效地使整個辦公室電腦系統安全，免受破壞性病毒的侵害。"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"Safe from danger, attack, or risk; protected against unauthorized access.","c":"安全的、牢固的、無憂的","s":"The online banking app uses advanced encryption to keep your financial transactions secure from hackers.","t":"這款網路銀行應用程式使用進階加密技術，以確保您的財務交易免受駭客攻擊且非常安全。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a fixed or stable manner.","c":"安全地；牢固地","s":"Larry carefully tugged his young daughter's seat belt to perfectly ensure that it was securely fastened before starting the car.","t":"賴瑞仔細地拉了拉他年幼女兒的安全帶，以完美確保在發動汽車前它是牢固地繫好的。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"the state of being free from danger or threat.","c":"安全（保障）；保全","s":"The massive international airport significantly increased its daily security after receiving a highly credible and terrifying anonymous threat.","t":"在收到極具可信度且可怕的匿名威脅後，這座龐大的國際機場顯著增加了其日常安全（保障）。"},{"w":"safe","p":"adj.","d":"Not in danger or likely to be harmed, hurt, or damaged.","c":"安全的、平安的、無危險的","s":"It is not safe to walk alone in the dark alley late at night, so you should call a ride-sharing taxi instead.","t":"深夜獨自走在黑暗的小巷裡是不安全的，所以你應該改叫計程車。"},{"w":"safety","p":"n. [U]","d":"The state of being safe and protected from danger, harm, or injury.","c":"安全、安全性","s":"For your own safety, please stand completely behind the yellow line while waiting for the MRT train to arrive.","t":"為了您自身的安全，在等待捷運列車抵達時，請完全站在黃線後方。"},{"w":"safely","p":"adv.","d":"In a safe way; without being hurt, damaged, or lost.","c":"安全地、平安地","s":"The mountain guide helped all the hikers cross the rocky river safely before the heavy storm started.","t":"在暴風雨開始之前，登山導遊協助所有登山客安全地越過了佈滿岩石的河流。"},{"w":"transport","p":"v.","d":"to take or carry people or goods from one place to another.","c":"運輸","s":"The highly reliable delivery company uses massive trucks to quickly transport valuable goods across the entire vast country.","t":"這家高度可靠的快遞公司使用巨大的卡車，迅速將有價值的貨物運輸穿越整個廣闊的國家。"},{"w":"transportation","p":"n.","d":"the action of transporting someone or something or the process of being transported.","c":"交通工具；運輸","s":"Efficient public transportation is absolutely vital for reducing terrible traffic jams and dangerous pollution in rapidly growing modern cities.","t":"高效率的大眾交通工具對於減少快速發展的現代城市中可怕的交通堵塞和危險的污染絕對是至關重要的。"},{"w":"lose","p":"v.","d":"To no longer have something because you do not know where it is, or to fail to win.","c":"遺失、失去、輸掉","s":"If you lose your passport while traveling abroad, you must contact your country's embassy immediately to get a new one.","t":"如果你在國外旅行時遺失了護照，你必須立刻聯絡你國家的大使館以取得新護照。"},{"w":"lost","p":"adj.","d":"Unable to be found, or not knowing where you are and how to get to your destination.","c":"遺失的、迷路的","s":"The police officer helped the crying little boy find his parents after he wandered away and became lost in the crowded night market.","t":"警察在那個哭泣的小男孩走失並在擁擠的夜市裡迷路的時候，幫助他找到了父母。"},{"w":"get lost","p":"phr.","d":"To not know where you are and be unable to find your way.","c":"迷路","s":"Make sure to download an offline map on your smartphone so you don't get lost while hiking in the remote mountains.","t":"確保在你的智慧型手機上下載離線地圖，這樣你在偏遠山區健行時才不會迷路。"},{"w":"lost","p":"adj.","d":"Feeling very confused, insecure, or not knowing what to do with your life.","c":"感到失落的、迷惘的、不知所措的","s":"After graduating from college, Chloe felt completely lost because she had no idea what kind of career she wanted to pursue.","t":"大學畢業後，克洛伊感到非常迷惘（失落的），因為她完全不知道自己想追求什麼樣的職業。"},{"w":"loose","p":"adj.","d":"not firmly or tightly fixed in place; detached or able to be detached.","c":"鬆的；寬鬆的","s":"If your new designer pants are much too loose around the waist, you should definitely wear a heavy leather belt.","t":"如果你新的設計師長褲在腰部太鬆的，你絕對應該繫一條厚重的皮帶。"},{"w":"on the loose","p":"phr.","d":"having escaped from confinement; at large.","c":"在逃","s":"The terrified town is panicking because an incredibly dangerous criminal attacked several people last night and is still on the loose.","t":"受驚的城鎮陷入恐慌，因為一名極度危險的罪犯昨晚攻擊了幾個人，而且目前仍然在逃。"},{"w":"break loose","p":"phr.","d":"to escape from physical restraint.","c":"掙脫","s":"The whole neighborhood is hiding inside because the aggressive lion at the local zoo has violently broken loose from its cage.","t":"整個社區都躲在室內，因為當地動物園具攻擊性的獅子猛烈地從籠子裡掙脫了。"},{"w":"portion","p":"n.","d":"a part of a whole; an amount, section, or piece of something.","c":"部分；一份","s":"Each hardworking team member fairly received a massive portion of the exciting prize money after finally winning the competitive tournament.","t":"每位辛勤工作的團隊成員在終於贏得競爭激烈的錦標賽後，公平地獲得了令人興奮的獎金的巨大一部分。"},{"w":"proportion","p":"n.","d":"a part, share, or number considered in comparative relation to a whole.","c":"比例","s":"A significantly large proportion of the young students in this high school actively plan to attend a prestigious university.","t":"這所高中裡有相當大比例的年輕學生積極計畫進入著名的大學就讀。"},{"w":"proportionate","p":"adj.","d":"Increasing or decreasing in size, amount, or degree according to something else; proportional.","c":"成比例的、相稱的","s":"The judge stated that the legal punishment must be proportionate to the seriousness of the crime committed.","t":"法官表示，法律懲罰必須與所犯親罪行的嚴重程度相稱（成比例）。"},{"w":"disproportionate","p":"adj.","d":"Too large or too small in comparison with something else.","c":"不成比例的、不相稱的","s":"A disproportionate amount of the company's budget is spent on advertising rather than improving product quality.","t":"公司不成比例的預算金額被花在廣告上，而不是提高產品品質。"},{"w":"spill","p":"v.","d":"to cause or allow liquid to flow over the edge of its container.","c":"灑出","s":"The clumsy child accidentally spilled his cold milk all over the expensive table and immediately began to cry loudly.","t":"笨拙的孩子不小心把他的冷牛奶灑出在昂貴的桌子上，立刻開始大聲哭泣。"},{"w":"spilled","p":"adj. / v.","d":"(Of a liquid) accidentally poured or flowed out from a container onto a surface.","c":"潑灑出來的、流出的","s":"Marcus used a paper towel to clean up the spilled coffee on his desk before it ruined his important reports.","t":"馬庫斯在潑灑出來的咖啡弄壞他的重要報告之前，用一張紙巾將其清理乾淨。"},{"w":"count on","p":"phr. v.","d":"To trust or rely on someone to do something, or to expect something to happen with certainty.","c":"指望、依靠、信賴","s":"You can always count on Chloe to help you move into your new apartment because she is a very loyal friend.","t":"你總是能指望（信賴）克洛伊來幫你搬進新公寓，因為她是一個非常講義氣的朋友。"},{"w":"rely on","p":"phr. v.","d":"To need or depend on someone or something completely in order to live, work, or succeed.","c":"依靠、依賴、信賴","s":"Many senior citizens rely on public transportation to go to the hospital because they can no longer drive safely.","t":"許多銀髮族依靠（依賴）大眾運輸前往醫院，因為他們已經無法安全地開車了。"},{"w":"depend on","p":"phr. v.","d":"To be decided or influenced by something else, or to rely on someone for support.","c":"取決於、依靠、依賴","s":"Whether the school will host the outdoor sports day this Saturday will depend on the weather condition.","t":"學校這週六是否會舉辦戶外運動會，將取決於天氣狀況。"},{"w":"dependent on","p":"phr.","d":"Needing someone or something else for financial support, survival, or success.","c":"依賴…的、仰賴…的","s":"Young children are entirely dependent on their parents for food, clothing, and a safe place to live.","t":"年幼的孩童在食物、衣物和安全的住所方面完全依賴他們的父母。"},{"w":"independent from","p":"phr.","d":"Free from the control, influence, or financial support of another person, organization, or country.","c":"獨立於…的、不受…控制的","s":"After years of hard work, Leo finally became financially independent from his parents and rented his own studio.","t":"經過多年的努力，里歐終於在財務上從父母那裡獨立出來，並租了自己的套房。"},{"w":"dependable","p":"adj.","d":"trustworthy and reliable.","c":"可靠的","s":"Carl is consistently one of the large company's most dependable employees because he absolutely never misses a strict deadline.","t":"卡爾始終是這家大公司最可靠的員工之一，因為他絕對不會錯過嚴格的截止日期。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"Able to be trusted to do what is expected or to work properly without failing.","c":"可靠的、可信賴的","s":"This old Japanese car is incredibly reliable; it has never broken down once during the past ten years.","t":"這輛舊的日本車非常可靠（可信賴）；在過去的十年間，它從未故障過一次。"},{"w":"carrier","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that carries, holds, or conveys something.","c":"運送者；航空公司","s":"The exhausted old woman politely requested that a helpful baggage carrier assist her to her luxurious hotel room upstairs.","t":"疲憊的老婦人禮貌地要求一位樂於助人的行李搬運工協助她前往樓上豪華的飯店房間。"},{"w":"accurately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is correct in all details; exactly.","c":"準確地","s":"The frightened woman accurately described the tall, dangerous man who suddenly stole her expensive purse right outside the busy bank.","t":"受驚的婦女準確地描述了那個在繁忙銀行外突然偷走她昂貴錢包的高大危險男子。"},{"w":"accuracy","p":"n.","d":"the quality or state of being correct or precise.","c":"準確性","s":"In highly complex financial reports, absolute accuracy is undeniably the most important factor for any successful international business.","t":"在高度複雜的財務報告中，絕對的準確性無疑是任何成功國際企業最重要的因素。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save from a dangerous or distressing situation.","c":"救援","s":"The incredibly brave firefighters in the hovering helicopter successfully rescued the terrified man from the violently burning wooden house.","t":"盤旋直升機上極其勇敢的消防員，成功地將驚恐的男子從猛烈燃燒的木屋中救援出來。"},{"w":"come to one's rescue","p":"phr.","d":"to help someone out of a bad situation.","c":"來救援某人","s":"Gary heroically came to my rescue when I foolishly locked myself out of my apartment in the freezing winter rain.","t":"當我愚蠢地在冰冷的冬雨中把自己鎖在公寓外時，蓋瑞英勇地來救援我。"},{"w":"artificial","p":"adj.","d":"made or produced by human beings rather than occurring naturally.","c":"人造的","s":"Tony's resilient father surprisingly has an artificial leg because he tragically lost his real one in a terrible car accident.","t":"東尼堅強的父親令人驚訝地裝有一條人造的腿，因為他在一場可怕的車禍中悲慘地失去了他真正的腿。"},{"w":"artificial intelligence","p":"n. [U]","d":"The simulation of human intelligence by computers or machines, enabling them to learn and solve problems.","c":"人工智慧 (AI)","s":"Many tech companies are investing billions of dollars in artificial intelligence to develop smarter software that can write essays and generate images.","t":"許多科技公司正投入數十億美元於人工智慧，以開發出能寫文章和生成圖片的更智慧軟體。"},{"w":"artificial additive","p":"n. [C]","d":"A synthetic substance added to food to improve its flavor, appearance, or to keep it fresh longer.","c":"人工添加物","s":"To maintain a healthy diet, you should avoid highly processed snacks that contain any artificial additive like chemical preservatives.","t":"為了維持健康的飲食，你應該避免食用含有化學防腐劑等任何人工添加物的高度加工零食。"},{"w":"artificial coloring","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"A synthetic substance added to food or drink to change its color or make it look more bright and attractive.","c":"人工色素","s":"The bright red candy gets its intense hue from artificial coloring rather than real strawberry juice.","t":"這款鮮紅色的糖果其強烈的色調是來自於人工色素，而不是真正的草莓汁。"},{"w":"chemical","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to chemistry, or resulting from the interaction of substances.","c":"化學的","s":"The factory was fined for releasing dangerous chemical waste into the nearby river, harming local wildlife.","t":"該工廠因將危險的化學廢料排入附近河流、危害當地野生動物而被處以罰款。"},{"w":"chemical","p":"n. [C]","d":"A distinct substance that is produced by or used in a chemical process.","c":"化學物質、化學製品","s":"You should wear protective gloves and goggles when handling a strong chemical like bleach or acid.","t":"在處理漂白水或酸液等強烈化學物質時，你應該配戴防護手套和護目鏡。"},{"w":"natural","p":"adj.","d":"Existing in or caused by nature; not made, artificial, or caused by humankind.","c":"天然的、大自然的","s":"This organic juice is made from 100% natural ingredients with no extra sugar or water added.","t":"這款有機果汁是由百分之百的天然成分製成，沒有添加額外的糖或水。"},{"w":"replace ... with","p":"v. phr.","d":"To put a new person or thing in the place of an old or broken one.","c":"用…取代/替換…","s":"The chef decided to replace the white sugar with natural honey to make the dessert much healthier.","t":"主廚決定用天然蜂蜜取代（替換）白糖，讓這道甜點更健康。"},{"w":"replacement","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of replacing someone or something.","c":"替代品；替換","s":"There is a convenient shop around here that constantly sells highly affordable replacement parts for completely broken racing bicycles.","t":"這附近有一家便利的商店，經常為完全損壞的賽車腳踏車出售非常負擔得起的替代零件。"},{"w":"substitute for","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be used or to act instead of another person or thing.","c":"代替、取代","s":"Margarine can substitute for butter in most baking recipes, though the final flavor might change slightly.","t":"在大多數烘焙食譜中，乳瑪琳可以代替（取代）奶油，儘管最終的風味可能會稍微改變。"},{"w":"substitute","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person or thing that is used or takes the place of another.","c":"替代品、代替者","s":"Meat substitutes made from plant protein have become incredibly popular among people who prefer vegetarian diets.","t":"由植物蛋白製成的肉類替代品在偏好素食的人群中變得非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"substitute teacher","p":"n. [C]","d":"A teacher who temporarily takes the place of a regular teacher who is absent or ill.","c":"代課老師","s":"When our regular English teacher was away on sick leave, a substitute teacher took over the class for the week.","t":"當我們原本的英文老師請病假時，一位代課老師接管了那一週的班級。"},{"w":"morally","p":"adv.","d":"with reference to the principles of right and wrong behavior.","c":"道德上","s":"The strict teacher carefully explained that it is morally wrong to maliciously spread false rumors about other innocent people.","t":"嚴格的老師仔細地解釋說，惡意散布關於其他無辜者的虛假謠言在道德上是錯誤的。"},{"w":"morality","p":"n.","d":"principles concerning the distinction between right and wrong or good and bad behavior.","c":"道德","s":"The fascinating philosophy class challenged the young students to deeply question the complex morality of highly controversial scientific decisions.","t":"這門引人入勝的哲學課挑戰年輕學生，去深入質疑極具爭議的科學決策中複雜的道德。"},{"w":"moral standard","p":"n. [C, usually plural]","d":"The principles or rules regarding what a society believes to be right and wrong behavior.","c":"道德標準","s":"Different cultures may have varying views on what constitutes a high moral standard regarding family obligations.","t":"不同的文化對於在家庭義務上何謂高道德標準可能會有不同的看法。"},{"w":"immoral","p":"adj.","d":"Morally wrong; not conforming to accepted standards of right behavior.","c":"不道德的","s":"Many people believe that cheating on an exam or lying to your friends is completely immoral.","t":"許多人認為考試作弊或對朋友撒謊是完全不道德的。"},{"w":"mortal","p":"adj. / n. [C]","d":"Unable to live forever; human and bound to die eventually; or causing death.","c":"凡人的、不能永生的、致命的；凡人","s":"In ancient Greek myths, Zeus was an all-powerful god, while the heroes he interacted with were mere mortal beings.","t":"在古希臘神話中，宙斯是一位全能的神，而與他互動的英雄們僅僅是不能永生（凡人）的存在。"},{"w":"immortal","p":"adj. / n. [C]","d":"Living forever; never dying or decaying; famous for all time.","c":"長生不老的、永生的、不朽的","s":"Vampires are often portrayed in modern movies as immortal creatures that never age or die of sickness.","t":"吸血鬼在現代電影中經常被描繪成不會變老也不會因病死亡的長生不老（永生）生物。"},{"w":"mortality","p":"n. [U]","d":"The state of being subject to death, or the condition of being human and unable to live forever.","c":"生命的有限性、必死性、死亡率","s":"Facing a serious illness often forces individuals to think about their own mortality and what matters most in life.","t":"面對嚴重的疾病往往會迫使個人去思考自己生命的有限性（必死性）以及生命中什麼才是最重要的。"},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"To agree to take something that is offered, or to say yes to an invitation, offer, or idea.","c":"接受、答應、認可","s":"It took Chloe several days to decide whether to accept the challenging job offer from the international firm.","t":"克洛伊花了幾天的時間才決定是否要接受那家國際公司極具挑戰性的工作邀約。"},{"w":"acceptance","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The act of accepting something, or the state of being approved, welcomed, or received into a group.","c":"接受、贊同、認可/接納","s":"After months of rigorous testing, the new mobile application finally gained widespread acceptance among users.","t":"經過數月的嚴格測試，這款新的手機應用程式終於在使用者之間獲得了廣泛的認可（接受）。"},{"w":"acceptable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be agreed on; suitable.","c":"可接受的","s":"In the distant past, it simply wasn't socially acceptable for professional women to wear incredibly short skirts in the workplace.","t":"在遙遠的過去，職業女性在工作場所穿極短的裙子在社會上根本是不可接受的。"},{"w":"unacceptable","p":"adj.","d":"not satisfactory or allowable.","c":"不可接受的","s":"Arriving over an hour late to a highly important business interview is completely unacceptable and will certainly cost you the job.","t":"參加極其重要的商業面試遲到超過一小時是完全不可接受的，且肯定會讓你失去這份工作。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"Including many different types of people and treating them all fairly and equally.","c":"具包容性的、包羅萬象的","s":"The company is deeply committed to building an inclusive workplace that values diversity and respects everyone.","t":"該公司致力於打造一個重視多元化並尊重每個人的具包容性的職場。"},{"w":"inclusive of","p":"phr.","d":"Including a specific item, expense, or person as part of a total package or amount.","c":"包含…在內的","s":"The monthly apartment rent is fully inclusive of water bills, electricity, and high-speed internet access.","t":"每月的公寓租金已完全包含水費、電費和高速網路費在內。"},{"w":"inclusion","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of including someone or something in a group, list, system, or activity.","c":"納入、包含、包容","s":"The community celebrated the inclusion of a new modern playground in the downtown public park plan.","t":"社區居民慶祝將一座新的現代化遊樂場納入市中心公共公園的計劃中。"},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"Limited to only one specific person, group, or area; not shared with others; or high-priced.","c":"獨有的、專屬的、排他的","s":"The television station successfully secured an exclusive interview with the famous Hollywood director.","t":"電視台成功取得了與那位著名好萊塢導演的獨家（專屬）專訪。"},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"the action of explaining the meaning of something.","c":"解釋；詮釋","s":"I am really not entirely sure if I completely agree with your unique interpretation of the complex movie's main character.","t":"我真的不完全確定我是否完全同意你對這部複雜電影主角的獨特詮釋。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person who interprets, especially one who translates speech orally.","c":"口譯員","s":"The talented professional interpreter flawlessly translated the foreign president's rapid speech for the massive audience watching completely live on television.","t":"才華洋溢的專業口譯員，完美無瑕地為完全在電視上觀看直播的廣大觀眾翻譯了外國總統快速的演講。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"To change spoken words from one language into another as someone is speaking.","c":"口譯","s":"Since the foreign ambassador did not speak Japanese, Chloe was hired to interpret for him during the official press conference.","t":"由於外國大使不會說日語，克洛伊被雇用在官方記者會期間為他進行口譯。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"To explain or decide the meaning of something, such as a work of art, a law, or a dream.","c":"解釋、詮釋","s":"Different critics may interpret the abstract painting in various ways, finding hidden messages that others miss.","t":"不同的評論家可能會以各種方式詮釋（解釋）這幅抽象畫，發現其他人忽略的隱含訊息。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person whose job is to translate spoken words from one language to another.","c":"口譯員","s":"Working as a conference interpreter requires not only excellent language skills but also the ability to think quickly under pressure.","t":"擔任會議口譯員不僅需要出色的語言能力，還需要具備在壓力下快速思考的能力。"},{"w":"translate ... into","p":"v. phr.","d":"To change writing or speech from one language into another language.","c":"把…翻譯成…","s":"It took the software engineers several months to translate the entire user manual into Spanish and German.","t":"軟體工程師們花了幾個月的時間才把整本使用手冊翻譯成西班牙文和德文。"},{"w":"translation","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The process of changing text or speech into another language, or the translated version of a text.","c":"翻譯、譯文、譯本","s":"The classic British novel has been published in translation in over fifty different countries around the world.","t":"這部經典的英國小說已經在世界上五十多個不同的國家出版了翻譯（譯本）。"},{"w":"offense","p":"n.","d":"annoyance or resentment brought about by a perceived insult to or disregard for oneself.","c":"冒犯；罪過","s":"She truly didn't mean to cause any offense, but her incredibly blunt words were always deeply upsetting sensitive people around her.","t":"她真的無意造成任何冒犯，但她極其直率的言詞總是深深激怒周圍敏感的人。"},{"w":"offensive","p":"adj.","d":"causing someone to feel deeply hurt, upset, or angry.","c":"冒犯的","s":"The extremely inappropriate and offensive joke that the foolish comedian told completely ruined the pleasant atmosphere of the formal dinner.","t":"那位愚蠢的喜劇演員說的極度不適當且冒犯的笑話，徹底毀了正式晚宴愉快的氣氛。"},{"w":"offend","p":"v.","d":"To make someone feel upset, angry, or insulted by doing or saying something rude.","c":"冒犯、得罪","s":"I really didn't mean to offend Marcus with my joke; I was just trying to be funny, but it hurt his feelings.","t":"我真的不是故意要用我的笑話冒犯（得罪）馬庫斯的；我只是想幽默一下，但卻傷到了他的感情。"},{"w":"offensive","p":"adj.","d":"Rude, insulting, or causing someone to feel deeply upset, angry, or displeased.","c":"冒犯的、無禮的、令人不快的","s":"The company immediately removed the controversial advertisement because many viewers found it highly offensive.","t":"該公司立刻撤下了這則具爭議性的廣告，因為許多觀眾覺得它非常具有冒犯性（無禮的）。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"To protect someone or something from physical attack, harm, danger, or strong criticism.","c":"防禦、保衛、為…辯護","s":"The brave soldiers fought hard to defend their country against the invading forces during the war.","t":"戰爭期間，勇敢的士兵們努力戰鬥以保衛（防禦）他們的國家免受入侵部隊的侵害。"},{"w":"defense","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"The act of protecting someone or something from attack, or the system used to protect.","c":"防禦、防衛、防守","s":"Vitamin C plays an important role in strengthening the body's natural defense against common colds.","t":"維他命 C 在增強身體對抗普通感冒的天然防禦能力中扮演著重要角色。"},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"Used or intended to protect against attack; or behaving in a way that shows you feel criticized or protective.","c":"防衛的、防守的、有戒心的","s":"When the manager asked Chloe about the project's delay, she became defensive and started blaming her teammates.","t":"當經理詢問克洛伊關於專案延誤的事時，她變得非常有戒心（採取防衛姿態）並開始指責她的隊友。"},{"w":"coarse","p":"adj.","d":"rough or loose in texture or grain; rude or vulgar.","c":"粗糙的；粗俗的","s":"The unruly students were severely punished by the strict principal for their completely coarse behavior in the quiet school classroom.","t":"不守規矩的學生因為在安靜的學校教室裡完全粗俗的行為，受到了嚴格校長的嚴厲懲罰。"},{"w":"coarsely","p":"adv.","d":"in a rough or harsh manner.","c":"粗糙地","s":"The hardworking chef quickly and coarsely chopped the fresh organic vegetables before heavily throwing them into the boiling hot soup.","t":"辛勤工作的廚師迅速且粗糙地切碎新鮮的有機蔬菜，然後重重地將它們扔進沸騰的熱湯中。"},{"w":"political","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the government or the public affairs of a country.","c":"政治的","s":"The confident president clearly clarified his strong position on complex political reform during his highly anticipated live televised speech.","t":"充滿自信的總統在備受期待的電視直播演講中，清楚闡明了他在複雜政治的改革上的堅定立場。"},{"w":"politician","p":"n.","d":"a person who is professionally involved in politics.","c":"政治人物","s":"The incredibly charismatic young politician successfully convinced thousands of energetic local voters to strongly support his brilliant new campaign.","t":"這位極具魅力的年輕政治人物成功說服了數千名充滿活力的當地選民強烈支持他出色的新競選活動。"},{"w":"politics","p":"n. [U]","d":"The activities, actions, and policies used to gain and hold power in a government or to influence a country.","c":"政治、政治學","s":"Marcus decided to study politics at university because he wanted to understand how laws and governments affect society.","t":"馬庫斯決定在大學學習政治（政治學），因為他想了解法律和政府是如何影響社會的。"},{"w":"political","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to the government, politics, or public affairs of a country.","c":"政治的","s":"The two major political parties held a series of public debates to discuss the new economic reforms before the election.","t":"這兩個主要的政治政黨在選舉前舉行了一系列的公開辯論，以討論新的經濟改革。"},{"w":"politician","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person who is professionally involved in politics, especially as an elected official or candidate.","c":"政治人物、政客","s":"Every politician must listen carefully to the needs of the local citizens in order to win their votes during the upcoming election.","t":"每位政治人物（政客）都必須仔細傾聽當地公民的需求，以便在即將到來的選舉中贏得他們的選票。"},{"w":"political figure","p":"phr.","d":"A well-known and influential person who plays a significant or prominent role in politics or government affairs.","c":"政治要員、重要政治人物","s":"The president is a prominent political figure who represents the nation both domestically and at international summits.","t":"總統是一位著名的重要政治人物（政治要員），在國內及國際峰會上都代表著國家。"},{"w":"physically-challenged","p":"adj.","d":"Having a physical condition that makes it difficult to move or do everyday activities easily.","c":"肢體障礙的、身體有障礙的","s":"The new museum installed modern ramps and wide elevators to ensure that physically-challenged-physically-challenged visitors can access every exhibition floor.","t":"這座新博物館安裝了現代化的坡道和寬敞的電梯，以確保肢體障礙的（身體有障礙的）訪客可以到達每個展覽樓層。"},{"w":"disabled","p":"adj.","d":"Having a physical or mental condition that limits a person's movements, senses, or activities.","c":"有身心障礙的、殘疾的","s":"The government provides special parking spaces near the entrance of public buildings for disabled citizens with valid permits.","t":"政府在公共建築物入口附近為持有有效許可證的有身心障礙的（殘疾的）公民提供專用停車位。"},{"w":"handicapped","p":"adj.","d":"having a physical or mental disability.","c":"有生理缺陷的；殘疾的","s":"Andy is thoughtfully installing a smooth concrete ramp so that handicapped customers can easily and safely access his new shop.","t":"安迪正體貼地安裝一個平滑的混凝土坡道，以便殘疾的（有生理缺陷的）顧客能輕鬆安全地進入他的新商店。"},{"w":"aspect","p":"n.","d":"a particular part or feature of something.","c":"方面","s":"Clearly communicating with angry customers is undoubtedly an incredibly important aspect of a successful retail salesperson's difficult daily job.","t":"與憤怒的顧客清晰溝通，無疑是成功的零售業務員艱難日常工作中一個極其重要的方面。"},{"w":"in many aspects","p":"phr.","d":"In many ways, features, or parts of a situation, plan, or subject.","c":"在許多方面","s":"Although the two smartphones look very similar from the outside, they are completely different in many aspects when it comes to performance.","t":"雖然這兩款智慧型手機從外觀上看起來非常相似，但在效能方面，它們在許多方面都完全不同。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A particular way of thinking about or considering something; a viewpoint or angle.","c":"觀點、看法、視角","s":"Traveling alone in a foreign country for a year helped Marcus gain a completely new perspective on life and career choices.","t":"隻身在外國旅行一年幫助馬庫斯獲得了對生活和職業選擇的全新觀點（看法）。"},{"w":"as far as i am concerned","p":"phr.","d":"Used to introduce your personal opinion, belief, or feelings about a particular topic.","c":"就我而言、在我看來","s":"As far as I am concerned, the new company policy about working from home is the best decision the management has made this year.","t":"就我而言（在我看來），公司關於居家辦公的新政策是管理階層今年做出的最佳決定。"},{"w":"in my opinion","p":"phr.","d":"Used to express what you personally think or believe about a specific matter.","c":"依我之見、在我看來","s":"In my opinion, learning how to manage your time effectively is far more important than just memorizing facts for a test.","t":"依我之見（在我看來），學習如何有效管理時間遠比只為考試死記硬背知識重要得多。"},{"w":"nasty","p":"adj.","d":"highly unpleasant, especially to the senses; physically repugnant.","c":"令人作嘔的；惡劣的","s":"Veronica's highly nasty and arrogant attitude usually made her incredibly patient teacher feel quite upset and deeply frustrated everyday.","t":"維羅妮卡高度惡劣的且傲慢的態度，通常讓她極具耐心的老師每天都感到相當難過和深深的挫折。"},{"w":"mock","p":"v.","d":"to tease or laugh at in a scornful or contemptuous manner.","c":"嘲笑","s":"Jan's cruel classmates maliciously mocked her brand new hairstyle, loudly saying that it looked incredibly strange and completely silly.","t":"珍殘酷的同學惡意地嘲笑她全新的髮型，大聲說它看起來極其奇怪且完全愚蠢。"},{"w":"mockery","p":"n.","d":"teasing and contemptuous language or behavior directed at a particular person or thing.","c":"嘲笑","s":"The arrogant manager made an absolute mockery of the junior employee's brilliant presentation, making everyone in the room incredibly uncomfortable.","t":"傲慢的經理對初階員工出色的簡報進行了絕對的嘲笑，讓房間裡的每個人都極度不舒服。"},{"w":"racial","p":"adj.","d":"of or relating to race.","c":"種族的","s":"The progressive new government officially guaranteed absolute racial equality for all diverse citizens living in the massive modern country.","t":"進步的新政府正式保證，為生活在這個龐大現代國家中所有多元公民提供絕對的種族的平等。"},{"w":"racial discrimination","p":"phr.","d":"prejudice, discrimination, or antagonism directed against someone of a different race.","c":"種族歧視","s":"The historic passage of the famous Civil Rights Act in 1964 officially made cruel racial discrimination completely illegal in the US.","t":"1964年著名民權法案的歷史性通過，正式使殘酷的種族歧視在美國完全非法。"},{"w":"insult","p":"n.","d":"a disrespectful or scornfully abusive remark or action.","c":"侮辱","s":"Sam is highly sensitive and often mistakenly takes people's constructive feedback as a deeply personal and incredibly cruel insult.","t":"山姆高度敏感，經常錯誤地將人們建設性的回饋當作深深的個人且極其殘酷的侮辱。"},{"w":"insulting","p":"adj.","d":"Rude, offensive, or disrespectful, and likely to deeply upset or anger someone.","c":"侮辱的、無禮的、冒犯的","s":"The customer's insulting remarks about the waiter's accent caused everyone in the restaurant to turn around in shock.","t":"那位顧客對服務生口音的侮辱性（無禮的）言論，讓餐廳裡的所有人都不禁震驚地轉過頭來看。"},{"w":"publish","p":"v.","d":"To prepare, print, and distribute a book, magazine, article, or song so that the public can buy or read it.","c":"出版、發行、刊登","s":"After working on her fantasy novel for over three years, Chloe finally found a company willing to publish it.","t":"在花了三年多創作她的奇幻小說後，克洛伊終於找到了一家願意出版它的公司。"},{"w":"publisher","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person or a company that prepares, prints, and sells books, magazines, or newspapers.","c":"出版商、出版社、發行商","s":"The famous publisher announced that they would release a special illustrated edition of the classic novel this winter.","t":"那家著名的出版商（出版社）宣布，他們將在今年冬天發行這部經典小說的特別插畫版。"},{"w":"add insult to injury","p":"phr.","d":"to act in a way that makes a bad situation worse.","c":"雪上加霜","s":"Jean's mean boss gave her much more difficult work to do, and to add insult to injury, he significantly lowered her salary.","t":"珍刻薄的老闆給了她更困難的工作，而且雪上加霜的是，他大幅降低了她的薪水。"},{"w":"chairman","p":"n.","d":"a person chosen to preside over a meeting.","c":"主席；董事長","s":"The authoritative chairman officially began the highly important business meeting by warmly welcoming all the newly elected board members.","t":"權威的主席正式開始了這場極其重要的商業會議，熱烈歡迎所有新當選的董事會成員。"},{"w":"genderless","p":"adj.","d":"lacking a specified gender; suitable for any gender.","c":"無性別的","s":"Some progressive modern clothing stores have recently started to creatively introduce comfortable genderless clothing options for extremely young children.","t":"一些進步的現代服飾店最近開始創造性地為極年輕的孩童推出舒適的無性別的服裝選擇。"},{"w":"publication","p":"n.","d":"the preparation and issuing of a book, journal, piece of music, or other work for public sale.","c":"出版物；發行","s":"Our highly successful magazine company reliably puts out two to three brilliant publications every single month for our eager readers.","t":"我們極其成功的雜誌公司，可靠地每個月為我們熱切的讀者發行兩到三份出色的出版物。"},{"w":"feminine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities or an appearance traditionally associated with women.","c":"女性化的","s":"Many traditional fashion designers incorrectly say that light pink is naturally a very feminine color specifically reserved for beautiful dresses.","t":"許多傳統的時裝設計師錯誤地說，淺粉紅色天生就是一種非常女性化的顏色，專門保留給美麗的洋裝。"},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"all of the people born and living at about the same time, regarded collectively.","c":"世代","s":"Colin's large and deeply historic family has proudly lived in this quiet rural village for six entire generations without ever leaving.","t":"柯林龐大且歷史悠久的家族自豪地在這個安靜的鄉村村莊生活了整整六個世代，從未離開過。"},{"w":"from generation to generation","p":"phr.","d":"passed down through successive generations of a family or society.","c":"代代相傳","s":"This beautiful ancient farm was proudly passed down from generation to generation in my large and deeply traditional family.","t":"這座美麗的古老農場在我龐大且極其傳統的家庭中自豪地代代相傳。"},{"w":"prior","p":"adj.","d":"existing or coming before in time, order, or importance.","c":"先前的","s":"We were unfortunately given absolutely no prior notice that the highly important afternoon meeting time would be suddenly and completely changed.","t":"我們不幸地完全沒有收到任何先前的通知，告知極其重要的下午會議時間將會突然且徹底地改變。"},{"w":"prior","p":"adj.","d":"Existing or happening before something else, or before a particular time.","c":"先前的、在先的","s":"Marcus had to cancel his dinner plans with Chloe because of a prior commitment at work that he couldn't skip.","t":"馬庫斯因為工作上先前的約定而無法抽身，不得不取消與克洛伊的晚餐計劃。"},{"w":"prior work experience","p":"phr.","d":"The practical skills and knowledge that a person has gained from jobs they held in the past.","c":"先前工作經驗、過往工作經驗","s":"The multinational company prefers to hire candidates who have at least three years of prior work experience in sales.","t":"這家跨國公司更傾向於聘用在銷售方面擁有至少三年過往工作經驗的應徵者。"},{"w":"prior knowledge","p":"phr.","d":"The information and understanding about a subject that a person already has before they start learning more about it.","c":"先前知識、既有知識","s":"The advanced physics professor assumed that all students in the class had some prior knowledge of basic calculus.","t":"高階物理學教授假定課堂上的所有學生對基礎微積分都已經具備了一些先前知識（既有知識）。"},{"w":"prior to","p":"phr.","d":"before.","c":"在...之前","s":"The strict teacher firmly asked the anxious students if they had any final questions prior to officially starting the difficult exam.","t":"嚴格的老師堅定地問焦慮的學生在正式開始困難的考試之前是否還有任何最後的問題。"},{"w":"majority","p":"n.","d":"the greater number.","c":"多數","s":"The vast majority of ambitious high school students in this rich neighborhood usually start attending college right after they graduate.","t":"這個富裕社區裡絕大多數雄心勃勃的高中生，通常在畢業後就立刻開始上大學。"},{"w":"the majority of","p":"phr.","d":"More than half of a total number of people or things; the larger part of something.","c":"大多數的、大部分的","s":"The majority of the students in this class prefer using digital tablets instead of traditional paper notebooks.","t":"這個班級裡的大多數學生更喜歡使用數位平板，而不是傳統的紙質筆記本。"},{"w":"major in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To study a specific subject as your primary focus or main field at a college or university.","c":"主修（某科系/專業）","s":"Marcus decided to major in computer science because he wants to develop mobile applications in the future.","t":"馬庫斯決定主修資訊工程，因為他未來想要開發手機應用程式。"},{"w":"major","p":"adj.","d":"Important, serious, or significant; greater in size, extent, or importance.","c":"主要的、重大的、重要的","s":"Regular exercise and a balanced diet play a major role in maintaining good physical and mental health.","t":"規律運動和均衡飲食在維持良好的身心健康中扮演著主要的（重要的）角色。"},{"w":"minor in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To study a secondary subject at a college or university alongside a main subject (major).","c":"輔修（某科系/專業）","s":"While Chloe is a business major, she also chose to minor in Japanese to expand her future career opportunities.","t":"雖然克洛伊是商學主修，但她也選擇輔修日文，以拓展她未來的職涯機會。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"Small, unimportant, or not serious when compared with other things of the same kind.","c":"次要的、輕微的、不重要的","s":"The car accident only caused some minor scratches on the bumper, and luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"這場車禍只在保險桿上造成了一些輕微的刮痕，幸運的是沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"minor","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person who is under the legal age of full responsibility (usually under 18 or 20).","c":"未成年人","s":"In many countries, a person under eighteen is legally considered a minor and cannot buy cigarettes or alcohol.","t":"在許多國家，未滿十八歲的人在法律上被視為未成年人，不能購買香菸或酒類。"},{"w":"minority","p":"n. [C, usually singular]","d":"A smaller part of a group; less than half of the total number of people or things.","c":"少數、少數派","s":"Marcus found himself in the minority when he voted against the weekend overtime plan, as most of his colleagues agreed to it.","t":"馬庫斯在投票反對週末加班計劃時發現自己屬於少數，因為他的大多數同事都同意了。"},{"w":"minority group","p":"n. [C]","d":"A group of people of a specific race, religion, or culture who live in a society where most people are different.","c":"少數族群、少數群體","s":"The government is introducing new policies to protect the cultural rights and languages of every minority group in the country.","t":"政府正在推行新政策，以保護國內每個少數族群（少數群體）的文化權益與語言。"},{"w":"commonplace","p":"adj.","d":"not unusual; ordinary.","c":"司空見慣的；普通的","s":"Serious technical problems with completely new computer technology tend to be extremely commonplace during the very early development stages.","t":"全新電腦科技的嚴重技術問題，在非常早期的發展階段往往是極度司空見慣的。"},{"w":"elsewhere","p":"adv.","d":"in, at, or to some other place or other places.","c":"在別處","s":"The busy local store did not have the specific kitchen knife that I desperately wanted, so I had to look elsewhere.","t":"繁忙的當地商店沒有我極度想要的那把特定菜刀，所以我只好在別處尋找。"},{"w":"scream","p":"v.","d":"to give a long, loud, piercing cry or cries expressing extreme emotion or pain.","c":"尖叫","s":"Whenever arrogant Brandon loudly brags about his minor accomplishments, it absolutely screams deep insecurity to absolutely everyone around him.","t":"每當傲慢的布蘭登大聲吹噓他微小的成就時，它絕對向周圍的每個人尖叫（表現出）深深的不安全感。"},{"w":"permit","p":"v.","d":"To allow something to happen or to give official permission for something.","c":"允許、准許","s":"The school rules do not permit students to use their mobile phones during formal examination hours.","t":"學校規定不允許學生在正式考試時間使用手機。"},{"w":"permit","p":"n. [C]","d":"An official document that gives you legal permission to do something.","c":"許可證、執照","s":"You must apply for a special parking permit before you can park your vehicle in this reserved downtown area.","t":"在您將車輛停放在此市區保留區之前，您必須先申請特殊的停車許可證。"},{"w":"permission","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of allowing someone to do something, or official approval.","c":"允許、許可、同意","s":"Leo had to ask his manager for permission to leave the office two hours early for a dental appointment.","t":"里歐必須向他的經理請求允許（許可），好提早兩小時離開辦公室去牙醫診所看診。"},{"w":"request for permission","p":"phr.","d":"A formal or polite ask to be allowed to do something.","c":"請求許可、申請准許","s":"The social media software sent a request for permission to access the user's photos before uploading the picture.","t":"該社群軟體在確認上傳圖片之前，發送了存取使用者相簿的請求許可。"},{"w":"permissible","p":"adj.","d":"permitted; allowed.","c":"允許的","s":"Wearing comfortable shorts in the hot summer is entirely permissible according to the modern company's progressive new dress code.","t":"根據這家現代公司進步的新著裝規定，在炎熱的夏天穿著舒適的短褲是完全允許的。"},{"w":"access","p":"v.","d":"To open a computer file, use a system, or enter a specific place.","c":"存取（電腦檔案）、進入、讀取","s":"Users can access their online banking accounts securely from anywhere in the world using the mobile app.","t":"使用者可以使用這款手機應用程式，從世界任何地方安全地存取（讀取）他們的網路銀行帳戶。"},{"w":"access","p":"n. [U]","d":"The right, opportunity, or means to use, see, or enter something.","c":"使用權、進入權、獲取管道","s":"The remote mountain village finally has access to clean drinking water and stable high-speed internet.","t":"這個偏遠的山區村莊終於擁有了乾淨飲用水與穩定高速網路的使用管道（獲取機會）。"},{"w":"gain access to","p":"phr. v.","d":"To succeed in entering a place, or getting the right to see or use something.","c":"獲得…的存取權/進入權","s":"Hackers often use phishing emails to trick employees and gain access to confidential company databases.","t":"駭客經常利用網路釣魚郵件來欺騙員工，進而獲得公司機密資料庫的存取權。"},{"w":"authorize","p":"v.","d":"To give official permission for something to happen or for someone to do something.","c":"授權、批准、准許","s":"The manager refused to authorize the extra budget because the marketing team did not provide a detailed report.","t":"經理拒絕批准（授權）這筆額外預算，因為行銷團隊沒有提供詳細的報告。"},{"w":"authorized","p":"adj.","d":"Having official permission or approval to do something or enter a place.","c":"經授權的、經批准的","s":"Only authorized personnel are allowed to enter the laboratory server room to ensure data security.","t":"只有經授權的工作人員才被允許進入實驗室的伺服器室，以確保數據安全。"},{"w":"unauthorized","p":"adj.","d":"Without official or legal permission or approval.","c":"未經授權的、未經許可的","s":"The security system automatically blocks any unauthorized attempts to log into the company's internal network.","t":"安全系統會自動阻斷任何未經授權的（未經許可的）登入公司內部網路之企圖。"},{"w":"authority","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The official power to make decisions, give orders, or enforce laws.","c":"權力、職權、當局","s":"The police officer has the legal authority to stop drivers and check their licenses for safety reasons.","t":"出於安全考量，警察擁有合法的權力（職權）來攔下駕駛人並檢查其駕照。"},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"To have a plan or purpose in mind when doing something.","c":"想要、打算、意圖","s":"I do not intend to cause any trouble, so I will quietly leave before the argument gets worse.","t":"我不打算製造任何麻煩，所以我會在爭吵惡化之前悄悄離開。"},{"w":"intend to v","p":"v. phr.","d":"To plan or design to perform a specific action.","c":"打算做…、計畫做…","s":"Marcus and Chloe intend to travel to Japan next winter to enjoy the hot springs and local cuisine.","t":"馬庫斯和克洛伊打算明年冬天去日本旅行，享受溫泉與當地美食。"},{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"a thing intended; an aim or plan.","c":"意圖","s":"Richard actually had absolutely no intention of attending the boring holiday party, but his persistent friend strongly forced him to go.","t":"理查實際上絕對沒有參加這個無聊節日派對的意圖，但他堅持不懈的朋友強烈強迫他去。"},{"w":"intentional","p":"adj.","d":"Done on purpose; deliberate and not accidental.","c":"故意的、刻意的","s":"The referee penalized the soccer player because his foul was clearly intentional and aimed at hurting the opponent.","t":"裁判處罰了那名足球員，因為他的犯規顯然是故意的，目的在於傷害對手。"},{"w":"unintentional","p":"adj.","d":"Not done on purpose; accidental or mistake-driven.","c":"無意的、非故意的、不小心的","s":"Please forgive Marcus for spilling the tea; it was completely unintentional and he already cleaned up the table.","t":"請原諒馬庫斯打翻茶水；這完全是無意的（不小心的），而且他已經把桌子清理乾淨了。"},{"w":"tend to v","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be likely to behave in a particular way or have a certain characteristic.","c":"往往會…、傾向於做…","s":"People tend to spend more money on online shopping when they feel highly stressed or bored.","t":"當人們感到壓力大或非常無聊時，往往會在網購上花更多錢。"},{"w":"tendency","p":"n. [C]","d":"A likelihood to happen or a way of behaving that is common.","c":"傾向、趨勢","s":"There is a growing tendency among young professionals to prioritize remote work options over higher salaries.","t":"在年輕的專業人士中，將遠距工作選項看得比高薪更重要的趨勢（傾向）正日益增長。"},{"w":"have the tendency to v","p":"phr.","d":"To often behave in a particular way or regularly do something.","c":"有…的傾向、往往會…","s":"Chloe has the tendency to check her business emails late at night, which sometimes affects her sleep.","t":"克洛伊有在深夜檢查工作郵件的傾向，這有時會影響她的睡眠。"},{"w":"be likely to v","p":"phr.","d":"Probable or expected to happen or do something.","c":"很有可能…","s":"According to the weather forecast, it is likely to rain heavily this afternoon, so you should bring an umbrella.","t":"根據天氣預報，今天下午很有可能會下大雨，所以你應該帶把傘。"},{"w":"be prone to ( nv-ing)","p":"phr.","d":"Likely to suffer from, do, or experience something negative or unpleasant.","c":"易於…的、往往會…（通常指負面事物）","s":"This old smartphone model is prone to crashing when you try to run multiple advanced applications at the same time.","t":"當你試圖同時執行多個高階應用程式時，這款舊手機機型易於（往往會）當機。"},{"w":"be inclined to v","p":"phr.","d":"Feeling willing or likely to do something or think in a particular way.","c":"傾向於…、想要…、頗有…的意願","s":"After reviewing the candidate's impressive prior work experience, the hiring manager is inclined to offer the position to Leo.","t":"在審查了應徵者令人印象深刻的過往工作經驗後，招聘經理傾向於（想要）把這個職位給里歐。"},{"w":"noble","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing fine personal qualities or high moral principles and ideals.","c":"高尚的；貴族的","s":"Tammy did a truly noble and courageous thing when she bravely stopped the angry young boys' violent physical fight immediately.","t":"當塔米立刻勇敢地阻止憤怒小男孩暴力的肢體衝突時，她做了一件真正高尚的且勇敢的事。"},{"w":"nobility","p":"n. [U]","d":"People of the highest social class who hold special titles, such as dukes or earls.","c":"貴族（階層）","s":"In medieval Europe, the nobility owned most of the land and held great political power over the common people.","t":"在中世紀的歐洲，貴族（階層）擁有大部分的土地，並對平民擁有巨大的政治權力。"},{"w":"the royal family","p":"phr.","d":"The family of the king or queen of a country.","c":"王室、皇室","s":"Millions of people watched the live television broadcast of the young prince's wedding to see the royal family.","t":"數百萬人觀看了年輕王子婚禮的電視直播，一睹王室（皇室）風采。"},{"w":"royalty","p":"n. [U]","d":"One or more members of a royal family, or royal status.","c":"皇室成員、王室身份","s":"Although she was treated like royalty wherever she traveled, the famous actress remained very humble and polite.","t":"儘管不論走到哪裡都受到如同皇室成員般的款待，這位著名的女演員依然非常謙遜且有禮貌。"},{"w":"loyal","p":"adj.","d":"Firm and constant in one's support for a person, country, or belief.","c":"忠誠的、忠心的","s":"Leo has been a loyal customer at this coffee shop for five years, visiting every single morning before work.","t":"里歐五年來一直是這家咖啡廳的忠實（忠誠）顧客，每天早上上班前都會光顧。"},{"w":"be loyal to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To show constant support or faithfulness to someone or something.","c":"忠於…、對…忠誠","s":"A well-trained guard dog will always be loyal to its owner and protect them from any potential danger.","t":"一隻訓練有素的警衛犬會永遠忠於牠的主人，並保護他們免受任何潛在的危險。"},{"w":"discriminate","p":"v.","d":"to make an unjust or prejudicial distinction in the treatment of different categories of people or things.","c":"歧視；區分","s":"The large international company strictly cannot discriminate against any potential employees simply on the unfair and completely illegal grounds of age.","t":"這家大型國際公司嚴格不能僅僅基於不公平且完全非法的年齡理由，來歧視任何潛在的員工。"},{"w":"discriminate against","p":"v. phr.","d":"To treat a person or a group worse than others because of their race, gender, age, etc.","c":"歧視、對…不公平對待","s":"It is strictly illegal for employers to discriminate against job applicants based on their religious beliefs.","t":"雇主根據求職者的宗教信仰而歧視他們，是完全違法的。"},{"w":"discrimination","p":"n. [U]","d":"The unfair treatment of different categories of people, especially on the grounds of race, age, or sex.","c":"歧視","s":"The international organization fights against all forms of discrimination to ensure everyone enjoys equal human rights.","t":"該國際組織致力於對抗一切形式的歧視，以確保每個人都享有平等的權。"},{"w":"racial discrimination","p":"phr.","d":"Unfair treatment of individuals based on their race or ethnic background.","c":"種族歧視","s":"The civil rights movement in the 1960s aimed to end racial discrimination and guarantee equal voting rights.","t":"1960 年代的民權運動旨在結束種族歧視，並保障平等的投票權。"},{"w":"gender discrimination","p":"phr.","d":"Unfair treatment of people based on their gender or sex, especially in the workplace.","c":"性別歧視","s":"To prevent gender discrimination, the company ensures that men and women receive equal pay for the same work.","t":"為了防止性別歧視，公司確保男女在相同的工作中獲得同等的薪酬。"},{"w":"age discrimination","p":"phr.","d":"Unfair treatment of individuals based on their age, often affecting older workers.","c":"年齡歧視","s":"Refusing to hire an experienced worker simply because they are over fifty is a clear example of age discrimination.","t":"僅僅因為年過五十而拒絕雇用一位經驗豐富的員工，就是一個明顯的年齡歧視案例。"},{"w":"prejudice","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"An unfair and unreasonable opinion or feeling formed without enough thought or knowledge.","c":"偏見","s":"We must educate young children properly to prevent them from developing prejudice against people from different cultures.","t":"We must properly educate young children to prevent them from developing 偏見 against people from different cultures."},{"w":"stereotype","p":"n. [C]","d":"A fixed, oversimplified, and often unfair belief about a particular type of person or thing.","c":"刻板印象","s":"The belief that all scientists are quiet and unsocial is a common stereotype that does not reflect reality.","t":"認為所有科學家都沉默寡言且不社交的看法，是一種不符合現實的常見刻板印象。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A strong feeling in favor of or against one group of people or one side in an argument, often unfair.","c":"偏見、偏心、成見","s":"The journalist was accused of bias because her article only reported the views of one political party.","t":"這名記者被指責帶有偏見（偏心），因為她的文章只報導了一個政黨的觀點。"},{"w":"biased","p":"adj.","d":"Unfairly preferring one person, group, or opinion over another.","c":"有偏見的、偏袒的","s":"The referee's biased decisions during the championship game sparked an angry protest from the losing team.","t":"裁判在冠軍賽中有偏見的（偏袒的）判決，引發了輸球隊伍的憤怒抗議。"},{"w":"unbiased","p":"adj.","d":"Able to judge fairly because you are not influenced by personal opinions or local interests.","c":"無偏見的、公正的","s":"A scientific study must remain completely unbiased by analyzing raw data without any personal expectations.","t":"科學研究必須藉由分析原始數據且不帶任何個人預期，以保持完全的公正（無偏見）。"},{"w":"impartial","p":"adj.","d":"Not supporting one person or group more than another; completely fair and neutral.","c":"公平的、無私的、中立的","s":"As a judge, it is Chloe's duty to remain impartial and listen to both sides of the legal case carefully.","t":"作為一名法官，克洛伊的職責是保持中立（公平無私），並仔細聆聽法律案件雙方的陳述。"},{"w":"just","p":"adj.","d":"Fair, right, and reasonable according to moral principles or the law.","c":"公正的、正義的、合理的","s":"The citizens demanded a just legal system where wealthy individuals cannot buy their way out of punishment.","t":"公民們要求一個公正的法律體系，在其中富人無法透過金錢來逃避懲罰。"},{"w":"justice","p":"n. [U]","d":"Fairness in the way people are treated, or the legal system that ensures fairness.","c":"正義、公正、公道","s":"The community gathered outside the courthouse to demand justice for the victim of the tragic accident.","t":"社區居民聚集在法院外，為那場悲慘事故的受害者尋求正義（公道）。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"hungry – literally translated","cards":[{"w":"hungry","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or displaying the need for food.","c":"飢餓的","s":"The extremely hungry little boy loudly asked his busy mother to quickly cook some delicious dinner.","t":"極度飢餓的小男孩大聲要求他忙碌的母親迅速煮一些美味的晚餐。"},{"w":"hunger","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of discomfort or weakness caused by lack of food.","c":"飢餓","s":"Lily's hunger didn't go away even after she eagerly ate two huge sandwiches for lunch.","t":"莉莉的飢餓即使在她渴望地吃了兩個巨大的三明治當午餐後也沒有消失。"},{"w":"hunger for","p":"phr.","d":"to have a strong desire for something.","c":"渴望","s":"Ever since he was a young student, ambitious George has always had a deep hunger for knowledge.","t":"自從他還是個年輕學生以來，雄心勃勃的喬治就一直對知識有著深深的渴望。"},{"w":"long for","p":"v. phr.","d":"To want something very much, especially when it is difficult to get or will take a long time.","c":"渴望得到…、盼望…","s":"After working in the busy city for years, Marcus began to long for a peaceful life in a quiet village.","t":"在忙碌的城市工作多年後，馬庫斯開始渴望得到安靜村莊裡的平靜生活。"},{"w":"long to v","p":"v. phr.","d":"To have a strong desire to perform a specific action or do something.","c":"渴望做…、極想做…","s":"Having lived abroad for over five years, Chloe longs to return home and spend time with her family.","t":"在國外生活了五年多，克洛伊渴望回到家鄉並陪伴她的家人。"},{"w":"desire","p":"v.","d":"To want something strongly or wish for something to happen.","c":"渴望、想要、要求","s":"The young entrepreneur truly desires to make a positive impact on society through her eco-friendly company.","t":"這位年輕的企業家真心渴望透過她那家環保概念的公司來對社會產生正面的影響。"},{"w":"desire","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A strong feeling of wanting to have something or wishing for something to happen.","c":"渴望、慾望、心願","s":"Leo expressed a strong desire to learn advanced Japanese cooking techniques from the master chef.","t":"里歐表達了想要向主廚學習高級日本料理烹飪技巧的強烈渴望（心願）。"},{"w":"aspire","p":"v.","d":"To have a strong hope or ambition to achieve something great or become successful.","c":"渴望（成就）、追求、立志","s":"Many young students in the sports program aspire to compete in the Olympic Games one day.","t":"體育培訓計畫中的許多年輕學生都立志（渴望）有一天能參加奧運會。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n. [C, usually plural]","d":"A strong hope, desire, or ambition to achieve something high or great.","c":"抱負、渴望、志向","s":"The university helps students fulfill their career aspirations by providing professional internships.","t":"這所大學透過提供專業的實習機會，來幫助學生實現他們的職涯抱負（志向）。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A strong desire to achieve success, power, wealth, or a specific high goal.","c":"雄心、抱負、野心","s":"Marcus has a great ambition to open his own law firm before he reaches the age of thirty-five.","t":"馬庫斯有著在三十五歲前開設自己律師事務所的遠大雄心（抱負）。"},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adj.","d":"Having or showing a strong desire and determination to succeed, or requiring a lot of effort.","c":"有雄心壯志的、野心勃勃的、艱巨的","s":"The city government announced an ambitious plan to transition all public transport to green energy within three years.","t":"市政府宣布了一項雄心勃勃的（艱巨的）計劃，要在三年內將所有大眾運輸工具轉型為綠色能源。"},{"w":"starve","p":"v.","d":"to suffer severely or die from hunger.","c":"挨餓","s":"The poor stray animals will eventually starve if the kind local residents do not regularly feed them.","t":"如果善良的當地居民不定期餵食牠們，可憐的流浪動物最終將會挨餓。"},{"w":"starvation","p":"n.","d":"suffering or death caused by hunger.","c":"飢餓；餓死","s":"The dedicated charity workers warned that if the villagers don't get food soon, they will die of starvation.","t":"盡責的慈善工作者警告說，如果村民們不快點得到食物，他們將會死於飢餓。"},{"w":"starving","p":"adj.","d":"Dying of hunger, or feeling extremely hungry.","c":"非常飢餓的、快餓死的","s":"After hiking for six hours without any snacks, Marcus felt absolutely starving by the time he reached the camp.","t":"在沒有任何零食的情況下健行了六個小時，馬庫斯到達營地時感到非常飢餓（快餓死了）。"},{"w":"starve to death","p":"v. phr.","d":"To die because there is not enough food to eat.","c":"餓死","s":"During the severe winter drought, many wild animals in the forest unfortunately starved to death due to the lack of plants.","t":"在寒冷的冬日嚴冬旱災期間，森林裡的許多野生動物遺憾地因為缺乏植物而餓死。"},{"w":"eat a horse","p":"idiom","d":"An expression used to say that you are extremely hungry.","c":"吃得下一頭牛（形容非常餓）","s":"I haven't had anything since breakfast, and it's already late in the evening; I could eat a horse right now!","t":"我自從早餐後就什麼都沒吃，現在都已經深夜了；我現在非常餓（吃得下一頭牛）！"},{"w":"appetite","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A natural desire to eat food, or a strong desire for something.","c":"食慾、胃口","s":"The delicious aroma of the grilled Japanese yakiniku immediately stimulated Chloe's appetite as she walked into the restaurant.","t":"當克洛伊走進餐廳時，美味的日本烤肉香氣立刻激起了她的食慾（胃口）。"},{"w":"ache","p":"n.","d":"a continuous or prolonged dull pain in a part of one's body.","c":"疼痛","s":"The terrible ache in George's right leg was significantly worse when the winter weather was extremely cold.","t":"當冬季天氣極度寒冷時，喬治右腿可怕的疼痛明顯變得更糟。"},{"w":"ache","p":"v.","d":"to suffer from a continuous dull pain.","c":"疼痛","s":"After confidently finishing the exhausting marathon race, my tired feet truly ached for an entire week.","t":"在自信地完成令人筋疲力盡的馬拉松比賽後，我疲憊的雙腳真的疼痛了整整一個星期。"},{"w":"headache","p":"n.","d":"a continuous pain in the head.","c":"頭痛","s":"Fiona had a mild headache this sunny morning, but she thankfully feels much better right now.","t":"費歐娜這個陽光明媚的早晨有輕微的頭痛，但幸虧她現在感覺好多了。"},{"w":"pain","p":"n.","d":"physical suffering or discomfort caused by illness or injury.","c":"痛楚","s":"Robert immediately went to see a professional doctor because he was experiencing sharp chest pain all morning.","t":"羅伯特立刻去看了專業醫生，因為他整個早上都經歷著劇烈的胸部痛楚。"},{"w":"chest pain","p":"phr.","d":"discomfort or pain that you feel anywhere along the front of your body between your neck and upper abdomen.","c":"胸痛","s":"The nervous elderly patient rushed to the busy hospital because he suddenly felt a severe chest pain.","t":"緊張的年老病患趕緊前往繁忙的醫院，因為他突然感到嚴重的胸痛。"},{"w":"be in pain","p":"phr.","d":"Experiencing physical suffering or discomfort caused by illness or injury.","c":"處於痛苦中、身體在痛","s":"After twisting his ankle during the basketball game, Marcus was in severe pain and could barely walk to the bench.","t":"在籃球賽中扭傷腳踝後，馬庫斯身體極為痛苦（非常痛），幾乎無法走到替補席。"},{"w":"painful","p":"adj.","d":"Causing physical pain, or causing distress, sadness, or emotional suffering.","c":"令人疼痛的、痛苦的、難堪的","s":"The dentist explained that extracting the wisdom tooth would be a bit painful, but the healing process would be fast.","t":"牙醫解釋說，拔除這顆智齒會有點令人疼痛，但復原過程會很快。"},{"w":"painful memory","p":"phr.","d":"A sad or distressing recollection from the past that still causes emotional suffering.","c":"痛苦的回憶、不堪回首的往事","s":"Losing her childhood pet was a deeply painful memory for Chloe, and she still gets emotional when talking about it.","t":"失去童年寵物對克洛伊來說是一段深刻且痛苦的回憶，她現在談到這件事時依然會情緒激動。"},{"w":"painkiller","p":"n. [C]","d":"A drug or medicine used to reduce or relieve physical pain.","c":"止痛藥","s":"Leo took a strong painkiller to handle his severe migraine so that he could focus on finishing his work reports.","t":"里歐服下了一顆強效止痛藥來應對他嚴重的偏頭痛，以便能專注於完成他的工作報告。"},{"w":"relieve the pain","p":"v. phr.","d":"To make a physical pain or emotional suffering less severe or disappear completely.","c":"緩解疼痛、減輕痛苦","s":"Applying a cold compress to a swollen muscle can help relieve the pain and reduce inflammation quickly.","t":"在腫脹的肌肉上進行冷敷有助於緩解疼痛並快速消除發炎。"},{"w":"ease the pain","p":"v. phr.","d":"To gradually lessen the intensity of physical discomfort or emotional distress.","c":"減輕疼痛、舒緩痛苦","s":"The doctor prescribed a special ointment to help ease the pain caused by the sunburn on Marcus's shoulders.","t":"醫生開了一款特別的軟膏，以幫助減輕（舒緩）馬庫斯肩膀上因曬傷所造成的疼痛。"},{"w":"reduce the pain","p":"v. phr.","d":"To lower the level or amount of physical pain you are experiencing.","c":"降低疼痛、減少痛苦","s":"Resting the injured wrist and elevating it on a soft pillow will significantly reduce the pain.","t":"讓受傷的手腕休息並將其抬高在軟枕頭上，將會顯著降低疼痛感。"},{"w":"connect","p":"v.","d":"to bring together or into contact so that a real or notional link is established.","c":"連接","s":"The modern new bridge will efficiently connect the two isolated towns across the wide and deep river.","t":"現代化的新橋將高效率地連接這座寬闊深邃河流兩岸兩個被孤立的城鎮。"},{"w":"connected","p":"adj.","d":"joined or linked together.","c":"相關的；連接的","s":"Intelligent Paul is incredibly interested in absolutely any complex topic that is closely connected to classical music.","t":"聰明的保羅對任何與古典音樂密切相關的複雜主題都極度感興趣。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a relationship in which a person, thing, or idea is linked or associated with something else.","c":"關聯","s":"The smart detective quickly realized that there was a hidden connection between the two seemingly unrelated crimes.","t":"聰明的警探迅速意識到，這兩起看似無關的犯罪之間有著隱藏的關聯。"},{"w":"stay connected","p":"phr.","d":"to maintain a relationship or communication with someone.","c":"保持聯繫","s":"Using modern social media makes it incredibly easy to stay connected with friends living in foreign countries.","t":"使用現代社群媒體讓與住在外國的朋友保持聯繫變得極其容易。"},{"w":"linked","p":"adj.","d":"connected or joined.","c":"連結的；有關聯的","s":"The researchers discovered that the rare illness is strongly linked to drinking heavily polluted river water.","t":"研究人員發現，這種罕見的疾病與飲用嚴重污染的河水有強烈的連結的（關聯）。"},{"w":"be connected with/to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be joined to something else, or to have a close logical or practical relationship with it.","c":"與…連結/相連、與…有關聯","s":"The printer must be connected to the main computer via a USB cable before you can print out the vocabulary lists.","t":"印表機必須透過 USB 線與主電腦相連，然後你才能列印出單字表。"},{"w":"be linked with/to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be physically connected, or to have a strong connection or causal relationship between two things.","c":"與…有聯繫/關聯","s":"Scientific research has shown that a high-sugar diet is closely linked to an increased risk of heart disease.","t":"科學研究已經顯示，高糖飲食與心臟病風險的增加密切相關（有因果聯繫）。"},{"w":"be associated with","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be connected in the mind, or to happen together with something else frequently.","c":"與…聯想在一起、與…有關聯","s":"The color red is often associated with danger, excitement, or passion in many different cultures.","t":"在許多不同的文化中，紅色經常與危險、興奮或激情聯想在一起（有關聯）。"},{"w":"be related to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To have a connection to something else, or to belong to the same family.","c":"與…有關、與…有親戚關係","s":"The drop in sales this month is directly related to the recent supply chain delays in shipping.","t":"本月銷售額的下降與最近航運供應鏈的延誤直接相關（有關）。"},{"w":"be involved in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To take part in an activity, event, or situation, or to be mixed up in something negative.","c":"參與…、涉入…、捲入…","s":"Marcus decided to be actively involved in the local charity project to help low-income families.","t":"馬庫斯決定積極參與當地的慈善計畫，以幫助低收入家庭。"},{"w":"have something to do with","p":"phr.","d":"To have a connection, relation, or concern with a particular matter or person.","c":"與…有些關係、與…有關","s":"I suspect that the strange noise from the kitchen has something to do with the old refrigerator.","t":"我懷疑廚房傳來的怪聲與那台舊冰箱有些關係。"},{"w":"contact","p":"v.","d":"To communicate with someone by calling, texting, emailing, or meeting them.","c":"聯絡、聯繫","s":"If you have any questions about the new schedule, please feel free to contact Chloe via email.","t":"如果你對新行程有任何疑問，請隨時透過電子郵件聯絡克洛伊。"},{"w":"contact","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"Communication or meeting between people, or a helpful person you know in an organization.","c":"聯絡、聯繫、熟人/聯絡人","s":"Marcus has lost contact with most of his high school classmates since he moved to Taipei for work.","t":"自從馬庫斯搬到台北工作後，他已經與大部分的高中同學失去了聯絡（聯繫）。"},{"w":"keep in contact with","p":"phr.","d":"To maintain communication with someone regularly over time.","c":"與…保持聯絡","s":"Thanks to modern social media applications, it is much easier to keep in contact with friends living abroad.","t":"拜現代社群媒體應用程式所賜，與旅居國外的朋友保持聯絡變得容易多了。"},{"w":"contact lens","p":"n. [C, usually plural]","d":"A thin plastic lens placed directly on the surface of the eye to improve vision.","c":"隱形眼鏡","s":"Chloe prefers wearing contact lenses when she goes out for formal dinners so she doesn't need her glasses.","t":"克洛伊出去參加正式晚宴時更喜歡配戴隱形眼鏡，這樣她就不需要戴眼鏡了。"},{"w":"compel","p":"v.","d":"to force or oblige someone to do something.","c":"迫使","s":"As there was something terribly wrong with the engine, the frightened pilot was compelled to land quickly.","t":"由於引擎出了嚴重的故障，受驚的飛行員被迫使迅速降落。"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"evoking interest, attention, or admiration in a powerfully irresistible way.","c":"令人信服的；引人入勝的","s":"The skilled lawyer presented a highly compelling argument that successfully convinced the jury to free the innocent man.","t":"技巧高超的律師提出了一個極其令人信服的論點，成功說服陪審團釋放了無辜的男子。"},{"w":"feel compelled to","p":"phr.","d":"to strongly think that you must do something.","c":"感到必須","s":"When I saw the helpless little puppy shivering in the cold rain, I felt compelled to help it.","t":"當我看到那隻無助的小狗在冷雨中發抖時，我感到必須幫助牠。"},{"w":"be compelled to","p":"phr.","d":"to be forced to do something.","c":"被迫","s":"Due to the sudden and devastating financial crisis, the company will be compelled to lay off many workers.","t":"由於突然且毀滅性的金融危機，公司將被迫解雇許多工人。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"To make someone completely believe that something is true or real.","c":"使確信、使相信、說服","s":"The lawyer managed to convince the jury that his client was completely innocent of the crime.","t":"律師成功地使陪審團確信他的當事人與這起犯罪毫無關係（完全無辜）。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"Making you believe that something is true or right because it sounds reasonable or genuine.","c":"有說服力的、令人信服的","s":"Marcus provided a convincing argument for the budget increase, backed up by clear data and charts.","t":"馬庫斯為增加預算提出了一個令人信服的（有說服力的）論點，並有明確的數據和圖表支持。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"To move someone to do something by giving them good reasons, arguments, or requests.","c":"說服、勸服（去做某事）","s":"Chloe tried hard to persuade her parents to let her study arts abroad next semester.","t":"克洛伊努力地想說服父母讓她下個學期去國外學習藝術。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"Able to make someone do or believe something by giving them good reasons.","c":"有說服力的、口才好的","s":"The marketing manager gave a highly persuasive presentation that won over the new international clients.","t":"行銷經理進行了一場極具說服力的簡報，贏得了新國外客戶的青睞。"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of convincing someone to do or believe something, or the ability to do this.","c":"說服、說服力","s":"It took a great deal of persuasion to get Marcus to join the weekend volunteer team.","t":"花了很大的說服（功夫）才讓馬庫斯加入週末的志工團隊。"},{"w":"talk ... into v-ing","p":"phr. v.","d":"To persuade someone to perform a specific action or do something.","c":"說服某人去做…、勸服某人做…","s":"The kids successfully talked their father into taking them to the amusement park this weekend.","t":"孩子們成功地說服爸爸這週末帶他們去遊樂園。"},{"w":"force","p":"v.","d":"To make someone do something that they do not want to do, by using power, laws, or threats.","c":"強迫、迫使","s":"The heavy rain and flooded roads forced the tour group to cancel their outdoor trip to the hot springs.","t":"大雨和道路積水迫使旅行團取消了前往溫泉的戶外行程。"},{"w":"force","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"Physical strength, power, or energy; or an organized group of people like the police or military.","c":"力量、威力、武力；部隊/警力","s":"The window was smashed with great force, suggesting that the thief used a heavy hammer to break in.","t":"窗戶是被巨大的力量砸碎的，這暗示著小偷使用了沉重的鐵錘破門而入。"},{"w":"join forces","p":"phr.","d":"To act together or work as a team with someone else to achieve a common goal.","c":"聯合、攜手合作","s":"The two tech companies decided to join forces to develop an advanced AI tool for English language learning.","t":"這兩家科技公司決定聯合（攜手合作），共同開發一款用於英語學習的高階人工智慧工具。"},{"w":"forceful","p":"adj.","d":"Expressing opinions strongly and clearly in a way that convinces or influences other people.","c":"強而有力的、有說服力的、有權勢的","s":"The professional educator gave a forceful speech about the great importance of incorporating digital tools into classrooms.","t":"這位專業的教育工作者發表了一場強而有力的（有說服力的）演講，闡述了將數位工具融入課堂的巨大重要性。"},{"w":"enforce","p":"v.","d":"to compel observance of or compliance with a law, rule, or obligation.","c":"執行","s":"The strict local police officers are working extremely hard to carefully enforce the brand new traffic laws.","t":"嚴格的當地警察正極其努力地工作，以仔細地執行全新的交通法規。"},{"w":"enforce","p":"v.","d":"To make people obey a rule, law, or decision.","c":"執行（法律）、實施（規定）","s":"The school principal warned that the teachers would strictly enforce the ban on cheating during the exams.","t":"校長警告，老師們將嚴格執行考試期間禁止作弊的禁令。"},{"w":"enforcement","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of making sure that a law, rule, or order is obeyed and followed by people.","c":"執行、實施、強制執行","s":"Strict enforcement of the speed limit rules has significantly reduced the number of traffic accidents on this highway.","t":"嚴格執行速限規定，已顯著減少了這條高速公路上的交通事故數量。"},{"w":"law enforcement","p":"n. [U]","d":"The activity of making people obey the law, or the public agencies (like the police) that do this.","c":"執法、執法機關/人員","s":"Many law enforcement officers were deployed to protect the public and maintain order during the political rally.","t":"許多執法（人員）被部署在政治集會期間，以保護大眾並維持秩序。"},{"w":"be in effect","p":"phr.","d":"(Of a law, rule, or contract) currently operating, valid, or being used at the present time.","c":"生效中、實行中","s":"The new government regulations regarding environmental protection will be in effect starting next Monday.","t":"關於環境保護的新政府法規將從下週一開始生效（實行中）。"},{"w":"take effect","p":"v. phr.","d":"To start to produce the intended result, or to officially become active or operational.","c":"開始生效、起作用","s":"The doctor said that the strong painkiller would take about twenty minutes to take effect.","t":"醫生說這顆強效止痛藥需要大約二十分鐘才會開始起作用（生效）。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"To make something stronger, such as a physical structure, an idea, or a specific feeling.","c":"強化、加強、鞏固","s":"The teacher gave students a quick online quiz after the lecture to reinforce the vocabulary words they just learned.","t":"老師在講課後讓學生進行了一次快速的線上測驗，以強化（加強）他們剛剛學到的單字。"},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to break down food in the alimentary canal into substances that can be absorbed and used by the body.","c":"消化","s":"It usually takes a few hours for your healthy stomach to completely digest a heavy and greasy meal.","t":"你健康的胃通常需要幾個小時才能完全消化一頓豐盛油膩的飯菜。"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process of breaking down food by mechanical and enzymatic action in the alimentary canal into substances that can be used by the body.","c":"消化","s":"Eating a massive amount of spicy food right before sleeping is generally very bad for your digestion.","t":"在睡覺前吃大量辛辣食物通常對你的消化非常不好。"},{"w":"digestive","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the process of digesting food.","c":"消化的","s":"Drinking plenty of fresh water every day is absolutely essential for maintaining a healthy digestive system.","t":"每天喝大量新鮮的水對於維持健康的消化的系統是絕對必要的。"},{"w":"bad for digestion","p":"phr.","d":"harmful to the stomach's ability to process food.","c":"對消化不良","s":"The knowledgeable doctor gently warned the patient that eating too quickly is surprisingly bad for digestion.","t":"知識淵博的醫生溫和地警告病患，吃得太快令人驚訝地對消化不良。"},{"w":"digestive system","p":"phr.","d":"the organs and glands in the body that are responsible for digestion.","c":"消化系統","s":"Consuming a lot of organic vegetables daily can effectively help your complex digestive system function much better.","t":"每天食用大量有機蔬菜能有效地幫助你複雜的消化系統運作得更好。"},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue firmly or obstinately in an opinion or a course of action in spite of difficulty, opposition, or failure.","c":"堅持；持續","s":"Although the strict teacher repeatedly told the young girl to stop talking, she stubbornly persisted with her bad behavior.","t":"儘管嚴格的老師屢次告訴那個年輕女孩停止講話，她還是固執地堅持著她的不良行為。"},{"w":"persistent","p":"adj.","d":"continuing firmly or obstinately in a course of action in spite of difficulty or opposition.","c":"持續的；堅持的","s":"Exhausted Matt constantly heard a persistent buzzing noise in his ears after attending the incredibly loud rock concert.","t":"疲憊的麥特在參加了極度吵雜的搖滾演唱會後，不斷聽到耳朵裡有持續的嗡嗡聲。"},{"w":"persistence","p":"n.","d":"firm or obstinate continuance in a course of action in spite of difficulty or opposition.","c":"堅持不懈","s":"Achieving massive success in the highly competitive business world definitely requires a great deal of hard work and persistence.","t":"在競爭高度激烈的商業世界中取得巨大成功，絕對需要大量的努力工作和堅持不懈。"},{"w":"continuous","p":"adj.","d":"forming an unbroken whole; without interruption.","c":"連續的","s":"The continuous and heavy winter rain completely flooded the quiet streets of the small rural town yesterday.","t":"連續的冬季大雨昨天徹底淹沒了這個鄉村小鎮安靜的街道。"},{"w":"persistently","p":"adv.","d":"in a persistent manner; continuously.","c":"堅持不懈地","s":"The annoying salesman persistently called my house four times last week trying to sell me a new product.","t":"那個煩人的推銷員上週堅持不懈地打電話到我家四次，試圖賣給我一個新產品。"},{"w":"syndrome","p":"n.","d":"a group of symptoms which consistently occur together, or a condition characterized by a set of associated symptoms.","c":"症候群","s":"The experienced doctor explained that this rare medical syndrome is most likely to seriously affect middle-aged working men.","t":"經驗豐富的醫生解釋說，這種罕見的醫學症候群最有可能嚴重影響中年的職業男性。"},{"w":"down syndrome","p":"phr.","d":"a congenital disorder arising from a chromosome defect, causing intellectual impairment and physical abnormalities.","c":"唐氏症","s":"The dedicated teacher works incredibly patiently with several wonderful children who were naturally born with Down syndrome.","t":"盡責的老師極其耐心地與幾個天生患有唐氏症的優秀孩子一起工作。"},{"w":"metabolic syndrome","p":"phr.","d":"a cluster of biochemical and physiological abnormalities associated with the development of cardiovascular disease and type 2 diabetes.","c":"代謝症候群","s":"A severe lack of daily exercise can unfortunately greatly increase your personal risk of developing metabolic syndrome.","t":"嚴重缺乏日常運動不幸地會大大增加你個人罹患代謝症候群的風險。"},{"w":"rare syndrome","p":"phr.","d":"a medical condition characterized by a unique set of symptoms that affects a small percentage of the population.","c":"罕見症候群","s":"The brilliant scientists are desperately trying to discover an effective cure for this highly dangerous and rare syndrome.","t":"才華洋溢的科學家正拚命試圖發現一種有效的方法，來治療這種高度危險且罕見症候群。"},{"w":"gene","p":"n.","d":"a unit of heredity which is transferred from a parent to offspring.","c":"基因","s":"The brilliant biology professor clearly explained how a single mutated gene can potentially cause serious health problems.","t":"才華洋溢的生物學教授清楚地解釋了單一突變的基因如何可能導致嚴重的健康問題。"},{"w":"genetic","p":"adj.","d":"of or relating to genes or heredity.","c":"基因的；遺傳的","s":"The professional doctors are completely unsure of the exact cause, but they strongly think the disease might be genetic.","t":"專業的醫生完全不確定確切的原因，但他們強烈認為這種疾病可能是遺傳的。"},{"w":"genetics","p":"n.","d":"the study of heredity and the variation of inherited characteristics.","c":"遺傳學","s":"The fascinating scientific field of genetics actively studies how physical traits are passed down from parents to their children.","t":"迷人的遺傳學科學領域積極研究身體特徵是如何從父母傳遞給他們的孩子。"},{"w":"genetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to genes or genetics.","c":"基因地","s":"These perfectly red and juicy tomatoes have been genetically modified to be completely resistant to dangerous farm insects.","t":"這些完美的紅色多汁番茄已經被基因地改造，以完全抵抗危險的農場昆蟲。"},{"w":"genetic defect","p":"phr.","d":"an abnormal characteristic or flaw inherited through genes.","c":"基因缺陷","s":"Unfortunately, the newborn baby was tragically diagnosed with a rare genetic defect that severely affects his weak heart.","t":"不幸的是，這名新生兒被悲慘地診斷出患有一種罕見的基因缺陷，嚴重影響了他虛弱的心臟。"},{"w":"genetic disorder","p":"phr.","d":"an illness caused by one or more abnormalities in the genome.","c":"遺傳性疾病","s":"People who suffer from this specific genetic disorder must take highly expensive prescription medicine every single day.","t":"罹患這種特定遺傳性疾病的人必須每天服用極其昂貴的處方藥。"},{"w":"genetically-modified","p":"adj.","d":"(Of food or organisms) having had its genetic structure changed artificially in a laboratory.","c":"基基因改造的、轉基因的","s":"Some consumers prefer to buy organic corn because they worry about the potential health risks of genetically-modified-genetically-modified food.","t":"一些消費者更喜歡購買有機玉米，因為他們擔心基因改造食品潛在的健康風險。"},{"w":"genetic defect","p":"n. [C]","d":"A fault or flaw in a person's or animal's genes that may cause a disease or physical problem.","c":"基因缺陷、遺傳性缺陷","s":"The medical screening test can detect a specific genetic defect before the baby is born, allowing for early treatment.","t":"這項醫學篩檢測試可以在寶寶出生前檢測出特定的基因缺陷，以便進行早期治療。"},{"w":"inherent","p":"adj.","d":"Existing as a natural, permanent, or basic part of something that cannot be removed.","c":"固有的、內在的、與生俱來的","s":"There are inherent risks in any financial investment, so you should always think carefully before risking your money.","t":"任何金融投資都有固有的（內在的）風險，因此在拿資金冒險之前，你應該總是仔細思考。"},{"w":"be inherent in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be a natural or inseparable part of a specific situation, system, or activity.","c":"存在於…之中、是…固有的","s":"The desire to explore the unknown seems to be inherent in human nature since the beginning of history.","t":"自歷史開端以來，探索未知的渴望似乎就存在於人類的天性之中（是人類天性固有的）。"},{"w":"gender","p":"n.","d":"either of the two sexes (male and female), especially when considered with reference to social and cultural differences.","c":"性別","s":"Progressive modern companies strongly believe that an applicant's gender and race absolutely shouldn't matter during the hiring process.","t":"進步的現代公司強烈認為，申請人的性別和種族在招募過程中絕對不應該有影響。"},{"w":"gender equality","p":"phr.","d":"the state in which access to rights or opportunities is unaffected by gender.","c":"性別平等","s":"The passionate political activists are constantly protesting in the busy streets to strongly demand absolute gender equality globally.","t":"熱情的政治活動家不斷在繁忙的街道上抗議，強烈要求全球絕對的性別平等。"},{"w":"gender discrimination","p":"phr.","d":"prejudice or discrimination based on a person's sex or gender.","c":"性別歧視","s":"The strict new government laws were officially created to completely prevent unfair gender discrimination in the modern workplace.","t":"嚴格的政府新法律被正式制定，以完全防止現代工作場所中不公平的性別歧視。"},{"w":"transgender","p":"adj.","d":"denoting or relating to a person whose sense of personal identity and gender does not correspond with their birth sex.","c":"跨性別的","s":"The supportive community enthusiastically held a vibrant parade to proudly celebrate and heavily support transgender individuals' basic rights.","t":"充滿支持的社區熱情地舉辦了一場充滿活力的遊行，自豪地慶祝並大力支持跨性別的個人的基本權利。"},{"w":"lgbtq","p":"n. [U] / adj.","d":"An acronym standing for Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, and Queer, used to describe a community of diverse sexual orientations and gender identities.","c":"跨性別族群、多元性別（者）","s":"The university hosted a cultural festival to promote inclusion and support for all LGBTQ students on campus.","t":"這所大學舉辦了一場文化節，以促進對校園內所有多元性別（LGBTQ）學生的包容與支持。"},{"w":"sex","p":"n.","d":"either of the two main categories (male and female) into which humans and many other living things are divided on the basis of their reproductive functions.","c":"性別","s":"The knowledgeable bird watcher explained that we can easily determine the sex of the rare bird by its colorful feathers.","t":"知識淵博的賞鳥者解釋說，我們可以透過這隻罕見鳥類色彩繽紛的羽毛輕鬆決定牠的性別。"},{"w":"homosexual","p":"adj. / n. [C]","d":"Attracted to people of the same sex or gender; a person who is sexually attracted to the same sex.","c":"同性戀的；同性戀者","s":"While homosexual relationships are openly celebrated in many modern societies, some traditional cultures still hold biases.","t":"雖然同性戀關係在許多現代社會中被公開祝福，但一些傳統文化仍然抱持著成見。"},{"w":"heterosexual","p":"adj. / n. [C]","d":"Attracted to people of the opposite sex or gender; a straight person.","c":"異性戀的；異性戀者","s":"The researcher gathered data from both homosexual and heterosexual couples to study modern patterns in relationship communication.","t":"研究人員收集了同性戀和異性戀伴侶的數據，以研究現代伴侶溝通的模式。"},{"w":"complicate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more difficult or confusing by causing it to be more complex.","c":"使複雜","s":"Please do not needlessly complicate this incredibly simple plan by adding so many highly confusing extra steps.","t":"請不要因為增加這麼多極度令人困惑的額外步驟，而毫無必要地使這個極其簡單的計畫複雜化。"},{"w":"complicated","p":"adj.","d":"consisting of many interconnecting parts or elements; intricate.","c":"複雜的","s":"Building a custom computer from scratch can honestly be a highly complicated process for complete beginners to learn.","t":"從頭開始組裝一台客製化電腦，對完全的初學者來說，老實說可能是一個高度複雜的學習過程。"},{"w":"complication","p":"n.","d":"a circumstance that complicates something; a secondary disease or condition aggravating an already existing one.","c":"併發症；複雜化","s":"The fragile elderly patient unfortunately died from severe medical complication in his weak heart and damaged lungs.","t":"脆弱的年老病患不幸死於他虛弱心臟和受損肺部嚴重的醫療併發症。"},{"w":"medical complication","p":"phr.","d":"an unfavorable evolution or consequence of a disease, a health condition, or a therapy.","c":"醫療併發症","s":"If you don't carefully take your prescribed antibiotics, you might unfortunately develop a highly dangerous medical complication.","t":"如果你不仔細服用你被開立的抗生素，你可能會不幸地發展出高度危險的醫療併發症。"},{"w":"highly complicated","p":"phr.","d":"extremely intricate or difficult to understand or analyze.","c":"高度複雜的","s":"The brilliant engineer successfully designed a highly complicated mechanical system that effectively powers the entire massive factory.","t":"才華洋溢的工程師成功設計了一個高度複雜的機械系統，有效地為整個龐大的工廠提供動力。"},{"w":"stature","p":"n.","d":"a person's natural height; importance or reputation gained by ability or achievement.","c":"身材；聲望","s":"Extremely talented Stephen Curry is undeniably one of the NBA's best basketball players despite his relatively short stature.","t":"儘管他相對較矮的身材，極具才華的史蒂芬·柯瑞無疑是NBA最好的籃球員之一。"},{"w":"short stature","p":"phr.","d":"a condition in which a person is significantly shorter than the average height.","c":"身材矮小","s":"Despite his noticeably short stature, the courageous young man confidently stood up to the highly aggressive and mean bullies.","t":"儘管他明顯地身材矮小，這個勇敢的年輕人還是自信地挺身對抗那些極具攻擊性且刻薄的惡霸。"},{"w":"tall stature","p":"phr.","d":"the state of being significantly taller than average.","c":"身材高大","s":"Because of her exceptionally tall stature, the graceful girl was naturally very good at playing competitive high school volleyball.","t":"因為她異常地身材高大，這個優雅的女孩天生就很擅長打競爭激烈的高中排球。"},{"w":"physical stature","p":"phr.","d":"the size or natural height of someone's body.","c":"體格","s":"The professional wrestler's incredibly intimidating physical stature made all of his nervous opponents instantly fear him in the ring.","t":"職業摔角手極具威嚇力的體格，讓他所有緊張的對手在擂台上立刻害怕他。"},{"w":"disability","p":"n.","d":"a physical or mental condition that limits a person's movements, senses, or activities.","c":"殘疾","s":"Friendly Gary unfortunately has a permanent physical disability that sadly makes it extremely difficult for him to walk normally.","t":"友善的蓋瑞不幸地有一種永久性的身體殘疾，令人遺憾地使他極難正常行走。"},{"w":"disable","p":"v.","d":"to put out of action or limit the function of something.","c":"使失效；使殘廢","s":"The highly skilled computer technician had to quickly disable the dangerous virus before it could completely destroy the entire network.","t":"技術高超的電腦技術人員必須迅速使這個危險的病毒失效，以免它徹底摧毀整個網路。"},{"w":"disabled","p":"adj.","d":"having a physical or mental condition that limits movements, senses, or activities.","c":"殘疾的","s":"The modern and highly inclusive city government recently built several brand new ramps specifically for disabled citizens to use safely.","t":"現代且高度包容的市政府最近建造了幾個全新的坡道，專門供殘疾的公民安全使用。"},{"w":"learning disability","p":"phr.","d":"a condition giving rise to difficulties in acquiring knowledge and skills to the level expected of those of the same age.","c":"學習障礙","s":"If an energetic child actually has a learning disability, it definitely doesn't mean they aren't intelligent or highly capable.","t":"如果一個精力充沛的孩子實際上患有學習障礙，這絕對不代表他們不聰明或能力不強。"},{"w":"inability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being unable to do something.","c":"無能","s":"Lazy Luke's apparent inability to successfully handle daily office stress makes him completely unsuitable for the demanding management job.","t":"懶惰的盧克明顯對成功處理日常辦公室壓力感到無能，這使他完全不適合這份要求極高的管理工作。"},{"w":"risk","p":"v.","d":"to expose someone or something valued to danger, harm, or loss.","c":"冒險","s":"The ambitious entrepreneur decided to bravely risk all of his personal savings to successfully start his innovative new technology company.","t":"雄心勃勃的企業家決定勇敢地冒險投入他所有的個人積蓄，以成功創辦他創新的新科技公司。"},{"w":"risky","p":"adj.","d":"full of the possibility of danger, failure, or loss.","c":"冒險的","s":"Driving a small car through the snowy mountains would be far too risky, so we smartly chose a safer alternative route.","t":"開小車穿過雪山會太冒險的了，所以我們聰明地選擇了一條更安全的替代路線。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"a situation involving exposure to danger.","c":"風險","s":"The brave firefighter courageously put his own valuable life at absolute risk to safely save the terrified family from the burning building.","t":"勇敢的消防員英勇地將自己寶貴的生命置於絕對的風險之中，以安全地將受驚的家庭從燃燒的建築物中救出。"},{"w":"run the risk of","p":"phr.","d":"to do something that might cause something bad to happen.","c":"冒...的風險","s":"If you constantly refuse to eat healthy green vegetables, you run the risk of developing serious long-term medical illnesses.","t":"如果你不斷拒絕吃健康的綠色蔬菜，你就會冒著發展出嚴重的長期醫療疾病的風險。"},{"w":"take a risk","p":"phr.","d":"to proceed in an action without certainty of the outcome, exposing oneself to potential failure.","c":"冒險","s":"Sometimes in order to achieve truly massive success in the competitive business world, you simply must take a risk.","t":"有時候，為了在競爭激烈的商業世界中取得真正巨大的成功，你根本就必須冒險。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"n.","d":"a feature or quality belonging typically to a person, place, or thing and serving to identify it.","c":"特徵","s":"Unwavering patience is widely considered to be one of gentle Jeffrey's absolute finest and most admirable personal characteristics.","t":"堅定不移的耐心被廣泛認為是溫和的傑佛瑞絕對最優秀、最令人欽佩的個人特徵之一。"},{"w":"unique characteristic","p":"phr.","d":"an attribute or trait that sets something apart from all others.","c":"獨特特徵","s":"The beautiful rare bird's most unique characteristic is its bright blue feathers that beautifully shine brightly in the warm sunlight.","t":"這隻美麗稀有鳥類最獨特特徵是牠在溫暖的陽光下美麗地閃耀的明亮藍色羽毛。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"adj.","d":"typical of a particular person, place, or thing.","c":"獨特的","s":"The unique and incredibly colorful spices used in traditional Indian cooking definitely have a highly characteristic and unforgettable flavor.","t":"傳統印度烹飪中使用的獨特且極其色彩繽紛的香料，絕對有一種高度獨特的且令人難忘的風味。"},{"w":"characterize","p":"v.","d":"to describe the distinctive nature or features of.","c":"描繪...的特性","s":"Experienced historians typically characterize the long and peaceful era by its surprising lack of violent international military conflicts.","t":"經驗豐富的歷史學家通常以其令人驚訝地缺乏暴力的國際軍事衝突，來描繪這個漫長和平時代的特性。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person in a novel, play, or movie.","c":"角色","s":"The fascinating fictional character in the incredibly popular fantasy novel embarks on a highly dangerous and truly magical adventure.","t":"這本極受歡迎的奇幻小說中迷人的虛構角色，展開了一場高度危險且真正充滿魔力的冒險。"},{"w":"character","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The combination of mental and moral qualities that make a person unique; personality.","c":"個性、人格、品質","s":"Marcus has a very strong and reliable character; he always stays calm and helps others during a crisis.","t":"馬庫斯有著非常堅強且可靠的個性（人格）；在危機期間，他總能保持冷靜並幫助他人。"},{"w":"character","p":"n. [C]","d":"A letter, number, or symbol used in writing or printing.","c":"字元、文字、符號","s":"Passwords for this secure online system must be at least eight characters long and include a number.","t":"這個安全線上系統的密碼長度必須至少為八個字元（符號），且必須包含一個數字。"},{"w":"chinese character","p":"n. [C]","d":"A logographic sign or symbol used in the Chinese writing system.","c":"中文字、漢字","s":"Learning to write each Chinese character correctly requires a lot of patience and attention to stroke order.","t":"學習正確地書寫每個中文字（漢字），需要極大的耐心以及對筆畫順序的注意。"},{"w":"character traits","p":"n. phr.","d":"Individual aspects of a person's behavior and mind that define their personality.","c":"人格特質、個性特徵","s":"Kindness, honesty, and punctuality are positive character traitses that employers value highly.","t":"善良、誠實和守時是雇主非常看重的正面人格特質（個性特徵）。"},{"w":"main character","p":"n. [C]","d":"The most important person in a story, novel, movie, or play.","c":"主角、主要角色","s":"Chloe felt deeply moved by the struggles and growth of the main character in the fantasy novel.","t":"克洛伊被那部奇幻小說中主角（主要角色）的掙扎與成長深深打動。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n.","d":"an insistent and peremptory request, made as if by right.","c":"需求","s":"Because of the sudden and highly unexpected winter storm, the local demand for warm electric heaters increased drastically overnight.","t":"由於突然且極其出乎意料的冬季風暴，當地對溫暖電暖器的需求在一夜之間急劇增加。"},{"w":"demand","p":"v.","d":"to ask authoritatively or brusquely.","c":"要求","s":"The deeply upset and extremely angry customer aggressively demanded to immediately speak with the busy store manager about her completely broken product.","t":"深感沮喪且極度憤怒的顧客積極地要求立刻與忙碌的店經理談談她完全損壞的產品。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"requiring much skill or effort.","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"Working actively as a professional hospital surgeon is incredibly demanding with extremely long daily hours and highly intense pressure.","t":"積極地作為一名專業的醫院外科醫生工作是極其費力的（要求高的），每天的工時極長且壓力極大。"},{"w":"highly demanding","p":"phr.","d":"requiring a tremendous amount of effort, skill, or energy.","c":"要求極高的","s":"The rigorous university medical program is highly demanding and strictly requires all ambitious students to study intensely every single night.","t":"嚴格的大學醫學課程是要求極高的，並嚴格要求所有雄心勃勃的學生每晚都必須密集地學習。"},{"w":"physical demand","p":"phr.","d":"the physical exertion required to perform a specific task.","c":"體力要求","s":"The incredibly intense physical demand of running a full marathon naturally requires absolute dedication and months of exhausting daily training.","t":"跑完一場全程馬拉松極其強烈的體力要求，自然需要絕對的奉獻精神和數個月令人筋疲力盡的日常訓練。"},{"w":"in high demand","p":"phr.","d":"Wanted or needed by many people; extremely popular.","c":"需求量很大的、供不應求的","s":"Software engineers with prior knowledge of artificial intelligence are in high demand in today's tech industry.","t":"具備人工智慧先前知識的軟體工程師，在當今的科技產業中需求量極大。"},{"w":"in short supply","p":"phr.","d":"Available only in small quantities; hard to find or obtain.","c":"供應不足的、短缺的","s":"Fresh vegetables and clean drinking water were in short supply right after the severe typhoon hit the city.","t":"強烈颱風襲擊該市後，新鮮蔬菜和乾淨的飲用水隨即供應不足（短缺）。"},{"w":"shortage","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A situation where there is not enough of something that is needed.","c":"短缺、不足","s":"The international manufacturing factory is facing a serious shortage of raw materials due to shipping delays.","t":"由於航運延誤，這家國際製造廠正遭遇嚴重的原料短缺。"},{"w":"on demand","p":"phr.","d":"Available whenever someone asks for it or wants to use it.","c":"隨選的、一經要求即提供的","s":"Modern consumers prefer to watch their favorite television shows on demand rather than waiting for a weekly broadcast.","t":"現代消費者更喜歡隨選（隨選隨看）觀看他們最喜歡的電視節目，而不是等待每週的系統廣播。"},{"w":"ott","p":"n. [U] / adj.","d":"Over-The-Top; media services offered directly to viewers via the internet, bypassing traditional cable or satellite.","c":"串流媒體服務、串流的（意指串流影音平台）","s":"Netflix and Disney+ are famous OTT platforms that allow users to access thousands of movies on demand.","t":"Netflix 和 Disney+ 是著名的串流媒體（OTT）平台，讓使用者可以隨選觀看數千部電影。"},{"w":"live stream","p":"n. [C] / v.","d":"A live broadcast of an event over the internet, or to broadcast video over the internet in real time.","c":"直播、線上直播","s":"The popular English teacher held a live stream last night to interact with students and answer grammar questions.","t":"那位受歡迎的英文老師昨晚舉行了線上直播，與學生互動並解答文法問題。"},{"w":"streaming","p":"n. [U]","d":"The activity of listening to music or watching video directly from the internet without downloading it first.","c":"串流、影音串流","s":"With the rise of music streaming services, very few people buy traditional physical CDs anymore.","t":"隨著音樂串流服務的興起，現在已經很少有人會購買傳統的實體 CD 了。"},{"w":"stream","p":"v.","d":"To transmit or receive video and audio data over the internet as a continuous flow.","c":"串流傳輸、線上播放","s":"Users can easily stream their favorite movies on demand to their mobile tablets using a stable 5G network.","t":"使用者可以使用穩定的 5G 網路，輕鬆地將喜愛的電影串流傳輸（線上播放）到他們的手提平板上。"},{"w":"stream","p":"n. [C]","d":"A continuous flow of things or people; or a small, narrow river.","c":"連續不斷（的流動）；小河、溪流","s":"Marcus and Chloe sat on a rock next to a cold mountain stream to enjoy their packed lunch during the hike.","t":"馬庫斯和克洛伊在健行時，坐在冰涼的山間溪流（小河）旁的岩石上，享受他們準備好的便當。"},{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a routine task, especially a household one.","c":"雜務","s":"One of my most incredibly boring daily chores is to carefully take the smelly garbage outside every single night.","t":"我最極度無聊的日常雜務之一，就是每晚小心地把發臭的垃圾拿到外面。"},{"w":"do household chores","p":"phr.","d":"to perform the routine tasks associated with maintaining a home.","c":"做家事","s":"A lot of busy modern people absolutely hate having to do household chores because they find them incredibly tedious and boring.","t":"許多忙碌的現代人絕對討厭必須做家事，因為他們覺得這極其乏味且無聊。"},{"w":"do housework","p":"phr.","d":"to complete regular tasks required to keep a house clean and functional.","c":"做家事","s":"Because both of my parents work extremely long hours, we strictly divide and do housework equally on the relaxing weekends.","t":"因為我父母工作時間都極長，我們在放鬆的週末嚴格地平分並平等地做家事。"},{"w":"daily chore","p":"phr.","d":"a specific routine task that must be done every day.","c":"日常雜務","s":"Feeding the energetic and deeply hungry dogs is an incredibly important daily chore that I must strictly complete every single morning.","t":"餵養精力充沛且極度飢餓的狗是一項極其重要的日常雜務，我每天早上都必須嚴格完成。"},{"w":"caretaker","p":"n.","d":"a person employed to look after people or animals.","c":"照顧者","s":"Exhausted Mary is seriously considering officially hiring an experienced and deeply compassionate caretaker to help care for her fragile elderly mother.","t":"疲憊的瑪麗正認真考慮正式聘請一位經驗豐富且極具同情心的照顧者，來幫助照顧她脆弱的年老母親。"},{"w":"care","p":"n.","d":"the provision of what is necessary for the health, welfare, maintenance, and protection of someone or something.","c":"照顧","s":"The tiny and incredibly fragile prematurely born baby required absolute specialized medical care in the busy hospital for several stressful weeks.","t":"弱小且極其脆弱的早產兒在繁忙的醫院裡，需要長達數個充滿壓力星期的絕對專門醫療照顧。"},{"w":"care for","p":"phr.","d":"to look after and provide for the needs of.","c":"照顧","s":"It requires an incredibly massive amount of profound patience and gentle kindness to properly care for a severely sick person.","t":"適當地照顧一個重病患者，需要極其大量的深厚耐心和溫柔的善良。"},{"w":"take care of","p":"phr.","d":"to keep someone or something safe and provided for.","c":"照顧","s":"When my parents peacefully travel abroad, my reliable older sister will securely take care of our highly energetic golden retriever.","t":"當我父母平靜地出國旅行時，我可靠的姊姊將會穩妥地照顧我們精力高度充沛的黃金獵犬。"},{"w":"careful","p":"adj.","d":"making sure of avoiding potential danger, mishap, or harm.","c":"小心的","s":"You absolutely must be incredibly careful when you cautiously drive your expensive new car on these dangerously icy mountain roads.","t":"當你小心翼翼地在這些危險結冰的山路上駕駛你昂貴的新車時，你絕對必須極其小心的。"},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adj.","d":"strong, healthy, and full of energy.","c":"精力充沛的","s":"Professional football players must absolutely be incredibly vigorous athletes capable of maintaining a highly intense level of physical performance.","t":"職業美式足球員絕對必須是極其精力充沛的運動員，能夠維持高度激烈的體能表現水準。"},{"w":"vigorously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that involves physical strength, effort, or energy.","c":"精神旺盛地","s":"The highly enthusiastic crowd cheered vigorously as the victorious home team finally scored the exciting winning goal in the final seconds.","t":"當勝利的主場球隊終於在最後幾秒踢進令人興奮的致勝球時，極度熱情的群眾精神旺盛地歡呼。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"showing or involving great activity or vitality.","c":"精力充沛的","s":"The highly energetic young puppy happily ran rapidly around the massive green park for two entire completely exhausting hours today.","t":"高度精力充沛的年輕小狗，今天快樂地在巨大的綠色公園裡快速奔跑了整整兩個完全令人筋疲力盡的小時。"},{"w":"vigorous exercise","p":"phr.","d":"physical activity that is hard and involves a lot of effort.","c":"劇烈運動","s":"Because Vicki is currently recovering from being terribly ill, she's definitely not completely ready for extremely vigorous exercise just yet.","t":"因為薇琪目前正從重病中康復，她絕對還沒有完全準備好進行極其劇烈運動。"},{"w":"vigor","p":"n.","d":"physical strength and good health.","c":"活力","s":"The previously exhausted older man surprisingly completed the difficult and lengthy hiking trail with the incredible vigor of a much younger person.","t":"先前筋疲力盡的老人，令人驚訝地以年輕許多的人那種令人難以置信的活力，完成了困難且漫長的登山步道。"},{"w":"indulge","p":"v.","d":"to allow oneself to enjoy the pleasure of.","c":"沉溺於；享受","s":"Hardworking Alice will occasionally gracefully indulge in a highly expensive glass of imported red wine with her delicious weekend dinner.","t":"辛勤工作的愛麗絲偶爾會優雅地享受（沉溺於）一杯極其昂貴的進口紅酒，搭配她美味的週末晚餐。"},{"w":"indulge oneself in","p":"phr.","d":"to allow oneself a special pleasure.","c":"放縱自己","s":"After successfully finishing the highly stressful project, tired Jim indulged himself in entertainment and joyfully took another massive slice of sweet chocolate cake.","t":"在成功完成充滿壓力的專案後，疲憊的吉姆放縱自己，愉快地又拿了一大塊甜巧克力蛋糕。"},{"w":"indulgent","p":"adj.","d":"having or indicating a tendency to be overly generous to or lenient with someone.","c":"溺愛的","s":"The deeply loving but overly indulgent grandparents constantly bought their excited grandchildren absolutely everything they ever loudly demanded at the busy store.","t":"深愛但過度溺愛的祖父母，不斷在繁忙的商店裡為他們興奮的孫子買下絕對所有他們大聲要求的東西。"},{"w":"indulgence","p":"n.","d":"the action or fact of indulging.","c":"放縱","s":"Eating an entire massive box of rich chocolate cookies is undeniably a highly unhealthy indulgence that you should definitely strictly avoid.","t":"吃掉一整大盒濃郁的巧克力餅乾，無疑是一種極度不健康的放縱，你絕對應該嚴格避免。"},{"w":"edible","p":"adj.","d":"fit to be eaten.","c":"可食用的","s":"The beautifully carved decorative fruit on the table is absolutely not edible, so please carefully ensure that you don't actually eat it.","t":"桌上雕刻精美的裝飾性水果絕對不是可食用的，所以請小心確保你沒有真的吃掉它。"},{"w":"inedible","p":"adj.","d":"not fit for eating.","c":"不可食用的","s":"Because the careless chef entirely burned the expensive steak, the completely ruined meal was officially considered highly inedible.","t":"因為粗心的主廚完全把昂貴的牛排烤焦了，這頓徹底毀掉的餐點被官方認為是高度不可食用的。"},{"w":"rot","p":"v.","d":"to decay or cause to decay by the action of bacteria and fungi.","c":"腐爛","s":"If you carelessly leave fresh meat outside the cold refrigerator in the hot summer, it will inevitably rot quickly.","t":"如果你在炎熱的夏天粗心地把新鮮的肉留在冰冷的冰箱外面，它不可避免地會極快地腐爛。"},{"w":"rotten","p":"adj.","d":"suffering from decay.","c":"腐爛的","s":"You absolutely should promptly get rid of the terribly rotten fruit sitting on the table because it will quickly attract annoying bugs.","t":"你絕對應該迅速處理掉放在桌上那極度腐爛的水果，因為它會很快吸引煩人的蟲子。"},{"w":"completely rotten","p":"phr.","d":"entirely decayed and unusable.","c":"完全腐爛的","s":"When the homeowner finally returned after a long vacation, he discovered that the vegetables in the fridge were completely rotten.","t":"當屋主在漫長的假期後終於回來時，他發現冰箱裡的蔬菜已經完全腐爛的。"},{"w":"rotten fruit","p":"phr.","d":"fruit that has decayed.","c":"腐爛的水果","s":"The aggressive swarm of incredibly annoying flies was immediately attracted to the terribly rotten fruit that was carelessly left in the sunny kitchen.","t":"具攻擊性且極度煩人的蒼蠅群，立刻被粗心地留在陽光明媚廚房裡的極度腐爛的水果所吸引。"},{"w":"intake","p":"n.","d":"an amount of food, air, or another substance taken into the body.","c":"攝取量","s":"The strict medical doctor strongly suggested that you should definitely try to significantly limit your daily intake of highly processed sugar.","t":"嚴格的醫生強烈建議你絕對應該嘗試顯著限制你高度加工糖的每日攝取量。"},{"w":"daily intake","p":"phr.","d":"the total amount of something consumed in one day.","c":"每日攝取量","s":"Consuming a massive amount of fresh clean water is absolutely essential for strictly maintaining your highly recommended daily intake of hydration.","t":"飲用大量新鮮乾淨的水，對於嚴格維持你強烈建議的水分每日攝取量絕對是不可或缺的。"},{"w":"limit one's intake","p":"phr.","d":"to restrict the amount of food, drink, or substance one consumes.","c":"限制某人的攝取量","s":"To lose excess weight, you must limit your intake of fried foods and sugary drinks.","t":"為了減掉過多的體重，你必須限制油炸食物和含糖飲料的攝取量。"},{"w":"food intake","p":"phr.","d":"the quantity of food a person or animal consumes.","c":"食物攝取量","s":"The dedicated professional athlete meticulously tracks his entire food intake every single day to perfectly ensure he remains in top physical shape.","t":"盡責的職業運動員每天一絲不苟地追蹤他整個的食物攝取量，以完美確保他保持在頂尖的身體狀態。"},{"w":"water intake","p":"phr.","d":"the amount of water a person drinks.","c":"水分攝取量","s":"During the incredibly hot and humid summer months, drastically increasing your pure water intake is undeniably crucial to avoiding highly dangerous dehydration.","t":"在極其炎熱潮濕的夏季月份，大幅增加你純粹的水分攝取量無疑是避免高度危險脫水的關鍵。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen; unavoidable.","c":"無可避免的","s":"If the two aggressive countries absolutely don't repair their deeply damaged relationship soon, a highly destructive military war will be completely inevitable.","t":"如果這兩個具攻擊性的國家不快點修復他們嚴重受損的關係，一場極具破壞性的軍事戰爭將是完全無可避免的。"},{"w":"inevitably","p":"adv.","d":"as is certain to happen; unavoidably.","c":"無可避免地","s":"Because the lazy student consistently refused to study properly, he inevitably failed the highly difficult and incredibly important final university exam.","t":"因為懶惰的學生始終拒絕適當地學習，他無可避免地沒有通過極度困難且極其重要的大學期末考。"},{"w":"unavoidable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be avoided, prevented, or ignored; inevitable.","c":"無法避免的","s":"The massive traffic jam on the busy highway was entirely unavoidable after the surprisingly severe and highly destructive sudden car accident occurred.","t":"在發生了令人驚訝的嚴重且極具破壞性的突發車禍後，繁忙高速公路上的巨大交通堵塞是完全無法避免的。"},{"w":"completely inevitable","p":"phr.","d":"absolutely certain to happen.","c":"完全無可避免的","s":"Due to the company's terrible financial decisions and greedy management, its total public bankruptcy was eventually deemed completely inevitable by all expert analysts.","t":"由於公司糟糕的財務決策和貪婪的管理層，其徹底的公開破產最終被所有專家分析師認為是完全無可避免的。"},{"w":"diabetes","p":"n.","d":"a disease in which the body's ability to produce or respond to the hormone insulin is impaired.","c":"糖尿病","s":"Despite tragically learning from his doctor that he has severe diabetes, stubborn Shawn still constantly eats a massive amount of terribly unhealthy sweets.","t":"儘管悲慘地從醫生那裡得知自己患有嚴重的糖尿病，固執的尚恩仍然不斷吃下大量極度不健康的甜食。"},{"w":"diabetic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or suffering from diabetes.","c":"糖尿病的","s":"The specialized medical clinic provides customized and healthy daily meal plans for their fragile diabetic patients.","t":"這家專業的醫療診所，嚴格為其脆弱的糖尿病的病患提供客製化且健康的每日膳食計畫。"},{"w":"type 2 diabetes","p":"phr.","d":"a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar.","c":"第二型糖尿病","s":"Because of his incredibly poor diet and severe lack of daily exercise, the tired older man unfortunately developed type 2 diabetes.","t":"由於他極其糟糕的飲食和嚴重缺乏日常運動，這位疲憊的老人不幸罹患了第二型糖尿病。"},{"w":"suffer from diabetes","p":"phr.","d":"to experience the symptoms and health problems associated with diabetes.","c":"罹患糖尿病","s":"Millions of totally unsuspecting people globally currently suffer from diabetes but tragically do not actively know they have the serious illness yet.","t":"全球目前有數百萬完全毫無防備的人正罹患糖尿病，但悲慘的是他們尚未主動知道自己患有這種嚴重的疾病。"},{"w":"literally","p":"adv.","d":"in a literal manner or sense; exactly.","c":"簡直；字面上","s":"When excited Brian finally called and happily asked surprised Linda out on a romantic date, she literally danced around her messy bedroom.","t":"當興奮的布萊恩終於打電話並快樂地約驚訝的琳達進行浪漫約會時，她簡直在她雜亂的臥室裡跳起舞來。"},{"w":"literal","p":"adj.","d":"taking words in their usual or most basic sense without metaphor or allegory.","c":"字面上的","s":"The highly frustrated foreign student was deeply confused because he incorrectly translated the complex English idiom using its entirely literal meaning.","t":"這位極度挫折的外國學生深感困惑，因為他使用完全字面上的意思錯誤地翻譯了這個複雜的英文慣用語。"},{"w":"literal meaning","p":"phr.","d":"the exact or strict meaning of a word or phrase.","c":"字面意義","s":"If you simply look at the literal meaning of the strange phrase, it makes absolutely no sense in this deeply complex context.","t":"如果你只看這個奇怪片語的字面意義，在這個極其複雜的語境中它絕對不合理。"},{"w":"literally translated","p":"phr.","d":"translated word for word.","c":"直譯","s":"The beautiful and deeply emotional traditional poem, when literally translated into modern English, unfortunately loses a massive amount of its profound cultural charm.","t":"這首美麗且情感深厚的傳統詩歌，當直譯成現代英文時，不幸地失去了大量的深厚文化魅力。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"blur – make a difference","cards":[{"w":"blur","p":"n.","d":"a thing that cannot be seen or heard clearly.","c":"模糊不清的事物","s":"The speeding sports car was just a fast red blur as it rapidly drove past the amazed crowd.","t":"那輛超速的跑車在快速駛過驚訝的人群時，只是一團快速紅色的模糊不清的事物。"},{"w":"blur","p":"v.","d":"to make or become unclear or less distinct.","c":"使模糊","s":"The innovative new science fiction film completely blurs the traditional line between hilarious comedy and serious drama.","t":"這部創新的新科幻電影完全使搞笑喜劇和嚴肅戲劇之間的傳統界線模糊。"},{"w":"blur the line between","p":"phr.","d":"to make it difficult to distinguish between two different things.","c":"模糊...之間的界線","s":"Highly realistic modern video games often blur the line between exciting digital entertainment and real-life physical sports.","t":"高度逼真的現代電玩遊戲經常模糊刺激的數位娛樂與現實生活體育之間的界線。"},{"w":"blurred","p":"adj.","d":"unable to see or be seen clearly.","c":"模糊不清的","s":"Without his expensive prescription glasses, the frustrated student's vision was completely blurred in the bright classroom.","t":"沒有他昂貴的處方眼鏡，這位沮喪學生在明亮教室裡的視線是完全模糊不清的。"},{"w":"blurry","p":"adj.","d":"lacking clear definition or focus.","c":"模糊的","s":"Because the camera lens was incredibly dirty, all the vacation photos turned out to be terribly blurry.","t":"因為相機鏡頭極度骯髒，所有假期照片拍出來都非常模糊的。"},{"w":"formation","p":"n.","d":"the action of forming or process of being formed.","c":"形成；構成","s":"Her father's strict moral teachings undoubtedly contributed heavily to the early formation of her own political beliefs.","t":"她父親嚴格的道德教誨無疑地對她自身政治信仰的早期形成有著重大的貢獻。"},{"w":"cloud formation","p":"phr.","d":"the arrangement or structure of clouds in the sky.","c":"雲層結構","s":"Anna confidently says that those dark and heavy cloud formation are a clear sign that a big storm is coming.","t":"安娜自信地說，那些黑暗厚重的雲層結構是強大風暴即將來臨的明顯跡象。"},{"w":"form","p":"v.","d":"to bring together parts or combine to create; the visible shape or configuration of something.","c":"形成；形狀","s":"The intelligent students decided to officially form a dedicated study group to carefully prepare for the difficult final exams.","t":"聰明的學生們決定正式形成（組成）一個專門的讀書小組，以仔細準備困難的期末考。"},{"w":"form","p":"n. [C]","d":"A type, kind, or appearance of something; or a document with blanks to fill in.","c":"形式、類型；表格","s":"Please fill out this application form with your prior work experience before submitting it to the HR manager.","t":"在將這份申請表格提交給人事經理之前，請先填寫您的過往工作經驗。"},{"w":"in the form of","p":"phr.","d":"Having the shape, type, or appearance of a specific thing.","c":"以…的形式、以…的方式","s":"The university provided financial assistance to the low-income student in the form of a monthly scholarship.","t":"這所大學以按月發放獎學金的形式，向這位低收入學生提供經濟援助。"},{"w":"art form","p":"n. [C]","d":"An activity or a field of expression that is considered a type of art, such as painting or dance.","c":"藝術形式","s":"Photography has been recognized as a serious art form that can capture deep human emotions.","t":"攝影已被公認為一種能夠捕捉人類深刻情感的嚴肅藝術形式。"},{"w":"formation","p":"n. [U, C]","d":"The process of bringing something into existence, or the specific way things are arranged.","c":"形成、構成；隊形、排列","s":"Extreme changes in temperature over millions of years led to the formation of these unique mountain rocks.","t":"數百萬年來極端的溫度變化，導致了這些獨特山岩的形成。"},{"w":"formless","p":"adj.","d":"without a clear or definite shape or structure.","c":"無定形的","s":"The mysterious magical creature appeared as a dark, formless shadow slowly moving across the completely silent room.","t":"那個神秘的魔法生物看起來像一個黑暗、無定形的影子，緩慢地穿過完全安靜的房間。"},{"w":"development","p":"n.","d":"the process of developing or being developed.","c":"發展","s":"The rapid technological development of advanced smartphones has significantly changed how humans quickly communicate with each other.","t":"先進智慧型手機快速的技術發展，已經顯著改變了人類彼此快速溝通的方式。"},{"w":"evolve","p":"v.","d":"to develop gradually, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","c":"演變；進化","s":"Our complicated science project eventually evolved into something that was quite remarkably different from what we originally planned.","t":"我們複雜的科學專案最終演變成一個與我們最初計畫相當顯著不同的東西。"},{"w":"evolution","p":"n.","d":"the gradual development of something, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","c":"演化；發展","s":"The fascinating evolution of modern computer technology over the last few decades has completely changed human society.","t":"過去幾十年間現代電腦科技迷人的演化已經徹底改變了人類社會。"},{"w":"evolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the gradual development of something.","c":"演化的","s":"The brilliant biology professor taught a highly complex course about the evolutionary history of strange deep-sea creatures.","t":"才華洋溢的生物學教授教授了一門關於奇異深海生物演化的歷史的高度複雜課程。"},{"w":"involve","p":"v.","d":"to have or include something as a necessary part.","c":"包含；牽涉","s":"This highly demanding corporate management job will definitely involve traveling to many different foreign countries every single month.","t":"這份要求極高的企業管理工作絕對會包含每個月到許多不同的外國國家出差。"},{"w":"be involved in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To take part in an activity, event, or situation, or to be deeply connected with it.","c":"參與…、涉入…、捲入…","s":"Marcus decided to be actively involved in the local charity project to help low-income families.","t":"馬庫斯決定積極參與當地的慈善計畫，以幫助低收入家庭。"},{"w":"revolve","p":"v.","d":"to move in a circle on a central axis.","c":"旋轉；圍繞","s":"The knowledgeable astronomy teacher clearly explained that the Earth naturally revolves around the glowing sun once a year.","t":"知識淵博的天文學老師清楚地解釋說，地球每年自然地圍繞發光的太陽旋轉一次。"},{"w":"revolve around","p":"v. phr.","d":"To move in a circular path around a central object; or to have something as the main interest or focus.","c":"圍繞…旋轉、以…為中心","s":"For the first few months, a new mother's daily schedule will completely revolve around her baby's needs.","t":"在最初的幾個月裡，新手媽媽的每日行程將完全以寶寶的需求為中心（圍繞著寶寶的需求）。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A complete circular movement made by an object around a central point.","c":"環繞、旋轉、公轉","s":"It takes about 365 days for the Earth to complete one full revolution around the sun.","t":"地球繞太陽完成一次完整的公轉（環繞）大約需要 365 天。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n. [C, U]","d":"A violent or total change in a country's political system, or a major change in ideas or methods.","c":"革命、重大變革","s":"The Industrial revolution in the 18th century completely changed the way goods were manufactured and produced.","t":"18 世紀的工業革命徹底改變了貨物的製造與生產方式。"},{"w":"revolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"Involving or causing a complete and dramatic change in ideas, methods, or systems.","c":"革命性的、突破性的、大變革的","s":"The research team developed a revolutionary new medicine that could successfully cure the genetic defect.","t":"研究團隊研發出了一種革命性的（突破性的）新藥，能夠成功治療該基因缺陷。"},{"w":"revolutionize","p":"v.","d":"To completely change the way something is done, built, or thought about.","c":"徹底改變、改革、帶來革命性變革","s":"The invention of smartphones has completely revolutionized the way modern people communicate and access information on demand.","t":"智慧型手機的發明，徹底改變了（帶來革命性變革）現代人溝通與隨選獲取資訊的方式。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is excluded from a general statement or does not follow a rule.","c":"例外","s":"I usually manage to sleep very peacefully at night, but last night's terrible loud thunderstorm was a major exception.","t":"我通常晚上都能睡得非常平靜，但昨晚可怕響亮的雷暴是一個重大的例外。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; outstanding.","c":"卓越的；例外的","s":"Jerry is truly an exceptional employee who consistently works incredibly hard and contributes significantly to our modern company.","t":"傑瑞真的是一位卓越的員工，他始終極其努力地工作，並對我們現代公司做出了重大貢獻。"},{"w":"exceptional circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"highly unusual or uncommon situations.","c":"例外情況","s":"The strict international company naturally only tolerates employee lateness in highly exceptional circumstances, such as severe transportation strikes.","t":"這家嚴格的國際公司自然只在高度的例外情況下容許員工遲到，例如嚴重的交通罷工。"},{"w":"exceptionally","p":"adv.","d":"to a greater degree than normal; unusually.","c":"異常地；非常","s":"Because the winter weather was exceptionally cold, the local government urgently opened extra shelters for the homeless citizens.","t":"因為冬季天氣異常地寒冷，當地政府緊急為無家可歸的公民開放了額外的庇護所。"},{"w":"extraordinary","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or remarkable.","c":"非凡的","s":"The brave young firefighter showed truly extraordinary courage when he bravely ran into the violently burning wooden house.","t":"這位勇敢的年輕消防員在勇敢跑進猛烈燃燒的木屋時，展現了真正非凡的勇氣。"},{"w":"span","p":"v. / n.","d":"to extend across in space or time; the full extent of something from end to end.","c":"橫跨；跨度","s":"The terrible economic impact from the sudden financial crisis unfortunately spanned every single dark corner of the struggling economy.","t":"突發金融危機造成的可怕經濟影響，不幸地橫跨了這個苦苦掙扎的經濟的每一個黑暗角落。"},{"w":"lifespan","p":"n.","d":"the length of time for which a person or animal lives or a thing functions.","c":"壽命","s":"Because of highly advanced modern medicine, the average human lifespan has significantly increased over the past entire century.","t":"因為高度先進的現代醫學，人類的平均壽命在過去整整一個世紀中已經顯著增加。"},{"w":"attention span","p":"n.","d":"the length of time a person can concentrate on a task without becoming distracted.","c":"注意力持續時間","s":"Teachers frequently complain that young children who constantly watch short internet videos have an incredibly brief attention span.","t":"老師們經常抱怨，不斷觀看網路短影音的幼童，其注意力持續時間極其短暫。"},{"w":"span across","p":"phr.","d":"to stretch completely from one side to another.","c":"橫跨","s":"The massive new steel bridge was specifically designed to beautifully span across the incredibly wide and deep river.","t":"這座巨大的新鋼橋被專門設計來美麗地橫跨這條極其寬闊且深邃的河流。"},{"w":"apart from","p":"phr.","d":"except for; in addition to.","c":"除了...之外","s":"Apart from the friendly guy named Fred, clever Janice has also proudly won several expensive prizes for her competitive roller skating.","t":"除了那個名叫弗雷德的友善男孩之外，聰明的珍妮絲也自豪地贏得了幾個競爭激烈的溜直排輪昂貴獎項。"},{"w":"apart","p":"adv.","d":"separated by a distance; into pieces.","c":"分開地","s":"Because they live in completely different countries, the two loving brothers have sadly lived far apart for years.","t":"因為他們住在完全不同的國家，這兩個充滿愛的兄弟令人遺憾地已經遠遠分開地生活了幾年。"},{"w":"fall apart","p":"phr.","d":"to break into pieces; to lose one's capacity to cope.","c":"散開；崩潰","s":"The cheap old wooden chair finally began to completely fall apart after being left outside in the pouring rain.","t":"那把便宜的舊木椅在傾盆大雨中被留在外面後，終於開始完全散開（解體）。"},{"w":"take apart","p":"phr.","d":"to separate something into its individual pieces.","c":"拆開","s":"The curious young boy carefully managed to take apart the broken radio to see exactly how it worked inside.","t":"好奇的小男孩小心翼翼地設法拆開了壞掉的收音機，想看看它裡面到底是如何運作的。"},{"w":"tell apart","p":"phr.","d":"to distinguish one person or thing from another.","c":"分辨","s":"The identical twin sisters look so incredibly similar that even their own closest friends cannot tell them apart easily.","t":"這對同卵雙胞胎姊妹看起來如此極度相似，以至於連她們自己最親密的朋友都無法輕易將她們分辨。"},{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make an action or process easy or easier.","c":"促進；使便利","s":"The brand new interactive teaching material specifically facilitates incredibly fast and effective learning for the young students in class.","t":"全新的互動教學教材特別促進了課堂上年輕學生極其快速且有效的學習。"},{"w":"facilitator","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that makes an action or process easy or easier.","c":"促進者；引導者","s":"The highly trained professional facilitator ensured that the difficult business negotiation smoothly proceeded without any angry physical arguments.","t":"訓練有素的專業引導者確保了困難的商業談判順利進行，沒有發生任何憤怒的肢體爭論。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a place, amenity, or piece of equipment provided for a particular purpose.","c":"設施","s":"The highly prestigious international university proudly boasts an incredibly modern sports facility available for all of its hardworking students.","t":"這所極具聲望的國際大學自豪地擁有一座極其現代化的體育設施，供其所有辛勤的學生使用。"},{"w":"highly facilitated","p":"phr.","d":"made significantly easier or smoother by someone or something.","c":"高度促進的","s":"The massive global trade agreement was highly facilitated by the dedicated efforts of the brilliant foreign political ambassadors.","t":"這項龐大的全球貿易協定，是在才華洋溢的外國政治大使的盡責努力下被高度促進的。"},{"w":"encounter","p":"n.","d":"an unexpected or casual meeting with someone or something; to unexpectedly experience.","c":"相遇；遭遇","s":"An exciting weekend trip to the massive city zoo gave little Jim his very first terrifying encounter with dangerous snakes.","t":"週末去大型城市動物園的刺激旅行，給了小吉姆他第一次與危險蛇類可怕的相遇。"},{"w":"encounter","p":"v.","d":"To experience something unexpected or difficult, or to meet someone by chance.","c":"遭遇（困難/問題）、不期而遇","s":"The project team might encounter some technical difficulties when trying to update the online testing system.","t":"專案團隊在試圖更新線上測驗系統時，可能會遭遇一些技術上的困難。"},{"w":"close encounter","p":"phr.","d":"a situation in which one comes very near to something dangerous or unusual.","c":"近距離接觸","s":"The brave hiker had an incredibly close encounter with a massive angry bear while wandering deep in the dark woods.","t":"勇敢的登山客在黑暗的森林深處漫遊時，與一隻巨大的憤怒熊有了一次令人難以置信的近距離接觸。"},{"w":"unexpected encounter","p":"phr.","d":"a meeting that happens without warning or planning.","c":"意外相遇","s":"Michelle had a completely unexpected encounter with a famous Hollywood movie star while nervously waiting at the busy international airport.","t":"蜜雪兒在繁忙的國際機場緊張地等待時，與一位著名的好萊塢電影明星有了一次完全的意外相遇。"},{"w":"bump into","p":"phr. v.","d":"To meet someone you know completely by chance when you did not expect to see them.","c":"巧遇、不期而遇、撞見","s":"Marcus was surprised to bump into his former English teacher at the Japanese buffet restaurant last night.","t":"馬庫斯昨晚在一家日本自助餐廳巧遇他以前的英文老師，感到非常驚喜。"},{"w":"run into","p":"phr. v.","d":"To meet someone by accident, or to experience unexpected problems or difficulties.","c":"巧遇、遇見；遭遇（困難）","s":"While traveling in Tokyo, Chloe happened to run into an old college classmate she hadn't seen for years.","t":"在東京旅行時，克洛伊碰巧巧遇了一位多年未見的大學舊同學。"},{"w":"face","p":"v.","d":"to confront and deal with or accept a difficult or unpleasant task or situation.","c":"面對","s":"The struggling company will inevitably face complete financial disaster if it doesn't quickly improve its terrible daily sales.","t":"如果這家苦苦掙扎的公司不迅速大幅改善其糟糕的日常銷售，它將無可避免地面對的財務災難。"},{"w":"be faced with","p":"v. phr.","d":"To have to deal with a difficult situation, problem, or choice.","c":"面臨…、面對…（通常指困難、挑戰）","s":"When the manufacturing factory closed down, Marcus was faced with the urgent need to find a new job.","t":"當製造工廠倒閉時，馬庫斯面臨著尋找新工作的迫切需求。"},{"w":"in the face of","p":"phr.","d":"While experiencing or dealing with a difficult situation, danger, or opposition.","c":"面對…、在…面前（通常指不畏艱難）","s":"Chloe remained completely calm in the face of danger and successfully guided the lost tourists out of the dark cave.","t":"面對危險，克洛伊保持完全冷靜，並成功引導迷路的遊客走出了黑暗的山洞。"},{"w":"face-to-face communication","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of talking directly to another person while being in the same physical place.","c":"面對面溝通","s":"Although text messages are convenient, face-to-face communication is still the best way to resolve serious personal conflicts.","t":"雖然簡訊很方便，但面對面溝通仍然是解決嚴重個人衝突的最佳方式。"},{"w":"enrich","p":"v.","d":"to improve or enhance the quality or value of.","c":"豐富","s":"The passionate history teacher uses deeply fascinating traditional stories to perfectly enrich the young students' understanding of ancient cultures.","t":"熱情的歷史老師使用極其迷人的傳統故事，來完美地豐富年輕學生對古代文化的理解。"},{"w":"enrichment","p":"n.","d":"the action of improving or enhancing the quality or value of something.","c":"豐富；充實","s":"Joey's wealthy parents constantly took him on lots of educational trips abroad, which definitely brought incredible enrichment to his childhood.","t":"喬伊富有的父母不斷帶他去國外進行許多教育旅行，這絕對為他的童年帶來了令人難以置信的豐富（充實）。"},{"w":"enriched","p":"adj.","d":"having added nutrients or improved quality.","c":"營養強化的；豐富的","s":"This completely healthy and delicious morning bread is specially enriched with extremely vital vitamins and important natural minerals.","t":"這款完全健康且美味的早晨麵包特別用極其重要的維生素和重要的天然礦物質進行了營養強化的。"},{"w":"enriching","p":"adj.","d":"providing rewarding value or improving the quality of something.","c":"使人充實的","s":"Volunteering at the crowded local animal shelter was a deeply enriching experience that taught the teenager absolute responsibility.","t":"在擁擠的當地動物收容所當志工是一次深深使人充實的經歷，教會了這個青少年絕對的責任感。"},{"w":"marvel","p":"n. / v.","d":"a wonderful or astonishing person or thing; to be filled with wonder or astonishment.","c":"奇蹟；感到驚嘆","s":"My knowledgeable grandfather always happily says that modern smart mobile phones are a truly incredible marvel of advanced modern technology.","t":"我知識淵博的祖父總是快樂地說，現代智慧型手機真的是先進現代科技一個令人難以置信的奇蹟。"},{"w":"marvel at","p":"phr.","d":"to look at or consider something with great surprise or admiration.","c":"對...感到驚嘆","s":"The romantic young couple silently stood outside to completely marvel at the breathtaking beauty of the incredibly bright shining stars.","t":"浪漫的年輕夫婦安靜地站在外面，完全對極其明亮閃耀星星令人驚嘆的美麗感到驚嘆。"},{"w":"marvelous","p":"adj.","d":"causing great wonder; extraordinary.","c":"極好的；令人驚嘆的","s":"The famous restaurant serves absolutely marvelous food that consistently attracts incredibly hungry and excited customers from all over the city.","t":"這家著名餐廳提供絕對極好的食物，不斷吸引來自城市各處極度飢餓且興奮的顧客。"},{"w":"marvelously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes great wonder or is extraordinarily good.","c":"奇蹟般地；極好地","s":"The highly talented classical piano player performed so marvelously that the completely amazed audience loudly cheered for several long minutes.","t":"這位極具才華的古典鋼琴家表演得如此極好地，以至於完全驚訝的觀眾大聲歡呼了幾段漫長的分鐘。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"charming and attractive; capturing attention.","c":"迷人的；吸引人的","s":"The colorful new fantasy video game was so deeply engaging that I completely lost track of the entire long afternoon.","t":"這款色彩繽紛的新奇幻電玩遊戲如此深深地吸引人的，以至於我完全忘了整個漫長的下午時間。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to occupy, attract, or involve someone's interest or attention.","c":"吸引；參與","s":"The passionate teacher uses completely fun and interactive daily activities to successfully engage her easily distracted and highly energetic students.","t":"熱情的老師使用完全有趣且互動的日常活動，成功地吸引她容易分心且精力高度充沛的學生。"},{"w":"engage in","p":"phr.","d":"to participate or become involved in.","c":"參與","s":"The incredibly tired manager was entirely too distracted to properly engage in their complex conversation about the new financial project.","t":"極度疲憊的經理完全太分心了，無法適當地參與他們關於新財務專案複雜的對話。"},{"w":"be engaged to sb","p":"v. phr.","d":"Having formally agreed to marry a specific person in the future.","c":"與某人訂婚","s":"After dating happily for over five years, Marcus announced that he was engaged to Chloe.","t":"在快樂地交往了五年多之後，馬庫斯宣布他已經與克洛伊訂婚了。"},{"w":"be engaged in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To be deeply busy, occupied, or involved in a specific activity or situation.","c":"正從事於…、忙於…、參與…","s":"The research team is currently engaged in a long-term scientific study regarding genetic defects.","t":"該研究團隊目前正從事於（忙於）一項關於基因缺陷的長期科學研究。"},{"w":"engage in (an activity)","p":"v. phr.","d":"To take part in or do a specific activity, discussion, or behavior.","c":"參加…、進行…、從事…（活動）","s":"Doctors strongly recommend that elderly people engage in light regular exercise to keep their hearts healthy.","t":"醫生強烈建議年長者進行（從事）規律的輕度運動，以保持心臟健康。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"the act of participation.","c":"訂婚；參與","s":"After dating for five wonderful years, the truly happy couple finally announced their incredibly exciting official romantic engagement.","t":"在度過美好的五年約會後，這對真正幸福的夫婦終於宣布了他們極其令人興奮的正式浪漫訂婚。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"Interesting, charming, and keeping your attention completely.","c":"迷人的、有吸引力的、引人入勝的","s":"The experienced English teacher designed an engaging web-based game that kept the students motivated to practice spelling.","t":"這位經驗豐富的英文老師設計了一款引人入勝的（有吸引力的）網頁遊戲，讓學生們保持練習拼字的動力。"},{"w":"take part in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To participate or be involved in an activity, event, or sport with other people.","c":"參加…、參與…","s":"Marcus encourages his children to take part in outdoor sports to stay healthy and build a strong character.","t":"馬庫斯鼓勵他的孩子們參加戶外運動，以保持健康並培養堅強的個性。"},{"w":"participate in","p":"v. phr.","d":"To take part in an event, a game, an activity, or an organized group.","c":"參加…、參與…","s":"Hundreds of international students from Taipei decided to participate in the summer English camp last year.","t":"去年，數百名來自台北的國際學生決定參加（參與）這場夏季英語營。"},{"w":"participant","p":"n. [C]","d":"A person who takes part in a specific activity, event, or research study.","c":"參與者、參加者","s":"Each participant in the financial investment seminar will receive a professional certificate after completing the course.","t":"這場金融投資研討會的每位參與者在完成課程後，都將獲得一張專業證書。"},{"w":"participation","p":"n. [U]","d":"The act of taking part in an activity, event, or discussion.","c":"參與、參加","s":"Active participation in classroom discussions is highly valued and will count toward your final grade.","t":"積極參與課堂討論是備受看重的，且會計入你的期末成績。"},{"w":"charming","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant or attractive.","c":"迷人的","s":"The highly polite and naturally charming young man easily made a completely wonderful first impression on his strict future boss.","t":"這位極度有禮貌且天生迷人的年輕人，輕鬆地給他嚴格的未來老闆留下了一個完全美好的第一印象。"},{"w":"reproduce","p":"v.","d":"to produce a copy or representation of; to produce offspring.","c":"複製；繁殖","s":"This highly advanced and incredibly expensive office photocopier can accurately reproduce beautiful and complex color photographs in just a few seconds.","t":"這台高度先進且極其昂貴的辦公室影印機，能在短短幾秒鐘內準確地複製美麗且複雜的彩色照片。"},{"w":"reproduction","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of making a copy of something; the production of offspring.","c":"複製品；繁殖","s":"The historical museum beautifully proudly displays a highly perfect reproduction of an extremely famous ancient Roman statue for curious tourists.","t":"歷史博物館美麗自豪地為好奇的遊客展示了一尊極其著名的古羅馬雕像的完美複製品。"},{"w":"reproductive","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or effecting reproduction.","c":"生殖的","s":"The brilliant scientist passionately studies the incredibly complex reproductive cycle of several completely rare and highly endangered exotic wild birds.","t":"才華洋溢的科學家熱情地研究幾種完全稀有且高度瀕危的異國野鳥極其複雜的生殖的週期。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"to make or manufacture from components or raw materials.","c":"生產","s":"The highly efficient new factory uses heavily automated machines to quickly produce thousands of extremely cheap plastic toys every day.","t":"高效率的新工廠使用重度自動化的機器，每天快速生產數千個極其便宜的塑膠玩具。"},{"w":"producer","p":"n.","d":"a person, company, or country that makes, grows, or supplies goods or commodities for sale.","c":"生產者；製作人","s":"The highly powerful Hollywood producer angrily demanded that the nervous director drastically change the boring ending of the movie.","t":"權力極大的好萊塢製作人憤怒地要求緊張的導演大幅改變電影無聊的結局。"},{"w":"representative","p":"n. / adj.","d":"a person chosen or appointed to act or speak for another or others; typical of a class, group, or body of opinion.","c":"代表；具代表性的","s":"His massive financial success as a dedicated businessman is highly representative of exactly what extremely hard work can accomplish.","t":"他作為一位盡責商人巨大的財務成功，高度具代表性的展示了極度努力工作究竟能成就什麼。"},{"w":"representative of","p":"phr.","d":"serving as a typical example of something.","c":"...的代表","s":"At the massive international trade show, Shawn confidently acted as a highly professional representative of this growing global technology company.","t":"在大型國際貿易展上，尚恩自信地擔任這家不斷成長的全球科技公司高度專業的代表。"},{"w":"represent","p":"v.","d":"to be entitled or appointed to act or speak for someone.","c":"代表","s":"The highly skilled and incredibly expensive lawyer will formally represent the totally innocent man during the highly publicized and stressful trial.","t":"技術高超且極其昂貴的律師，將在高度公開且充滿壓力的審判中正式代表這個完全無辜的男人。"},{"w":"representation","p":"n.","d":"the action of speaking or acting on behalf of someone or the state of being so represented.","c":"表現；代表","s":"The community strongly demands completely fair and deeply equal political representation in the highly powerful national government without any hesitation.","t":"社區強烈要求在權力極大的國家政府中毫不猶豫地獲得完全公平且深刻平等的政治代表。"},{"w":"sales representative","p":"phr.","d":"an employee of a company who travels around a particular area selling the company's goods to shops and other businesses.","c":"業務代表","s":"The enthusiastic and highly persuasive sales representative cleverly managed to quickly sell the incredibly expensive new software to the hesitant client.","t":"熱情且極具說服力的業務代表巧妙地設法迅速將極其昂貴的新軟體賣給了猶豫不決的客戶。"},{"w":"on behalf of","p":"phr.","d":"As the representative of someone else, or speaking and acting for them.","c":"代表…、替…","s":"Chloe accepted the professional teaching award on behalf of the entire English department.","t":"克洛伊代表整個英文學系接受了這座專業教學獎。"},{"w":"stand for","p":"phr. v.","d":"To represent a word, an idea, or a belief, especially as an abbreviation or a symbol.","c":"代表（字詞縮寫）；象徵、主張","s":"In the field of digital media, the letters OTT stand for \"Over-The-Top\" streaming services.","t":"在數位媒體領域中，字母 OTT 代表「串流媒體（Over-The-Top）」服務。"},{"w":"symbolize","p":"v.","d":"To be a symbol of something, or to represent a deeper quality or feeling.","c":"象徵、代表","s":"In many fantasy novels, the white horse is used to symbolize purity, justice, and absolute goodness.","t":"在許多奇幻小說中，白馬被用來象徵純潔、正義與絕對的善良。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n. [C]","d":"A sign, shape, or object that is used to represent something else, such as an idea or quality.","c":"象徵、標誌、符號","s":"The dove has long been recognized globally as a universal symbol of peace and unbiased harmony.","t":"鴿子長期以來在全球被公認為和平與無偏見和諧的通用象徵。"},{"w":"be symbolic of","p":"v. phr.","d":"Serving as a symbol, or representing something else in a significant way.","c":"象徵…的、代表…的","s":"The lighting of the Olympic flame is deeply symbolic of unity and friendship among different nations.","t":"奧運聖火的點燃，深深象徵著不同國家之間的團結與友誼。"},{"w":"destination","p":"n.","d":"the place to which someone or something is going or being sent.","c":"目的地","s":"Belize is widely famous globally as a relatively cheap vacation destination featuring truly great ocean diving and completely beautiful relaxing beaches.","t":"貝里斯作為一個相對便宜的度假目的地在全球廣為人知，以真正絕佳的海洋潛水和完全美麗放鬆的海灘為特色。"},{"w":"tourist destination","p":"phr.","d":"a place that is popular with people who are on holiday.","c":"旅遊勝地","s":"The incredibly historic and perfectly preserved ancient European city remains an extremely popular tourist destination for completely eager international travelers.","t":"這座極具歷史意義且保存完美的古老歐洲城市，仍然是熱切國際旅客極受歡迎的旅遊勝地。"},{"w":"tourist attraction","p":"n. [C]","d":"A place of interest that people visit for pleasure, culture, or entertainment.","c":"觀光景點、旅遊勝地","s":"Taipei 101 is a world-famous tourist attraction that draws millions of international visitors to Taiwan every year.","t":"台北101是一個世界聞名的觀光景點，每年都吸引數百萬國際遊客來到台灣。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n. [C]","d":"A building or feature that is easily recognized, especially one that guides people or has historical importance.","c":"地標、里程碑","s":"The historic red brick station building serves as a major landmark in the center of Tokyo.","t":"這座歷史悠久的紅磚車站建築是東京市中心的一個重要地標。"},{"w":"scenic spot","p":"n. [C]","d":"A specific place known for its beautiful natural views and landscapes.","c":"風景區、景點","s":"The mountain hot spring resort is a popular scenic spot where travelers can enjoy beautiful lake views.","t":"這座山區溫泉度假村是一個受歡迎的風景區（景點），旅客可以在那裡欣賞美麗的湖景。"},{"w":"wander","p":"v.","d":"to walk or move in a leisurely, casual, or aimless way.","c":"漫遊；徘徊","s":"Completely lost Shawn sadly wandered the dark and rainy city streets, having absolutely no idea where he actually needed to securely go.","t":"完全迷路的尚恩悲傷地在黑暗多雨的城市街道上徘徊，完全不知道他實際上需要安全地去哪裡。"},{"w":"wander off","p":"phr.","d":"to leave a place or group without permission or unexpectedly.","c":"走失；離開","s":"Irresponsible parents should never allow their energetic young children to wander off alone in the massive park.","t":"不負責任的父母不應該舒服地允許他們精力充沛的幼童，單獨在巨大的公園裡走失（離開）。"},{"w":"wandering","p":"adj.","d":"traveling aimlessly from place to place.","c":"漫遊的；流浪的","s":"The lonely wandering dog desperately searched the completely empty alleyways for absolutely any small scraps of leftover human food.","t":"孤獨流浪的狗拚命地在完全空蕩的巷弄裡尋找任何微小的人類殘羹剩飯。"},{"w":"wander around","p":"phr.","d":"to walk around a place casually without a specific goal.","c":"四處閒逛","s":"During our relaxing summer vacation, we decided to wander around the charming old town for hours.","t":"在我們輕鬆的暑假中，我們決定在這座迷人的老城鎮裡四處閒逛好幾個小時。"},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to make a formal application or request.","c":"申請","s":"If you genuinely want this highly competitive internship, you absolutely must completely apply for it before the incredibly strict Friday deadline.","t":"如果你真心想要這個競爭高度激烈的實習，你絕對必須在極其嚴格的星期五截止日期前完全申請它。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a formal request to an authority for something; the action of putting something into operation.","c":"應用；申請","s":"This complex new mechanical tool that has just recently been invented actually has many completely different and highly useful practical application.","t":"這個剛發明不久的複雜新機械工具，實際上擁有許多完全不同且非常實用的應用。"},{"w":"job application","p":"phr.","d":"a formal request to be considered for a position of employment.","c":"求職申請","s":"Nadia confidently gave her detailed job application to the busy secretary and was completely surprisingly soon called back for a formal interview.","t":"納迪婭自信地將她詳細的求職申請交給忙碌的秘書，並完全令人驚訝地很快被叫回去進行正式面試。"},{"w":"fill in the application form","p":"v. phr.","d":"To complete a document by writing down your personal details and answers in the blanks.","c":"填寫申請表","s":"Please remember to fill in the application form completely before submitting your resume to the HR manager.","t":"在將您的履歷提交給人事經理之前，請記得完整地填寫申請表。"},{"w":"applicant","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes a formal application for something, typically a job.","c":"申請人","s":"The strict international technology company received over five hundred impressive resumes from incredibly hopeful applicant for the single management position.","t":"這家嚴格的國際科技公司收到了超過五百份來自極度充滿希望的申請人的令人印象深刻的履歷，只為了這一個管理職位。"},{"w":"applicable","p":"adj.","d":"relevant or appropriate.","c":"適用的","s":"The complex safety rules carefully described in this completely detailed manual are strictly applicable to absolutely everyone working in the busy factory.","t":"這本極其詳細的手冊中仔細描述的複雜安全規定，嚴格適用的於繁忙工廠中工作的絕對每個人。"},{"w":"apply for a job","p":"v. phr.","d":"To make a formal, written request to a company asking to be hired for a specific position.","c":"應徵工作、申請工作","s":"Marcus decided to apply for a job at the new technology firm located in the Daan district.","t":"馬庫斯決定去應徵位於大安區的那家新科技公司的工作。"},{"w":"apply for a school","p":"v. phr.","d":"To submit a formal request and necessary documents to be admitted into an educational institution.","c":"申請學校","s":"Before you apply for a school abroad, you must achieve a high score on standardized English exams like the TOEFL.","t":"在你申請國外學校之前，你必須在托福等標準化英文測驗中取得高分。"},{"w":"apply for a scholarship","p":"v. phr.","d":"To formally request financial aid from an institution to help pay for your education.","c":"申請獎學金","s":"Since her family was low-income, Chloe had to apply for a scholarship to cover her university tuition fees.","t":"由於她的家庭收入較低，克洛伊必須申請獎學金來支付她的大學學費。"},{"w":"apply to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To use a rule, idea, or piece of information in a specific situation, or to be relevant to someone.","c":"應用於…、適用於…","s":"The new safety regulations regarding school field trips apply to all educational institutions in Taiwan.","t":"關於學校戶外教學的新安全規定，適用於台灣所有的教育機構。"},{"w":"application","p":"n. [C]","d":"A computer program or mobile software designed to perform a specific task for the user (often shortened to \"app\").","c":"應用程式","s":"This interactive vocabulary application allows students to track their test performance and practice spelling on mobile phones.","t":"這款互動式單字應用程式讓學生能在手機上追蹤自己的測驗表現並練習拼字。"},{"w":"apply sth to","p":"v. phr.","d":"To spread a substance, such as cream, ointment, or paint, onto a surface.","c":"將…塗抹於…","s":"You should gently apply the medical ointment to your shoulders to ease the pain from the severe sunburn.","t":"你應該將醫療軟膏輕輕地塗抹於肩膀上，以減輕嚴重曬傷所造成的疼痛。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to give intellectual, moral, and social instruction to someone.","c":"教育","s":"The highly passionate librarian tirelessly worked to properly educate the completely confused new students on the complex computer catalog system.","t":"熱情極高的圖書館員不知疲倦地工作，以適當地在複雜的電腦目錄系統上教育完全困惑的新學生。"},{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the process of receiving or giving systematic instruction, especially at a school or university.","c":"教育","s":"Acquiring a high-quality university education is widely considered absolutely vital for eventually securing a completely stable and highly profitable modern career.","t":"獲得高品質的大學教育被廣泛認為對於最終獲得一份完全穩定且高利潤的現代職業是絕對至關重要的。"},{"w":"educational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the provision of education; intended or serving to educate or enlighten.","c":"教育的；有教育意義的","s":"The long historical movie was certainly highly educational, but unfortunately, absolutely all the young energetic students thought it was incredibly boring.","t":"這部長篇歷史電影確實高度有教育意義的，但不幸的是，絕對所有年輕充滿活力的學生都認為它極其無聊。"},{"w":"access","p":"n. / v.","d":"the means or opportunity to approach or enter a place; to approach or enter.","c":"進入（的權利）；存取","s":"You will definitely need a highly special electronic security card to properly access this highly restricted and completely secret part of the building.","t":"你肯定需要一張非常特殊的電子安全卡，才能適當地進入（存取）建築物這個受到高度限制且完全機密的部分。"},{"w":"have access to","p":"phr.","d":"to have the right or opportunity to use something.","c":"有權限使用...","s":"Only officially registered university students and strict professors actually have completely free access to the massive historical books in the old library.","t":"只有正式註冊的大學生和嚴格的教授實際上才有權限完全免費使用舊圖書館裡的大量歷史書籍。"},{"w":"gain access to","p":"phr.","d":"to obtain the ability to enter a place or look at something.","c":"獲得存取/進入權","s":"The skilled computer hacker unfortunately managed to gain access to the secure and private national banking system.","t":"這位技術高超的電腦駭客不幸地設法迅速獲得存取/進入權，進入安全且隱私的國家銀行系統。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be reached or entered.","c":"易接近的；可使用的","s":"The progressive modern city brilliantly ensured that absolutely all highly important public buildings are completely accessible to physically disabled citizens in wheelchairs.","t":"這個進步的現代城市出色地確保了絕對所有極其重要的公共建築，都對坐輪椅的肢體殘疾公民是完全易接近的（可使用的）。"},{"w":"accessibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to approach, reach, enter, speak with, or use.","c":"可達性；無障礙","s":"Improving the overall physical accessibility of the terribly designed old train station is undeniably a highly urgent priority for the new city mayor.","t":"改善設計糟糕的舊火車站整體的實體無障礙（可達性），無疑是新任市長極度緊迫的首要任務。"},{"w":"specialist","p":"n.","d":"a person who concentrates primarily on a particular subject or activity.","c":"專家；專科醫生","s":"A highly experienced skin specialist at the incredibly busy local hospital desperately tried to quickly find out exactly what was wrong with the poor patient.","t":"極其繁忙的當地醫院裡一位經驗豐富的皮膚專科醫生拚命試圖迅速查明可憐的病患到底出了什麼問題。"},{"w":"computer specialist","p":"phr.","d":"a person with advanced knowledge of computer systems.","c":"電腦專家","s":"Intelligent Fiona is currently studying incredibly hard at the modern university to eventually become a highly paid and totally respected computer specialist.","t":"聰明的費歐娜目前正在現代化大學裡極其努力地學習，以最終成為一名高薪且完全受人尊敬的電腦專家。"},{"w":"specialize in","p":"v.","d":"to concentrate on and become expert in a particular subject or skill.","c":"專攻","s":"That popular and delicious international restaurant specifically chooses to specialize in spicy and authentic Indian curry dishes.","t":"那家極受歡迎且美味的國際餐廳，特別聰明地選擇專攻辛辣且道地的印度咖哩菜餚。"},{"w":"expert","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very knowledgeable about or skillful in a particular area.","c":"專家","s":"If you struggle with complex legal tax problems, you should consider hiring a trained financial expert immediately.","t":"如果你正在與複雜的合法稅務問題掙扎，你應該強烈考慮立刻聘請一位受過訓練的財務專家。"},{"w":"specialized","p":"adj.","d":"requiring or involving detailed and specific knowledge or training.","c":"專業的","s":"Fixing that rare and expensive vintage sports car requires specialized tools that ordinary mechanics do not possess.","t":"修理那輛罕見且昂貴的復古跑車，嚴格需要普通的技工根本沒有的專業的工具。"},{"w":"imitate","p":"v.","d":"to copy or simulate.","c":"模仿","s":"Young children often learn basic social behaviors by trying to imitate the actions of their parents.","t":"幼童通常藉由試著模仿父母的行為來學習基本的社交行為。"},{"w":"imitation","p":"n.","d":"the action of using someone or something as a model.","c":"模仿；仿製品","s":"The talented young comedian did an absolutely fantastic and highly entertaining imitation of the completely famous pop singer Michael Jackson singing on stage.","t":"才華洋溢的年輕喜劇演員對完全著名的流行歌手麥可·傑克森在舞台上唱歌進行了絕對美妙且極具娛樂性的模仿。"},{"w":"imitative","p":"adj.","d":"copying or following a model or example.","c":"模仿的","s":"Early classical art in that deeply historic region was often heavily imitative of the highly complex beautiful styles brought over by the conquering ancient Romans.","t":"該深具歷史意義地區的早期古典藝術，往往重度模仿的征服的古羅馬人帶來的極其複雜美麗風格。"},{"w":"fake","p":"adj.","d":"not genuine; imitation or counterfeit.","c":"假的","s":"The naive tourist foolishly bought what heavily looked like an extremely expensive designer bag, but it completely turned out to clearly be a cheap fake copy.","t":"天真的遊客愚蠢地買了一個看起來像極其昂貴設計師包的東西，但它完全證明顯然是一個便宜的假的仿製品。"},{"w":"realm","p":"n.","d":"a kingdom; a field or domain of activity or interest.","c":"領域；王國","s":"The exciting and fascinating story mainly takes place in a magical realm that is full of strange and dangerous wild creatures.","t":"刺激且迷人的故事主要發生在一個神奇的領域（王國），那裡充滿了奇怪且危險的野生生物。"},{"w":"magical realm","p":"phr.","d":"a fictional world where magic exists.","c":"魔法王國","s":"The brave young hero courageously traveled into a dark and unpredictable magical realm to successfully save his kidnapped younger brother.","t":"勇敢的年輕英雄英勇地進入了一個黑暗且不可預測的魔法王國，以成功安全地拯救他被綁架的弟弟。"},{"w":"in the realm of","p":"phr.","d":"within the specific area or field of something.","c":"在...領域中","s":"Significant new discoveries in the realm of modern medical science continue to improve human life every single day.","t":"現代醫學科學領域中的重大新發現，每天都持續改善人類的生活。"},{"w":"kingdom","p":"n.","d":"a country, state, or territory ruled by a king or queen.","c":"王國","s":"The benevolent and widely respected old queen ruled her peaceful and wealthy kingdom for over sixty glorious years.","t":"真正仁慈且深受廣泛尊敬的老女王，統治她和平且富有的王國超過六十個輝煌的年頭。"},{"w":"domain","p":"n.","d":"an area of territory owned or controlled by a ruler or government; a specified sphere of activity or knowledge.","c":"領域；領土","s":"Complex mathematical physics is the specific domain of highly trained scientists, not ordinary people.","t":"複雜的數學物理是受過高度訓練的科學家的特定領域，而不是一般人的領域。"},{"w":"array","p":"n.","d":"an impressive display or range of a particular type of thing.","c":"一系列；陣列","s":"There is a surprisingly wide and impressive array of brightly colored flowers and useful modern gardening products available at the busy weekend market.","t":"在繁忙的週末市場上，有著令人驚訝地廣泛且令人難以置信的令人印象深刻的一系列色彩鮮豔的花朵和有用的現代園藝產品直接可用。"},{"w":"an array of","p":"phr.","d":"a large group of things or people, especially one that is attractive or causes admiration.","c":"一系列","s":"The massive modern international supermarket proudly offers an array of fresh tropical fruits imported from sunny South America.","t":"這家大型的現代國際超市自豪地提供一系列從陽光充足的南美洲進口的新鮮熱帶水果。"},{"w":"a vast array of","p":"phr.","d":"a very large and impressive collection or display.","c":"大量的一系列","s":"The wealthy collector owns a vast array of rare and expensive antique silver coins.","t":"這位富有的收藏家擁有大量的一系列稀有且昂貴的古董銀幣。"},{"w":"a wide array of","p":"phr.","d":"a broad and diverse collection.","c":"廣泛的一系列","s":"To satisfy all its customers, the popular new bakery offers a wide array of sweet and delicious fresh pastries.","t":"為了滿足所有顧客，這家受歡迎的新麵包店提供各式各樣香甜美味的新鮮糕點。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activity done for enjoyment when one is not working.","c":"娛樂；消遣","s":"The exhausted and stressed workers need adequate time for healthy recreation to maintain their mental health.","t":"疲憊且壓力大的員工需要足夠的時間從事健康的休閒娛樂，以維持心理健康。"},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or denoting activity done for enjoyment when one is not working.","c":"娛樂的；休閒的","s":"The modern community center securely provides all sorts of highly exciting recreational activities for energetic young children to happily take part in during their free time.","t":"現代社區中心安全地為精力充沛的幼童提供了各種極其令人興奮的娛樂的活動，讓他們在空閒時間快樂地參與。"},{"w":"recreational activities","p":"phr.","d":"things people do for fun and enjoyment.","c":"休閒活動","s":"During the relaxing summer vacation, we enjoy doing fun recreational activities like swimming and reading.","t":"在輕鬆的暑假期間，我們喜歡從事有趣的休閒活動，例如游泳和閱讀。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to bring something into existence.","c":"創造","s":"The brilliant and passionate chef constantly manages to create new and delicious dishes for his wealthy restaurant customers.","t":"才華洋溢且深具熱情的廚師不斷設法積極地為他富有的餐廳顧客創造全新且美味的菜餚。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or involving the imagination or original ideas, especially in the production of an artistic work.","c":"有創意的","s":"The creatively designer came up with a completely new idea for the poster that nobody had seen before.","t":"這位有創意的設計師為海報想出了一個從未有人見過的全新點子。"},{"w":"skeptical","p":"adj.","d":"not easily convinced; having doubts or reservations.","c":"懷疑的","s":"Highly intelligent Carla is understandably quite skeptical about her realistic chances of actually getting the highly competitive new office job in the city.","t":"聰明的卡拉對她實際獲得這份城市中競爭激烈的新辦公室工作的現實機會感到相當懷疑的，這是可以理解的。"},{"w":"skeptic","p":"n.","d":"a person inclined to question or doubt all accepted opinions.","c":"懷疑論者","s":"Even the most stubborn skeptic in the completely quiet room had to finally totally admit that the brilliant new scientific theory actually worked flawlessly.","t":"即使是安靜的房間裡最固執的懷疑論者，最終也不得不承認這個出色的新科學理論實際上完美無瑕地運作。"},{"w":"skepticism","p":"n.","d":"a skeptical attitude; doubt as to the truth of something.","c":"懷疑態度","s":"Despite the government's highly positive official promises, there is still widespread public skepticism heavily surrounding the complex new economic policy.","t":"儘管政府有積極的官方承諾，但對於這項複雜的新經濟政策，公眾仍然普遍存在著強烈的懷疑態度。"},{"w":"be skeptical about","p":"phr.","d":"to have doubts regarding something.","c":"對...感到懷疑","s":"It is absolutely natural to be highly skeptical about surprisingly cheap products sold on the vast internet by completely unknown companies.","t":"對於在廣闊網路上由完全未知的公司出售的驚人廉價產品對（此）感到高度懷疑是絕對自然的。"},{"w":"doubtful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling uncertain about something.","c":"可疑的；懷疑的","s":"Because the sky is incredibly dark and cloudy, it is highly doubtful that we will safely see the beautiful sun at all today.","t":"因為天空極其黑暗且多雲，我們今天是否能安全地看到美麗的太陽是高度懷疑的。"},{"w":"distinguish","p":"v.","d":"to recognize or treat someone or something as different.","c":"區分；分辨","s":"The completely identical young twins can actually only be successfully distinguished from one another by carefully looking closely at the specific color of their eyes.","t":"這對完全同卵的年輕雙胞胎，實際上只能透過仔細近看她們眼睛的特定顏色，才能成功地從彼此中被區分出來。"},{"w":"distinguish between","p":"phr.","d":"to recognize the difference between two people or things.","c":"區分（兩者）","s":"Young children must learn to distinguish between right and wrong.","t":"幼童必須學會分辨是非對錯。"},{"w":"distinguish from","p":"phr.","d":"to show how one thing is different from another.","c":"區別","s":"The fascinating tall giraffe is easily distinguished from all other wild animals by its incredibly long neck and unique brown spots.","t":"迷人的高大長頸鹿很容易透過牠令人難以置信的長脖子和獨特的棕色斑點與所有其他野生動物區別開來。"},{"w":"distinguishable","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to be recognized or identified as different.","c":"可辨別的","s":"The fake painting was barely distinguishable from the original, fooling even the experts.","t":"這幅假畫與真跡幾乎無法區分，甚至連專家都被騙了。"},{"w":"distinguished","p":"adj.","d":"Successful, authoritative, and commanding great respect from others due to excellence.","c":"卓越的、傑出的、著名的","s":"The university invited a distinguished professor of financial theory to deliver a speech at the summer camp.","t":"這所大學邀請了一位在金融理論領域卓越的（傑出的）教授在夏令營上發表專題演講。"},{"w":"tell","p":"v.","d":"To know, realize, or judge something correctly based on evidence or signs.","c":"看得出、能分辨、知道","s":"I could tell from Chloe's bright smile that she had successfully passed her standardized English exam.","t":"從克洛伊燦爛的笑容中，我看得出（知道）她已經成功通過了她的標準化英文測驗。"},{"w":"tell a from b","p":"v. phr.","d":"To distinguish one person or thing from another based on their unique traits.","c":"分辨A與B","s":"Without looking at the label, it is almost impossible to tell a from b genetically-modified corn.","t":"如果不看標籤，幾乎不可能分辨有機玉米與基因改造玉米。"},{"w":"tell the difference","p":"v. phr.","d":"To recognize or identify how two or more things or people are not the same.","c":"辨別差異、看出不同","s":"The two twin brothers look so much alike that even their classmates can hardly tell the difference between them.","t":"這對雙胞胎兄弟長得實在太像了，甚至連他們的同班同學都很難辨別他們之間的差異（看出不同）。"},{"w":"make a difference","p":"v. phr.","d":"To have a significant effect, improvement, or influence on a person, situation, or thing.","c":"產生影響、有關係、起作用","s":"Incorporating interactive web games into the curriculum can truly make a huge difference in student motivation.","t":"將互動式網頁遊戲融入課程中，確實能對學生的學習動機產生巨大的影響（起作用）。"}]}];
